-- BSB verses (5182). Requires books and chapters first.
insert into public.verses (chapter_id, number, osis_ref, text)
select c.id, x.verse, x.ref, x.body
from (values
('MAT', 23, 10, 'MAT.23.10', 'Nor are you to be called instructors, for you have one Instructor, the Christ.'),
('MAT', 23, 11, 'MAT.23.11', 'The greatest among you shall be your servant.'),
('MAT', 23, 12, 'MAT.23.12', 'For whoever exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted.'),
('MAT', 23, 13, 'MAT.23.13', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You shut the kingdom of heaven in men’s faces. You yourselves do not enter, nor will you let in those who wish to enter.'),
('MAT', 23, 15, 'MAT.23.15', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You traverse land and sea to win a single convert, and when he becomes one, you make him twice as much a son of hell as you are.'),
('MAT', 23, 16, 'MAT.23.16', 'Woe to you, blind guides! You say, ‘If anyone swears by the temple, it means nothing; but if anyone swears by the gold of the temple, he is bound by his oath.’'),
('MAT', 23, 17, 'MAT.23.17', 'You blind fools! Which is greater: the gold, or the temple that makes it sacred?'),
('MAT', 23, 18, 'MAT.23.18', 'And you say, ‘If anyone swears by the altar, it means nothing; but if anyone swears by the gift on it, he is bound by his oath.’'),
('MAT', 23, 19, 'MAT.23.19', 'You blind men! Which is greater: the gift, or the altar that makes it sacred?'),
('MAT', 23, 20, 'MAT.23.20', 'So then, he who swears by the altar swears by it and by everything on it.'),
('MAT', 23, 21, 'MAT.23.21', 'And he who swears by the temple swears by it and by the One who dwells in it.'),
('MAT', 23, 22, 'MAT.23.22', 'And he who swears by heaven swears by God’s throne and by the One who sits on it.'),
('MAT', 23, 23, 'MAT.23.23', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You pay tithes of mint, dill, and cumin. But you have disregarded the weightier matters of the law: justice, mercy, and faithfulness. You should have practiced the latter, without neglecting the former.'),
('MAT', 23, 24, 'MAT.23.24', 'You blind guides! You strain out a gnat but swallow a camel.'),
('MAT', 23, 25, 'MAT.23.25', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence.'),
('MAT', 23, 26, 'MAT.23.26', 'Blind Pharisee! First clean the inside of the cup and dish, so that the outside may become clean as well.'),
('MAT', 23, 27, 'MAT.23.27', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You are like whitewashed tombs, which look beautiful on the outside but on the inside are full of dead men’s bones and every kind of impurity.'),
('MAT', 23, 28, 'MAT.23.28', 'In the same way, on the outside you appear to be righteous, but on the inside you are full of hypocrisy and wickedness.'),
('MAT', 23, 29, 'MAT.23.29', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You build tombs for the prophets and decorate the monuments of the righteous.'),
('MAT', 23, 30, 'MAT.23.30', 'And you say, ‘If we had lived in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partners with them in shedding the blood of the prophets.’'),
('MAT', 23, 31, 'MAT.23.31', 'So you testify against yourselves that you are the sons of those who murdered the prophets.'),
('MAT', 23, 32, 'MAT.23.32', 'Fill up, then, the measure of the sin of your fathers.'),
('MAT', 23, 33, 'MAT.23.33', 'You snakes! You brood of vipers! How will you escape the sentence of hell?'),
('MAT', 23, 34, 'MAT.23.34', 'Because of this, I am sending you prophets and wise men and teachers. Some of them you will kill and crucify, and others you will flog in your synagogues and persecute from town to town.'),
('MAT', 23, 35, 'MAT.23.35', 'And so upon you will come all the righteous blood shed on earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah son of Berechiah, whom you murdered between the temple and the altar.'),
('MAT', 23, 36, 'MAT.23.36', 'Truly I tell you, all these things will come upon this generation.'),
('MAT', 23, 37, 'MAT.23.37', 'O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those sent to her, how often I have longed to gather your children together, as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, but you were unwilling!'),
('MAT', 23, 38, 'MAT.23.38', 'Look, your house is left to you desolate.'),
('MAT', 23, 39, 'MAT.23.39', 'For I tell you that you will not see Me again until you say, ‘Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord.’”'),
('MAT', 24, 1, 'MAT.24.1', 'As Jesus left the temple and was walking away, His disciples came up to Him to point out its buildings.'),
('MAT', 24, 2, 'MAT.24.2', '“Do you see all these things?” He replied. “Truly I tell you, not one stone here will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”'),
('MAT', 24, 3, 'MAT.24.3', 'While Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives, the disciples came to Him privately. “Tell us,” they said, “when will these things happen, and what will be the sign of Your coming and of the end of the age?”'),
('MAT', 24, 4, 'MAT.24.4', 'Jesus answered, “See to it that no one deceives you.'),
('MAT', 24, 5, 'MAT.24.5', 'For many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am the Christ,’ and will deceive many.'),
('MAT', 24, 6, 'MAT.24.6', 'You will hear of wars and rumors of wars, but see to it that you are not alarmed. These things must happen, but the end is still to come.'),
('MAT', 24, 7, 'MAT.24.7', 'Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be famines and earthquakes in various places.'),
('MAT', 24, 8, 'MAT.24.8', 'All these are the beginning of birth pains.'),
('MAT', 24, 9, 'MAT.24.9', 'Then they will deliver you over to be persecuted and killed, and you will be hated by all nations because of My name.'),
('MAT', 24, 10, 'MAT.24.10', 'At that time many will fall away and will betray and hate one another,'),
('MAT', 24, 11, 'MAT.24.11', 'and many false prophets will arise and deceive many.'),
('MAT', 24, 12, 'MAT.24.12', 'Because of the multiplication of wickedness, the love of most will grow cold.'),
('MAT', 24, 13, 'MAT.24.13', 'But the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.'),
('MAT', 24, 14, 'MAT.24.14', 'And this gospel of the kingdom will be preached in all the world as a testimony to all nations, and then the end will come.'),
('MAT', 24, 15, 'MAT.24.15', 'So when you see standing in the holy place ‘the abomination of desolation,’ spoken of by the prophet Daniel (let the reader understand),'),
('MAT', 24, 16, 'MAT.24.16', 'then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains.'),
('MAT', 24, 17, 'MAT.24.17', 'Let no one on the housetop come down to retrieve anything from his house.'),
('MAT', 24, 18, 'MAT.24.18', 'And let no one in the field return for his cloak.'),
('MAT', 24, 19, 'MAT.24.19', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers!'),
('MAT', 24, 20, 'MAT.24.20', 'Pray that your flight will not occur in the winter or on the Sabbath.'),
('MAT', 24, 21, 'MAT.24.21', 'For at that time there will be great tribulation, unseen from the beginning of the world until now, and never to be seen again.'),
('MAT', 24, 22, 'MAT.24.22', 'If those days had not been cut short, nobody would be saved. But for the sake of the elect, those days will be cut short.'),
('MAT', 24, 23, 'MAT.24.23', 'At that time, if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is the Christ!’ or ‘There He is!’ do not believe it.'),
('MAT', 24, 24, 'MAT.24.24', 'For false Christs and false prophets will appear and perform great signs and wonders to deceive even the elect, if that were possible.'),
('MAT', 24, 25, 'MAT.24.25', 'See, I have told you in advance.'),
('MAT', 24, 26, 'MAT.24.26', 'So if they tell you, ‘There He is, in the wilderness,’ do not go out, or, ‘Here He is, in the inner rooms,’ do not believe it.'),
('MAT', 24, 27, 'MAT.24.27', 'For just as the lightning comes from the east and flashes as far as the west, so will be the coming of the Son of Man.'),
('MAT', 24, 28, 'MAT.24.28', 'Wherever there is a carcass, there the vultures will gather.'),
('MAT', 24, 29, 'MAT.24.29', 'Immediately after the tribulation of those days: ‘The sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light; the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken.’'),
('MAT', 24, 30, 'MAT.24.30', 'At that time the sign of the Son of Man will appear in heaven, and all the tribes of the earth will mourn. They will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.'),
('MAT', 24, 31, 'MAT.24.31', 'And He will send out His angels with a loud trumpet call, and they will gather His elect from the four winds, from one end of the heavens to the other.'),
('MAT', 24, 32, 'MAT.24.32', 'Now learn this lesson from the fig tree: As soon as its branches become tender and sprout leaves, you know that summer is near.'),
('MAT', 24, 33, 'MAT.24.33', 'So also, when you see all these things, you will know that He is near, right at the door.'),
('MAT', 24, 34, 'MAT.24.34', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.'),
('MAT', 24, 35, 'MAT.24.35', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.'),
('MAT', 24, 36, 'MAT.24.36', 'No one knows about that day or hour, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.'),
('MAT', 24, 37, 'MAT.24.37', 'As it was in the days of Noah, so will it be at the coming of the Son of Man.'),
('MAT', 24, 38, 'MAT.24.38', 'For in the days before the flood, people were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, up to the day Noah entered the ark.'),
('MAT', 24, 39, 'MAT.24.39', 'And they were oblivious until the flood came and swept them all away. So will it be at the coming of the Son of Man.'),
('MAT', 24, 40, 'MAT.24.40', 'Two men will be in the field: one will be taken and the other left.'),
('MAT', 24, 41, 'MAT.24.41', 'Two women will be grinding at the mill: one will be taken and the other left.'),
('MAT', 24, 42, 'MAT.24.42', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know the day on which your Lord will come.'),
('MAT', 24, 43, 'MAT.24.43', 'But understand this: If the homeowner had known in which watch of the night the thief was coming, he would have kept watch and would not have let his house be broken into.'),
('MAT', 24, 44, 'MAT.24.44', 'For this reason, you also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour you do not expect.'),
('MAT', 24, 45, 'MAT.24.45', 'Who then is the faithful and wise servant, whom the master has put in charge of his household, to give the others their food at the proper time?'),
('MAT', 24, 46, 'MAT.24.46', 'Blessed is that servant whose master finds him doing so when he returns.'),
('MAT', 24, 47, 'MAT.24.47', 'Truly I tell you, he will put him in charge of all his possessions.'),
('MAT', 24, 48, 'MAT.24.48', 'But suppose that servant is wicked and says in his heart, ‘My master will be away a long time.’'),
('MAT', 24, 49, 'MAT.24.49', 'And he begins to beat his fellow servants and to eat and drink with drunkards.'),
('MAT', 24, 50, 'MAT.24.50', 'The master of that servant will come on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not anticipate.'),
('MAT', 24, 51, 'MAT.24.51', 'Then he will cut him to pieces and assign him a place with the hypocrites, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.'),
('MAT', 25, 1, 'MAT.25.1', '“At that time the kingdom of heaven will be like ten virgins who took their lamps and went out to meet the bridegroom.'),
('MAT', 25, 2, 'MAT.25.2', 'Five of them were foolish, and five were wise.'),
('MAT', 25, 3, 'MAT.25.3', 'The foolish ones took their lamps but did not take along any extra oil.'),
('MAT', 25, 4, 'MAT.25.4', 'But the wise ones took oil in flasks along with their lamps.'),
('MAT', 25, 5, 'MAT.25.5', 'When the bridegroom was delayed, they all became drowsy and fell asleep.'),
('MAT', 25, 6, 'MAT.25.6', 'At midnight the cry rang out: ‘Here is the bridegroom! Come out to meet him!’'),
('MAT', 25, 7, 'MAT.25.7', 'Then all the virgins woke up and trimmed their lamps.'),
('MAT', 25, 8, 'MAT.25.8', 'The foolish ones said to the wise, ‘Give us some of your oil; our lamps are going out.’'),
('MAT', 25, 9, 'MAT.25.9', '‘No,’ said the wise ones, ‘or there may not be enough for both us and you. Instead, go to those who sell oil and buy some for yourselves.’'),
('MAT', 25, 10, 'MAT.25.10', 'But while they were on their way to buy it, the bridegroom arrived. Those who were ready went in with him to the wedding banquet, and the door was shut.'),
('MAT', 25, 11, 'MAT.25.11', 'Later the other virgins arrived and said, ‘Lord, lord, open the door for us!’'),
('MAT', 25, 12, 'MAT.25.12', 'But he replied, ‘Truly I tell you, I do not know you.’'),
('MAT', 25, 13, 'MAT.25.13', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know the day or the hour.'),
('MAT', 25, 14, 'MAT.25.14', 'For it is just like a man going on a journey, who called his servants and entrusted them with his possessions.'),
('MAT', 25, 15, 'MAT.25.15', 'To one he gave five talents, to another two talents, and to another one talent—each according to his own ability. And he went on his journey.'),
('MAT', 25, 16, 'MAT.25.16', 'The servant who had received the five talents went at once and put them to work and gained five more.'),
('MAT', 25, 17, 'MAT.25.17', 'Likewise, the one with the two talents gained two more.'),
('MAT', 25, 18, 'MAT.25.18', 'But the servant who had received the one talent went off, dug a hole in the ground, and hid his master’s money.'),
('MAT', 25, 19, 'MAT.25.19', 'After a long time the master of those servants returned and settled accounts with them.'),
('MAT', 25, 20, 'MAT.25.20', 'The servant who had received the five talents came and presented five more. ‘Master,’ he said, ‘you entrusted me with five talents. See, I have gained five more.’'),
('MAT', 25, 21, 'MAT.25.21', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Enter into the joy of your master!’'),
('MAT', 25, 22, 'MAT.25.22', 'The servant who had received the two talents also came and said, ‘Master, you entrusted me with two talents. See, I have gained two more.’'),
('MAT', 25, 23, 'MAT.25.23', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Enter into the joy of your master!’'),
('MAT', 25, 24, 'MAT.25.24', 'Finally, the servant who had received the one talent came and said, ‘Master, I knew that you are a hard man, reaping where you have not sown and gathering where you have not scattered seed.'),
('MAT', 25, 25, 'MAT.25.25', 'So I was afraid and went out and hid your talent in the ground. See, you have what belongs to you.’'),
('MAT', 25, 26, 'MAT.25.26', '‘You wicked, lazy servant!’ replied his master. ‘You knew that I reap where I have not sown and gather where I have not scattered seed.'),
('MAT', 25, 27, 'MAT.25.27', 'Then you should have deposited my money with the bankers, and on my return I would have received it back with interest.'),
('MAT', 25, 28, 'MAT.25.28', 'Therefore take the talent from him and give it to the one who has ten talents.'),
('MAT', 25, 29, 'MAT.25.29', 'For everyone who has will be given more, and he will have an abundance. But the one who does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.'),
('MAT', 25, 30, 'MAT.25.30', 'And throw that worthless servant into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.’'),
('MAT', 25, 31, 'MAT.25.31', 'When the Son of Man comes in His glory, and all the angels with Him, He will sit on His glorious throne.'),
('MAT', 25, 32, 'MAT.25.32', 'All the nations will be gathered before Him, and He will separate the people one from another, as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats.'),
('MAT', 25, 33, 'MAT.25.33', 'He will place the sheep on His right and the goats on His left.'),
('MAT', 25, 34, 'MAT.25.34', 'Then the King will say to those on His right, ‘Come, you who are blessed by My Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.'),
('MAT', 25, 35, 'MAT.25.35', 'For I was hungry and you gave Me something to eat, I was thirsty and you gave Me something to drink, I was a stranger and you took Me in,'),
('MAT', 25, 36, 'MAT.25.36', 'I was naked and you clothed Me, I was sick and you looked after Me, I was in prison and you visited Me.’'),
('MAT', 25, 37, 'MAT.25.37', 'Then the righteous will answer Him, ‘Lord, when did we see You hungry and feed You, or thirsty and give You something to drink?'),
('MAT', 25, 38, 'MAT.25.38', 'When did we see You a stranger and take You in, or naked and clothe You?'),
('MAT', 25, 39, 'MAT.25.39', 'When did we see You sick or in prison and visit You?’'),
('MAT', 25, 40, 'MAT.25.40', 'And the King will reply, ‘Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers of Mine, you did for Me.’'),
('MAT', 25, 41, 'MAT.25.41', 'Then He will say to those on His left, ‘Depart from Me, you who are cursed, into the eternal fire prepared for the devil and his angels.'),
('MAT', 25, 42, 'MAT.25.42', 'For I was hungry and you gave Me nothing to eat, I was thirsty and you gave Me nothing to drink,'),
('MAT', 25, 43, 'MAT.25.43', 'I was a stranger and you did not take Me in, I was naked and you did not clothe Me, I was sick and in prison and you did not look after Me.’'),
('MAT', 25, 44, 'MAT.25.44', 'And they too will reply, ‘Lord, when did we see You hungry or thirsty or a stranger or naked or sick or in prison, and did not minister to You?’'),
('MAT', 25, 45, 'MAT.25.45', 'Then the King will answer, ‘Truly I tell you, whatever you did not do for one of the least of these, you did not do for Me.’'),
('MAT', 25, 46, 'MAT.25.46', 'And they will go away into eternal punishment, but the righteous into eternal life.”'),
('MAT', 26, 1, 'MAT.26.1', 'When Jesus had finished saying all these things, He told His disciples,'),
('MAT', 26, 2, 'MAT.26.2', '“You know that the Passover is two days away, and the Son of Man will be handed over to be crucified.”'),
('MAT', 26, 3, 'MAT.26.3', 'At that time the chief priests and elders of the people assembled in the courtyard of the high priest, whose name was Caiaphas,'),
('MAT', 26, 4, 'MAT.26.4', 'and they conspired to arrest Jesus covertly and kill Him.'),
('MAT', 26, 5, 'MAT.26.5', '“But not during the feast,” they said, “or there may be a riot among the people.”'),
('MAT', 26, 6, 'MAT.26.6', 'While Jesus was in Bethany in the home of Simon the Leper,'),
('MAT', 26, 7, 'MAT.26.7', 'a woman came to Him with an alabaster jar of expensive perfume, which she poured on His head as He reclined at the table.'),
('MAT', 26, 8, 'MAT.26.8', 'When the disciples saw this, they were indignant and asked, “Why this waste?'),
('MAT', 26, 9, 'MAT.26.9', 'This perfume could have been sold at a high price, and the money given to the poor.”'),
('MAT', 26, 10, 'MAT.26.10', 'Aware of this, Jesus asked, “Why are you bothering this woman? She has done a beautiful deed to Me.'),
('MAT', 26, 11, 'MAT.26.11', 'The poor you will always have with you, but you will not always have Me.'),
('MAT', 26, 12, 'MAT.26.12', 'By pouring this perfume on Me, she has prepared My body for burial.'),
('MAT', 26, 13, 'MAT.26.13', 'Truly I tell you, wherever this gospel is preached in all the world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”'),
('MAT', 26, 14, 'MAT.26.14', 'Then one of the Twelve, the one called Judas Iscariot, went to the chief priests'),
('MAT', 26, 15, 'MAT.26.15', 'and asked, “What are you willing to give me if I hand Him over to you?” And they set out for him thirty pieces of silver.'),
('MAT', 26, 16, 'MAT.26.16', 'So from then on Judas looked for an opportunity to betray Jesus.'),
('MAT', 26, 17, 'MAT.26.17', 'On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, the disciples came to Jesus and asked, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”'),
('MAT', 26, 18, 'MAT.26.18', 'He answered, “Go into the city to a certain man and tell him that the Teacher says, ‘My time is near. I will keep the Passover with My disciples at your house.’”'),
('MAT', 26, 19, 'MAT.26.19', 'So the disciples did as Jesus had directed them and prepared the Passover.'),
('MAT', 26, 20, 'MAT.26.20', 'When evening came, Jesus was reclining with the twelve disciples.'),
('MAT', 26, 21, 'MAT.26.21', 'And while they were eating, He said to them, “Truly I tell you, one of you will betray Me.”'),
('MAT', 26, 22, 'MAT.26.22', 'They were deeply grieved and began to ask Him one after another, “Surely not I, Lord?”'),
('MAT', 26, 23, 'MAT.26.23', 'Jesus answered, “The one who has dipped his hand into the bowl with Me will betray Me.'),
('MAT', 26, 24, 'MAT.26.24', 'The Son of Man will go just as it is written about Him, but woe to that man by whom He is betrayed. It would be better for him if he had not been born.”'),
('MAT', 26, 25, 'MAT.26.25', 'Then Judas, who would betray Him, said, “Surely not I, Rabbi?” Jesus answered, “You have said it yourself.”'),
('MAT', 26, 26, 'MAT.26.26', 'While they were eating, Jesus took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to the disciples, saying, “Take and eat; this is My body.”'),
('MAT', 26, 27, 'MAT.26.27', 'Then He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying, “Drink from it, all of you.'),
('MAT', 26, 28, 'MAT.26.28', 'This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many for the forgiveness of sins.'),
('MAT', 26, 29, 'MAT.26.29', 'I tell you, I will not drink of this fruit of the vine from now on until that day when I drink it anew with you in My Father’s kingdom.”'),
('MAT', 26, 30, 'MAT.26.30', 'And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.'),
('MAT', 26, 31, 'MAT.26.31', 'Then Jesus said to them, “This very night you will all fall away on account of Me. For it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep of the flock will be scattered.’'),
('MAT', 26, 32, 'MAT.26.32', 'But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”'),
('MAT', 26, 33, 'MAT.26.33', 'Peter said to Him, “Even if all fall away on account of You, I never will.”'),
('MAT', 26, 34, 'MAT.26.34', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus declared, “this very night, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.”'),
('MAT', 26, 35, 'MAT.26.35', 'Peter replied, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You.” And all the other disciples said the same thing.'),
('MAT', 26, 36, 'MAT.26.36', 'Then Jesus went with His disciples to a place called Gethsemane, and He told them, “Sit here while I go over there and pray.”'),
('MAT', 26, 37, 'MAT.26.37', 'He took with Him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee and began to be sorrowful and deeply distressed.'),
('MAT', 26, 38, 'MAT.26.38', 'Then He said to them, “My soul is consumed with sorrow to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch with Me.”'),
('MAT', 26, 39, 'MAT.26.39', 'Going a little farther, He fell facedown and prayed, “My Father, if it is possible, let this cup pass from Me. Yet not as I will, but as You will.”'),
('MAT', 26, 40, 'MAT.26.40', 'Then Jesus returned to the disciples and found them sleeping. “Were you not able to keep watch with Me for one hour?” He asked Peter.'),
('MAT', 26, 41, 'MAT.26.41', '“Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the body is weak.”'),
('MAT', 26, 42, 'MAT.26.42', 'A second time He went away and prayed, “My Father, if this cup cannot pass unless I drink it, may Your will be done.”'),
('MAT', 26, 43, 'MAT.26.43', 'And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy.'),
('MAT', 26, 44, 'MAT.26.44', 'So He left them and went away once more and prayed a third time, saying the same thing.'),
('MAT', 26, 45, 'MAT.26.45', 'Then He returned to the disciples and said, “Are you still sleeping and resting? Look, the hour is near, and the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.'),
('MAT', 26, 46, 'MAT.26.46', 'Rise, let us go! See, My betrayer is approaching!”'),
('MAT', 26, 47, 'MAT.26.47', 'While Jesus was still speaking, Judas, one of the Twelve, arrived, accompanied by a large crowd armed with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests and elders of the people.'),
('MAT', 26, 48, 'MAT.26.48', 'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them: “The One I kiss is the man; arrest Him.”'),
('MAT', 26, 49, 'MAT.26.49', 'Going directly to Jesus, he said, “Greetings, Rabbi!” and kissed Him.'),
('MAT', 26, 50, 'MAT.26.50', '“Friend,” Jesus replied, “do what you came for.” Then the men stepped forward, seized Jesus, and arrested Him.'),
('MAT', 26, 51, 'MAT.26.51', 'At this, one of Jesus’ companions drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.'),
('MAT', 26, 52, 'MAT.26.52', '“Put your sword back in its place,” Jesus said to him. “For all who draw the sword will die by the sword.'),
('MAT', 26, 53, 'MAT.26.53', 'Are you not aware that I can call on My Father, and He will at once put at My disposal more than twelve legions of angels?'),
('MAT', 26, 54, 'MAT.26.54', 'But how then would the Scriptures be fulfilled that say it must happen this way?”'),
('MAT', 26, 55, 'MAT.26.55', 'At that time Jesus said to the crowd, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as you would an outlaw? Every day I sat teaching in the temple courts, and you did not arrest Me.'),
('MAT', 26, 56, 'MAT.26.56', 'But this has all happened so that the writings of the prophets would be fulfilled.” Then all the disciples deserted Him and fled.'),
('MAT', 26, 57, 'MAT.26.57', 'Those who had arrested Jesus led Him away to the house of Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and elders had gathered.'),
('MAT', 26, 58, 'MAT.26.58', 'But Peter followed Him at a distance, right up to the courtyard of the high priest. And he went in and sat down with the guards to see the outcome.'),
('MAT', 26, 59, 'MAT.26.59', 'Now the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin were seeking false testimony against Jesus in order to put Him to death.'),
('MAT', 26, 60, 'MAT.26.60', 'But they did not find any, though many false witnesses came forward. Finally two came forward'),
('MAT', 26, 61, 'MAT.26.61', 'and declared, “This man said, ‘I am able to destroy the temple of God and rebuild it in three days.’”'),
('MAT', 26, 62, 'MAT.26.62', 'So the high priest stood up and asked Him, “Have You no answer? What are these men testifying against You?”'),
('MAT', 26, 63, 'MAT.26.63', 'But Jesus remained silent. Then the high priest said to Him, “I charge You under oath by the living God: Tell us if You are the Christ, the Son of God.”'),
('MAT', 26, 64, 'MAT.26.64', '“You have said it yourself,” Jesus answered. “But I say to all of you, from now on you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming on the clouds of heaven.”'),
('MAT', 26, 65, 'MAT.26.65', 'At this, the high priest tore his clothes and declared, “He has blasphemed! Why do we need any more witnesses? Look, now you have heard the blasphemy.'),
('MAT', 26, 66, 'MAT.26.66', 'What do you think?” “He deserves to die,” they answered.'),
('MAT', 26, 67, 'MAT.26.67', 'Then they spit in His face and struck Him. Others slapped Him'),
('MAT', 26, 68, 'MAT.26.68', 'and said, “Prophesy to us, Christ! Who hit You?”'),
('MAT', 26, 69, 'MAT.26.69', 'Meanwhile, Peter was sitting out in the courtyard, and a servant girl came up to him. “You also were with Jesus the Galilean,” she said.'),
('MAT', 26, 70, 'MAT.26.70', 'But he denied it before them all: “I do not know what you are talking about.”'),
('MAT', 26, 71, 'MAT.26.71', 'When Peter had gone out to the gateway, another servant girl saw him and said to the people there, “This man was with Jesus of Nazareth.”'),
('MAT', 26, 72, 'MAT.26.72', 'And again he denied it with an oath: “I do not know the man!”'),
('MAT', 26, 73, 'MAT.26.73', 'After a little while, those standing nearby came up to Peter. “Surely you are one of them,” they said, “for your accent gives you away.”'),
('MAT', 26, 74, 'MAT.26.74', 'At that he began to curse and swear to them, “I do not know the man!” And immediately a rooster crowed.'),
('MAT', 26, 75, 'MAT.26.75', 'Then Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken: “Before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.” And he went outside and wept bitterly.'),
('MAT', 27, 1, 'MAT.27.1', 'When morning came, all the chief priests and elders of the people conspired against Jesus to put Him to death.'),
('MAT', 27, 2, 'MAT.27.2', 'They bound Him, led Him away, and handed Him over to Pilate the governor.'),
('MAT', 27, 3, 'MAT.27.3', 'When Judas, who had betrayed Him, saw that Jesus was condemned, he was filled with remorse and returned the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders.'),
('MAT', 27, 4, 'MAT.27.4', '“I have sinned by betraying innocent blood,” he said. “What is that to us?” they replied. “You bear the responsibility.”'),
('MAT', 27, 5, 'MAT.27.5', 'So Judas threw the silver into the temple and left. Then he went away and hanged himself.'),
('MAT', 27, 6, 'MAT.27.6', 'The chief priests picked up the pieces of silver and said, “It is unlawful to put this into the treasury, since it is blood money.”'),
('MAT', 27, 7, 'MAT.27.7', 'After conferring together, they used the money to buy the potter’s field as a burial place for foreigners.'),
('MAT', 27, 8, 'MAT.27.8', 'That is why it has been called the Field of Blood to this day.'),
('MAT', 27, 9, 'MAT.27.9', 'Then what was spoken through Jeremiah the prophet was fulfilled: “They took the thirty pieces of silver, the price set on Him by the people of Israel,'),
('MAT', 27, 10, 'MAT.27.10', 'and they gave them for the potter’s field, as the Lord had commanded me.”'),
('MAT', 27, 11, 'MAT.27.11', 'Meanwhile Jesus stood before the governor, who questioned Him: “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.'),
('MAT', 27, 12, 'MAT.27.12', 'And when He was accused by the chief priests and elders, He gave no answer.'),
('MAT', 27, 13, 'MAT.27.13', 'Then Pilate asked Him, “Do You not hear how many charges they are bringing against You?”'),
('MAT', 27, 14, 'MAT.27.14', 'But Jesus gave no answer, not even to a single charge, much to the governor’s amazement.'),
('MAT', 27, 15, 'MAT.27.15', 'Now it was the governor’s custom at the feast to release to the crowd a prisoner of their choosing.'),
('MAT', 27, 16, 'MAT.27.16', 'At that time they were holding a notorious prisoner named Barabbas.'),
('MAT', 27, 17, 'MAT.27.17', 'So when the crowd had assembled, Pilate asked them, “Which one do you want me to release to you: Barabbas, or Jesus who is called Christ?”'),
('MAT', 27, 18, 'MAT.27.18', 'For he knew it was out of envy that they had handed Jesus over to him.'),
('MAT', 27, 19, 'MAT.27.19', 'While Pilate was sitting on the judgment seat, his wife sent him this message: “Have nothing to do with that innocent man, for I have suffered terribly in a dream today because of Him.”'),
('MAT', 27, 20, 'MAT.27.20', 'But the chief priests and elders persuaded the crowds to ask for Barabbas and to have Jesus put to death.'),
('MAT', 27, 21, 'MAT.27.21', '“Which of the two do you want me to release to you?” asked the governor. “Barabbas,” they replied.'),
('MAT', 27, 22, 'MAT.27.22', '“What then should I do with Jesus who is called Christ?” Pilate asked. They all answered, “Crucify Him!”'),
('MAT', 27, 23, 'MAT.27.23', '“Why?” asked Pilate. “What evil has He done?” But they shouted all the louder, “Crucify Him!”'),
('MAT', 27, 24, 'MAT.27.24', 'When Pilate saw that he was accomplishing nothing, but that instead a riot was breaking out, he took water and washed his hands before the crowd. “I am innocent of this man’s blood,” he said. “You bear the responsibility.”'),
('MAT', 27, 25, 'MAT.27.25', 'All the people answered, “His blood be on us and on our children!”'),
('MAT', 27, 26, 'MAT.27.26', 'So Pilate released Barabbas to them. But he had Jesus flogged, and handed Him over to be crucified.'),
('MAT', 27, 27, 'MAT.27.27', 'Then the governor’s soldiers took Jesus into the Praetorium and gathered the whole company around Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 28, 'MAT.27.28', 'They stripped Him and put a scarlet robe on Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 29, 'MAT.27.29', 'And they twisted together a crown of thorns and set it on His head. They put a staff in His right hand, knelt down before Him, and mocked Him, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!”'),
('MAT', 27, 30, 'MAT.27.30', 'Then they spit on Him and took the staff and struck Him on the head repeatedly.'),
('MAT', 27, 31, 'MAT.27.31', 'After they had mocked Him, they removed the robe and put His own clothes back on Him. Then they led Him away to crucify Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 32, 'MAT.27.32', 'Along the way they found a man from Cyrene, named Simon, and they forced him to carry the cross of Jesus.'),
('MAT', 27, 33, 'MAT.27.33', 'And when they came to a place called Golgotha, which means The Place of the Skull,'),
('MAT', 27, 34, 'MAT.27.34', 'they offered Him wine to drink, mixed with gall; but after tasting it, He refused to drink it.'),
('MAT', 27, 35, 'MAT.27.35', 'When they had crucified Him, they divided up His garments by casting lots.'),
('MAT', 27, 36, 'MAT.27.36', 'And sitting down, they kept watch over Him there.'),
('MAT', 27, 37, 'MAT.27.37', 'Above His head they posted the written charge against Him: THIS IS JESUS, THE KING OF THE JEWS.'),
('MAT', 27, 38, 'MAT.27.38', 'Two robbers were crucified with Him, one on His right and the other on His left.'),
('MAT', 27, 39, 'MAT.27.39', 'And those who passed by heaped abuse on Him, shaking their heads'),
('MAT', 27, 40, 'MAT.27.40', 'and saying, “You who are going to destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days, save Yourself! If You are the Son of God, come down from the cross!”'),
('MAT', 27, 41, 'MAT.27.41', 'In the same way, the chief priests, scribes, and elders mocked Him, saying,'),
('MAT', 27, 42, 'MAT.27.42', '“He saved others, but He cannot save Himself. He is the King of Israel! Let Him come down now from the cross, and we will believe in Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 43, 'MAT.27.43', 'He trusts in God. Let God deliver Him now if He wants Him. For He said, ‘I am the Son of God.’”'),
('MAT', 27, 44, 'MAT.27.44', 'In the same way, even the robbers who were crucified with Him berated Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 45, 'MAT.27.45', 'From the sixth hour until the ninth hour darkness came over all the land.'),
('MAT', 27, 46, 'MAT.27.46', 'About the ninth hour Jesus cried out in a loud voice, “Eli, Eli, lema sabachthani?” which means, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”'),
('MAT', 27, 47, 'MAT.27.47', 'When some of those standing there heard this, they said, “He is calling Elijah.”'),
('MAT', 27, 48, 'MAT.27.48', 'One of them quickly ran and brought a sponge. He filled it with sour wine, put it on a reed, and held it up for Jesus to drink.'),
('MAT', 27, 49, 'MAT.27.49', 'But the others said, “Leave Him alone. Let us see if Elijah comes to save Him.”'),
('MAT', 27, 50, 'MAT.27.50', 'When Jesus had cried out again in a loud voice, He yielded up His spirit.'),
('MAT', 27, 51, 'MAT.27.51', 'At that moment the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom. The earth quaked, and the rocks were split.'),
('MAT', 27, 52, 'MAT.27.52', 'The tombs broke open, and the bodies of many saints who had fallen asleep were raised.'),
('MAT', 27, 53, 'MAT.27.53', 'After Jesus’ resurrection, when they had come out of the tombs, they entered the holy city and appeared to many people.'),
('MAT', 27, 54, 'MAT.27.54', 'When the centurion and those with him who were guarding Jesus saw the earthquake and all that had happened, they were terrified and said, “Truly this was the Son of God.”'),
('MAT', 27, 55, 'MAT.27.55', 'And many women were there, watching from a distance. They had followed Jesus from Galilee to minister to Him.'),
('MAT', 27, 56, 'MAT.27.56', 'Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and the mother of Zebedee’s sons.'),
('MAT', 27, 57, 'MAT.27.57', 'When it was evening, there came a rich man from Arimathea named Joseph, who himself was a disciple of Jesus.'),
('MAT', 27, 58, 'MAT.27.58', 'He went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus, and Pilate ordered that it be given to him.'),
('MAT', 27, 59, 'MAT.27.59', 'So Joseph took the body, wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,'),
('MAT', 27, 60, 'MAT.27.60', 'and placed it in his own new tomb that he had cut into the rock. Then he rolled a great stone across the entrance to the tomb and went away.'),
('MAT', 27, 61, 'MAT.27.61', 'Mary Magdalene and the other Mary were sitting there opposite the tomb.'),
('MAT', 27, 62, 'MAT.27.62', 'The next day, the one after Preparation Day, the chief priests and Pharisees assembled before Pilate.'),
('MAT', 27, 63, 'MAT.27.63', '“Sir,” they said, “we remember that while He was alive that deceiver said, ‘After three days I will rise again.’'),
('MAT', 27, 64, 'MAT.27.64', 'So give the order that the tomb be secured until the third day. Otherwise, His disciples may come and steal Him away and tell the people He has risen from the dead. And this last deception would be worse than the first.”'),
('MAT', 27, 65, 'MAT.27.65', '“You have a guard,” Pilate said. “Go, make the tomb as secure as you know how.”'),
('MAT', 27, 66, 'MAT.27.66', 'So they went and secured the tomb by sealing the stone and posting the guard.'),
('MAT', 28, 1, 'MAT.28.1', 'After the Sabbath, at dawn on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene and the other Mary went to see the tomb.'),
('MAT', 28, 2, 'MAT.28.2', 'Suddenly there was a great earthquake, for an angel of the Lord descended from heaven, rolled away the stone, and sat on it.'),
('MAT', 28, 3, 'MAT.28.3', 'His appearance was like lightning, and his clothes were white as snow.'),
('MAT', 28, 4, 'MAT.28.4', 'The guards trembled in fear of him and became like dead men.'),
('MAT', 28, 5, 'MAT.28.5', 'But the angel said to the women, “Do not be afraid, for I know that you are looking for Jesus, who was crucified.'),
('MAT', 28, 6, 'MAT.28.6', 'He is not here; He has risen, just as He said! Come, see the place where He lay.'),
('MAT', 28, 7, 'MAT.28.7', 'Then go quickly and tell His disciples, ‘He has risen from the dead and is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him.’ See, I have told you.”'),
('MAT', 28, 8, 'MAT.28.8', 'So they hurried away from the tomb in fear and great joy, and ran to tell His disciples.'),
('MAT', 28, 9, 'MAT.28.9', 'Suddenly Jesus met them and said, “Greetings!” They came to Him, grasped His feet, and worshiped Him.'),
('MAT', 28, 10, 'MAT.28.10', '“Do not be afraid,” said Jesus. “Go and tell My brothers to go to Galilee. There they will see Me.”'),
('MAT', 28, 11, 'MAT.28.11', 'While the women were on their way, some of the guards went into the city and reported to the chief priests all that had happened.'),
('MAT', 28, 12, 'MAT.28.12', 'And after the chief priests had met with the elders and formed a plan, they gave the soldiers a large sum of money'),
('MAT', 28, 13, 'MAT.28.13', 'and instructed them: “You are to say, ‘His disciples came by night and stole Him away while we were asleep.’'),
('MAT', 28, 14, 'MAT.28.14', 'If this report reaches the governor, we will satisfy him and keep you out of trouble.”'),
('MAT', 28, 15, 'MAT.28.15', 'So the guards took the money and did as they were instructed. And this account has been circulated among the Jews to this very day.'),
('MAT', 28, 16, 'MAT.28.16', 'Meanwhile, the eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain Jesus had designated.'),
('MAT', 28, 17, 'MAT.28.17', 'When they saw Him, they worshiped Him, but some doubted.'),
('MAT', 28, 18, 'MAT.28.18', 'Then Jesus came to them and said, “All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to Me.'),
('MAT', 28, 19, 'MAT.28.19', 'Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit,'),
('MAT', 28, 20, 'MAT.28.20', 'and teaching them to obey all that I have commanded you. And surely I am with you always, even to the end of the age.”'),
('MRK', 1, 1, 'MRK.1.1', 'This is the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.'),
('MRK', 1, 2, 'MRK.1.2', 'As it is written in Isaiah the prophet: “Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way.”'),
('MRK', 1, 3, 'MRK.1.3', '“A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.’”'),
('MRK', 1, 4, 'MRK.1.4', 'John the Baptist appeared in the wilderness, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sins.'),
('MRK', 1, 5, 'MRK.1.5', 'People went out to him from all of Jerusalem and the countryside of Judea. Confessing their sins, they were baptized by him in the Jordan River.'),
('MRK', 1, 6, 'MRK.1.6', 'John was clothed in camel’s hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.'),
('MRK', 1, 7, 'MRK.1.7', 'And he proclaimed: “After me will come One more powerful than I, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to stoop down and untie.'),
('MRK', 1, 8, 'MRK.1.8', 'I baptize you with water, but He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.”'),
('MRK', 1, 9, 'MRK.1.9', 'In those days Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee and was baptized by John in the Jordan.'),
('MRK', 1, 10, 'MRK.1.10', 'As soon as Jesus came up out of the water, He saw the heavens breaking open and the Spirit descending on Him like a dove.'),
('MRK', 1, 11, 'MRK.1.11', 'And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”'),
('MRK', 1, 12, 'MRK.1.12', 'At once the Spirit drove Jesus into the wilderness,'),
('MRK', 1, 13, 'MRK.1.13', 'and He was there for forty days, being tempted by Satan. He was with the wild animals, and the angels ministered to Him.'),
('MRK', 1, 14, 'MRK.1.14', 'After the arrest of John, Jesus went into Galilee and proclaimed the gospel of God.'),
('MRK', 1, 15, 'MRK.1.15', '“The time is fulfilled,” He said, “and the kingdom of God is near. Repent and believe in the gospel!”'),
('MRK', 1, 16, 'MRK.1.16', 'As Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen.'),
('MRK', 1, 17, 'MRK.1.17', '“Come, follow Me,” Jesus said, “and I will make you fishers of men.”'),
('MRK', 1, 18, 'MRK.1.18', 'And at once they left their nets and followed Him.'),
('MRK', 1, 19, 'MRK.1.19', 'Going on a little farther, He saw James son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat, mending their nets.'),
('MRK', 1, 20, 'MRK.1.20', 'Immediately Jesus called them, and they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men and followed Him.'),
('MRK', 1, 21, 'MRK.1.21', 'Then Jesus and His companions went to Capernaum, and right away Jesus entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and began to teach.'),
('MRK', 1, 22, 'MRK.1.22', 'The people were astonished at His teaching, because He taught as one who had authority, and not as the scribes.'),
('MRK', 1, 23, 'MRK.1.23', 'Suddenly a man with an unclean spirit cried out in the synagogue:'),
('MRK', 1, 24, 'MRK.1.24', '“What do You want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”'),
('MRK', 1, 25, 'MRK.1.25', 'But Jesus rebuked the spirit. “Be silent!” He said. “Come out of him!”'),
('MRK', 1, 26, 'MRK.1.26', 'At this, the unclean spirit threw the man into convulsions and came out with a loud shriek.'),
('MRK', 1, 27, 'MRK.1.27', 'All the people were amazed and began to ask one another, “What is this? A new teaching with authority! He commands even the unclean spirits, and they obey Him!”'),
('MRK', 1, 28, 'MRK.1.28', 'And the news about Jesus spread quickly through the whole region of Galilee.'),
('MRK', 1, 29, 'MRK.1.29', 'As soon as Jesus and His companions had left the synagogue, they went with James and John to the home of Simon and Andrew.'),
('MRK', 1, 30, 'MRK.1.30', 'Simon’s mother-in-law was sick in bed with a fever, and they promptly told Jesus about her.'),
('MRK', 1, 31, 'MRK.1.31', 'So He went to her, took her by the hand, and helped her up. The fever left her, and she began to serve them.'),
('MRK', 1, 32, 'MRK.1.32', 'That evening, after sunset, people brought to Jesus all the sick and demon-possessed,'),
('MRK', 1, 33, 'MRK.1.33', 'and the whole town gathered at the door.'),
('MRK', 1, 34, 'MRK.1.34', 'And He healed many who were ill with various diseases and drove out many demons. But He would not allow the demons to speak, because they knew who He was.'),
('MRK', 1, 35, 'MRK.1.35', 'Early in the morning, while it was still dark, Jesus got up and went out to a solitary place to pray.'),
('MRK', 1, 36, 'MRK.1.36', 'Simon and his companions went to look for Him,'),
('MRK', 1, 37, 'MRK.1.37', 'and when they found Him, they said, “Everyone is looking for You!”'),
('MRK', 1, 38, 'MRK.1.38', 'But Jesus answered, “Let us go on to the neighboring towns so I can preach there as well, for that is why I have come.”'),
('MRK', 1, 39, 'MRK.1.39', 'So He went throughout Galilee, preaching in their synagogues and driving out demons.'),
('MRK', 1, 40, 'MRK.1.40', 'Then a leper came to Jesus, begging on his knees: “If You are willing, You can make me clean.”'),
('MRK', 1, 41, 'MRK.1.41', 'Moved with compassion, Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!”'),
('MRK', 1, 42, 'MRK.1.42', 'And immediately the leprosy left him, and the man was cleansed.'),
('MRK', 1, 43, 'MRK.1.43', 'Jesus promptly sent him away with a stern warning:'),
('MRK', 1, 44, 'MRK.1.44', '“See that you don’t tell anyone. But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”'),
('MRK', 1, 45, 'MRK.1.45', 'But the man went out and openly began to proclaim and spread the news. Consequently, Jesus could no longer enter a town in plain view, but He stayed out in solitary places. Yet people came to Him from every quarter.'),
('MRK', 2, 1, 'MRK.2.1', 'A few days later Jesus went back to Capernaum. And when the people heard that He was home,'),
('MRK', 2, 2, 'MRK.2.2', 'they gathered in such large numbers that there was no more room, not even outside the door, as Jesus spoke the word to them.'),
('MRK', 2, 3, 'MRK.2.3', 'Then a paralytic was brought to Him, carried by four men.'),
('MRK', 2, 4, 'MRK.2.4', 'Since they were unable to get to Jesus through the crowd, they uncovered the roof above Him, made an opening, and lowered the paralytic on his mat.'),
('MRK', 2, 5, 'MRK.2.5', 'When Jesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins are forgiven.”'),
('MRK', 2, 6, 'MRK.2.6', 'But some of the scribes were sitting there and thinking in their hearts,'),
('MRK', 2, 7, 'MRK.2.7', '“Why does this man speak like this? He is blaspheming! Who can forgive sins but God alone?”'),
('MRK', 2, 8, 'MRK.2.8', 'At once Jesus knew in His spirit that they were thinking this way within themselves. “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?” He asked.'),
('MRK', 2, 9, 'MRK.2.9', '“Which is easier: to say to a paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up, pick up your mat, and walk’?'),
('MRK', 2, 10, 'MRK.2.10', 'But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...” He said to the paralytic,'),
('MRK', 2, 11, 'MRK.2.11', '“I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”'),
('MRK', 2, 12, 'MRK.2.12', 'And immediately the man got up, picked up his mat, and walked out in front of them all. As a result, they were all astounded and glorified God, saying, “We have never seen anything like this!”'),
('MRK', 2, 13, 'MRK.2.13', 'Once again Jesus went out beside the sea. All the people came to Him, and He taught them there.'),
('MRK', 2, 14, 'MRK.2.14', 'As He was walking along, He saw Levi son of Alphaeus sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him, and Levi got up and followed Him.'),
('MRK', 2, 15, 'MRK.2.15', 'While Jesus was dining at Levi’s house, many tax collectors and sinners were eating with Him and His disciples—for there were many who followed Him.'),
('MRK', 2, 16, 'MRK.2.16', 'When the scribes who were Pharisees saw Jesus eating with these people, they asked His disciples, “Why does He eat with tax collectors and sinners?”'),
('MRK', 2, 17, 'MRK.2.17', 'On hearing this, Jesus told them, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick. I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.”'),
('MRK', 2, 18, 'MRK.2.18', 'Now John’s disciples and the Pharisees were often fasting. So people came to Jesus and asked, “Why don’t Your disciples fast like John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees?”'),
('MRK', 2, 19, 'MRK.2.19', 'Jesus replied, “How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them? As long as He is with them, they cannot fast.'),
('MRK', 2, 20, 'MRK.2.20', 'But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.'),
('MRK', 2, 21, 'MRK.2.21', 'No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. If he does, the new piece will pull away from the old, and a worse tear will result.'),
('MRK', 2, 22, 'MRK.2.22', 'And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.”'),
('MRK', 2, 23, 'MRK.2.23', 'One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain as they walked along.'),
('MRK', 2, 24, 'MRK.2.24', 'So the Pharisees said to Him, “Look, why are they doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?”'),
('MRK', 2, 25, 'MRK.2.25', 'Jesus replied, “Have you never read what David did when he and his companions were hungry and in need?'),
('MRK', 2, 26, 'MRK.2.26', 'During the high priesthood of Abiathar, he entered the house of God and ate the consecrated bread, which was lawful only for the priests. And he gave some to his companions as well.”'),
('MRK', 2, 27, 'MRK.2.27', 'Then Jesus declared, “The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath.'),
('MRK', 2, 28, 'MRK.2.28', 'Therefore, the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.”'),
('MRK', 3, 1, 'MRK.3.1', 'Once again Jesus entered the synagogue, and a man with a withered hand was there.'),
('MRK', 3, 2, 'MRK.3.2', 'In order to accuse Jesus, they were watching to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.'),
('MRK', 3, 3, 'MRK.3.3', 'Then Jesus said to the man with the withered hand, “Stand up among us.”'),
('MRK', 3, 4, 'MRK.3.4', 'And He asked them, “Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?” But they were silent.'),
('MRK', 3, 5, 'MRK.3.5', 'Jesus looked around at them with anger and sorrow at their hardness of heart. Then He said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” So he stretched it out, and it was restored.'),
('MRK', 3, 6, 'MRK.3.6', 'At this, the Pharisees went out and began plotting with the Herodians how they might kill Jesus.'),
('MRK', 3, 7, 'MRK.3.7', 'So Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, accompanied by a large crowd from Galilee, Judea,'),
('MRK', 3, 8, 'MRK.3.8', 'Jerusalem, Idumea, the region beyond the Jordan, and the vicinity of Tyre and Sidon. The large crowd came to Him when they heard what great things He was doing.'),
('MRK', 3, 9, 'MRK.3.9', 'Jesus asked His disciples to have a boat ready for Him so that the crowd would not crush Him.'),
('MRK', 3, 10, 'MRK.3.10', 'For He had healed so many that all who had diseases were pressing forward to touch Him.'),
('MRK', 3, 11, 'MRK.3.11', 'And when the unclean spirits saw Him, they fell down before Him and cried out, “You are the Son of God!”'),
('MRK', 3, 12, 'MRK.3.12', 'But He warned them sternly not to make Him known.'),
('MRK', 3, 13, 'MRK.3.13', 'Then Jesus went up on the mountain and called for those He wanted, and they came to Him.'),
('MRK', 3, 14, 'MRK.3.14', 'He appointed twelve of them, whom He designated as apostles, to accompany Him, to be sent out to preach,'),
('MRK', 3, 15, 'MRK.3.15', 'and to have authority to drive out demons.'),
('MRK', 3, 16, 'MRK.3.16', 'These are the twelve He appointed: Simon (whom He named Peter),'),
('MRK', 3, 17, 'MRK.3.17', 'James son of Zebedee and his brother John (whom He named Boanerges, meaning “Sons of Thunder”),'),
('MRK', 3, 18, 'MRK.3.18', 'Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,'),
('MRK', 3, 19, 'MRK.3.19', 'and Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.'),
('MRK', 3, 20, 'MRK.3.20', 'Then Jesus went home, and once again a crowd gathered, so that He and His disciples could not even eat.'),
('MRK', 3, 21, 'MRK.3.21', 'When His family heard about this, they went out to take custody of Him, saying, “He is out of His mind.”'),
('MRK', 3, 22, 'MRK.3.22', 'And the scribes who had come down from Jerusalem were saying, “He is possessed by Beelzebul,” and, “By the prince of the demons He drives out demons.”'),
('MRK', 3, 23, 'MRK.3.23', 'So Jesus called them together and began to speak to them in parables: “How can Satan drive out Satan?'),
('MRK', 3, 24, 'MRK.3.24', 'If a kingdom is divided against itself, it cannot stand.'),
('MRK', 3, 25, 'MRK.3.25', 'If a house is divided against itself, it cannot stand.'),
('MRK', 3, 26, 'MRK.3.26', 'And if Satan is divided and rises against himself, he cannot stand; his end has come.'),
('MRK', 3, 27, 'MRK.3.27', 'Indeed, no one can enter a strong man’s house to steal his possessions unless he first ties up the strong man. Then he can plunder his house.'),
('MRK', 3, 28, 'MRK.3.28', 'Truly I tell you, the sons of men will be forgiven all sins and blasphemies, as many as they utter.'),
('MRK', 3, 29, 'MRK.3.29', 'But whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will never be forgiven; he is guilty of eternal sin.”'),
('MRK', 3, 30, 'MRK.3.30', 'Jesus made this statement because they were saying, “He has an unclean spirit.”'),
('MRK', 3, 31, 'MRK.3.31', 'Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came and stood outside. They sent someone in to summon Him,'),
('MRK', 3, 32, 'MRK.3.32', 'and a crowd was sitting around Him. “Look,” He was told, “Your mother and brothers are outside, asking for You.”'),
('MRK', 3, 33, 'MRK.3.33', 'But Jesus replied, “Who are My mother and My brothers?”'),
('MRK', 3, 34, 'MRK.3.34', 'Looking at those seated in a circle around Him, He said, “Here are My mother and My brothers!'),
('MRK', 3, 35, 'MRK.3.35', 'For whoever does the will of God is My brother and sister and mother.”'),
('MRK', 4, 1, 'MRK.4.1', 'Once again Jesus began to teach beside the sea, and such a large crowd gathered around Him that He got into a boat and sat in it, while all the people crowded along the shore.'),
('MRK', 4, 2, 'MRK.4.2', 'And He taught them many things in parables, and in His teaching He said,'),
('MRK', 4, 3, 'MRK.4.3', '“Listen! A farmer went out to sow his seed.'),
('MRK', 4, 4, 'MRK.4.4', 'And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, and the birds came and devoured it.'),
('MRK', 4, 5, 'MRK.4.5', 'Some fell on rocky ground, where it did not have much soil. It sprang up quickly because the soil was shallow.'),
('MRK', 4, 6, 'MRK.4.6', 'But when the sun rose, the seedlings were scorched, and they withered because they had no root.'),
('MRK', 4, 7, 'MRK.4.7', 'Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up and choked the seedlings, and they yielded no crop.'),
('MRK', 4, 8, 'MRK.4.8', 'Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprouted, grew up, and produced a crop—one bearing thirtyfold, another sixtyfold, and another a hundredfold.”'),
('MRK', 4, 9, 'MRK.4.9', 'Then Jesus said, “He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”'),
('MRK', 4, 10, 'MRK.4.10', 'As soon as Jesus was alone with the Twelve and those around Him, they asked Him about the parable.'),
('MRK', 4, 11, 'MRK.4.11', 'He replied, “The mystery of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to those on the outside everything is expressed in parables,'),
('MRK', 4, 12, 'MRK.4.12', 'so that, ‘they may be ever seeing but never perceiving, and ever hearing but never understanding; otherwise they might turn and be forgiven.’”'),
('MRK', 4, 13, 'MRK.4.13', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Do you not understand this parable? Then how will you understand any of the parables?'),
('MRK', 4, 14, 'MRK.4.14', 'The farmer sows the word.'),
('MRK', 4, 15, 'MRK.4.15', 'Some are like the seeds along the path, where the word is sown. As soon as they hear it, Satan comes and takes away the word that was sown in them.'),
('MRK', 4, 16, 'MRK.4.16', 'Some are like the seeds sown on rocky ground. They hear the word and at once receive it with joy.'),
('MRK', 4, 17, 'MRK.4.17', 'But they themselves have no root, and they remain for only a season. When trouble or persecution comes because of the word, they quickly fall away.'),
('MRK', 4, 18, 'MRK.4.18', 'Others are like the seeds sown among the thorns. They hear the word,'),
('MRK', 4, 19, 'MRK.4.19', 'but the worries of this life, the deceitfulness of wealth, and the desire for other things come in and choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful.'),
('MRK', 4, 20, 'MRK.4.20', 'Still others are like the seeds sown on good soil. They hear the word, receive it, and produce a crop—thirtyfold, sixtyfold, or a hundredfold.”'),
('MRK', 4, 21, 'MRK.4.21', 'Jesus also said to them, “Does anyone bring in a lamp to put it under a basket or under a bed? Doesn’t he set it on a stand?'),
('MRK', 4, 22, 'MRK.4.22', 'For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, and nothing concealed that will not be brought to light.'),
('MRK', 4, 23, 'MRK.4.23', 'If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.”'),
('MRK', 4, 24, 'MRK.4.24', 'He went on to say, “Pay attention to what you hear. With the measure you use, it will be measured to you, and even more will be added to you.'),
('MRK', 4, 25, 'MRK.4.25', 'For whoever has will be given more. But whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.”'),
('MRK', 4, 26, 'MRK.4.26', 'Jesus also said, “The kingdom of God is like a man who scatters seed on the ground.'),
('MRK', 4, 27, 'MRK.4.27', 'Night and day he sleeps and wakes, and the seed sprouts and grows, though he knows not how.'),
('MRK', 4, 28, 'MRK.4.28', 'All by itself the earth produces a crop—first the stalk, then the head, then grain that ripens within.'),
('MRK', 4, 29, 'MRK.4.29', 'And as soon as the grain is ripe, he swings the sickle, because the harvest has come.”'),
('MRK', 4, 30, 'MRK.4.30', 'Then He asked, “To what can we compare the kingdom of God? With what parable shall we present it?'),
('MRK', 4, 31, 'MRK.4.31', 'It is like a mustard seed, which is the smallest of all seeds sown upon the earth.'),
('MRK', 4, 32, 'MRK.4.32', 'But after it is planted, it grows to be the largest of all garden plants and puts forth great branches, so that the birds of the air nest in its shade.”'),
('MRK', 4, 33, 'MRK.4.33', 'With many such parables Jesus spoke the word to them, to the extent that they could understand.'),
('MRK', 4, 34, 'MRK.4.34', 'He did not tell them anything without using a parable. But privately He explained everything to His own disciples.'),
('MRK', 4, 35, 'MRK.4.35', 'When that evening came, He said to His disciples, “Let us cross to the other side.”'),
('MRK', 4, 36, 'MRK.4.36', 'After they had dismissed the crowd, they took Jesus with them, since He was already in the boat. And there were other boats with Him.'),
('MRK', 4, 37, 'MRK.4.37', 'Soon a violent windstorm came up, and the waves were breaking over the boat, so that it was being swamped.'),
('MRK', 4, 38, 'MRK.4.38', 'But Jesus was in the stern, sleeping on the cushion. So they woke Him and said, “Teacher, don’t You care that we are perishing?”'),
('MRK', 4, 39, 'MRK.4.39', 'Then Jesus got up and rebuked the wind and the sea. “Silence!” He commanded. “Be still!” And the wind died down, and it was perfectly calm.'),
('MRK', 4, 40, 'MRK.4.40', '“Why are you so afraid?” He asked. “Do you still have no faith?”'),
('MRK', 4, 41, 'MRK.4.41', 'Overwhelmed with fear, they asked one another, “Who is this, that even the wind and the sea obey Him?”'),
('MRK', 5, 1, 'MRK.5.1', 'On the other side of the sea, they arrived in the region of the Gerasenes.'),
('MRK', 5, 2, 'MRK.5.2', 'As soon as Jesus got out of the boat, He was met by a man with an unclean spirit, who was coming from the tombs.'),
('MRK', 5, 3, 'MRK.5.3', 'This man had been living in the tombs and could no longer be restrained, even with chains.'),
('MRK', 5, 4, 'MRK.5.4', 'Though he was often bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains and shattered the shackles. Now there was no one with the strength to subdue him.'),
('MRK', 5, 5, 'MRK.5.5', 'Night and day in the tombs and in the mountains he kept crying out and cutting himself with stones.'),
('MRK', 5, 6, 'MRK.5.6', 'When the man saw Jesus from a distance, he ran and fell on his knees before Him.'),
('MRK', 5, 7, 'MRK.5.7', 'And he shouted in a loud voice, “What do You want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You before God not to torture me!”'),
('MRK', 5, 8, 'MRK.5.8', 'For Jesus had already declared, “Come out of this man, you unclean spirit!”'),
('MRK', 5, 9, 'MRK.5.9', '“What is your name?” Jesus asked. “My name is Legion,” he replied, “for we are many.”'),
('MRK', 5, 10, 'MRK.5.10', 'And he begged Jesus repeatedly not to send them out of that region.'),
('MRK', 5, 11, 'MRK.5.11', 'There on the nearby hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding.'),
('MRK', 5, 12, 'MRK.5.12', 'So the demons begged Jesus, “Send us to the pigs, so that we may enter them.”'),
('MRK', 5, 13, 'MRK.5.13', 'He gave them permission, and the unclean spirits came out and went into the pigs, and the herd of about two thousand rushed down the steep bank into the sea and drowned in the water.'),
('MRK', 5, 14, 'MRK.5.14', 'Those tending the pigs ran off and reported this in the town and countryside, and the people went out to see what had happened.'),
('MRK', 5, 15, 'MRK.5.15', 'When they came to Jesus, they saw the man who had been possessed by the legion of demons sitting there, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid.'),
('MRK', 5, 16, 'MRK.5.16', 'Those who had seen it described what had happened to the demon-possessed man and also to the pigs.'),
('MRK', 5, 17, 'MRK.5.17', 'And the people began to beg Jesus to leave their region.'),
('MRK', 5, 18, 'MRK.5.18', 'As He was getting into the boat, the man who had been possessed by the demons begged to go with Him.'),
('MRK', 5, 19, 'MRK.5.19', 'But Jesus would not allow him. “Go home to your own people,” He said, “and tell them how much the Lord has done for you, and what mercy He has shown you.”'),
('MRK', 5, 20, 'MRK.5.20', 'So the man went away and began to proclaim throughout the Decapolis how much Jesus had done for him. And everyone was amazed.'),
('MRK', 5, 21, 'MRK.5.21', 'When Jesus had again crossed by boat to the other side, a large crowd gathered around Him beside the sea.'),
('MRK', 5, 22, 'MRK.5.22', 'A synagogue leader named Jairus arrived, and seeing Jesus, he fell at His feet'),
('MRK', 5, 23, 'MRK.5.23', 'and pleaded with Him urgently, “My little daughter is near death. Please come and place Your hands on her, so that she will be healed and live.”'),
('MRK', 5, 24, 'MRK.5.24', 'So Jesus went with him, and a large crowd followed and pressed around Him.'),
('MRK', 5, 25, 'MRK.5.25', 'And a woman was there who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years.'),
('MRK', 5, 26, 'MRK.5.26', 'She had borne much agony under the care of many physicians and had spent all she had, but to no avail. Instead, her condition had only grown worse.'),
('MRK', 5, 27, 'MRK.5.27', 'When the woman heard about Jesus, she came up through the crowd behind Him and touched His cloak.'),
('MRK', 5, 28, 'MRK.5.28', 'For she kept saying, “If only I touch His garments, I will be healed.”'),
('MRK', 5, 29, 'MRK.5.29', 'Immediately her bleeding stopped, and she sensed in her body that she was healed of her affliction.'),
('MRK', 5, 30, 'MRK.5.30', 'At once Jesus was aware that power had gone out from Him. Turning to the crowd, He asked, “Who touched My garments?”'),
('MRK', 5, 31, 'MRK.5.31', 'His disciples answered, “You can see the crowd pressing in on You, and yet You ask, ‘Who touched Me?’”'),
('MRK', 5, 32, 'MRK.5.32', 'But He kept looking around to see who had done this.'),
('MRK', 5, 33, 'MRK.5.33', 'Then the woman, knowing what had happened to her, came and fell down before Him trembling in fear, and she told Him the whole truth.'),
('MRK', 5, 34, 'MRK.5.34', '“Daughter,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you. Go in peace and be free of your affliction.”'),
('MRK', 5, 35, 'MRK.5.35', 'While He was still speaking, messengers from the house of Jairus arrived and said, “Your daughter is dead; why bother the Teacher anymore?”'),
('MRK', 5, 36, 'MRK.5.36', 'But Jesus overheard their conversation and said to Jairus, “Do not be afraid; just believe.”'),
('MRK', 5, 37, 'MRK.5.37', 'And He did not allow anyone to accompany Him except Peter, James, and John the brother of James.'),
('MRK', 5, 38, 'MRK.5.38', 'When they arrived at the house of the synagogue leader, Jesus saw the commotion and the people weeping and wailing loudly.'),
('MRK', 5, 39, 'MRK.5.39', 'He went inside and asked, “Why all this commotion and weeping? The child is not dead, but asleep.”'),
('MRK', 5, 40, 'MRK.5.40', 'And they laughed at Him. After He had put them all outside, He took the child’s father and mother and His own companions, and went in to see the child.'),
('MRK', 5, 41, 'MRK.5.41', 'Taking her by the hand, Jesus said, “Talitha koum!” which means, “Little girl, I say to you, get up!”'),
('MRK', 5, 42, 'MRK.5.42', 'Immediately the girl got up and began to walk around (she was twelve years old). And at once they were utterly astounded.'),
('MRK', 5, 43, 'MRK.5.43', 'Then Jesus gave strict orders that no one should know about this, and He told them to give her something to eat.'),
('MRK', 6, 1, 'MRK.6.1', 'Jesus went on from there and came to His hometown, accompanied by His disciples.'),
('MRK', 6, 2, 'MRK.6.2', 'When the Sabbath came, He began to teach in the synagogue, and many who heard Him were astonished. “Where did this man get these ideas?” they asked. “What is this wisdom He has been given? And how can He perform such miracles?'),
('MRK', 6, 3, 'MRK.6.3', 'Isn’t this the carpenter, the son of Mary and the brother of James, Joses, Judas, and Simon? Aren’t His sisters here with us as well?” And they took offense at Him.'),
('MRK', 6, 4, 'MRK.6.4', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Only in his hometown, among his relatives, and in his own household is a prophet without honor.”'),
('MRK', 6, 5, 'MRK.6.5', 'So He could not perform any miracles there, except to lay His hands on a few of the sick and heal them.'),
('MRK', 6, 6, 'MRK.6.6', 'And He was amazed at their unbelief. And He went around from village to village, teaching the people.'),
('MRK', 6, 7, 'MRK.6.7', 'Then Jesus called the Twelve to Him and began to send them out two by two, giving them authority over unclean spirits.'),
('MRK', 6, 8, 'MRK.6.8', 'He instructed them to take nothing but a staff for the journey—no bread, no bag, no money in their belts—'),
('MRK', 6, 9, 'MRK.6.9', 'and to wear sandals, but not a second tunic.'),
('MRK', 6, 10, 'MRK.6.10', 'And He told them, “When you enter a house, stay there until you leave that area.'),
('MRK', 6, 11, 'MRK.6.11', 'If anyone will not welcome you or listen to you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that place, as a testimony against them.”'),
('MRK', 6, 12, 'MRK.6.12', 'So they set out and preached that the people should repent.'),
('MRK', 6, 13, 'MRK.6.13', 'They also drove out many demons and healed many of the sick, anointing them with oil.'),
('MRK', 6, 14, 'MRK.6.14', 'Now King Herod heard about this, for Jesus’ name had become well known, and people were saying, “John the Baptist has risen from the dead! That is why miraculous powers are at work in him.”'),
('MRK', 6, 15, 'MRK.6.15', 'Others were saying, “He is Elijah,” and still others, “He is a prophet, like one of the prophets of old.”'),
('MRK', 6, 16, 'MRK.6.16', 'But when Herod heard this, he said, “John, whom I beheaded, has risen from the dead!”'),
('MRK', 6, 17, 'MRK.6.17', 'For Herod himself had ordered that John be arrested and bound and imprisoned, on account of his brother Philip’s wife Herodias, whom Herod had married.'),
('MRK', 6, 18, 'MRK.6.18', 'For John had been telling Herod, “It is not lawful for you to have your brother’s wife!”'),
('MRK', 6, 19, 'MRK.6.19', 'So Herodias held a grudge against John and wanted to kill him. But she had been unable,'),
('MRK', 6, 20, 'MRK.6.20', 'because Herod feared John and protected him, knowing that he was a righteous and holy man. When he heard John’s words, he was greatly perplexed; yet he listened to him gladly.'),
('MRK', 6, 21, 'MRK.6.21', 'On Herod’s birthday, her opportunity arose. Herod held a banquet for his nobles and military commanders and the leading men of Galilee.'),
('MRK', 6, 22, 'MRK.6.22', 'When the daughter of Herodias came and danced, she pleased Herod and his guests, and the king said to the girl, “Ask me for whatever you wish, and I will give it to you.”'),
('MRK', 6, 23, 'MRK.6.23', 'And he swore to her, “Whatever you ask of me, I will give you, up to half my kingdom!”'),
('MRK', 6, 24, 'MRK.6.24', 'Then she went out and asked her mother, “What should I request?” And her mother answered, “The head of John the Baptist.”'),
('MRK', 6, 25, 'MRK.6.25', 'At once the girl hurried back to the king with her request: “I want you to give me the head of John the Baptist on a platter immediately.”'),
('MRK', 6, 26, 'MRK.6.26', 'The king was consumed with sorrow, but because of his oaths and his guests, he did not want to refuse her.'),
('MRK', 6, 27, 'MRK.6.27', 'So without delay, the king commanded that John’s head be brought in. He sent an executioner, who went and beheaded him in the prison.'),
('MRK', 6, 28, 'MRK.6.28', 'The man brought John’s head on a platter and presented it to the girl, who gave it to her mother.'),
('MRK', 6, 29, 'MRK.6.29', 'When John’s disciples heard about this, they came and took his body and placed it in a tomb.'),
('MRK', 6, 30, 'MRK.6.30', 'Meanwhile, the apostles gathered around Jesus and brought Him news of all they had done and taught.'),
('MRK', 6, 31, 'MRK.6.31', 'And He said to them, “Come with Me privately to a solitary place, and let us rest for a while.” For many people were coming and going, and they did not even have time to eat.'),
('MRK', 6, 32, 'MRK.6.32', 'So they went away in a boat by themselves to a solitary place.'),
('MRK', 6, 33, 'MRK.6.33', 'But many people saw them leaving and recognized them. They ran together on foot from all the towns and arrived before them.'),
('MRK', 6, 34, 'MRK.6.34', 'When Jesus stepped ashore and saw a large crowd, He had compassion on them, because they were like sheep without a shepherd. And He began to teach them many things.'),
('MRK', 6, 35, 'MRK.6.35', 'By now the hour was already late. So the disciples came to Jesus and said, “This is a desolate place, and the hour is already late.'),
('MRK', 6, 36, 'MRK.6.36', 'Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding countryside and villages and buy themselves something to eat.”'),
('MRK', 6, 37, 'MRK.6.37', 'But Jesus told them, “You give them something to eat.” They asked Him, “Should we go out and spend two hundred denarii to give all of them bread to eat?”'),
('MRK', 6, 38, 'MRK.6.38', '“Go and see how many loaves you have,” He told them. And after checking, they said, “Five—and two fish.”'),
('MRK', 6, 39, 'MRK.6.39', 'Then Jesus directed them to have the people sit in groups on the green grass.'),
('MRK', 6, 40, 'MRK.6.40', 'So they sat down in groups of hundreds and fifties.'),
('MRK', 6, 41, 'MRK.6.41', 'Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing and broke the loaves. Then He gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And He divided the two fish among them all.'),
('MRK', 6, 42, 'MRK.6.42', 'They all ate and were satisfied,'),
('MRK', 6, 43, 'MRK.6.43', 'and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces of bread and fish.'),
('MRK', 6, 44, 'MRK.6.44', 'And there were five thousand men who had eaten the loaves.'),
('MRK', 6, 45, 'MRK.6.45', 'Immediately Jesus made His disciples get into the boat and go on ahead of Him to Bethsaida, while He dismissed the crowd.'),
('MRK', 6, 46, 'MRK.6.46', 'After bidding them farewell, He went up on the mountain to pray.'),
('MRK', 6, 47, 'MRK.6.47', 'When evening came, the boat was in the middle of the sea, and Jesus was alone on land.'),
('MRK', 6, 48, 'MRK.6.48', 'He could see that the disciples were straining to row, because the wind was against them. About the fourth watch of the night, Jesus went out to them, walking on the sea. He intended to pass by them,'),
('MRK', 6, 49, 'MRK.6.49', 'but when they saw Him walking on the sea, they cried out, thinking He was a ghost—'),
('MRK', 6, 50, 'MRK.6.50', 'for they all saw Him and were terrified. But Jesus spoke up at once: “Take courage! It is I. Do not be afraid.”'),
('MRK', 6, 51, 'MRK.6.51', 'Then He climbed into the boat with them, and the wind died down. And the disciples were utterly astounded,'),
('MRK', 6, 52, 'MRK.6.52', 'for they had not understood about the loaves, but their hearts had been hardened.'),
('MRK', 6, 53, 'MRK.6.53', 'When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret and moored the boat.'),
('MRK', 6, 54, 'MRK.6.54', 'As soon as they got out of the boat, the people recognized Jesus'),
('MRK', 6, 55, 'MRK.6.55', 'and ran through that whole region, carrying the sick on mats to wherever they heard He was.'),
('MRK', 6, 56, 'MRK.6.56', 'And wherever He went—villages and towns and countrysides—they laid the sick in the marketplaces and begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak. And all who touched Him were healed.'),
('MRK', 7, 1, 'MRK.7.1', 'Then the Pharisees and some of the scribes who had come from Jerusalem gathered around Jesus,'),
('MRK', 7, 2, 'MRK.7.2', 'and they saw some of His disciples eating with hands that were defiled—that is, unwashed.'),
('MRK', 7, 3, 'MRK.7.3', 'Now in holding to the tradition of the elders, the Pharisees and all the Jews do not eat until they wash their hands ceremonially.'),
('MRK', 7, 4, 'MRK.7.4', 'And on returning from the market, they do not eat unless they wash. And there are many other traditions for them to observe, including the washing of cups, pitchers, kettles, and couches for dining.'),
('MRK', 7, 5, 'MRK.7.5', 'So the Pharisees and scribes questioned Jesus: “Why do Your disciples not walk according to the tradition of the elders? Instead, they eat with defiled hands.”'),
('MRK', 7, 6, 'MRK.7.6', 'Jesus answered them, “Isaiah prophesied correctly about you hypocrites, as it is written: ‘These people honor Me with their lips, but their hearts are far from Me.'),
('MRK', 7, 7, 'MRK.7.7', 'They worship Me in vain; they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’'),
('MRK', 7, 8, 'MRK.7.8', 'You have disregarded the commandment of God to keep the tradition of men.”'),
('MRK', 7, 9, 'MRK.7.9', 'He went on to say, “You neatly set aside the command of God to maintain your own tradition.'),
('MRK', 7, 10, 'MRK.7.10', 'For Moses said, ‘Honor your father and your mother’ and ‘Anyone who curses his father or mother must be put to death.’'),
('MRK', 7, 11, 'MRK.7.11', 'But you say that if a man says to his father or mother, ‘Whatever you would have received from me is Corban’ (that is, a gift devoted to God),'),
('MRK', 7, 12, 'MRK.7.12', 'he is no longer permitted to do anything for his father or mother.'),
('MRK', 7, 13, 'MRK.7.13', 'Thus you nullify the word of God by the tradition you have handed down. And you do so in many such matters.”'),
('MRK', 7, 14, 'MRK.7.14', 'Once again Jesus called the crowd to Him and said, “All of you, listen to Me and understand:'),
('MRK', 7, 15, 'MRK.7.15', 'Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him; but the things that come out of a man, these are what defile him.”'),
('MRK', 7, 17, 'MRK.7.17', 'After Jesus had left the crowd and gone into the house, His disciples inquired about the parable.'),
('MRK', 7, 18, 'MRK.7.18', '“Are you still so dull?” He asked. “Do you not understand? Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him,'),
('MRK', 7, 19, 'MRK.7.19', 'because it does not enter his heart, but it goes into the stomach and then is eliminated.” (Thus all foods are clean.)'),
('MRK', 7, 20, 'MRK.7.20', 'He continued: “What comes out of a man, that is what defiles him.'),
('MRK', 7, 21, 'MRK.7.21', 'For from within the hearts of men come evil thoughts, sexual immorality, theft, murder, adultery,'),
('MRK', 7, 22, 'MRK.7.22', 'greed, wickedness, deceit, debauchery, envy, slander, arrogance, and foolishness.'),
('MRK', 7, 23, 'MRK.7.23', 'All these evils come from within, and these are what defile a man.”'),
('MRK', 7, 24, 'MRK.7.24', 'Jesus left that place and went to the region of Tyre. Not wanting anyone to know He was there, He entered a house, but was unable to escape their notice.'),
('MRK', 7, 25, 'MRK.7.25', 'Instead, a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit soon heard about Jesus, and she came and fell at His feet.'),
('MRK', 7, 26, 'MRK.7.26', 'Now she was a Greek woman of Syrophoenician origin, and she kept asking Jesus to drive the demon out of her daughter.'),
('MRK', 7, 27, 'MRK.7.27', '“First let the children have their fill,” He said. “For it is not right to take the children’s bread and toss it to the dogs.”'),
('MRK', 7, 28, 'MRK.7.28', '“Yes, Lord,” she replied, “even the dogs under the table eat the children’s crumbs.”'),
('MRK', 7, 29, 'MRK.7.29', 'Then Jesus told her, “Because of this answer, you may go. The demon has left your daughter.”'),
('MRK', 7, 30, 'MRK.7.30', 'And she went home and found her child lying on the bed, and the demon was gone.'),
('MRK', 7, 31, 'MRK.7.31', 'Then Jesus left the region of Tyre and went through Sidon to the Sea of Galilee and into the region of the Decapolis.'),
('MRK', 7, 32, 'MRK.7.32', 'Some people brought to Him a man who was deaf and hardly able to speak, and they begged Jesus to place His hand on him.'),
('MRK', 7, 33, 'MRK.7.33', 'So Jesus took him aside privately, away from the crowd, and put His fingers into the man’s ears. Then He spit and touched the man’s tongue.'),
('MRK', 7, 34, 'MRK.7.34', 'And looking up to heaven, He sighed deeply and said to him, “Ephphatha!” (which means, “Be opened!”).'),
('MRK', 7, 35, 'MRK.7.35', 'Immediately the man’s ears were opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak plainly.'),
('MRK', 7, 36, 'MRK.7.36', 'Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone. But the more He ordered them, the more widely they proclaimed it.'),
('MRK', 7, 37, 'MRK.7.37', 'The people were utterly astonished and said, “He has done all things well! He makes even the deaf hear and the mute speak!”'),
('MRK', 8, 1, 'MRK.8.1', 'In those days the crowd once again became very large, and they had nothing to eat. Jesus called the disciples to Him and said,'),
('MRK', 8, 2, 'MRK.8.2', '“I have compassion for this crowd, because they have already been with Me three days and have nothing to eat.'),
('MRK', 8, 3, 'MRK.8.3', 'If I send them home hungry, they will faint along the way. For some of them have come a great distance.”'),
('MRK', 8, 4, 'MRK.8.4', 'His disciples replied, “Where in this desolate place could anyone find enough bread to feed all these people?”'),
('MRK', 8, 5, 'MRK.8.5', '“How many loaves do you have?” Jesus asked. “Seven,” they replied.'),
('MRK', 8, 6, 'MRK.8.6', 'And He instructed the crowd to sit down on the ground. Then He took the seven loaves, gave thanks and broke them, and gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And they distributed them to the crowd.'),
('MRK', 8, 7, 'MRK.8.7', 'They also had a few small fish, and Jesus blessed them and ordered that these be set before them as well.'),
('MRK', 8, 8, 'MRK.8.8', 'The people ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up seven basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.'),
('MRK', 8, 9, 'MRK.8.9', 'And about four thousand men were present. And when Jesus had dismissed the crowd,'),
('MRK', 8, 10, 'MRK.8.10', 'He immediately got into the boat with His disciples and went to the district of Dalmanutha.'),
('MRK', 8, 11, 'MRK.8.11', 'Then the Pharisees came and began to argue with Jesus, testing Him by demanding from Him a sign from heaven.'),
('MRK', 8, 12, 'MRK.8.12', 'Jesus sighed deeply in His spirit and said, “Why does this generation demand a sign? Truly I tell you, no sign will be given to this generation.”'),
('MRK', 8, 13, 'MRK.8.13', 'And He left them, got back into the boat, and crossed to the other side.'),
('MRK', 8, 14, 'MRK.8.14', 'Now the disciples had forgotten to take bread, except for one loaf they had with them in the boat.'),
('MRK', 8, 15, 'MRK.8.15', '“Watch out!” He cautioned them. “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of Herod.”'),
('MRK', 8, 16, 'MRK.8.16', 'So they began to discuss with one another the fact that they had no bread.'),
('MRK', 8, 17, 'MRK.8.17', 'Aware of their conversation, Jesus asked them, “Why are you debating about having no bread? Do you still not see or understand? Do you have such hard hearts?'),
('MRK', 8, 18, 'MRK.8.18', '‘Having eyes, do you not see? And having ears, do you not hear?’ And do you not remember?'),
('MRK', 8, 19, 'MRK.8.19', 'When I broke the five loaves for the five thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Twelve,” they answered.'),
('MRK', 8, 20, 'MRK.8.20', '“And when I broke the seven loaves for the four thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Seven,” they said.'),
('MRK', 8, 21, 'MRK.8.21', 'Then He asked them, “Do you still not understand?”'),
('MRK', 8, 22, 'MRK.8.22', 'When they arrived at Bethsaida, some people brought a blind man and begged Jesus to touch him.'),
('MRK', 8, 23, 'MRK.8.23', 'So He took the blind man by the hand and led him out of the village. Then He spit on the man’s eyes and placed His hands on him. “Can you see anything?” He asked.'),
('MRK', 8, 24, 'MRK.8.24', 'The man looked up and said, “I can see the people, but they look like trees walking around.”'),
('MRK', 8, 25, 'MRK.8.25', 'Once again Jesus placed His hands on the man’s eyes, and when he opened them his sight was restored, and he could see everything clearly.'),
('MRK', 8, 26, 'MRK.8.26', 'Jesus sent him home and said, “Do not go back into the village.”'),
('MRK', 8, 27, 'MRK.8.27', 'Then Jesus and His disciples went on to the villages around Caesarea Philippi. On the way, He questioned His disciples: “Who do people say I am?”'),
('MRK', 8, 28, 'MRK.8.28', 'They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, one of the prophets.”'),
('MRK', 8, 29, 'MRK.8.29', '“But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?” Peter answered, “You are the Christ.”'),
('MRK', 8, 30, 'MRK.8.30', 'And Jesus warned them not to tell anyone about Him.'),
('MRK', 8, 31, 'MRK.8.31', 'Then He began to teach them that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and that He must be killed and after three days rise again.'),
('MRK', 8, 32, 'MRK.8.32', 'He spoke this message quite frankly, and Peter took Him aside and began to rebuke Him.'),
('MRK', 8, 33, 'MRK.8.33', 'But Jesus, turning and looking at His disciples, rebuked Peter and said, “Get behind Me, Satan! For you do not have in mind the things of God, but the things of men.”'),
('MRK', 8, 34, 'MRK.8.34', 'Then Jesus called the crowd to Him along with His disciples, and He told them, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross and follow Me.'),
('MRK', 8, 35, 'MRK.8.35', 'For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake and for the gospel will save it.'),
('MRK', 8, 36, 'MRK.8.36', 'What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet forfeit his soul?'),
('MRK', 8, 37, 'MRK.8.37', 'Or what can a man give in exchange for his soul?'),
('MRK', 8, 38, 'MRK.8.38', 'If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words in this adulterous and sinful generation, the Son of Man will also be ashamed of him when He comes in His Father’s glory with the holy angels.”'),
('MRK', 9, 1, 'MRK.9.1', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Truly I tell you, there are some standing here who will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God arrive with power.”'),
('MRK', 9, 2, 'MRK.9.2', 'After six days Jesus took with Him Peter, James, and John, and led them up a high mountain by themselves. There He was transfigured before them.'),
('MRK', 9, 3, 'MRK.9.3', 'His clothes became radiantly white, brighter than any launderer on earth could bleach them.'),
('MRK', 9, 4, 'MRK.9.4', 'And Elijah and Moses appeared before them, talking with Jesus.'),
('MRK', 9, 5, 'MRK.9.5', 'Peter said to Jesus, “Rabbi, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters—one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.”'),
('MRK', 9, 6, 'MRK.9.6', 'For they were all so terrified that Peter did not know what else to say.'),
('MRK', 9, 7, 'MRK.9.7', 'Then a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and a voice came from the cloud: “This is My beloved Son. Listen to Him!”'),
('MRK', 9, 8, 'MRK.9.8', 'Suddenly, when they looked around, they saw no one with them except Jesus.'),
('MRK', 9, 9, 'MRK.9.9', 'As they were coming down the mountain, Jesus admonished them not to tell anyone what they had seen until the Son of Man had risen from the dead.'),
('MRK', 9, 10, 'MRK.9.10', 'So they kept this matter to themselves, discussing what it meant to rise from the dead.'),
('MRK', 9, 11, 'MRK.9.11', 'And they asked Jesus, “Why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?”'),
('MRK', 9, 12, 'MRK.9.12', 'He replied, “Elijah does indeed come first, and he restores all things. Why then is it written that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected?'),
('MRK', 9, 13, 'MRK.9.13', 'But I tell you that Elijah has indeed come, and they have done to him whatever they wished, just as it is written about him.”'),
('MRK', 9, 14, 'MRK.9.14', 'When they returned to the other disciples, they saw a large crowd around them, and scribes arguing with them.'),
('MRK', 9, 15, 'MRK.9.15', 'As soon as all the people saw Jesus, they were filled with awe and ran to greet Him.'),
('MRK', 9, 16, 'MRK.9.16', '“What are you disputing with them?” He asked.'),
('MRK', 9, 17, 'MRK.9.17', 'Someone in the crowd replied, “Teacher, I brought You my son, who has a spirit that makes him mute.'),
('MRK', 9, 18, 'MRK.9.18', 'Whenever it seizes him, it throws him to the ground. He foams at the mouth, gnashes his teeth, and becomes rigid. I asked Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”'),
('MRK', 9, 19, 'MRK.9.19', '“O unbelieving generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you? How long must I put up with you? Bring the boy to Me.”'),
('MRK', 9, 20, 'MRK.9.20', 'So they brought him, and seeing Jesus, the spirit immediately threw the boy into a convulsion. He fell to the ground and rolled around, foaming at the mouth.'),
('MRK', 9, 21, 'MRK.9.21', 'Jesus asked the boy’s father, “How long has this been with him?” “From childhood,” he said.'),
('MRK', 9, 22, 'MRK.9.22', '“It often throws him into the fire or into the water, trying to kill him. But if You can do anything, have compassion on us and help us.”'),
('MRK', 9, 23, 'MRK.9.23', '“If You can?” echoed Jesus. “All things are possible to him who believes!”'),
('MRK', 9, 24, 'MRK.9.24', 'Immediately the boy’s father cried out, “I do believe; help my unbelief!”'),
('MRK', 9, 25, 'MRK.9.25', 'When Jesus saw that a crowd had come running, He rebuked the unclean spirit. “You deaf and mute spirit,” He said, “I command you to come out and never enter him again.”'),
('MRK', 9, 26, 'MRK.9.26', 'After shrieking and convulsing him violently, the spirit came out. The boy became like a corpse, so that many said, “He is dead.”'),
('MRK', 9, 27, 'MRK.9.27', 'But Jesus took him by the hand and helped him to his feet, and he stood up.'),
('MRK', 9, 28, 'MRK.9.28', 'After Jesus had gone into the house, His disciples asked Him privately, “Why couldn’t we drive it out?”'),
('MRK', 9, 29, 'MRK.9.29', 'Jesus answered, “This kind cannot come out, except by prayer.”'),
('MRK', 9, 30, 'MRK.9.30', 'Going on from there, they passed through Galilee. But Jesus did not want anyone to know,'),
('MRK', 9, 31, 'MRK.9.31', 'because He was teaching His disciples. He told them, “The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men. They will kill Him, and after three days He will rise.”'),
('MRK', 9, 32, 'MRK.9.32', 'But they did not understand this statement, and they were afraid to ask Him about it.'),
('MRK', 9, 33, 'MRK.9.33', 'Then they came to Capernaum. While Jesus was in the house, He asked them, “What were you discussing on the way?”'),
('MRK', 9, 34, 'MRK.9.34', 'But they were silent, for on the way they had been arguing about which of them was the greatest.'),
('MRK', 9, 35, 'MRK.9.35', 'Sitting down, Jesus called the Twelve and said, “If anyone wants to be first, he must be the last of all and the servant of all.”'),
('MRK', 9, 36, 'MRK.9.36', 'Then He had a little child stand among them. Taking the child in His arms, He said to them,'),
('MRK', 9, 37, 'MRK.9.37', '“Whoever welcomes one of these little children in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes not only Me, but the One who sent Me.”'),
('MRK', 9, 38, 'MRK.9.38', 'John said to Him, “Teacher, we saw someone else driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”'),
('MRK', 9, 39, 'MRK.9.39', '“Do not stop him,” Jesus replied. “For no one who performs a miracle in My name can turn around and speak evil of Me.'),
('MRK', 9, 40, 'MRK.9.40', 'For whoever is not against us is for us.'),
('MRK', 9, 41, 'MRK.9.41', 'Indeed, if anyone gives you even a cup of water because you bear the name of Christ, truly I tell you, he will never lose his reward.'),
('MRK', 9, 42, 'MRK.9.42', 'But if anyone causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea.'),
('MRK', 9, 43, 'MRK.9.43', 'If your hand causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life crippled than to have two hands and go into hell, into the unquenchable fire.'),
('MRK', 9, 45, 'MRK.9.45', 'If your foot causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life lame than to have two feet and be thrown into hell.'),
('MRK', 9, 47, 'MRK.9.47', 'And if your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of God with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hell,'),
('MRK', 9, 48, 'MRK.9.48', 'where ‘their worm never dies, and the fire is never quenched.’'),
('MRK', 9, 49, 'MRK.9.49', 'For everyone will be salted with fire.'),
('MRK', 9, 50, 'MRK.9.50', 'Salt is good, but if the salt loses its saltiness, with what will you season it? Have salt among yourselves, and be at peace with one another.”'),
('MRK', 10, 1, 'MRK.10.1', 'Then Jesus left that place and went into the region of Judea, beyond the Jordan. Again the crowds came to Him and He taught them, as was His custom.'),
('MRK', 10, 2, 'MRK.10.2', 'Some Pharisees came to test Him. “Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife?” they inquired.'),
('MRK', 10, 3, 'MRK.10.3', '“What did Moses command you?” He replied.'),
('MRK', 10, 4, 'MRK.10.4', 'They answered, “Moses permitted a man to write his wife a certificate of divorce and send her away.”'),
('MRK', 10, 5, 'MRK.10.5', 'But Jesus told them, “Moses wrote this commandment for you because of your hardness of heart.'),
('MRK', 10, 6, 'MRK.10.6', 'However, from the beginning of creation, ‘God made them male and female.’'),
('MRK', 10, 7, 'MRK.10.7', '‘For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife,'),
('MRK', 10, 8, 'MRK.10.8', 'and the two will become one flesh.’ So they are no longer two, but one flesh.'),
('MRK', 10, 9, 'MRK.10.9', 'Therefore what God has joined together, let man not separate.”'),
('MRK', 10, 10, 'MRK.10.10', 'When they were back inside the house, the disciples asked Jesus about this matter.'),
('MRK', 10, 11, 'MRK.10.11', 'So He told them, “Whoever divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery against her.'),
('MRK', 10, 12, 'MRK.10.12', 'And if a woman divorces her husband and marries another man, she commits adultery.”'),
('MRK', 10, 13, 'MRK.10.13', 'Now people were bringing the little children to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them, and the disciples rebuked those who brought them.'),
('MRK', 10, 14, 'MRK.10.14', 'But when Jesus saw this, He was indignant and told them, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.'),
('MRK', 10, 15, 'MRK.10.15', 'Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”'),
('MRK', 10, 16, 'MRK.10.16', 'And He took the children in His arms, placed His hands on them, and blessed them.'),
('MRK', 10, 17, 'MRK.10.17', 'As Jesus started on His way, a man ran up and knelt before Him. “Good Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”'),
('MRK', 10, 18, 'MRK.10.18', '“Why do you call Me good?” Jesus replied. “No one is good except God alone.'),
('MRK', 10, 19, 'MRK.10.19', 'You know the commandments: ‘Do not murder, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not bear false witness, do not cheat others, honor your father and mother.’”'),
('MRK', 10, 20, 'MRK.10.20', '“Teacher,” he replied, “all these I have kept from my youth.”'),
('MRK', 10, 21, 'MRK.10.21', 'Jesus looked at him, loved him, and said to him, “There is one thing you lack: Go, sell everything you own and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”'),
('MRK', 10, 22, 'MRK.10.22', 'But the man was saddened by these words and went away in sorrow, because he had great wealth.'),
('MRK', 10, 23, 'MRK.10.23', 'Then Jesus looked around and said to His disciples, “How hard it is for the rich to enter the kingdom of God!”'),
('MRK', 10, 24, 'MRK.10.24', 'And the disciples were amazed at His words. But Jesus said to them again, “Children, how hard it is to enter the kingdom of God!'),
('MRK', 10, 25, 'MRK.10.25', 'It is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”'),
('MRK', 10, 26, 'MRK.10.26', 'They were even more astonished and said to one another, “Who then can be saved?”'),
('MRK', 10, 27, 'MRK.10.27', 'Jesus looked at them and said, “With man this is impossible, but not with God. For all things are possible with God.”'),
('MRK', 10, 28, 'MRK.10.28', 'Peter began to say to Him, “Look, we have left everything and followed You.”'),
('MRK', 10, 29, 'MRK.10.29', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “no one who has left home or brothers or sisters or mother or father or children or fields for My sake and for the gospel'),
('MRK', 10, 30, 'MRK.10.30', 'will fail to receive a hundredfold in the present age—houses and brothers and sisters and mothers and children and fields, along with persecutions—and in the age to come, eternal life.'),
('MRK', 10, 31, 'MRK.10.31', 'But many who are first will be last, and the last will be first.”'),
('MRK', 10, 32, 'MRK.10.32', 'As they were going up the road to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking ahead of them. The disciples were amazed, but those who followed were afraid. Again Jesus took the Twelve aside and began to tell them what was going to happen to Him:'),
('MRK', 10, 33, 'MRK.10.33', '“Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be delivered over to the chief priests and scribes. They will condemn Him to death and will deliver Him over to the Gentiles,'),
('MRK', 10, 34, 'MRK.10.34', 'who will mock Him and spit on Him and flog Him and kill Him. And after three days He will rise again.”'),
('MRK', 10, 35, 'MRK.10.35', 'Then James and John, the sons of Zebedee, came to Jesus and declared, “Teacher, we want You to do for us whatever we ask.”'),
('MRK', 10, 36, 'MRK.10.36', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” He inquired.'),
('MRK', 10, 37, 'MRK.10.37', 'They answered, “Grant that one of us may sit at Your right hand and the other at Your left in Your glory.”'),
('MRK', 10, 38, 'MRK.10.38', '“You do not know what you are asking,” Jesus replied. “Can you drink the cup I will drink, or be baptized with the baptism I will undergo?”'),
('MRK', 10, 39, 'MRK.10.39', '“We can,” the brothers answered. “You will drink the cup that I drink,” Jesus said, “and you will be baptized with the baptism that I undergo.'),
('MRK', 10, 40, 'MRK.10.40', 'But to sit at My right or left is not Mine to grant. These seats belong to those for whom they have been prepared.”'),
('MRK', 10, 41, 'MRK.10.41', 'When the ten heard about this, they became indignant with James and John.'),
('MRK', 10, 42, 'MRK.10.42', 'So Jesus called them together and said, “You know that those regarded as rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their superiors exercise authority over them.'),
('MRK', 10, 43, 'MRK.10.43', 'But it shall not be this way among you. Instead, whoever wants to become great among you must be your servant,'),
('MRK', 10, 44, 'MRK.10.44', 'and whoever wants to be first must be the slave of all.'),
('MRK', 10, 45, 'MRK.10.45', 'For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many.”'),
('MRK', 10, 46, 'MRK.10.46', 'Next, they came to Jericho. And as Jesus and His disciples were leaving Jericho with a large crowd, a blind beggar named Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, was sitting beside the road.'),
('MRK', 10, 47, 'MRK.10.47', 'When he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”'),
('MRK', 10, 48, 'MRK.10.48', 'Many people admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”'),
('MRK', 10, 49, 'MRK.10.49', 'Jesus stopped and said, “Call him.” So they called the blind man. “Take courage!” they said. “Get up! He is calling for you.”'),
('MRK', 10, 50, 'MRK.10.50', 'Throwing off his cloak, Bartimaeus jumped up and came to Jesus.'),
('MRK', 10, 51, 'MRK.10.51', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” Jesus asked. “Rabboni,” said the blind man, “let me see again.”'),
('MRK', 10, 52, 'MRK.10.52', '“Go,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you.” And immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus along the road.'),
('MRK', 11, 1, 'MRK.11.1', 'As they approached Jerusalem and came to Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent out two of His disciples'),
('MRK', 11, 2, 'MRK.11.2', 'and said to them, “Go into the village ahead of you, and as soon as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there, on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.'),
('MRK', 11, 3, 'MRK.11.3', 'If anyone asks, ‘Why are you doing this?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it and will return it shortly.’”'),
('MRK', 11, 4, 'MRK.11.4', 'So they went and found the colt outside in the street, tied at a doorway. They untied it,'),
('MRK', 11, 5, 'MRK.11.5', 'and some who were standing there asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”'),
('MRK', 11, 6, 'MRK.11.6', 'The disciples answered as Jesus had instructed them, and the people gave them permission.'),
('MRK', 11, 7, 'MRK.11.7', 'Then they led the colt to Jesus and threw their cloaks over it, and He sat on it.'),
('MRK', 11, 8, 'MRK.11.8', 'Many in the crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others spread branches they had cut from the fields.'),
('MRK', 11, 9, 'MRK.11.9', 'The ones who went ahead and those who followed were shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!”'),
('MRK', 11, 10, 'MRK.11.10', '“Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!” “Hosanna in the highest!”'),
('MRK', 11, 11, 'MRK.11.11', 'Then Jesus entered Jerusalem and went into the temple courts. He looked around at everything, but since it was already late, He went out to Bethany with the Twelve.'),
('MRK', 11, 12, 'MRK.11.12', 'The next day, when they had left Bethany, Jesus was hungry.'),
('MRK', 11, 13, 'MRK.11.13', 'Seeing in the distance a fig tree in leaf, He went to see if there was any fruit on it. But when He reached it, He found nothing on it except leaves, since it was not the season for figs.'),
('MRK', 11, 14, 'MRK.11.14', 'Then He said to the tree, “May no one ever eat of your fruit again.” And His disciples heard this statement.'),
('MRK', 11, 15, 'MRK.11.15', 'When they arrived in Jerusalem, Jesus entered the temple courts and began to drive out those who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling doves.'),
('MRK', 11, 16, 'MRK.11.16', 'And He would not allow anyone to carry merchandise through the temple courts.'),
('MRK', 11, 17, 'MRK.11.17', 'Then Jesus began to teach them, and He declared, “Is it not written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’? But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”'),
('MRK', 11, 18, 'MRK.11.18', 'When the chief priests and scribes heard this, they looked for a way to kill Him. For they were afraid of Him, because the whole crowd was astonished at His teaching.'),
('MRK', 11, 19, 'MRK.11.19', 'And when evening came, Jesus and His disciples went out of the city.'),
('MRK', 11, 20, 'MRK.11.20', 'As they were walking back in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered from its roots.'),
('MRK', 11, 21, 'MRK.11.21', 'Peter remembered it and said, “Look, Rabbi! The fig tree You cursed has withered.”'),
('MRK', 11, 22, 'MRK.11.22', '“Have faith in God,” Jesus said to them.'),
('MRK', 11, 23, 'MRK.11.23', '“Truly I tell you that if anyone says to this mountain, ‘Be lifted up and thrown into the sea,’ and has no doubt in his heart but believes that it will happen, it will be done for him.'),
('MRK', 11, 24, 'MRK.11.24', 'Therefore I tell you, whatever you ask for in prayer, believe that you have received it, and it will be yours.'),
('MRK', 11, 25, 'MRK.11.25', 'And when you stand to pray, if you hold anything against another, forgive it, so that your Father in heaven will forgive your trespasses as well.”'),
('MRK', 11, 27, 'MRK.11.27', 'After their return to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking in the temple courts, and the chief priests, scribes, and elders came up to Him.'),
('MRK', 11, 28, 'MRK.11.28', '“By what authority are You doing these things?” they asked. “And who gave You the authority to do them?”'),
('MRK', 11, 29, 'MRK.11.29', '“I will ask you one question,” Jesus replied, “and if you answer Me, I will tell you by what authority I am doing these things.'),
('MRK', 11, 30, 'MRK.11.30', 'John’s baptism—was it from heaven or from men? Answer Me!”'),
('MRK', 11, 31, 'MRK.11.31', 'They deliberated among themselves what they should answer: “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why then did you not believe him?’'),
('MRK', 11, 32, 'MRK.11.32', 'But if we say, ‘From men’...” they were afraid of the people, for they all held that John truly was a prophet.'),
('MRK', 11, 33, 'MRK.11.33', 'So they answered, “We do not know.” And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”'),
('MRK', 12, 1, 'MRK.12.1', 'Then Jesus began to speak to them in parables: “A man planted a vineyard. He put a wall around it, dug a wine vat, and built a watchtower. Then he rented it out to some tenants and went away on a journey.'),
('MRK', 12, 2, 'MRK.12.2', 'At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard.'),
('MRK', 12, 3, 'MRK.12.3', 'But they seized the servant, beat him, and sent him away empty-handed.'),
('MRK', 12, 4, 'MRK.12.4', 'Then he sent them another servant, and they struck him over the head and treated him shamefully.'),
('MRK', 12, 5, 'MRK.12.5', 'He sent still another, and this one they killed. He sent many others; some they beat and others they killed.'),
('MRK', 12, 6, 'MRK.12.6', 'Finally, having one beloved son, he sent him to them. ‘They will respect my son,’ he said.'),
('MRK', 12, 7, 'MRK.12.7', 'But the tenants said to one another, ‘This is the heir. Come, let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’'),
('MRK', 12, 8, 'MRK.12.8', 'So they seized the son, killed him, and threw him out of the vineyard.'),
('MRK', 12, 9, 'MRK.12.9', 'What then will the owner of the vineyard do? He will come and kill those tenants and give the vineyard to others.'),
('MRK', 12, 10, 'MRK.12.10', 'Have you never read this Scripture: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.'),
('MRK', 12, 11, 'MRK.12.11', 'This is from the Lord, and it is marvelous in our eyes’?”'),
('MRK', 12, 12, 'MRK.12.12', 'At this, the leaders sought to arrest Jesus, for they knew that He had spoken this parable against them. But fearing the crowd, they left Him and went away.'),
('MRK', 12, 13, 'MRK.12.13', 'Later, they sent some of the Pharisees and Herodians to catch Jesus in His words.'),
('MRK', 12, 14, 'MRK.12.14', '“Teacher,” they said, “we know that You are honest and seek favor from no one. Indeed, You are impartial and teach the way of God in accordance with the truth. Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar or not? Should we pay them or not?”'),
('MRK', 12, 15, 'MRK.12.15', 'But Jesus saw through their hypocrisy and said, “Why are you testing Me? Bring Me a denarius to inspect.”'),
('MRK', 12, 16, 'MRK.12.16', 'So they brought it, and He asked them, “Whose image is this? And whose inscription?” “Caesar’s,” they answered.'),
('MRK', 12, 17, 'MRK.12.17', 'Then Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.” And they marveled at Him.'),
('MRK', 12, 18, 'MRK.12.18', 'Then the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to Jesus and questioned Him:'),
('MRK', 12, 19, 'MRK.12.19', '“Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies and leaves a wife but no children, the man is to marry his brother’s widow and raise up offspring for him.'),
('MRK', 12, 20, 'MRK.12.20', 'Now there were seven brothers. The first one married and died, leaving no children.'),
('MRK', 12, 21, 'MRK.12.21', 'Then the second one married the widow, but he also died and left no children. And the third did likewise.'),
('MRK', 12, 22, 'MRK.12.22', 'In this way, none of the seven left any children. And last of all, the woman died.'),
('MRK', 12, 23, 'MRK.12.23', 'In the resurrection, then, whose wife will she be? For all seven were married to her.”'),
('MRK', 12, 24, 'MRK.12.24', 'Jesus said to them, “Aren’t you mistaken, because you do not know the Scriptures or the power of God?'),
('MRK', 12, 25, 'MRK.12.25', 'When the dead rise, they will neither marry nor be given in marriage. Instead, they will be like the angels in heaven.'),
('MRK', 12, 26, 'MRK.12.26', 'But concerning the dead rising, have you not read about the burning bush in the Book of Moses, how God told him, ‘I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob’?'),
('MRK', 12, 27, 'MRK.12.27', 'He is not the God of the dead, but of the living. You are badly mistaken!”'),
('MRK', 12, 28, 'MRK.12.28', 'Now one of the scribes had come up and heard their debate. Noticing how well Jesus had answered them, he asked Him, “Which commandment is the most important of all?”'),
('MRK', 12, 29, 'MRK.12.29', 'Jesus replied, “This is the most important: ‘Hear, O Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is One.'),
('MRK', 12, 30, 'MRK.12.30', 'Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind and with all your strength.’'),
('MRK', 12, 31, 'MRK.12.31', 'The second is this: ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’ No other commandment is greater than these.”'),
('MRK', 12, 32, 'MRK.12.32', '“Right, Teacher,” the scribe replied. “You have stated correctly that God is One and there is no other but Him,'),
('MRK', 12, 33, 'MRK.12.33', 'and to love Him with all your heart and with all your understanding and with all your strength, and to love your neighbor as yourself. This is more important than all burnt offerings and sacrifices.”'),
('MRK', 12, 34, 'MRK.12.34', 'When Jesus saw that the man had answered wisely, He said, “You are not far from the kingdom of God.” And no one dared to question Him any further.'),
('MRK', 12, 35, 'MRK.12.35', 'While Jesus was teaching in the temple courts, He asked, “How can the scribes say that the Christ is the Son of David?'),
('MRK', 12, 36, 'MRK.12.36', 'Speaking by the Holy Spirit, David himself declared: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand until I put Your enemies under Your feet.”’'),
('MRK', 12, 37, 'MRK.12.37', 'David himself calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be David’s son?” And the large crowd listened to Him with delight.'),
('MRK', 12, 38, 'MRK.12.38', 'In His teaching Jesus also said, “Watch out for the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, to receive greetings in the marketplaces,'),
('MRK', 12, 39, 'MRK.12.39', 'and to have the chief seats in the synagogues and the places of honor at banquets.'),
('MRK', 12, 40, 'MRK.12.40', 'They defraud widows of their houses, and for a show make lengthy prayers. These men will receive greater condemnation.”'),
('MRK', 12, 41, 'MRK.12.41', 'As Jesus was sitting opposite the treasury, He watched the crowd putting money into it. And many rich people put in large amounts.'),
('MRK', 12, 42, 'MRK.12.42', 'Then one poor widow came and put in two small copper coins, which amounted to a small fraction of a denarius.'),
('MRK', 12, 43, 'MRK.12.43', 'Jesus called His disciples to Him and said, “Truly I tell you, this poor widow has put more than all the others into the treasury.'),
('MRK', 12, 44, 'MRK.12.44', 'For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”'),
('MRK', 13, 1, 'MRK.13.1', 'As Jesus was leaving the temple, one of His disciples said to Him, “Teacher, look at the magnificent stones and buildings!”'),
('MRK', 13, 2, 'MRK.13.2', '“Do you see all these great buildings?” Jesus replied. “Not one stone here will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”'),
('MRK', 13, 3, 'MRK.13.3', 'While Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives opposite the temple, Peter, James, John, and Andrew asked Him privately,'),
('MRK', 13, 4, 'MRK.13.4', '“Tell us, when will these things happen? And what will be the sign that they are about to be fulfilled?”'),
('MRK', 13, 5, 'MRK.13.5', 'Jesus began by telling them, “See to it that no one deceives you.'),
('MRK', 13, 6, 'MRK.13.6', 'Many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am He,’ and will deceive many.'),
('MRK', 13, 7, 'MRK.13.7', 'When you hear of wars and rumors of wars, do not be alarmed. These things must happen, but the end is still to come.'),
('MRK', 13, 8, 'MRK.13.8', 'Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be earthquakes in various places, as well as famines. These are the beginning of birth pains.'),
('MRK', 13, 9, 'MRK.13.9', 'So be on your guard. You will be delivered over to the councils and beaten in the synagogues. On My account you will stand before governors and kings as witnesses to them.'),
('MRK', 13, 10, 'MRK.13.10', 'And the gospel must first be proclaimed to all the nations.'),
('MRK', 13, 11, 'MRK.13.11', 'But when they arrest you and hand you over, do not worry beforehand what to say. Instead, speak whatever you are given at that time, for it will not be you speaking, but the Holy Spirit.'),
('MRK', 13, 12, 'MRK.13.12', 'Brother will betray brother to death, and a father his child. Children will rise against their parents and have them put to death.'),
('MRK', 13, 13, 'MRK.13.13', 'You will be hated by everyone because of My name, but the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.'),
('MRK', 13, 14, 'MRK.13.14', 'So when you see the abomination of desolation standing where it should not be (let the reader understand), then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains.'),
('MRK', 13, 15, 'MRK.13.15', 'Let no one on the housetop go back inside to retrieve anything from his house.'),
('MRK', 13, 16, 'MRK.13.16', 'And let no one in the field return for his cloak.'),
('MRK', 13, 17, 'MRK.13.17', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers!'),
('MRK', 13, 18, 'MRK.13.18', 'Pray that this will not occur in the winter.'),
('MRK', 13, 19, 'MRK.13.19', 'For those will be days of tribulation unseen from the beginning of God’s creation until now, and never to be seen again.'),
('MRK', 13, 20, 'MRK.13.20', 'If the Lord had not cut short those days, nobody would be saved. But for the sake of the elect, whom He has chosen, He has cut them short.'),
('MRK', 13, 21, 'MRK.13.21', 'At that time if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is the Christ!’ or ‘There He is!’ do not believe it.'),
('MRK', 13, 22, 'MRK.13.22', 'For false Christs and false prophets will appear and perform signs and wonders to deceive even the elect, if that were possible.'),
('MRK', 13, 23, 'MRK.13.23', 'So be on your guard; I have told you everything in advance.'),
('MRK', 13, 24, 'MRK.13.24', 'But in those days, after that tribulation: ‘The sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light;'),
('MRK', 13, 25, 'MRK.13.25', 'the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken.’'),
('MRK', 13, 26, 'MRK.13.26', 'At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in the clouds with great power and glory.'),
('MRK', 13, 27, 'MRK.13.27', 'And He will send out the angels to gather His elect from the four winds, from the ends of the earth to the ends of heaven.'),
('MRK', 13, 28, 'MRK.13.28', 'Now learn this lesson from the fig tree: As soon as its branches become tender and sprout leaves, you know that summer is near.'),
('MRK', 13, 29, 'MRK.13.29', 'So also, when you see these things happening, know that He is near, right at the door.'),
('MRK', 13, 30, 'MRK.13.30', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.'),
('MRK', 13, 31, 'MRK.13.31', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.'),
('MRK', 13, 32, 'MRK.13.32', 'No one knows about that day or hour, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.'),
('MRK', 13, 33, 'MRK.13.33', 'Be on your guard and stay alert! For you do not know when the appointed time will come.'),
('MRK', 13, 34, 'MRK.13.34', 'It is like a man going on a journey who left his house, put each servant in charge of his own task, and instructed the doorkeeper to keep watch.'),
('MRK', 13, 35, 'MRK.13.35', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know when the master of the house will return—whether in the evening, at midnight, when the rooster crows, or in the morning.'),
('MRK', 13, 36, 'MRK.13.36', 'Otherwise, he may arrive without notice and find you sleeping.'),
('MRK', 13, 37, 'MRK.13.37', 'And what I say to you, I say to everyone: Keep watch!”'),
('MRK', 14, 1, 'MRK.14.1', 'Now the Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread were two days away, and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a covert way to arrest Jesus and kill Him.'),
('MRK', 14, 2, 'MRK.14.2', '“But not during the feast,” they said, “or there may be a riot among the people.”'),
('MRK', 14, 3, 'MRK.14.3', 'While Jesus was in Bethany reclining at the table in the home of Simon the Leper, a woman came with an alabaster jar of expensive perfume, made of pure nard. She broke open the jar and poured it on Jesus’ head.'),
('MRK', 14, 4, 'MRK.14.4', 'Some of those present, however, expressed their indignation to one another: “Why this waste of perfume?'),
('MRK', 14, 5, 'MRK.14.5', 'It could have been sold for over three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor.” And they scolded her.'),
('MRK', 14, 6, 'MRK.14.6', 'But Jesus said, “Leave her alone; why are you bothering her? She has done a beautiful deed to Me.'),
('MRK', 14, 7, 'MRK.14.7', 'The poor you will always have with you, and you can help them whenever you want. But you will not always have Me.'),
('MRK', 14, 8, 'MRK.14.8', 'She has done what she could to anoint My body in advance of My burial.'),
('MRK', 14, 9, 'MRK.14.9', 'And truly I tell you, wherever the gospel is preached in all the world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”'),
('MRK', 14, 10, 'MRK.14.10', 'Then Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve, went to the chief priests to betray Jesus to them.'),
('MRK', 14, 11, 'MRK.14.11', 'They were delighted to hear this, and they promised to give him money. So Judas began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus.'),
('MRK', 14, 12, 'MRK.14.12', 'On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, when the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed, Jesus’ disciples asked Him, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”'),
('MRK', 14, 13, 'MRK.14.13', 'So He sent two of His disciples and told them, “Go into the city, and a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him,'),
('MRK', 14, 14, 'MRK.14.14', 'and whichever house he enters, say to the owner, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is My guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’'),
('MRK', 14, 15, 'MRK.14.15', 'And he will show you a large upper room, furnished and ready. Make preparations for us there.”'),
('MRK', 14, 16, 'MRK.14.16', 'So the disciples left and went into the city, where they found everything as Jesus had described. And they prepared the Passover.'),
('MRK', 14, 17, 'MRK.14.17', 'When evening came, Jesus arrived with the Twelve.'),
('MRK', 14, 18, 'MRK.14.18', 'And while they were reclining and eating, Jesus said, “Truly I tell you, one of you who is eating with Me will betray Me.”'),
('MRK', 14, 19, 'MRK.14.19', 'They began to be grieved and to ask Him one after another, “Surely not I?”'),
('MRK', 14, 20, 'MRK.14.20', 'He answered, “It is one of the Twelve—the one who is dipping his hand into the bowl with Me.'),
('MRK', 14, 21, 'MRK.14.21', 'The Son of Man will go just as it is written about Him, but woe to that man by whom He is betrayed! It would be better for him if he had not been born.”'),
('MRK', 14, 22, 'MRK.14.22', 'While they were eating, Jesus took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to the disciples, saying, “Take it; this is My body.”'),
('MRK', 14, 23, 'MRK.14.23', 'Then He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave it to them, and they all drank from it.'),
('MRK', 14, 24, 'MRK.14.24', 'He said to them, “This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many.'),
('MRK', 14, 25, 'MRK.14.25', 'Truly I tell you, I will no longer drink of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it anew in the kingdom of God.”'),
('MRK', 14, 26, 'MRK.14.26', 'And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.'),
('MRK', 14, 27, 'MRK.14.27', 'Then Jesus said to them, “You will all fall away, for it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered.’'),
('MRK', 14, 28, 'MRK.14.28', 'But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”'),
('MRK', 14, 29, 'MRK.14.29', 'Peter declared, “Even if all fall away, I never will.”'),
('MRK', 14, 30, 'MRK.14.30', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “this very night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”'),
('MRK', 14, 31, 'MRK.14.31', 'But Peter kept insisting, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You.” And all the others said the same thing.'),
('MRK', 14, 32, 'MRK.14.32', 'Then they came to a place called Gethsemane, and Jesus told His disciples, “Sit here while I pray.”'),
('MRK', 14, 33, 'MRK.14.33', 'He took with Him Peter, James, and John, and began to be deeply troubled and distressed.'),
('MRK', 14, 34, 'MRK.14.34', 'Then He said to them, “My soul is consumed with sorrow to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch.”'),
('MRK', 14, 35, 'MRK.14.35', 'Going a little farther, He fell to the ground and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour would pass from Him.'),
('MRK', 14, 36, 'MRK.14.36', '“Abba, Father,” He said, “all things are possible for You. Take this cup from Me. Yet not what I will, but what You will.”'),
('MRK', 14, 37, 'MRK.14.37', 'Then Jesus returned and found them sleeping. “Simon, are you asleep?” He asked. “Were you not able to keep watch for one hour?'),
('MRK', 14, 38, 'MRK.14.38', 'Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the body is weak.”'),
('MRK', 14, 39, 'MRK.14.39', 'Again He went away and prayed, saying the same thing.'),
('MRK', 14, 40, 'MRK.14.40', 'And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy. And they did not know what to answer Him.'),
('MRK', 14, 41, 'MRK.14.41', 'When Jesus returned the third time, He said, “Are you still sleeping and resting? That is enough! The hour has come. Look, the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.'),
('MRK', 14, 42, 'MRK.14.42', 'Rise, let us go. See, My betrayer is approaching!”'),
('MRK', 14, 43, 'MRK.14.43', 'While Jesus was still speaking, Judas, one of the Twelve, arrived, accompanied by a crowd armed with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests, scribes, and elders.'),
('MRK', 14, 44, 'MRK.14.44', 'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them: “The One I kiss is the man; arrest Him and lead Him away securely.”'),
('MRK', 14, 45, 'MRK.14.45', 'Going directly to Jesus, he said, “Rabbi!” and kissed Him.'),
('MRK', 14, 46, 'MRK.14.46', 'Then the men seized Jesus and arrested Him.'),
('MRK', 14, 47, 'MRK.14.47', 'And one of the bystanders drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.'),
('MRK', 14, 48, 'MRK.14.48', 'Jesus asked the crowd, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as you would an outlaw?'),
('MRK', 14, 49, 'MRK.14.49', 'Every day I was with you, teaching in the temple courts, and you did not arrest Me. But this has happened that the Scriptures would be fulfilled.”'),
('MRK', 14, 50, 'MRK.14.50', 'Then everyone deserted Him and fled.'),
('MRK', 14, 51, 'MRK.14.51', 'One young man who had been following Jesus was wearing a linen cloth around his body. They caught hold of him,'),
('MRK', 14, 52, 'MRK.14.52', 'but he pulled free of the linen cloth and ran away naked.'),
('MRK', 14, 53, 'MRK.14.53', 'They led Jesus away to the high priest, and all the chief priests, elders, and scribes assembled.'),
('MRK', 14, 54, 'MRK.14.54', 'Peter followed Him at a distance, right into the courtyard of the high priest. And he sat with the officers and warmed himself by the fire.'),
('MRK', 14, 55, 'MRK.14.55', 'Now the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin were seeking testimony against Jesus to put Him to death, but they did not find any.'),
('MRK', 14, 56, 'MRK.14.56', 'For many bore false witness against Jesus, but their testimony was inconsistent.'),
('MRK', 14, 57, 'MRK.14.57', 'Then some men stood up and testified falsely against Him:'),
('MRK', 14, 58, 'MRK.14.58', '“We heard Him say, ‘I will destroy this man-made temple, and in three days I will build another that is made without hands.’”'),
('MRK', 14, 59, 'MRK.14.59', 'But even their testimony was inconsistent.'),
('MRK', 14, 60, 'MRK.14.60', 'So the high priest stood up before them and questioned Jesus, “Have You no answer? What are these men testifying against You?”'),
('MRK', 14, 61, 'MRK.14.61', 'But Jesus remained silent and made no reply. Again the high priest questioned Him, “Are You the Christ, the Son of the Blessed One?”'),
('MRK', 14, 62, 'MRK.14.62', '“I am,” said Jesus, “and you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming with the clouds of heaven.”'),
('MRK', 14, 63, 'MRK.14.63', 'At this, the high priest tore his clothes and declared, “Why do we need any more witnesses?'),
('MRK', 14, 64, 'MRK.14.64', 'You have heard the blasphemy. What is your verdict?” And they all condemned Him as deserving of death.'),
('MRK', 14, 65, 'MRK.14.65', 'Then some of them began to spit on Him. They blindfolded Him, struck Him with their fists, and said to Him, “Prophesy!” And the officers received Him with slaps in His face.'),
('MRK', 14, 66, 'MRK.14.66', 'While Peter was in the courtyard below, one of the servant girls of the high priest came down'),
('MRK', 14, 67, 'MRK.14.67', 'and saw him warming himself there. She looked at Peter and said, “You also were with Jesus the Nazarene.”'),
('MRK', 14, 68, 'MRK.14.68', 'But he denied it. “I do not know or even understand what you are talking about,” he said. Then he went out to the gateway, and the rooster crowed.'),
('MRK', 14, 69, 'MRK.14.69', 'There the servant girl saw him and again said to those standing nearby, “This man is one of them.”'),
('MRK', 14, 70, 'MRK.14.70', 'But he denied it again. After a little while, those standing nearby said once more to Peter, “Surely you are one of them, for you too are a Galilean.”'),
('MRK', 14, 71, 'MRK.14.71', 'But he began to curse and swear, “I do not know this man of whom you speak!”'),
('MRK', 14, 72, 'MRK.14.72', 'And immediately the rooster crowed a second time. Then Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.” And he broke down and wept.'),
('MRK', 15, 1, 'MRK.15.1', 'Early in the morning, the chief priests, elders, scribes, and the whole Sanhedrin devised a plan. They bound Jesus, led Him away, and handed Him over to Pilate.'),
('MRK', 15, 2, 'MRK.15.2', 'So Pilate questioned Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.'),
('MRK', 15, 3, 'MRK.15.3', 'And the chief priests began to accuse Him of many things.'),
('MRK', 15, 4, 'MRK.15.4', 'Then Pilate questioned Him again, “Have You no answer? Look how many charges they are bringing against You!”'),
('MRK', 15, 5, 'MRK.15.5', 'But to Pilate’s amazement, Jesus made no further reply.'),
('MRK', 15, 6, 'MRK.15.6', 'Now it was Pilate’s custom at the feast to release to the people a prisoner of their choosing.'),
('MRK', 15, 7, 'MRK.15.7', 'And a man named Barabbas was imprisoned with the rebels who had committed murder during the insurrection.'),
('MRK', 15, 8, 'MRK.15.8', 'So the crowd went up and began asking Pilate to keep his custom.'),
('MRK', 15, 9, 'MRK.15.9', '“Do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?” Pilate asked.'),
('MRK', 15, 10, 'MRK.15.10', 'For he knew it was out of envy that the chief priests had handed Jesus over.'),
('MRK', 15, 11, 'MRK.15.11', 'But the chief priests stirred up the crowd to have him release Barabbas to them instead.'),
('MRK', 15, 12, 'MRK.15.12', 'So Pilate asked them again, “What then do you want me to do with the One you call the King of the Jews?”'),
('MRK', 15, 13, 'MRK.15.13', 'And they shouted back, “Crucify Him!”'),
('MRK', 15, 14, 'MRK.15.14', '“Why?” asked Pilate. “What evil has He done?” But they shouted all the louder, “Crucify Him!”'),
('MRK', 15, 15, 'MRK.15.15', 'And wishing to satisfy the crowd, Pilate released Barabbas to them. But he had Jesus flogged, and handed Him over to be crucified.'),
('MRK', 15, 16, 'MRK.15.16', 'Then the soldiers led Jesus away into the palace (that is, the Praetorium) and called the whole company together.'),
('MRK', 15, 17, 'MRK.15.17', 'They dressed Him in a purple robe, twisted together a crown of thorns, and set it on His head.'),
('MRK', 15, 18, 'MRK.15.18', 'And they began to salute Him: “Hail, King of the Jews!”'),
('MRK', 15, 19, 'MRK.15.19', 'They kept striking His head with a staff and spitting on Him. And they knelt down and bowed before Him.'),
('MRK', 15, 20, 'MRK.15.20', 'After they had mocked Him, they removed the purple robe and put His own clothes back on Him. Then they led Him out to crucify Him.'),
('MRK', 15, 21, 'MRK.15.21', 'Now Simon of Cyrene, the father of Alexander and Rufus, was passing by on his way in from the country, and the soldiers forced him to carry the cross of Jesus.'),
('MRK', 15, 22, 'MRK.15.22', 'They brought Jesus to a place called Golgotha, which means The Place of the Skull.'),
('MRK', 15, 23, 'MRK.15.23', 'There they offered Him wine mixed with myrrh, but He did not take it.'),
('MRK', 15, 24, 'MRK.15.24', 'And they crucified Him. They also divided His garments by casting lots to decide what each of them would take.'),
('MRK', 15, 25, 'MRK.15.25', 'It was the third hour when they crucified Him.'),
('MRK', 15, 26, 'MRK.15.26', 'And the charge inscribed against Him read: THE KING OF THE JEWS.'),
('MRK', 15, 27, 'MRK.15.27', 'Along with Jesus, they crucified two robbers, one on His right and one on His left.'),
('MRK', 15, 29, 'MRK.15.29', 'And those who passed by heaped abuse on Him, shaking their heads and saying, “Aha! You who are going to destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days,'),
('MRK', 15, 30, 'MRK.15.30', 'come down from the cross and save Yourself!”'),
('MRK', 15, 31, 'MRK.15.31', 'In the same way, the chief priests and scribes mocked Him among themselves, saying, “He saved others, but He cannot save Himself!'),
('MRK', 15, 32, 'MRK.15.32', 'Let the Christ, the King of Israel, come down now from the cross, so that we may see and believe!” And even those who were crucified with Him berated Him.'),
('MRK', 15, 33, 'MRK.15.33', 'From the sixth hour until the ninth hour darkness came over all the land.'),
('MRK', 15, 34, 'MRK.15.34', 'At the ninth hour, Jesus cried out in a loud voice, “Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani?” which means, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”'),
('MRK', 15, 35, 'MRK.15.35', 'When some of those standing nearby heard this, they said, “Behold, He is calling Elijah.”'),
('MRK', 15, 36, 'MRK.15.36', 'And someone ran and filled a sponge with sour wine. He put it on a reed and held it up for Jesus to drink, saying, “Leave Him alone. Let us see if Elijah comes to take Him down.”'),
('MRK', 15, 37, 'MRK.15.37', 'But Jesus let out a loud cry and breathed His last.'),
('MRK', 15, 38, 'MRK.15.38', 'And the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom.'),
('MRK', 15, 39, 'MRK.15.39', 'When the centurion standing there in front of Jesus saw how He had breathed His last, he said, “Truly this man was the Son of God!”'),
('MRK', 15, 40, 'MRK.15.40', 'And there were also women watching from a distance. Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James the younger and of Joses, and Salome.'),
('MRK', 15, 41, 'MRK.15.41', 'These women had followed Jesus and ministered to Him while He was in Galilee, and there were many other women who had come up to Jerusalem with Him.'),
('MRK', 15, 42, 'MRK.15.42', 'Now it was already evening. Since it was Preparation Day (that is, the day before the Sabbath),'),
('MRK', 15, 43, 'MRK.15.43', 'Joseph of Arimathea, a prominent Council member who himself was waiting for the kingdom of God, boldly went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus.'),
('MRK', 15, 44, 'MRK.15.44', 'Pilate was surprised to hear that Jesus was already dead, so he summoned the centurion to ask if this was so.'),
('MRK', 15, 45, 'MRK.15.45', 'When Pilate had confirmed it with the centurion, he granted the body to Joseph.'),
('MRK', 15, 46, 'MRK.15.46', 'So Joseph bought a linen cloth, took down the body of Jesus, wrapped it in the cloth, and placed it in a tomb that had been cut out of the rock. Then he rolled a stone against the entrance to the tomb.'),
('MRK', 15, 47, 'MRK.15.47', 'Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joseph saw where His body was placed.'),
('MRK', 16, 1, 'MRK.16.1', 'When the Sabbath was over, Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought spices so they could go and anoint the body of Jesus.'),
('MRK', 16, 2, 'MRK.16.2', 'Very early on the first day of the week, just after sunrise, they went to the tomb.'),
('MRK', 16, 3, 'MRK.16.3', 'They were asking one another, “Who will roll away the stone from the entrance of the tomb?”'),
('MRK', 16, 4, 'MRK.16.4', 'But when they looked up, they saw that the stone had been rolled away, even though it was extremely large.'),
('MRK', 16, 5, 'MRK.16.5', 'When they entered the tomb, they saw a young man dressed in a white robe sitting on the right side, and they were alarmed.'),
('MRK', 16, 6, 'MRK.16.6', 'But he said to them, “Do not be alarmed. You are looking for Jesus the Nazarene, who was crucified. He has risen! He is not here! See the place where they put Him.'),
('MRK', 16, 7, 'MRK.16.7', 'But go, tell His disciples and Peter, ‘He is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him, just as He told you.’”'),
('MRK', 16, 8, 'MRK.16.8', 'So the women left the tomb and ran away, trembling and bewildered. And in their fear they did not say a word to anyone.'),
('MRK', 16, 9, 'MRK.16.9', 'Early on the first day of the week, after Jesus had risen, He appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom He had driven out seven demons.'),
('MRK', 16, 10, 'MRK.16.10', 'She went and told those who had been with Him, who were mourning and weeping.'),
('MRK', 16, 11, 'MRK.16.11', 'And when they heard that Jesus was alive and she had seen Him, they did not believe it.'),
('MRK', 16, 12, 'MRK.16.12', 'After this, Jesus appeared in a different form to two of them as they walked along in the country.'),
('MRK', 16, 13, 'MRK.16.13', 'And they went back and reported it to the rest, but they did not believe them either.'),
('MRK', 16, 14, 'MRK.16.14', 'Later, as they were eating, Jesus appeared to the Eleven and rebuked them for their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they did not believe those who had seen Him after He had risen.'),
('MRK', 16, 15, 'MRK.16.15', 'And He said to them, “Go into all the world and preach the gospel to every creature.'),
('MRK', 16, 16, 'MRK.16.16', 'Whoever believes and is baptized will be saved, but whoever does not believe will be condemned.'),
('MRK', 16, 17, 'MRK.16.17', 'And these signs will accompany those who believe: In My name they will drive out demons; they will speak in new tongues;'),
('MRK', 16, 18, 'MRK.16.18', 'they will pick up snakes with their hands, and if they drink any deadly poison, it will not harm them; they will lay their hands on the sick, and they will be made well.”'),
('MRK', 16, 19, 'MRK.16.19', 'After the Lord Jesus had spoken to them, He was taken up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God.'),
('MRK', 16, 20, 'MRK.16.20', 'And they went out and preached everywhere, and the Lord worked through them, confirming His word by the signs that accompanied it.'),
('LUK', 1, 1, 'LUK.1.1', 'Many have undertaken to compose an account of the things that have been fulfilled among us,'),
('LUK', 1, 2, 'LUK.1.2', 'just as they were handed down to us by the initial eyewitnesses and servants of the word.'),
('LUK', 1, 3, 'LUK.1.3', 'Therefore, having carefully investigated everything from the beginning, it seemed good also to me to write an orderly account for you, most excellent Theophilus,'),
('LUK', 1, 4, 'LUK.1.4', 'so that you may know the certainty of the things you have been taught.'),
('LUK', 1, 5, 'LUK.1.5', 'In the time of Herod king of Judea there was a priest named Zechariah, who belonged to the priestly division of Abijah, and whose wife Elizabeth was a descendant of Aaron.'),
('LUK', 1, 6, 'LUK.1.6', 'Both of them were righteous in the sight of God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and decrees of the Lord.'),
('LUK', 1, 7, 'LUK.1.7', 'But they had no children, because Elizabeth was barren, and they were both well along in years.'),
('LUK', 1, 8, 'LUK.1.8', 'One day while Zechariah’s division was on duty and he was serving as priest before God,'),
('LUK', 1, 9, 'LUK.1.9', 'he was chosen by lot, according to the custom of the priesthood, to enter the temple of the Lord and burn incense.'),
('LUK', 1, 10, 'LUK.1.10', 'And at the hour of the incense offering, the whole congregation was praying outside.'),
('LUK', 1, 11, 'LUK.1.11', 'Just then an angel of the Lord appeared to Zechariah, standing at the right side of the altar of incense.'),
('LUK', 1, 12, 'LUK.1.12', 'When Zechariah saw him, he was startled and gripped with fear.'),
('LUK', 1, 13, 'LUK.1.13', 'But the angel said to him, “Do not be afraid, Zechariah, because your prayer has been heard. Your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you are to give him the name John.'),
('LUK', 1, 14, 'LUK.1.14', 'He will be a joy and delight to you, and many will rejoice at his birth,'),
('LUK', 1, 15, 'LUK.1.15', 'for he will be great in the sight of the Lord. He shall never take wine or strong drink, and he will be filled with the Holy Spirit even from his mother’s womb.'),
('LUK', 1, 16, 'LUK.1.16', 'Many of the sons of Israel he will turn back to the Lord their God.'),
('LUK', 1, 17, 'LUK.1.17', 'And he will go on before the Lord in the spirit and power of Elijah, to turn the hearts of the fathers to their children and the disobedient to the wisdom of the righteous—to make ready a people prepared for the Lord.”'),
('LUK', 1, 18, 'LUK.1.18', '“How can I be sure of this?” Zechariah asked the angel. “I am an old man, and my wife is well along in years.”'),
('LUK', 1, 19, 'LUK.1.19', '“I am Gabriel,” replied the angel. “I stand in the presence of God, and I have been sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news.'),
('LUK', 1, 20, 'LUK.1.20', 'And now you will be silent and unable to speak until the day this comes to pass, because you did not believe my words, which will be fulfilled at their proper time.”'),
('LUK', 1, 21, 'LUK.1.21', 'Meanwhile, the people were waiting for Zechariah and wondering why he took so long in the temple.'),
('LUK', 1, 22, 'LUK.1.22', 'When he came out and was unable to speak to them, they realized he had seen a vision in the temple. He kept making signs to them but remained unable to speak.'),
('LUK', 1, 23, 'LUK.1.23', 'And when the days of his service were complete, he returned home.'),
('LUK', 1, 24, 'LUK.1.24', 'After these days, his wife Elizabeth became pregnant and for five months remained in seclusion. She declared,'),
('LUK', 1, 25, 'LUK.1.25', '“The Lord has done this for me. In these days He has shown me favor and taken away my disgrace among the people.”'),
('LUK', 1, 26, 'LUK.1.26', 'In the sixth month, God sent the angel Gabriel to a town in Galilee called Nazareth,'),
('LUK', 1, 27, 'LUK.1.27', 'to a virgin pledged in marriage to a man named Joseph, who was of the house of David. And the virgin’s name was Mary.'),
('LUK', 1, 28, 'LUK.1.28', 'The angel appeared to her and said, “Greetings, you who are highly favored! The Lord is with you.”'),
('LUK', 1, 29, 'LUK.1.29', 'Mary was greatly troubled at his words and wondered what kind of greeting this might be.'),
('LUK', 1, 30, 'LUK.1.30', 'So the angel told her, “Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God.'),
('LUK', 1, 31, 'LUK.1.31', 'Behold, you will conceive and give birth to a son, and you are to give Him the name Jesus.'),
('LUK', 1, 32, 'LUK.1.32', 'He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High. The Lord God will give Him the throne of His father David,'),
('LUK', 1, 33, 'LUK.1.33', 'and He will reign over the house of Jacob forever. His kingdom will never end!”'),
('LUK', 1, 34, 'LUK.1.34', '“How can this be,” Mary asked the angel, “since I am a virgin?”'),
('LUK', 1, 35, 'LUK.1.35', 'The angel replied, “The Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you. So the Holy One to be born will be called the Son of God.'),
('LUK', 1, 36, 'LUK.1.36', 'Look, even Elizabeth your relative has conceived a son in her old age, and she who was called barren is in her sixth month.'),
('LUK', 1, 37, 'LUK.1.37', 'For no word from God will ever fail.”'),
('LUK', 1, 38, 'LUK.1.38', '“I am the Lord’s servant,” Mary answered. “May it happen to me according to your word.” Then the angel left her.'),
('LUK', 1, 39, 'LUK.1.39', 'In those days Mary got ready and hurried to a town in the hill country of Judah,'),
('LUK', 1, 40, 'LUK.1.40', 'where she entered the home of Zechariah and greeted Elizabeth.'),
('LUK', 1, 41, 'LUK.1.41', 'When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the baby leaped in her womb, and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit.'),
('LUK', 1, 42, 'LUK.1.42', 'In a loud voice she exclaimed, “Blessed are you among women, and blessed is the fruit of your womb!'),
('LUK', 1, 43, 'LUK.1.43', 'And why am I so honored, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?'),
('LUK', 1, 44, 'LUK.1.44', 'For as soon as the sound of your greeting reached my ears, the baby in my womb leaped for joy.'),
('LUK', 1, 45, 'LUK.1.45', 'Blessed is she who has believed that the Lord’s word to her will be fulfilled.”'),
('LUK', 1, 46, 'LUK.1.46', 'Then Mary said: “My soul magnifies the Lord,'),
('LUK', 1, 47, 'LUK.1.47', 'and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior!'),
('LUK', 1, 48, 'LUK.1.48', 'For He has looked with favor on the humble state of His servant. From now on all generations will call me blessed.'),
('LUK', 1, 49, 'LUK.1.49', 'For the Mighty One has done great things for me. Holy is His name.'),
('LUK', 1, 50, 'LUK.1.50', 'His mercy extends to those who fear Him, from generation to generation.'),
('LUK', 1, 51, 'LUK.1.51', 'He has performed mighty deeds with His arm; He has scattered those who are proud in the thoughts of their hearts.'),
('LUK', 1, 52, 'LUK.1.52', 'He has brought down rulers from their thrones, but has exalted the humble.'),
('LUK', 1, 53, 'LUK.1.53', 'He has filled the hungry with good things, but has sent the rich away empty.'),
('LUK', 1, 54, 'LUK.1.54', 'He has helped His servant Israel, remembering to be merciful,'),
('LUK', 1, 55, 'LUK.1.55', 'as He promised to our fathers, to Abraham and his descendants forever.”'),
('LUK', 1, 56, 'LUK.1.56', 'Mary stayed with Elizabeth for about three months and then returned home.'),
('LUK', 1, 57, 'LUK.1.57', 'When the time came for Elizabeth to have her child, she gave birth to a son.'),
('LUK', 1, 58, 'LUK.1.58', 'Her neighbors and relatives heard that the Lord had shown her great mercy, and they rejoiced with her.'),
('LUK', 1, 59, 'LUK.1.59', 'On the eighth day, when they came to circumcise the child, they were going to name him after his father Zechariah.'),
('LUK', 1, 60, 'LUK.1.60', 'But his mother replied, “No! He shall be called John.”'),
('LUK', 1, 61, 'LUK.1.61', 'They said to her, “There is no one among your relatives who bears this name.”'),
('LUK', 1, 62, 'LUK.1.62', 'So they made signs to his father to find out what he wanted to name the child.'),
('LUK', 1, 63, 'LUK.1.63', 'Zechariah asked for a tablet and wrote, “His name is John.” And they were all amazed.'),
('LUK', 1, 64, 'LUK.1.64', 'Immediately Zechariah’s mouth was opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak, praising God.'),
('LUK', 1, 65, 'LUK.1.65', 'All their neighbors were filled with awe, and people throughout the hill country of Judea were talking about these events.'),
('LUK', 1, 66, 'LUK.1.66', 'And all who heard this wondered in their hearts and asked, “What then will this child become?” For the Lord’s hand was with him.'),
('LUK', 1, 67, 'LUK.1.67', 'Then his father Zechariah was filled with the Holy Spirit and prophesied:'),
('LUK', 1, 68, 'LUK.1.68', '“Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, because He has visited and redeemed His people.'),
('LUK', 1, 69, 'LUK.1.69', 'He has raised up a horn of salvation for us in the house of His servant David,'),
('LUK', 1, 70, 'LUK.1.70', 'as He spoke through His holy prophets, those of ages past,'),
('LUK', 1, 71, 'LUK.1.71', 'salvation from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us,'),
('LUK', 1, 72, 'LUK.1.72', 'to show mercy to our fathers and to remember His holy covenant,'),
('LUK', 1, 73, 'LUK.1.73', 'the oath He swore to our father Abraham, to grant us'),
('LUK', 1, 74, 'LUK.1.74', 'deliverance from hostile hands, that we may serve Him without fear,'),
('LUK', 1, 75, 'LUK.1.75', 'in holiness and righteousness before Him all the days of our lives.'),
('LUK', 1, 76, 'LUK.1.76', 'And you, child, will be called a prophet of the Most High; for you will go on before the Lord to prepare the way for Him,'),
('LUK', 1, 77, 'LUK.1.77', 'to give to His people the knowledge of salvation through the forgiveness of their sins,'),
('LUK', 1, 78, 'LUK.1.78', 'because of the tender mercy of our God, by which the Dawn will visit us from on high,'),
('LUK', 1, 79, 'LUK.1.79', 'to shine on those who live in darkness and in the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the path of peace.”'),
('LUK', 1, 80, 'LUK.1.80', 'And the child grew and became strong in spirit; and he lived in the wilderness until the time of his public appearance to Israel.'),
('LUK', 2, 1, 'LUK.2.1', 'Now in those days a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that a census should be taken of the whole empire.'),
('LUK', 2, 2, 'LUK.2.2', 'This was the first census to take place while Quirinius was governor of Syria.'),
('LUK', 2, 3, 'LUK.2.3', 'And everyone went to his own town to register.'),
('LUK', 2, 4, 'LUK.2.4', 'So Joseph also went up from Nazareth in Galilee to Judea, to the city of David called Bethlehem, since he was from the house and line of David.'),
('LUK', 2, 5, 'LUK.2.5', 'He went there to register with Mary, who was pledged to him in marriage and was expecting a child.'),
('LUK', 2, 6, 'LUK.2.6', 'While they were there, the time came for her Child to be born.'),
('LUK', 2, 7, 'LUK.2.7', 'And she gave birth to her firstborn, a Son. She wrapped Him in swaddling cloths and laid Him in a manger, because there was no room for them in the inn.'),
('LUK', 2, 8, 'LUK.2.8', 'And there were shepherds residing in the fields nearby, keeping watch over their flocks by night.'),
('LUK', 2, 9, 'LUK.2.9', 'Just then an angel of the Lord stood before them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them, and they were terrified.'),
('LUK', 2, 10, 'LUK.2.10', 'But the angel said to them, “Do not be afraid! For behold, I bring you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:'),
('LUK', 2, 11, 'LUK.2.11', 'Today in the city of David a Savior has been born to you. He is Christ the Lord!'),
('LUK', 2, 12, 'LUK.2.12', 'And this will be a sign to you: You will find a baby wrapped in swaddling cloths and lying in a manger.”'),
('LUK', 2, 13, 'LUK.2.13', 'And suddenly there appeared with the angel a great multitude of the heavenly host, praising God and saying:'),
('LUK', 2, 14, 'LUK.2.14', '“Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace to men on whom His favor rests!”'),
('LUK', 2, 15, 'LUK.2.15', 'When the angels had left them and gone into heaven, the shepherds said to one another, “Let us go to Bethlehem and see this thing that has happened, which the Lord has made known to us.”'),
('LUK', 2, 16, 'LUK.2.16', 'So they hurried off and found Mary and Joseph and the Baby, who was lying in the manger.'),
('LUK', 2, 17, 'LUK.2.17', 'After they had seen the Child, they spread the message they had received about Him.'),
('LUK', 2, 18, 'LUK.2.18', 'And all who heard it were amazed at what the shepherds said to them.'),
('LUK', 2, 19, 'LUK.2.19', 'But Mary treasured up all these things and pondered them in her heart.'),
('LUK', 2, 20, 'LUK.2.20', 'The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all they had heard and seen, which was just as the angel had told them.'),
('LUK', 2, 21, 'LUK.2.21', 'When the eight days before His circumcision had passed, He was named Jesus, the name the angel had given Him before He was conceived.'),
('LUK', 2, 22, 'LUK.2.22', 'And when the time of purification according to the Law of Moses was complete, His parents brought Him to Jerusalem to present Him to the Lord'),
('LUK', 2, 23, 'LUK.2.23', '(as it is written in the Law of the Lord: “Every firstborn male shall be consecrated to the Lord”),'),
('LUK', 2, 24, 'LUK.2.24', 'and to offer the sacrifice specified in the Law of the Lord: “A pair of turtledoves or two young pigeons.”'),
('LUK', 2, 25, 'LUK.2.25', 'Now there was a man in Jerusalem named Simeon, who was righteous and devout. He was waiting for the consolation of Israel, and the Holy Spirit was upon him.'),
('LUK', 2, 26, 'LUK.2.26', 'The Holy Spirit had revealed to him that he would not see death before he had seen the Lord’s Christ.'),
('LUK', 2, 27, 'LUK.2.27', 'Led by the Spirit, he went into the temple courts. And when the parents brought in the child Jesus to do for Him what was customary under the Law,'),
('LUK', 2, 28, 'LUK.2.28', 'Simeon took Him in his arms and blessed God, saying:'),
('LUK', 2, 29, 'LUK.2.29', '“Sovereign Lord, as You have promised, You now dismiss Your servant in peace.'),
('LUK', 2, 30, 'LUK.2.30', 'For my eyes have seen Your salvation,'),
('LUK', 2, 31, 'LUK.2.31', 'which You have prepared in the sight of all people,'),
('LUK', 2, 32, 'LUK.2.32', 'a light for revelation to the Gentiles, and for glory to Your people Israel.”'),
('LUK', 2, 33, 'LUK.2.33', 'The Child’s father and mother were amazed at what was spoken about Him.'),
('LUK', 2, 34, 'LUK.2.34', 'Then Simeon blessed them and said to His mother Mary: “Behold, this Child is appointed to cause the rise and fall of many in Israel, and to be a sign that will be spoken against,'),
('LUK', 2, 35, 'LUK.2.35', 'so that the thoughts of many hearts will be revealed—and a sword will pierce your soul as well.”'),
('LUK', 2, 36, 'LUK.2.36', 'There was also a prophetess named Anna, the daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Asher, who was well along in years. She had been married for seven years,'),
('LUK', 2, 37, 'LUK.2.37', 'and then was a widow to the age of eighty-four. She never left the temple, but worshiped night and day, fasting and praying.'),
('LUK', 2, 38, 'LUK.2.38', 'Coming forward at that moment, she gave thanks to God and spoke about the Child to all who were waiting for the redemption of Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 2, 39, 'LUK.2.39', 'When Jesus’ parents had done everything required by the Law of the Lord, they returned to Galilee, to their own town of Nazareth.'),
('LUK', 2, 40, 'LUK.2.40', 'And the Child grew and became strong. He was filled with wisdom, and the grace of God was upon Him.'),
('LUK', 2, 41, 'LUK.2.41', 'Every year His parents went to Jerusalem for the Feast of the Passover.'),
('LUK', 2, 42, 'LUK.2.42', 'And when He was twelve years old, they went up according to the custom of the Feast.'),
('LUK', 2, 43, 'LUK.2.43', 'When those days were over and they were returning home, the boy Jesus remained behind in Jerusalem, but His parents were unaware He had stayed.'),
('LUK', 2, 44, 'LUK.2.44', 'Assuming He was in their company, they traveled on for a day before they began to look for Him among their relatives and friends.'),
('LUK', 2, 45, 'LUK.2.45', 'When they could not find Him, they returned to Jerusalem to search for Him.'),
('LUK', 2, 46, 'LUK.2.46', 'Finally, after three days they found Him in the temple courts, sitting among the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions.'),
('LUK', 2, 47, 'LUK.2.47', 'And all who heard Him were astounded at His understanding and His answers.'),
('LUK', 2, 48, 'LUK.2.48', 'When His parents saw Him, they were astonished. “Child, why have You done this to us?” His mother asked. “Your father and I have been anxiously searching for You.”'),
('LUK', 2, 49, 'LUK.2.49', '“Why were you looking for Me?” He asked. “Did you not know that I had to be in My Father’s house?”'),
('LUK', 2, 50, 'LUK.2.50', 'But they did not understand the statement He was making to them.'),
('LUK', 2, 51, 'LUK.2.51', 'Then He went down to Nazareth with them and was obedient to them. But His mother treasured up all these things in her heart.'),
('LUK', 2, 52, 'LUK.2.52', 'And Jesus grew in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and man.'),
('LUK', 3, 1, 'LUK.3.1', 'In the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, while Pontius Pilate was governor of Judea, Herod tetrarch of Galilee, his brother Philip tetrarch of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias tetrarch of Abilene,'),
('LUK', 3, 2, 'LUK.3.2', 'during the high priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, the word of God came to John son of Zechariah in the wilderness.'),
('LUK', 3, 3, 'LUK.3.3', 'He went into all the region around the Jordan, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sins,'),
('LUK', 3, 4, 'LUK.3.4', 'as it is written in the book of the words of Isaiah the prophet: “A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.'),
('LUK', 3, 5, 'LUK.3.5', 'Every valley shall be filled in, and every mountain and hill made low. The crooked ways shall be made straight, and the rough ways smooth.'),
('LUK', 3, 6, 'LUK.3.6', 'And all humanity will see God’s salvation.’”'),
('LUK', 3, 7, 'LUK.3.7', 'Then John said to the crowds coming out to be baptized by him, “You brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the coming wrath?'),
('LUK', 3, 8, 'LUK.3.8', 'Produce fruit, then, in keeping with repentance. And do not begin to say to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham as our father.’ For I tell you that out of these stones God can raise up children for Abraham.'),
('LUK', 3, 9, 'LUK.3.9', 'The axe lies ready at the root of the trees, and every tree that does not produce good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.”'),
('LUK', 3, 10, 'LUK.3.10', 'The crowds asked him, “What then should we do?”'),
('LUK', 3, 11, 'LUK.3.11', 'John replied, “Whoever has two tunics should share with him who has none, and whoever has food should do the same.”'),
('LUK', 3, 12, 'LUK.3.12', 'Even tax collectors came to be baptized. “Teacher,” they asked, “what should we do?”'),
('LUK', 3, 13, 'LUK.3.13', '“Collect no more than you are authorized,” he answered.'),
('LUK', 3, 14, 'LUK.3.14', 'Then some soldiers asked him, “And what should we do?” “Do not take money by force or false accusation,” he said. “Be content with your wages.”'),
('LUK', 3, 15, 'LUK.3.15', 'The people were waiting expectantly and were all wondering in their hearts if John could be the Christ.'),
('LUK', 3, 16, 'LUK.3.16', 'John answered all of them: “I baptize you with water, but One more powerful than I will come, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.'),
('LUK', 3, 17, 'LUK.3.17', 'His winnowing fork is in His hand to clear His threshing floor and to gather the wheat into His barn; but He will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.”'),
('LUK', 3, 18, 'LUK.3.18', 'With these and many other exhortations, John proclaimed the good news to the people.'),
('LUK', 3, 19, 'LUK.3.19', 'But when he rebuked Herod the tetrarch regarding his brother’s wife Herodias and all the evils he had done,'),
('LUK', 3, 20, 'LUK.3.20', 'Herod added this to them all: He locked John up in prison.'),
('LUK', 3, 21, 'LUK.3.21', 'When all the people were being baptized, Jesus was baptized too. And as He was praying, heaven was opened,'),
('LUK', 3, 22, 'LUK.3.22', 'and the Holy Spirit descended on Him in a bodily form like a dove. And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”'),
('LUK', 3, 23, 'LUK.3.23', 'Jesus Himself was about thirty years old when He began His ministry. He was regarded as the son of Joseph, the son of Heli,'),
('LUK', 3, 24, 'LUK.3.24', 'the son of Matthat, the son of Levi, the son of Melchi, the son of Jannai, the son of Joseph,'),
('LUK', 3, 25, 'LUK.3.25', 'the son of Mattathias, the son of Amos, the son of Nahum, the son of Esli, the son of Naggai,'),
('LUK', 3, 26, 'LUK.3.26', 'the son of Maath, the son of Mattathias, the son of Semein, the son of Josech, the son of Joda,'),
('LUK', 3, 27, 'LUK.3.27', 'the son of Joanan, the son of Rhesa, the son of Zerubbabel, the son of Shealtiel, the son of Neri,'),
('LUK', 3, 28, 'LUK.3.28', 'the son of Melchi, the son of Addi, the son of Cosam, the son of Elmadam, the son of Er,'),
('LUK', 3, 29, 'LUK.3.29', 'the son of Joshua, the son of Eliezer, the son of Jorim, the son of Matthat, the son of Levi,'),
('LUK', 3, 30, 'LUK.3.30', 'the son of Simeon, the son of Judah, the son of Joseph, the son of Jonam, the son of Eliakim,'),
('LUK', 3, 31, 'LUK.3.31', 'the son of Melea, the son of Menna, the son of Mattatha, the son of Nathan, the son of David,'),
('LUK', 3, 32, 'LUK.3.32', 'the son of Jesse, the son of Obed, the son of Boaz, the son of Sala, the son of Nahshon,'),
('LUK', 3, 33, 'LUK.3.33', 'the son of Amminadab, the son of Admin, the son of Arni, the son of Hezron, the son of Perez, the son of Judah,'),
('LUK', 3, 34, 'LUK.3.34', 'the son of Jacob, the son of Isaac, the son of Abraham, the son of Terah, the son of Nahor,'),
('LUK', 3, 35, 'LUK.3.35', 'the son of Serug, the son of Reu, the son of Peleg, the son of Eber, the son of Shelah,'),
('LUK', 3, 36, 'LUK.3.36', 'the son of Cainan, the son of Arphaxad, the son of Shem, the son of Noah, the son of Lamech,'),
('LUK', 3, 37, 'LUK.3.37', 'the son of Methuselah, the son of Enoch, the son of Jared, the son of Mahalalel, the son of Cainan,'),
('LUK', 3, 38, 'LUK.3.38', 'the son of Enosh, the son of Seth, the son of Adam, the son of God.'),
('LUK', 4, 1, 'LUK.4.1', 'Then Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness,'),
('LUK', 4, 2, 'LUK.4.2', 'where for forty days He was tempted by the devil. He ate nothing during those days, and when they had ended, He was hungry.'),
('LUK', 4, 3, 'LUK.4.3', 'The devil said to Him, “If You are the Son of God, tell this stone to become bread.”'),
('LUK', 4, 4, 'LUK.4.4', 'But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone.’”'),
('LUK', 4, 5, 'LUK.4.5', 'Then the devil led Him up to a high place and showed Him in an instant all the kingdoms of the world.'),
('LUK', 4, 6, 'LUK.4.6', '“I will give You authority over all these kingdoms and all their glory,” he said. “For it has been relinquished to me, and I can give it to anyone I wish.'),
('LUK', 4, 7, 'LUK.4.7', 'So if You worship me, it will all be Yours.”'),
('LUK', 4, 8, 'LUK.4.8', 'But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.’”'),
('LUK', 4, 9, 'LUK.4.9', 'Then the devil led Him to Jerusalem and set Him on the pinnacle of the temple. “If You are the Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down from here.'),
('LUK', 4, 10, 'LUK.4.10', 'For it is written: ‘He will command His angels concerning You to guard You carefully,'),
('LUK', 4, 11, 'LUK.4.11', 'and they will lift You up in their hands, so that You will not strike Your foot against a stone.’”'),
('LUK', 4, 12, 'LUK.4.12', 'But Jesus answered, “It also says, ‘Do not put the Lord your God to the test.’”'),
('LUK', 4, 13, 'LUK.4.13', 'When the devil had finished every temptation, he left Him until an opportune time.'),
('LUK', 4, 14, 'LUK.4.14', 'Jesus returned to Galilee in the power of the Spirit, and the news about Him spread throughout the surrounding region.'),
('LUK', 4, 15, 'LUK.4.15', 'He taught in their synagogues and was glorified by everyone.'),
('LUK', 4, 16, 'LUK.4.16', 'Then Jesus came to Nazareth, where He had been brought up. As was His custom, He entered the synagogue on the Sabbath. And when He stood up to read,'),
('LUK', 4, 17, 'LUK.4.17', 'the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to Him. Unrolling it, He found the place where it was written:'),
('LUK', 4, 18, 'LUK.4.18', '“The Spirit of the Lord is on Me, because He has anointed Me to preach good news to the poor. He has sent Me to proclaim liberty to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to release the oppressed,'),
('LUK', 4, 19, 'LUK.4.19', 'to proclaim the year of the Lord’s favor.”'),
('LUK', 4, 20, 'LUK.4.20', 'Then He rolled up the scroll, returned it to the attendant, and sat down. The eyes of everyone in the synagogue were fixed on Him,'),
('LUK', 4, 21, 'LUK.4.21', 'and He began by saying, “Today this Scripture is fulfilled in your hearing.”'),
('LUK', 4, 22, 'LUK.4.22', 'All spoke well of Him and marveled at the gracious words that came from His lips. “Isn’t this the son of Joseph?” they asked.'),
('LUK', 4, 23, 'LUK.4.23', 'Jesus said to them, “Surely you will quote this proverb to Me: ‘Physician, heal yourself! Do here in Your hometown what we have heard that You did in Capernaum.’”'),
('LUK', 4, 24, 'LUK.4.24', 'Then He added, “Truly I tell you, no prophet is accepted in his hometown.'),
('LUK', 4, 25, 'LUK.4.25', 'But I tell you truthfully that there were many widows in Israel in the time of Elijah, when the sky was shut for three and a half years and great famine swept over all the land.'),
('LUK', 4, 26, 'LUK.4.26', 'Yet Elijah was not sent to any of them, but to the widow of Zarephath in Sidon.'),
('LUK', 4, 27, 'LUK.4.27', 'And there were many lepers in Israel in the time of Elisha the prophet. Yet not one of them was cleansed—only Naaman the Syrian.”'),
('LUK', 4, 28, 'LUK.4.28', 'On hearing this, all the people in the synagogue were enraged.'),
('LUK', 4, 29, 'LUK.4.29', 'They got up, drove Him out of the town, and led Him to the brow of the hill on which the town was built, in order to throw Him over the cliff.'),
('LUK', 4, 30, 'LUK.4.30', 'But Jesus passed through the crowd and went on His way.'),
('LUK', 4, 31, 'LUK.4.31', 'Then He went down to Capernaum, a town in Galilee, and on the Sabbath He began to teach the people.'),
('LUK', 4, 32, 'LUK.4.32', 'They were astonished at His teaching, because His message had authority.'),
('LUK', 4, 33, 'LUK.4.33', 'In the synagogue there was a man possessed by the spirit of an unclean demon. He cried out in a loud voice,'),
('LUK', 4, 34, 'LUK.4.34', '“Ha! What do You want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”'),
('LUK', 4, 35, 'LUK.4.35', 'But Jesus rebuked the demon. “Be silent!” He said. “Come out of him!” At this, the demon threw the man down before them all and came out without harming him.'),
('LUK', 4, 36, 'LUK.4.36', 'All the people were overcome with amazement and asked one another, “What is this message? With authority and power He commands the unclean spirits, and they come out!”'),
('LUK', 4, 37, 'LUK.4.37', 'And the news about Jesus spread throughout the surrounding region.'),
('LUK', 4, 38, 'LUK.4.38', 'After Jesus had left the synagogue, He went to the home of Simon, whose mother-in-law was suffering from a high fever. So they appealed to Jesus on her behalf,'),
('LUK', 4, 39, 'LUK.4.39', 'and He stood over her and rebuked the fever, and it left her. And she got up at once and began to serve them.'),
('LUK', 4, 40, 'LUK.4.40', 'At sunset, all who were ill with various diseases were brought to Jesus, and laying His hands on each one, He healed them.'),
('LUK', 4, 41, 'LUK.4.41', 'Demons also came out of many people, shouting, “You are the Son of God!” But He rebuked the demons and would not allow them to speak, because they knew He was the Christ.'),
('LUK', 4, 42, 'LUK.4.42', 'At daybreak, Jesus went out to a solitary place, and the crowds were looking for Him. They came to Him and tried to keep Him from leaving.'),
('LUK', 4, 43, 'LUK.4.43', 'But Jesus told them, “I must preach the good news of the kingdom of God to the other towns as well, because that is why I was sent.”'),
('LUK', 4, 44, 'LUK.4.44', 'And He continued to preach in the synagogues of Judea.'),
('LUK', 5, 1, 'LUK.5.1', 'On one occasion, while Jesus was standing by the Lake of Gennesaret with the crowd pressing in on Him to hear the word of God,'),
('LUK', 5, 2, 'LUK.5.2', 'He saw two boats at the edge of the lake. The fishermen had left them and were washing their nets.'),
('LUK', 5, 3, 'LUK.5.3', 'Jesus got into the boat belonging to Simon and asked him to put out a little from shore. And sitting down, He taught the people from the boat.'),
('LUK', 5, 4, 'LUK.5.4', 'When Jesus had finished speaking, He said to Simon, “Put out into deep water and let down your nets for a catch.”'),
('LUK', 5, 5, 'LUK.5.5', '“Master,” Simon replied, “we have worked hard all night without catching anything. But because You say so, I will let down the nets.”'),
('LUK', 5, 6, 'LUK.5.6', 'When they had done so, they caught such a large number of fish that their nets began to tear.'),
('LUK', 5, 7, 'LUK.5.7', 'So they signaled to their partners in the other boat to come and help them, and they came and filled both boats so full that they began to sink.'),
('LUK', 5, 8, 'LUK.5.8', 'When Simon Peter saw this, he fell at Jesus’ knees. “Go away from me, Lord,” he said, “for I am a sinful man.”'),
('LUK', 5, 9, 'LUK.5.9', 'For he and his companions were astonished at the catch of fish they had taken,'),
('LUK', 5, 10, 'LUK.5.10', 'and so were his partners James and John, the sons of Zebedee. “Do not be afraid,” Jesus said to Simon. “From now on you will catch men.”'),
('LUK', 5, 11, 'LUK.5.11', 'And when they had brought their boats ashore, they left everything and followed Him.'),
('LUK', 5, 12, 'LUK.5.12', 'While Jesus was in one of the towns, a man came along who was covered with leprosy. When he saw Jesus, he fell facedown and begged Him, “Lord, if You are willing, You can make me clean.”'),
('LUK', 5, 13, 'LUK.5.13', 'Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!” And immediately the leprosy left him.'),
('LUK', 5, 14, 'LUK.5.14', '“Do not tell anyone,” Jesus instructed him. “But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”'),
('LUK', 5, 15, 'LUK.5.15', 'But the news about Jesus spread all the more, and great crowds came to hear Him and to be healed of their sicknesses.'),
('LUK', 5, 16, 'LUK.5.16', 'Yet He frequently withdrew to the wilderness to pray.'),
('LUK', 5, 17, 'LUK.5.17', 'One day Jesus was teaching, and the Pharisees and teachers of the law were sitting there. People had come from Jerusalem and from every village of Galilee and Judea, and the power of the Lord was present for Him to heal the sick.'),
('LUK', 5, 18, 'LUK.5.18', 'Just then some men came carrying a paralyzed man on a mat. They tried to bring him inside to set him before Jesus,'),
('LUK', 5, 19, 'LUK.5.19', 'but they could not find a way through the crowd. So they went up on the roof and lowered him on his mat through the tiles into the middle of the crowd, right in front of Jesus.'),
('LUK', 5, 20, 'LUK.5.20', 'When Jesus saw their faith, He said, “Friend, your sins are forgiven.”'),
('LUK', 5, 21, 'LUK.5.21', 'But the scribes and Pharisees began thinking to themselves, “Who is this man who speaks blasphemy? Who can forgive sins but God alone?”'),
('LUK', 5, 22, 'LUK.5.22', 'Knowing what they were thinking, Jesus replied, “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?'),
('LUK', 5, 23, 'LUK.5.23', 'Which is easier: to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up and walk’?'),
('LUK', 5, 24, 'LUK.5.24', 'But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on the earth to forgive sins…” He said to the paralytic, “I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”'),
('LUK', 5, 25, 'LUK.5.25', 'And immediately the man stood up before them, took what he had been lying on, and went home glorifying God.'),
('LUK', 5, 26, 'LUK.5.26', 'Everyone was taken with amazement and glorified God. They were filled with awe and said, “We have seen remarkable things today.”'),
('LUK', 5, 27, 'LUK.5.27', 'After this, Jesus went out and saw a tax collector named Levi sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him,'),
('LUK', 5, 28, 'LUK.5.28', 'and Levi got up, left everything, and followed Him.'),
('LUK', 5, 29, 'LUK.5.29', 'Then Levi hosted a great banquet for Jesus at his house. A large crowd of tax collectors was there, along with others who were eating with them.'),
('LUK', 5, 30, 'LUK.5.30', 'But the Pharisees and their scribes complained to Jesus’ disciples, “Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and sinners?”'),
('LUK', 5, 31, 'LUK.5.31', 'Jesus answered, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick.'),
('LUK', 5, 32, 'LUK.5.32', 'I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners, to repentance.”'),
('LUK', 5, 33, 'LUK.5.33', 'Then they said to Him, “John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees frequently fast and pray, but Yours keep on eating and drinking.”'),
('LUK', 5, 34, 'LUK.5.34', 'Jesus replied, “Can you make the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them?'),
('LUK', 5, 35, 'LUK.5.35', 'But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.”'),
('LUK', 5, 36, 'LUK.5.36', 'He also told them a parable: “No one tears a piece of cloth from a new garment and sews it on an old one. If he does, he will tear the new garment as well, and the patch from the new will not match the old.'),
('LUK', 5, 37, 'LUK.5.37', 'And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the new wine will burst the skins, the wine will spill, and the wineskins will be ruined.'),
('LUK', 5, 38, 'LUK.5.38', 'Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.'),
('LUK', 5, 39, 'LUK.5.39', 'And no one after drinking old wine wants new, for he says, ‘The old is better.’”'),
('LUK', 6, 1, 'LUK.6.1', 'One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain, rub them in their hands, and eat them.'),
('LUK', 6, 2, 'LUK.6.2', 'But some of the Pharisees asked, “Why are you doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?”'),
('LUK', 6, 3, 'LUK.6.3', 'Jesus replied, “Have you not read what David did when he and his companions were hungry?'),
('LUK', 6, 4, 'LUK.6.4', 'He entered the house of God, took the consecrated bread and gave it to his companions, and ate what is lawful only for the priests to eat.”'),
('LUK', 6, 5, 'LUK.6.5', 'Then Jesus declared, “The Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.”'),
('LUK', 6, 6, 'LUK.6.6', 'On another Sabbath Jesus entered the synagogue and was teaching, and a man was there whose right hand was withered.'),
('LUK', 6, 7, 'LUK.6.7', 'Looking for a reason to accuse Jesus, the scribes and Pharisees were watching Him closely to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.'),
('LUK', 6, 8, 'LUK.6.8', 'But Jesus knew their thoughts and said to the man with the withered hand, “Get up and stand among us.” So he got up and stood there.'),
('LUK', 6, 9, 'LUK.6.9', 'Then Jesus said to them, “I ask you, which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?”'),
('LUK', 6, 10, 'LUK.6.10', 'And after looking around at all of them, He said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” He did so, and it was restored.'),
('LUK', 6, 11, 'LUK.6.11', 'But the scribes and Pharisees were filled with rage and began to discuss with one another what they might do to Jesus.'),
('LUK', 6, 12, 'LUK.6.12', 'In those days Jesus went out to the mountain to pray, and He spent the night in prayer to God.'),
('LUK', 6, 13, 'LUK.6.13', 'When daylight came, He called His disciples to Him and chose twelve of them, whom He also designated as apostles:'),
('LUK', 6, 14, 'LUK.6.14', 'Simon, whom He named Peter, and his brother Andrew; James and John; Philip and Bartholomew;'),
('LUK', 6, 15, 'LUK.6.15', 'Matthew and Thomas; James son of Alphaeus and Simon called the Zealot;'),
('LUK', 6, 16, 'LUK.6.16', 'Judas son of James, and Judas Iscariot, who became a traitor.'),
('LUK', 6, 17, 'LUK.6.17', 'Then Jesus came down with them and stood on a level place. A large crowd of His disciples was there, along with a great number of people from all over Judea, Jerusalem, and the seacoast of Tyre and Sidon.'),
('LUK', 6, 18, 'LUK.6.18', 'They had come to hear Him and to be healed of their diseases, and those troubled by unclean spirits were healed.'),
('LUK', 6, 19, 'LUK.6.19', 'The entire crowd was trying to touch Him, because power was coming from Him and healing them all.'),
('LUK', 6, 20, 'LUK.6.20', 'Looking up at His disciples, Jesus said: “Blessed are you who are poor, for yours is the kingdom of God.'),
('LUK', 6, 21, 'LUK.6.21', 'Blessed are you who hunger now, for you will be filled. Blessed are you who weep now, for you will laugh.'),
('LUK', 6, 22, 'LUK.6.22', 'Blessed are you when people hate you, and when they exclude you and insult you and reject your name as evil because of the Son of Man.'),
('LUK', 6, 23, 'LUK.6.23', 'Rejoice in that day and leap for joy, because great is your reward in heaven. For their fathers treated the prophets in the same way.'),
('LUK', 6, 24, 'LUK.6.24', 'But woe to you who are rich, for you have already received your comfort.'),
('LUK', 6, 25, 'LUK.6.25', 'Woe to you who are well fed now, for you will hunger. Woe to you who laugh now, for you will mourn and weep.'),
('LUK', 6, 26, 'LUK.6.26', 'Woe to you when all men speak well of you, for their fathers treated the false prophets in the same way.'),
('LUK', 6, 27, 'LUK.6.27', 'But to those of you who will listen, I say: Love your enemies, do good to those who hate you,'),
('LUK', 6, 28, 'LUK.6.28', 'bless those who curse you, pray for those who mistreat you.'),
('LUK', 6, 29, 'LUK.6.29', 'If someone strikes you on one cheek, turn to him the other also. And if someone takes your cloak, do not withhold your tunic as well.'),
('LUK', 6, 30, 'LUK.6.30', 'Give to everyone who asks you, and if anyone takes what is yours, do not demand it back.'),
('LUK', 6, 31, 'LUK.6.31', 'Do to others as you would have them do to you.'),
('LUK', 6, 32, 'LUK.6.32', 'If you love those who love you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners love those who love them.'),
('LUK', 6, 33, 'LUK.6.33', 'If you do good to those who do good to you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners do the same.'),
('LUK', 6, 34, 'LUK.6.34', 'And if you lend to those from whom you expect repayment, what credit is that to you? Even sinners lend to sinners, expecting to be repaid in full.'),
('LUK', 6, 35, 'LUK.6.35', 'But love your enemies, do good to them, and lend to them, expecting nothing in return. Then your reward will be great, and you will be sons of the Most High; for He is kind to the ungrateful and wicked.'),
('LUK', 6, 36, 'LUK.6.36', 'Be merciful, just as your Father is merciful.'),
('LUK', 6, 37, 'LUK.6.37', 'Do not judge, and you will not be judged. Do not condemn, and you will not be condemned. Forgive, and you will be forgiven.'),
('LUK', 6, 38, 'LUK.6.38', 'Give, and it will be given to you. A good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over will be poured into your lap. For with the measure you use, it will be measured back to you.”'),
('LUK', 6, 39, 'LUK.6.39', 'Jesus also told them a parable: “Can a blind man lead a blind man? Will they not both fall into a pit?'),
('LUK', 6, 40, 'LUK.6.40', 'A disciple is not above his teacher, but everyone who is fully trained will be like his teacher.'),
('LUK', 6, 41, 'LUK.6.41', 'Why do you look at the speck in your brother’s eye but fail to notice the beam in your own eye?'),
('LUK', 6, 42, 'LUK.6.42', 'How can you say, ‘Brother, let me take the speck out of your eye,’ while you yourself fail to see the beam in your own eye? You hypocrite! First take the beam out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother’s eye.'),
('LUK', 6, 43, 'LUK.6.43', 'No good tree bears bad fruit, nor does a bad tree bear good fruit.'),
('LUK', 6, 44, 'LUK.6.44', 'For each tree is known by its own fruit. Indeed, figs are not gathered from thornbushes, nor grapes from brambles.'),
('LUK', 6, 45, 'LUK.6.45', 'The good man brings good things out of the good treasure of his heart, and the evil man brings evil things out of the evil treasure of his heart. For out of the overflow of the heart the mouth speaks.'),
('LUK', 6, 46, 'LUK.6.46', 'Why do you call Me ‘Lord, Lord,’ but do not do what I say?'),
('LUK', 6, 47, 'LUK.6.47', 'I will show you what he is like who comes to Me and hears My words and acts on them:'),
('LUK', 6, 48, 'LUK.6.48', 'He is like a man building a house, who dug down deep and laid his foundation on the rock. When the flood came, the torrent crashed against that house but could not shake it, because it was well built.'),
('LUK', 6, 49, 'LUK.6.49', 'But the one who hears My words and does not act on them is like a man who built his house on ground without a foundation. The torrent crashed against that house, and immediately it fell—and great was its destruction!”'),
('LUK', 7, 1, 'LUK.7.1', 'When Jesus had concluded His discourse in the hearing of the people, He went to Capernaum.'),
('LUK', 7, 2, 'LUK.7.2', 'There a highly valued servant of a centurion was sick and about to die.'),
('LUK', 7, 3, 'LUK.7.3', 'When the centurion heard about Jesus, he sent some Jewish elders to ask Him to come and heal his servant.'),
('LUK', 7, 4, 'LUK.7.4', 'They came to Jesus and pleaded with Him earnestly, “This man is worthy to have You grant this,'),
('LUK', 7, 5, 'LUK.7.5', 'for he loves our nation and has built our synagogue.”'),
('LUK', 7, 6, 'LUK.7.6', 'So Jesus went with them. But when He was not far from the house, the centurion sent friends with the message: “Lord, do not trouble Yourself, for I am not worthy to have You come under my roof.'),
('LUK', 7, 7, 'LUK.7.7', 'That is why I did not consider myself worthy to come to You. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.'),
('LUK', 7, 8, 'LUK.7.8', 'For I myself am a man under authority, with soldiers under me. I tell one to go, and he goes, and another to come, and he comes. I tell my servant to do something, and he does it.”'),
('LUK', 7, 9, 'LUK.7.9', 'When Jesus heard this, He marveled at the centurion. Turning to the crowd following Him, He said, “I tell you, not even in Israel have I found such great faith.”'),
('LUK', 7, 10, 'LUK.7.10', 'And when the messengers returned to the house, they found the servant in good health.'),
('LUK', 7, 11, 'LUK.7.11', 'Soon afterward, Jesus went to a town called Nain. His disciples went with Him, accompanied by a large crowd.'),
('LUK', 7, 12, 'LUK.7.12', 'As He approached the town gate, He saw a dead man being carried out, the only son of his mother, and she was a widow. And a large crowd from the town was with her.'),
('LUK', 7, 13, 'LUK.7.13', 'When the Lord saw her, He had compassion on her and said, “Do not weep.”'),
('LUK', 7, 14, 'LUK.7.14', 'Then He went up and touched the coffin, and those carrying it stood still. “Young man,” He said, “I tell you, get up!”'),
('LUK', 7, 15, 'LUK.7.15', 'And the dead man sat up and began to speak! Then Jesus gave him back to his mother.'),
('LUK', 7, 16, 'LUK.7.16', 'A sense of awe swept over all of them, and they glorified God. “A great prophet has appeared among us!” they said. “God has visited His people!”'),
('LUK', 7, 17, 'LUK.7.17', 'And the news about Jesus spread throughout Judea and all the surrounding region.'),
('LUK', 7, 18, 'LUK.7.18', 'Then John’s disciples informed him about all these things.'),
('LUK', 7, 19, 'LUK.7.19', 'So John called two of his disciples and sent them to ask the Lord, “Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?”'),
('LUK', 7, 20, 'LUK.7.20', 'When the men came to Jesus, they said, “John the Baptist sent us to ask, ‘Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?’”'),
('LUK', 7, 21, 'LUK.7.21', 'At that very hour Jesus healed many people of their diseases, afflictions, and evil spirits, and He gave sight to many who were blind.'),
('LUK', 7, 22, 'LUK.7.22', 'So He replied, “Go back and report to John what you have seen and heard: The blind receive sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, and the good news is preached to the poor.'),
('LUK', 7, 23, 'LUK.7.23', 'Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of Me.”'),
('LUK', 7, 24, 'LUK.7.24', 'After John’s messengers had left, Jesus began to speak to the crowds about John: “What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed swaying in the wind?'),
('LUK', 7, 25, 'LUK.7.25', 'Otherwise, what did you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? Look, those who wear elegant clothing and live in luxury are found in palaces.'),
('LUK', 7, 26, 'LUK.7.26', 'What then did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.'),
('LUK', 7, 27, 'LUK.7.27', 'This is the one about whom it is written: ‘Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way before You.’'),
('LUK', 7, 28, 'LUK.7.28', 'I tell you, among those born of women there is no one greater than John, yet even the least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.”'),
('LUK', 7, 29, 'LUK.7.29', 'All the people who heard this, even the tax collectors, acknowledged God’s justice. For they had received the baptism of John.'),
('LUK', 7, 30, 'LUK.7.30', 'But the Pharisees and experts in the law rejected God’s purpose for themselves, because they had not been baptized by John.'),
('LUK', 7, 31, 'LUK.7.31', '“To what, then, can I compare the men of this generation? What are they like?'),
('LUK', 7, 32, 'LUK.7.32', 'They are like children sitting in the marketplace and calling out to one another: ‘We played the flute for you, and you did not dance; we sang a dirge, and you did not weep.’'),
('LUK', 7, 33, 'LUK.7.33', 'For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine, and you say, ‘He has a demon!’'),
('LUK', 7, 34, 'LUK.7.34', 'The Son of Man came eating and drinking, and you say, ‘Look at this glutton and drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!’'),
('LUK', 7, 35, 'LUK.7.35', 'But wisdom is vindicated by all her children.”'),
('LUK', 7, 36, 'LUK.7.36', 'Then one of the Pharisees invited Jesus to eat with him, and He entered the Pharisee’s house and reclined at the table.'),
('LUK', 7, 37, 'LUK.7.37', 'When a sinful woman from that town learned that Jesus was dining there, she brought an alabaster jar of perfume.'),
('LUK', 7, 38, 'LUK.7.38', 'As she stood behind Him at His feet weeping, she began to wet His feet with her tears and wipe them with her hair. Then she kissed His feet and anointed them with the perfume.'),
('LUK', 7, 39, 'LUK.7.39', 'When the Pharisee who had invited Jesus saw this, he said to himself, “If this man were a prophet, He would know who this is and what kind of woman is touching Him—for she is a sinner!”'),
('LUK', 7, 40, 'LUK.7.40', 'But Jesus answered him, “Simon, I have something to tell you.” “Tell me, Teacher,” he said.'),
('LUK', 7, 41, 'LUK.7.41', '“Two men were debtors to a certain moneylender. One owed him five hundred denarii, and the other fifty.'),
('LUK', 7, 42, 'LUK.7.42', 'When they were unable to repay him, he forgave both of them. Which one, then, will love him more?”'),
('LUK', 7, 43, 'LUK.7.43', '“I suppose the one who was forgiven more,” Simon replied. “You have judged correctly,” Jesus said.'),
('LUK', 7, 44, 'LUK.7.44', 'And turning toward the woman, He said to Simon, “Do you see this woman? When I entered your house, you did not give Me water for My feet, but she wet My feet with her tears and wiped them with her hair.'),
('LUK', 7, 45, 'LUK.7.45', 'You did not greet Me with a kiss, but she has not stopped kissing My feet since I arrived.'),
('LUK', 7, 46, 'LUK.7.46', 'You did not anoint My head with oil, but she has anointed My feet with perfume.'),
('LUK', 7, 47, 'LUK.7.47', 'Therefore I tell you, her many sins have been forgiven, for she has loved much. But he who has been forgiven little loves little.”'),
('LUK', 7, 48, 'LUK.7.48', 'Then Jesus said to her, “Your sins are forgiven.”'),
('LUK', 7, 49, 'LUK.7.49', 'But those at the table began to say to themselves, “Who is this who even forgives sins?”'),
('LUK', 7, 50, 'LUK.7.50', 'And Jesus told the woman, “Your faith has saved you; go in peace.”'),
('LUK', 8, 1, 'LUK.8.1', 'Soon afterward, Jesus traveled from one town and village to another, preaching and proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God. The Twelve were with Him,'),
('LUK', 8, 2, 'LUK.8.2', 'as well as some women who had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities: Mary called Magdalene, from whom seven demons had gone out,'),
('LUK', 8, 3, 'LUK.8.3', 'Joanna the wife of Herod’s household manager Chuza, Susanna, and many others. These women were ministering to them out of their own means.'),
('LUK', 8, 4, 'LUK.8.4', 'While a large crowd was gathering and people were coming to Jesus from town after town, He told them this parable:'),
('LUK', 8, 5, 'LUK.8.5', '“A farmer went out to sow his seed. And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, where it was trampled, and the birds of the air devoured it.'),
('LUK', 8, 6, 'LUK.8.6', 'Some fell on rocky ground, and when it came up, the seedlings withered because they had no moisture.'),
('LUK', 8, 7, 'LUK.8.7', 'Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up with it and choked the seedlings.'),
('LUK', 8, 8, 'LUK.8.8', 'Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprang up and produced a crop—a hundredfold.” As Jesus said this, He called out, “He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”'),
('LUK', 8, 9, 'LUK.8.9', 'Then His disciples asked Him what this parable meant.'),
('LUK', 8, 10, 'LUK.8.10', 'He replied, “The knowledge of the mysteries of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to others I speak in parables, so that, ‘though seeing, they may not see; though hearing, they may not understand.’'),
('LUK', 8, 11, 'LUK.8.11', 'Now this is the meaning of the parable: The seed is the word of God.'),
('LUK', 8, 12, 'LUK.8.12', 'The seeds along the path are those who hear, but the devil comes and takes away the word from their hearts, so that they may not believe and be saved.'),
('LUK', 8, 13, 'LUK.8.13', 'The seeds on rocky ground are those who hear the word and receive it with joy, but they have no root. They believe for a season, but in the time of testing, they fall away.'),
('LUK', 8, 14, 'LUK.8.14', 'The seeds that fell among the thorns are those who hear, but as they go on their way, they are choked by the worries, riches, and pleasures of this life, and their fruit does not mature.'),
('LUK', 8, 15, 'LUK.8.15', 'But the seeds on good soil are those with a noble and good heart, who hear the word, cling to it, and by persevering produce a crop.'),
('LUK', 8, 16, 'LUK.8.16', 'No one lights a lamp and covers it with a jar or puts it under a bed. Instead, he sets it on a stand, so those who enter can see the light.'),
('LUK', 8, 17, 'LUK.8.17', 'For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, and nothing concealed that will not be made known and brought to light.'),
('LUK', 8, 18, 'LUK.8.18', 'Pay attention, therefore, to how you listen. Whoever has will be given more, but whoever does not have, even what he thinks he has will be taken away from him.”'),
('LUK', 8, 19, 'LUK.8.19', 'Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came to see Him, but they were unable to reach Him because of the crowd.'),
('LUK', 8, 20, 'LUK.8.20', 'He was told, “Your mother and brothers are standing outside, wanting to see You.”'),
('LUK', 8, 21, 'LUK.8.21', 'But He replied, “My mother and brothers are those who hear the word of God and carry it out.”'),
('LUK', 8, 22, 'LUK.8.22', 'One day Jesus said to His disciples, “Let us cross to the other side of the lake.” So He got into a boat with them and set out.'),
('LUK', 8, 23, 'LUK.8.23', 'As they sailed, He fell asleep, and a windstorm came down on the lake, so that the boat was being swamped, and they were in great danger.'),
('LUK', 8, 24, 'LUK.8.24', 'The disciples went and woke Him, saying, “Master, Master, we are perishing!” Then Jesus got up and rebuked the wind and the raging waters, and they subsided, and all was calm.'),
('LUK', 8, 25, 'LUK.8.25', '“Where is your faith?” He asked. Frightened and amazed, they asked one another, “Who is this? He commands even the winds and the water, and they obey Him!”'),
('LUK', 8, 26, 'LUK.8.26', 'Then they sailed to the region of the Gerasenes, across the lake from Galilee.'),
('LUK', 8, 27, 'LUK.8.27', 'When Jesus stepped ashore, He was met by a demon-possessed man from the town. For a long time this man had not worn clothing or lived in a house, but he stayed in the tombs.'),
('LUK', 8, 28, 'LUK.8.28', 'When the man saw Jesus, he cried out and fell down before Him, shouting in a loud voice, “What do You want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You not to torture me!”'),
('LUK', 8, 29, 'LUK.8.29', 'For Jesus had commanded the unclean spirit to come out of the man. Many times it had seized him, and though he was bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains and been driven by the demon into solitary places.'),
('LUK', 8, 30, 'LUK.8.30', '“What is your name?” Jesus asked. “Legion,” he replied, because many demons had gone into him.'),
('LUK', 8, 31, 'LUK.8.31', 'And the demons kept begging Jesus not to order them to go into the Abyss.'),
('LUK', 8, 32, 'LUK.8.32', 'There on the hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding. So the demons begged Jesus to let them enter the pigs, and He gave them permission.'),
('LUK', 8, 33, 'LUK.8.33', 'Then the demons came out of the man and went into the pigs, and the herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and was drowned.'),
('LUK', 8, 34, 'LUK.8.34', 'When those tending the pigs saw what had happened, they ran off and reported this in the town and countryside.'),
('LUK', 8, 35, 'LUK.8.35', 'So the people went out to see what had happened. They came to Jesus and found the man whom the demons had left, sitting at Jesus’ feet, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid.'),
('LUK', 8, 36, 'LUK.8.36', 'Meanwhile, those who had seen it reported how the demon-possessed man had been healed.'),
('LUK', 8, 37, 'LUK.8.37', 'Then all the people of the region of the Gerasenes asked Jesus to depart from them, because great fear had taken hold of them. So He got into the boat and started back.'),
('LUK', 8, 38, 'LUK.8.38', 'The man whom the demons had left begged to go with Jesus. But He sent him away, saying,'),
('LUK', 8, 39, 'LUK.8.39', '“Return home and describe how much God has done for you.” So the man went away and proclaimed all over the town how much Jesus had done for him.'),
('LUK', 8, 40, 'LUK.8.40', 'When Jesus returned, the crowd welcomed Him, for they had all been waiting for Him.'),
('LUK', 8, 41, 'LUK.8.41', 'Just then a synagogue leader named Jairus came and fell at Jesus’ feet. He begged Him to come to his house,'),
('LUK', 8, 42, 'LUK.8.42', 'because his only daughter, who was about twelve, was dying. As Jesus went with him, the crowds pressed around Him,'),
('LUK', 8, 43, 'LUK.8.43', 'including a woman who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years. She had spent all her money on physicians, but no one was able to heal her.'),
('LUK', 8, 44, 'LUK.8.44', 'She came up behind Jesus and touched the fringe of His cloak, and immediately her bleeding stopped.'),
('LUK', 8, 45, 'LUK.8.45', '“Who touched Me?” Jesus asked. But they all denied it. “Master,” said Peter, “the people are crowding and pressing against You.”'),
('LUK', 8, 46, 'LUK.8.46', 'But Jesus declared, “Someone touched Me, for I know that power has gone out from Me.”'),
('LUK', 8, 47, 'LUK.8.47', 'Then the woman, seeing that she could not escape notice, came trembling and fell down before Him. In the presence of all the people, she explained why she had touched Him and how she had immediately been healed.'),
('LUK', 8, 48, 'LUK.8.48', '“Daughter,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you. Go in peace.”'),
('LUK', 8, 49, 'LUK.8.49', 'While He was still speaking, someone arrived from the house of the synagogue leader. “Your daughter is dead,” he told Jairus. “Do not bother the Teacher anymore.”'),
('LUK', 8, 50, 'LUK.8.50', 'But Jesus overheard them and said to Jairus, “Do not be afraid; just believe, and she will be healed.”'),
('LUK', 8, 51, 'LUK.8.51', 'When He entered the house, He did not allow anyone to go in with Him except Peter, John, James, and the child’s father and mother.'),
('LUK', 8, 52, 'LUK.8.52', 'Meanwhile, everyone was weeping and mourning for her. But Jesus said, “Stop weeping; she is not dead but asleep.”'),
('LUK', 8, 53, 'LUK.8.53', 'And they laughed at Him, knowing that she was dead.'),
('LUK', 8, 54, 'LUK.8.54', 'But Jesus took her by the hand and called out, “Child, get up!”'),
('LUK', 8, 55, 'LUK.8.55', 'Her spirit returned, and at once she got up. And He directed that she be given something to eat.'),
('LUK', 8, 56, 'LUK.8.56', 'Her parents were astounded, but Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone what had happened.'),
('LUK', 9, 1, 'LUK.9.1', 'Then Jesus called the Twelve together and gave them power and authority over all demons, and power to cure diseases.'),
('LUK', 9, 2, 'LUK.9.2', 'And He sent them out to proclaim the kingdom of God and to heal the sick.'),
('LUK', 9, 3, 'LUK.9.3', '“Take nothing for the journey,” He told them, “no staff, no bag, no bread, no money, no second tunic.'),
('LUK', 9, 4, 'LUK.9.4', 'Whatever house you enter, stay there until you leave that area.'),
('LUK', 9, 5, 'LUK.9.5', 'If anyone does not welcome you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that town, as a testimony against them.”'),
('LUK', 9, 6, 'LUK.9.6', 'So they set out and went from village to village, preaching the gospel and healing people everywhere.'),
('LUK', 9, 7, 'LUK.9.7', 'When Herod the tetrarch heard about all that was happening, he was perplexed. For some were saying that John had risen from the dead,'),
('LUK', 9, 8, 'LUK.9.8', 'others that Elijah had appeared, and still others that a prophet of old had arisen.'),
('LUK', 9, 9, 'LUK.9.9', '“I beheaded John,” Herod said, “but who is this man I hear such things about?” And he kept trying to see Jesus.'),
('LUK', 9, 10, 'LUK.9.10', 'Then the apostles returned and reported to Jesus all that they had done. Taking them away privately, He withdrew to a town called Bethsaida.'),
('LUK', 9, 11, 'LUK.9.11', 'But the crowds found out and followed Him. He welcomed them and spoke to them about the kingdom of God, and He healed those who needed healing.'),
('LUK', 9, 12, 'LUK.9.12', 'As the day neared its end, the Twelve came to Jesus and said, “Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding villages and countryside for lodging and provisions. For we are in a desolate place here.”'),
('LUK', 9, 13, 'LUK.9.13', 'But Jesus told them, “You give them something to eat.” “We have only five loaves of bread and two fish,” they answered, “unless we go and buy food for all these people.”'),
('LUK', 9, 14, 'LUK.9.14', '(There were about five thousand men.) He told His disciples, “Have them sit down in groups of about fifty each.”'),
('LUK', 9, 15, 'LUK.9.15', 'They did so, and everyone was seated.'),
('LUK', 9, 16, 'LUK.9.16', 'Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing and broke them. Then He gave them to the disciples to set before the people.'),
('LUK', 9, 17, 'LUK.9.17', 'They all ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.'),
('LUK', 9, 18, 'LUK.9.18', 'One day as Jesus was praying in private and the disciples were with Him, He questioned them: “Who do the crowds say I am?”'),
('LUK', 9, 19, 'LUK.9.19', 'They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, that a prophet of old has arisen.”'),
('LUK', 9, 20, 'LUK.9.20', '“But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?” Peter answered, “The Christ of God.”'),
('LUK', 9, 21, 'LUK.9.21', 'Jesus strictly warned them not to tell this to anyone.'),
('LUK', 9, 22, 'LUK.9.22', '“The Son of Man must suffer many things,” He said. “He must be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and He must be killed and on the third day be raised to life.”'),
('LUK', 9, 23, 'LUK.9.23', 'Then Jesus said to all of them, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow Me.'),
('LUK', 9, 24, 'LUK.9.24', 'For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake will save it.'),
('LUK', 9, 25, 'LUK.9.25', 'What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet lose or forfeit his very self?'),
('LUK', 9, 26, 'LUK.9.26', 'If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words, the Son of Man will be ashamed of him when He comes in His glory and in the glory of the Father and of the holy angels.'),
('LUK', 9, 27, 'LUK.9.27', 'But I tell you truly, some who are standing here will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 9, 28, 'LUK.9.28', 'About eight days after Jesus had said these things, He took with Him Peter, John, and James, and went up on a mountain to pray.'),
('LUK', 9, 29, 'LUK.9.29', 'And as He was praying, the appearance of His face changed, and His clothes became radiantly white.'),
('LUK', 9, 30, 'LUK.9.30', 'Suddenly two men, Moses and Elijah, began talking with Jesus.'),
('LUK', 9, 31, 'LUK.9.31', 'They appeared in glory and spoke about His departure, which He was about to accomplish at Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 9, 32, 'LUK.9.32', 'Meanwhile Peter and his companions were overcome by sleep, but when they awoke, they saw Jesus’ glory and the two men standing with Him.'),
('LUK', 9, 33, 'LUK.9.33', 'As Moses and Elijah were leaving, Peter said to Jesus, “Master, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters—one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.” (He did not know what he was saying.)'),
('LUK', 9, 34, 'LUK.9.34', 'While Peter was speaking, a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and they were afraid as they entered the cloud.'),
('LUK', 9, 35, 'LUK.9.35', 'And a voice came from the cloud, saying, “This is My Son, whom I have chosen. Listen to Him!”'),
('LUK', 9, 36, 'LUK.9.36', 'After the voice had spoken, only Jesus was present with them. The disciples kept this to themselves, and in those days they did not tell anyone what they had seen.'),
('LUK', 9, 37, 'LUK.9.37', 'The next day, when they came down from the mountain, Jesus was met by a large crowd.'),
('LUK', 9, 38, 'LUK.9.38', 'Suddenly a man in the crowd cried out, “Teacher, I beg You to look at my son, for he is my only child.'),
('LUK', 9, 39, 'LUK.9.39', 'A spirit keeps seizing him, and he screams abruptly. It throws him into convulsions so that he foams at the mouth. It keeps mauling him and rarely departs from him.'),
('LUK', 9, 40, 'LUK.9.40', 'I begged Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”'),
('LUK', 9, 41, 'LUK.9.41', '“O unbelieving and perverse generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you and put up with you? Bring your son here.”'),
('LUK', 9, 42, 'LUK.9.42', 'Even while the boy was approaching, the demon slammed him to the ground in a convulsion. But Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, healed the boy, and gave him back to his father.'),
('LUK', 9, 43, 'LUK.9.43', 'And they were all astonished at the greatness of God. While everyone was marveling at all that Jesus was doing, He said to His disciples,'),
('LUK', 9, 44, 'LUK.9.44', '“Let these words sink into your ears: The Son of Man is about to be delivered into the hands of men.”'),
('LUK', 9, 45, 'LUK.9.45', 'But they did not understand this statement. It was veiled from them so that they could not comprehend it, and they were afraid to ask Him about it.'),
('LUK', 9, 46, 'LUK.9.46', 'Then an argument started among the disciples as to which of them would be the greatest.'),
('LUK', 9, 47, 'LUK.9.47', 'But Jesus, knowing the thoughts of their hearts, had a little child stand beside Him.'),
('LUK', 9, 48, 'LUK.9.48', 'And He said to them, “Whoever welcomes this little child in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes the One who sent Me. For whoever is the least among all of you, he is the greatest.”'),
('LUK', 9, 49, 'LUK.9.49', '“Master,” said John, “we saw someone driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”'),
('LUK', 9, 50, 'LUK.9.50', '“Do not stop him,” Jesus replied, “for whoever is not against you is for you.”'),
('LUK', 9, 51, 'LUK.9.51', 'As the day of His ascension approached, Jesus resolutely set out for Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 9, 52, 'LUK.9.52', 'He sent messengers on ahead, who went into a village of the Samaritans to make arrangements for Him.'),
('LUK', 9, 53, 'LUK.9.53', 'But the people there refused to welcome Him, because He was heading for Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 9, 54, 'LUK.9.54', 'When the disciples James and John saw this, they asked, “Lord, do You want us to call down fire from heaven to consume them?”'),
('LUK', 9, 55, 'LUK.9.55', 'But Jesus turned and rebuked them.'),
('LUK', 9, 56, 'LUK.9.56', 'And He and His disciples went on to another village.'),
('LUK', 9, 57, 'LUK.9.57', 'As they were walking along the road, someone said to Jesus, “I will follow You wherever You go.”'),
('LUK', 9, 58, 'LUK.9.58', 'Jesus replied, “Foxes have dens and birds of the air have nests, but the Son of Man has no place to lay His head.”'),
('LUK', 9, 59, 'LUK.9.59', 'Then He said to another man, “Follow Me.” The man replied, “Lord, first let me go and bury my father.”'),
('LUK', 9, 60, 'LUK.9.60', 'But Jesus told him, “Let the dead bury their own dead. You, however, go and proclaim the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 9, 61, 'LUK.9.61', 'Still another said, “I will follow You, Lord; but first let me bid farewell to my family.”'),
('LUK', 9, 62, 'LUK.9.62', 'Then Jesus declared, “No one who puts his hand to the plow and then looks back is fit for the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 10, 1, 'LUK.10.1', 'After this, the Lord appointed seventy-two others and sent them two by two ahead of Him to every town and place He was about to visit.'),
('LUK', 10, 2, 'LUK.10.2', 'And He told them, “The harvest is plentiful, but the workers are few. Ask the Lord of the harvest, therefore, to send out workers into His harvest.'),
('LUK', 10, 3, 'LUK.10.3', 'Go! I am sending you out like lambs among wolves.'),
('LUK', 10, 4, 'LUK.10.4', 'Carry no purse or bag or sandals. Do not greet anyone along the road.'),
('LUK', 10, 5, 'LUK.10.5', 'Whatever house you enter, begin by saying, ‘Peace to this house.’'),
('LUK', 10, 6, 'LUK.10.6', 'If a man of peace is there, your peace will rest on him; if not, it will return to you.'),
('LUK', 10, 7, 'LUK.10.7', 'Stay at the same house, eating and drinking whatever you are offered. For the worker is worthy of his wages. Do not move around from house to house.'),
('LUK', 10, 8, 'LUK.10.8', 'If you enter a town and they welcome you, eat whatever is set before you.'),
('LUK', 10, 9, 'LUK.10.9', 'Heal the sick who are there and tell them, ‘The kingdom of God is near you.’'),
('LUK', 10, 10, 'LUK.10.10', 'But if you enter a town and they do not welcome you, go into the streets and declare,'),
('LUK', 10, 11, 'LUK.10.11', '‘Even the dust of your town that clings to our feet, we wipe off as a testimony against you. Yet be sure of this: The kingdom of God is near.’'),
('LUK', 10, 12, 'LUK.10.12', 'I tell you, it will be more bearable on that day for Sodom than for that town.'),
('LUK', 10, 13, 'LUK.10.13', 'Woe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes.'),
('LUK', 10, 14, 'LUK.10.14', 'But it will be more bearable for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment than for you.'),
('LUK', 10, 15, 'LUK.10.15', 'And you, Capernaum, will you be lifted up to heaven? No, you will be brought down to Hades!'),
('LUK', 10, 16, 'LUK.10.16', 'Whoever listens to you listens to Me; whoever rejects you rejects Me; and whoever rejects Me rejects the One who sent Me.”'),
('LUK', 10, 17, 'LUK.10.17', 'The seventy-two returned with joy and said, “Lord, even the demons submit to us in Your name.”'),
('LUK', 10, 18, 'LUK.10.18', 'So He told them, “I saw Satan fall like lightning from heaven.'),
('LUK', 10, 19, 'LUK.10.19', 'Behold, I have given you authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will harm you.'),
('LUK', 10, 20, 'LUK.10.20', 'Nevertheless, do not rejoice that the spirits submit to you, but rejoice that your names are written in heaven.”'),
('LUK', 10, 21, 'LUK.10.21', 'At that time Jesus rejoiced in the Holy Spirit and declared, “I praise You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because You have hidden these things from the wise and learned, and revealed them to little children. Yes, Father, for this was well-pleasing in Your sight.'),
('LUK', 10, 22, 'LUK.10.22', 'All things have been entrusted to Me by My Father. No one knows who the Son is except the Father, and no one knows who the Father is except the Son and those to whom the Son chooses to reveal Him.”'),
('LUK', 10, 23, 'LUK.10.23', 'Then Jesus turned to the disciples and said privately, “Blessed are the eyes that see what you see.'),
('LUK', 10, 24, 'LUK.10.24', 'For I tell you that many prophets and kings desired to see what you see but did not see it, and to hear what you hear but did not hear it.”'),
('LUK', 10, 25, 'LUK.10.25', 'One day an expert in the law stood up to test Him. “Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”'),
('LUK', 10, 26, 'LUK.10.26', '“What is written in the Law?” Jesus replied. “How do you read it?”'),
('LUK', 10, 27, 'LUK.10.27', 'He answered, “‘Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your strength and with all your mind’ and ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’”'),
('LUK', 10, 28, 'LUK.10.28', '“You have answered correctly,” Jesus said. “Do this and you will live.”'),
('LUK', 10, 29, 'LUK.10.29', 'But wanting to justify himself, he asked Jesus, “And who is my neighbor?”'),
('LUK', 10, 30, 'LUK.10.30', 'Jesus took up this question and said, “A man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho when he fell into the hands of robbers. They stripped him, beat him, and went away, leaving him half dead.'),
('LUK', 10, 31, 'LUK.10.31', 'Now by chance a priest was going down the same road, but when he saw him, he passed by on the other side.'),
('LUK', 10, 32, 'LUK.10.32', 'So too, when a Levite came to that spot and saw him, he passed by on the other side.'),
('LUK', 10, 33, 'LUK.10.33', 'But a Samaritan on a journey came upon him, and when he saw him, he had compassion.'),
('LUK', 10, 34, 'LUK.10.34', 'He went to him and bandaged his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. Then he put him on his own animal, brought him to an inn, and took care of him.'),
('LUK', 10, 35, 'LUK.10.35', 'The next day he took out two denarii and gave them to the innkeeper. ‘Take care of him,’ he said, ‘and on my return I will repay you for any additional expense.’'),
('LUK', 10, 36, 'LUK.10.36', 'Which of these three do you think was a neighbor to the man who fell into the hands of robbers?”'),
('LUK', 10, 37, 'LUK.10.37', '“The one who showed him mercy,” replied the expert in the law. Then Jesus told him, “Go and do likewise.”'),
('LUK', 10, 38, 'LUK.10.38', 'As they traveled along, Jesus entered a village where a woman named Martha welcomed Him into her home.'),
('LUK', 10, 39, 'LUK.10.39', 'She had a sister named Mary, who sat at the Lord’s feet listening to His message.'),
('LUK', 10, 40, 'LUK.10.40', 'But Martha was distracted by all the preparations to be made. She came to Jesus and said, “Lord, do You not care that my sister has left me to serve alone? Tell her to help me!”'),
('LUK', 10, 41, 'LUK.10.41', '“Martha, Martha,” the Lord replied, “you are worried and upset about many things.'),
('LUK', 10, 42, 'LUK.10.42', 'But only one thing is necessary. Mary has chosen the good portion, and it will not be taken away from her.”'),
('LUK', 11, 1, 'LUK.11.1', 'One day in a place where Jesus had just finished praying, one of His disciples requested, “Lord, teach us to pray, just as John taught his disciples.”'),
('LUK', 11, 2, 'LUK.11.2', 'So Jesus told them, “When you pray, say: ‘Father, hallowed be Your name. Your kingdom come.'),
('LUK', 11, 3, 'LUK.11.3', 'Give us each day our daily bread.'),
('LUK', 11, 4, 'LUK.11.4', 'And forgive us our sins, for we also forgive everyone who sins against us. And lead us not into temptation.’”'),
('LUK', 11, 5, 'LUK.11.5', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Suppose one of you goes to his friend at midnight and says, ‘Friend, lend me three loaves of bread,'),
('LUK', 11, 6, 'LUK.11.6', 'because a friend of mine has come to me on a journey, and I have nothing to set before him.’'),
('LUK', 11, 7, 'LUK.11.7', 'And suppose the one inside answers, ‘Do not bother me. My door is already shut, and my children and I are in bed. I cannot get up to give you anything.’'),
('LUK', 11, 8, 'LUK.11.8', 'I tell you, even though he will not get up to provide for him because of his friendship, yet because of the man’s persistence, he will get up and give him as much as he needs.'),
('LUK', 11, 9, 'LUK.11.9', 'So I tell you: Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock, and the door will be opened to you.'),
('LUK', 11, 10, 'LUK.11.10', 'For everyone who asks receives; he who seeks finds; and to him who knocks, the door will be opened.'),
('LUK', 11, 11, 'LUK.11.11', 'What father among you, if his son asks for a fish, will give him a snake instead?'),
('LUK', 11, 12, 'LUK.11.12', 'Or if he asks for an egg, will give him a scorpion?'),
('LUK', 11, 13, 'LUK.11.13', 'So if you who are evil know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father in heaven give the Holy Spirit to those who ask Him!”'),
('LUK', 11, 14, 'LUK.11.14', 'One day Jesus was driving out a demon that was mute. And when the demon was gone, the man who had been mute spoke. The crowds were amazed,'),
('LUK', 11, 15, 'LUK.11.15', 'but some of them said, “It is by Beelzebul, the prince of the demons, that He drives out demons.”'),
('LUK', 11, 16, 'LUK.11.16', 'And others tested Him by demanding a sign from heaven.'),
('LUK', 11, 17, 'LUK.11.17', 'Knowing their thoughts, Jesus said to them, “Every kingdom divided against itself will be laid waste, and a house divided against a house will fall.'),
('LUK', 11, 18, 'LUK.11.18', 'If Satan is divided against himself, how can his kingdom stand? After all, you say that I drive out demons by Beelzebul.'),
('LUK', 11, 19, 'LUK.11.19', 'And if I drive out demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your sons drive them out? So then, they will be your judges.'),
('LUK', 11, 20, 'LUK.11.20', 'But if I drive out demons by the finger of God, then the kingdom of God has come upon you.'),
('LUK', 11, 21, 'LUK.11.21', 'When a strong man, fully armed, guards his house, his possessions are secure.'),
('LUK', 11, 22, 'LUK.11.22', 'But when someone stronger attacks and overpowers him, he takes away the armor in which the man trusted, and then he divides up his plunder.'),
('LUK', 11, 23, 'LUK.11.23', 'He who is not with Me is against Me, and he who does not gather with Me scatters.'),
('LUK', 11, 24, 'LUK.11.24', 'When an unclean spirit comes out of a man, it passes through arid places seeking rest and does not find it. Then it says, ‘I will return to the house I left.’'),
('LUK', 11, 25, 'LUK.11.25', 'On its return, it finds the house swept clean and put in order.'),
('LUK', 11, 26, 'LUK.11.26', 'Then it goes and brings seven other spirits more wicked than itself, and they go in and dwell there. And the final plight of that man is worse than the first.”'),
('LUK', 11, 27, 'LUK.11.27', 'As Jesus was saying these things, a woman in the crowd raised her voice and said, “Blessed is the womb that bore You, and blessed are the breasts that nursed You!”'),
('LUK', 11, 28, 'LUK.11.28', 'But He replied, “Blessed rather are those who hear the word of God and obey it.”'),
('LUK', 11, 29, 'LUK.11.29', 'As the crowds were increasing, Jesus said, “This is a wicked generation. It demands a sign, but none will be given it except the sign of Jonah.'),
('LUK', 11, 30, 'LUK.11.30', 'For as Jonah was a sign to the Ninevites, so the Son of Man will be a sign to this generation.'),
('LUK', 11, 31, 'LUK.11.31', 'The Queen of the South will rise at the judgment with the men of this generation and condemn them; for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and now One greater than Solomon is here.'),
('LUK', 11, 32, 'LUK.11.32', 'The men of Nineveh will stand at the judgment with this generation and condemn it; for they repented at the preaching of Jonah, and now One greater than Jonah is here.'),
('LUK', 11, 33, 'LUK.11.33', 'No one lights a lamp and puts it in a cellar or under a basket. Instead, he sets it on a stand, so those who enter can see the light.'),
('LUK', 11, 34, 'LUK.11.34', 'Your eye is the lamp of your body. When your eyes are good, your whole body also is full of light. But when they are bad, your body is full of darkness.'),
('LUK', 11, 35, 'LUK.11.35', 'Be careful, then, that the light within you is not darkness.'),
('LUK', 11, 36, 'LUK.11.36', 'So if your whole body is full of light, with no part of it in darkness, you will be radiant, as though a lamp were shining on you.”'),
('LUK', 11, 37, 'LUK.11.37', 'As Jesus was speaking, a Pharisee invited Him to dine with him; so He went in and reclined at the table.'),
('LUK', 11, 38, 'LUK.11.38', 'But the Pharisee was surprised to see that Jesus did not first wash before the meal.'),
('LUK', 11, 39, 'LUK.11.39', 'Then the Lord said, “Now you Pharisees clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside you are full of greed and wickedness.'),
('LUK', 11, 40, 'LUK.11.40', 'You fools! Did not the One who made the outside make the inside as well?'),
('LUK', 11, 41, 'LUK.11.41', 'But give as alms the things that are within you, and behold, everything will be clean for you.'),
('LUK', 11, 42, 'LUK.11.42', 'Woe to you Pharisees! For you pay tithes of mint, rue, and every herb, but you disregard justice and the love of God. You should have practiced the latter without neglecting the former.'),
('LUK', 11, 43, 'LUK.11.43', 'Woe to you Pharisees! For you love the chief seats in the synagogues and the greetings in the marketplaces.'),
('LUK', 11, 44, 'LUK.11.44', 'Woe to you! For you are like unmarked graves, which men walk over without even noticing.”'),
('LUK', 11, 45, 'LUK.11.45', 'One of the experts in the law told Him, “Teacher, when You say these things, You insult us as well.”'),
('LUK', 11, 46, 'LUK.11.46', '“Woe to you as well, experts in the law!” He replied. “For you weigh men down with heavy burdens, but you yourselves will not lift a finger to lighten their load.'),
('LUK', 11, 47, 'LUK.11.47', 'Woe to you! For you build tombs for the prophets, but it was your fathers who killed them.'),
('LUK', 11, 48, 'LUK.11.48', 'So you are witnesses consenting to the deeds of your fathers: They killed the prophets, and you build their tombs.'),
('LUK', 11, 49, 'LUK.11.49', 'Because of this, the wisdom of God said, ‘I will send them prophets and apostles; some of them they will kill and others they will persecute.’'),
('LUK', 11, 50, 'LUK.11.50', 'As a result, this generation will be charged with the blood of all the prophets that has been shed since the foundation of the world,'),
('LUK', 11, 51, 'LUK.11.51', 'from the blood of Abel to the blood of Zechariah, who was killed between the altar and the sanctuary. Yes, I tell you, all of it will be charged to this generation.'),
('LUK', 11, 52, 'LUK.11.52', 'Woe to you experts in the law! For you have taken away the key to knowledge. You yourselves have not entered, and you have hindered those who were entering.”'),
('LUK', 11, 53, 'LUK.11.53', 'As Jesus went on from there, the scribes and Pharisees began to oppose Him bitterly and to ply Him with questions about many things,'),
('LUK', 11, 54, 'LUK.11.54', 'waiting to catch Him in something He might say.'),
('LUK', 12, 1, 'LUK.12.1', 'In the meantime, a crowd of many thousands had gathered, so that they were trampling one another. Jesus began to speak first to His disciples: “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.'),
('LUK', 12, 2, 'LUK.12.2', 'There is nothing concealed that will not be disclosed, and nothing hidden that will not be made known.'),
('LUK', 12, 3, 'LUK.12.3', 'What you have spoken in the dark will be heard in the daylight, and what you have whispered in the inner rooms will be proclaimed from the housetops.'),
('LUK', 12, 4, 'LUK.12.4', 'I tell you, My friends, do not be afraid of those who kill the body and after that can do no more.'),
('LUK', 12, 5, 'LUK.12.5', 'But I will show you whom you should fear: Fear the One who, after you have been killed, has authority to throw you into hell. Yes, I tell you, fear Him!'),
('LUK', 12, 6, 'LUK.12.6', 'Are not five sparrows sold for two pennies? Yet not one of them is forgotten by God.'),
('LUK', 12, 7, 'LUK.12.7', 'And even the very hairs of your head are all numbered. So do not be afraid; you are worth more than many sparrows.'),
('LUK', 12, 8, 'LUK.12.8', 'I tell you, everyone who confesses Me before men, the Son of Man will also confess him before the angels of God.'),
('LUK', 12, 9, 'LUK.12.9', 'But whoever denies Me before men will be denied before the angels of God.'),
('LUK', 12, 10, 'LUK.12.10', 'And everyone who speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven, but whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven.'),
('LUK', 12, 11, 'LUK.12.11', 'When you are brought before synagogues, rulers, and authorities, do not worry about how to defend yourselves or what to say.'),
('LUK', 12, 12, 'LUK.12.12', 'For at that time the Holy Spirit will teach you what you should say.”'),
('LUK', 12, 13, 'LUK.12.13', 'Someone in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.”'),
('LUK', 12, 14, 'LUK.12.14', 'But Jesus replied, “Man, who appointed Me judge or executor between you?”'),
('LUK', 12, 15, 'LUK.12.15', 'And He said to them, “Watch out! Guard yourselves against every form of greed, for one’s life does not consist in the abundance of his possessions.”'),
('LUK', 12, 16, 'LUK.12.16', 'Then He told them a parable: “The ground of a certain rich man produced an abundance.'),
('LUK', 12, 17, 'LUK.12.17', 'So he thought to himself, ‘What shall I do, since I have nowhere to store my crops?’'),
('LUK', 12, 18, 'LUK.12.18', 'Then he said, ‘This is what I will do: I will tear down my barns and will build bigger ones, and there I will store up all my grain and my goods.'),
('LUK', 12, 19, 'LUK.12.19', 'Then I will say to myself, “You have plenty of good things laid up for many years. Take it easy. Eat, drink, and be merry!”’'),
('LUK', 12, 20, 'LUK.12.20', 'But God said to him, ‘You fool! This very night your life will be required of you. Then who will own what you have accumulated?’'),
('LUK', 12, 21, 'LUK.12.21', 'This is how it will be for anyone who stores up treasure for himself but is not rich toward God.”'),
('LUK', 12, 22, 'LUK.12.22', 'Then Jesus said to His disciples, “Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat, or about your body, what you will wear.'),
('LUK', 12, 23, 'LUK.12.23', 'For life is more than food, and the body more than clothes.'),
('LUK', 12, 24, 'LUK.12.24', 'Consider the ravens: They do not sow or reap, they have no storehouse or barn; yet God feeds them. How much more valuable you are than the birds!'),
('LUK', 12, 25, 'LUK.12.25', 'Who of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life?'),
('LUK', 12, 26, 'LUK.12.26', 'So if you cannot do such a small thing, why do you worry about the rest?'),
('LUK', 12, 27, 'LUK.12.27', 'Consider how the lilies grow: They do not labor or spin. Yet I tell you, not even Solomon in all his glory was adorned like one of these.'),
('LUK', 12, 28, 'LUK.12.28', 'If that is how God clothes the grass of the field, which is here today and tomorrow is thrown into the furnace, how much more will He clothe you, O you of little faith!'),
('LUK', 12, 29, 'LUK.12.29', 'And do not be concerned about what you will eat or drink. Do not worry about it.'),
('LUK', 12, 30, 'LUK.12.30', 'For the Gentiles of the world strive after all these things, and your Father knows that you need them.'),
('LUK', 12, 31, 'LUK.12.31', 'But seek His kingdom, and these things will be added unto you.'),
('LUK', 12, 32, 'LUK.12.32', 'Do not be afraid, little flock, for your Father is pleased to give you the kingdom.'),
('LUK', 12, 33, 'LUK.12.33', 'Sell your possessions and give to the poor. Provide yourselves with purses that will not wear out, an inexhaustible treasure in heaven, where no thief approaches and no moth destroys.'),
('LUK', 12, 34, 'LUK.12.34', 'For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.'),
('LUK', 12, 35, 'LUK.12.35', 'Be dressed for service and keep your lamps burning.'),
('LUK', 12, 36, 'LUK.12.36', 'Then you will be like servants waiting for their master to return from the wedding banquet, so that when he comes and knocks, they can open the door for him at once.'),
('LUK', 12, 37, 'LUK.12.37', 'Blessed are those servants whom the master finds on watch when he returns. Truly I tell you, he will dress himself to serve and will have them recline at the table, and he himself will come and wait on them.'),
('LUK', 12, 38, 'LUK.12.38', 'Even if he comes in the second or third watch of the night and finds them alert, those servants will be blessed.'),
('LUK', 12, 39, 'LUK.12.39', 'But understand this: If the homeowner had known at what hour the thief was coming, he would not have let his house be broken into.'),
('LUK', 12, 40, 'LUK.12.40', 'You also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour you do not expect.”'),
('LUK', 12, 41, 'LUK.12.41', '“Lord,” said Peter, “are You addressing this parable to us, or to everyone else as well?”'),
('LUK', 12, 42, 'LUK.12.42', 'And the Lord answered, “Who then is the faithful and wise manager, whom the master puts in charge of his servants to give them their portion at the proper time?'),
('LUK', 12, 43, 'LUK.12.43', 'Blessed is that servant whose master finds him doing so when he returns.'),
('LUK', 12, 44, 'LUK.12.44', 'Truly I tell you, he will put him in charge of all his possessions.'),
('LUK', 12, 45, 'LUK.12.45', 'But suppose that servant says in his heart, ‘My master will be a long time in coming,’ and he begins to beat the menservants and maidservants, and to eat and drink and get drunk.'),
('LUK', 12, 46, 'LUK.12.46', 'The master of that servant will come on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not anticipate. Then he will cut him to pieces and assign him a place with the unbelievers.'),
('LUK', 12, 47, 'LUK.12.47', 'That servant who knows his master’s will but does not get ready or follow his instructions will be beaten with many blows.'),
('LUK', 12, 48, 'LUK.12.48', 'But the one who unknowingly does things worthy of punishment will be beaten with few blows. From everyone who has been given much, much will be required; and from him who has been entrusted with much, even more will be demanded.'),
('LUK', 12, 49, 'LUK.12.49', 'I have come to ignite a fire on the earth, and how I wish it were already kindled!'),
('LUK', 12, 50, 'LUK.12.50', 'But I have a baptism to undergo, and how distressed I am until it is accomplished!'),
('LUK', 12, 51, 'LUK.12.51', 'Do you think that I have come to bring peace to the earth? No, I tell you, but division.'),
('LUK', 12, 52, 'LUK.12.52', 'From now on, five in one household will be divided, three against two and two against three.'),
('LUK', 12, 53, 'LUK.12.53', 'They will be divided, father against son and son against father, mother against daughter and daughter against mother, mother-in-law against daughter-in-law and daughter-in-law against mother-in-law.”'),
('LUK', 12, 54, 'LUK.12.54', 'Then Jesus said to the crowds, “As soon as you see a cloud rising in the west, you say, ‘A shower is coming,’ and that is what happens.'),
('LUK', 12, 55, 'LUK.12.55', 'And when the south wind blows, you say, ‘It will be hot,’ and it is.'),
('LUK', 12, 56, 'LUK.12.56', 'You hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the earth and sky. Why don’t you know how to interpret the present time?'),
('LUK', 12, 57, 'LUK.12.57', 'And why don’t you judge for yourselves what is right?'),
('LUK', 12, 58, 'LUK.12.58', 'Make every effort to reconcile with your adversary while you are on your way to the magistrate. Otherwise, he may drag you off to the judge, and the judge may hand you over to the officer, and the officer may throw you into prison.'),
('LUK', 12, 59, 'LUK.12.59', 'I tell you, you will not get out until you have paid the very last penny.”'),
('LUK', 13, 1, 'LUK.13.1', 'At that time some of those present told Jesus about the Galileans whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices.'),
('LUK', 13, 2, 'LUK.13.2', 'To this He replied, “Do you think that these Galileans were worse sinners than all the other Galileans, because they suffered this way?'),
('LUK', 13, 3, 'LUK.13.3', 'No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.'),
('LUK', 13, 4, 'LUK.13.4', 'Or those eighteen who were killed when the tower of Siloam collapsed on them: Do you think that they were more sinful than all the others living in Jerusalem?'),
('LUK', 13, 5, 'LUK.13.5', 'No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.”'),
('LUK', 13, 6, 'LUK.13.6', 'Then Jesus told this parable: “A man had a fig tree that was planted in his vineyard. He went to look for fruit on it but did not find any.'),
('LUK', 13, 7, 'LUK.13.7', 'So he said to the keeper of the vineyard, ‘Look, for the past three years I have come to search for fruit on this fig tree and haven’t found any. Therefore cut it down! Why should it use up the soil?’'),
('LUK', 13, 8, 'LUK.13.8', '‘Sir,’ the man replied, ‘leave it alone again this year, until I dig around it and fertilize it.'),
('LUK', 13, 9, 'LUK.13.9', 'If it bears fruit next year, fine. But if not, you can cut it down.’”'),
('LUK', 13, 10, 'LUK.13.10', 'One Sabbath Jesus was teaching in one of the synagogues,'),
('LUK', 13, 11, 'LUK.13.11', 'and a woman there had been disabled by a spirit for eighteen years. She was hunched over and could not stand up straight.'),
('LUK', 13, 12, 'LUK.13.12', 'When Jesus saw her, He called her over and said, “Woman, you are set free from your disability.”'),
('LUK', 13, 13, 'LUK.13.13', 'Then He placed His hands on her, and immediately she straightened up and began to glorify God.'),
('LUK', 13, 14, 'LUK.13.14', 'But the synagogue leader was indignant that Jesus had healed on the Sabbath. “There are six days for work,” he told the crowd. “So come and be healed on those days and not on the Sabbath.”'),
('LUK', 13, 15, 'LUK.13.15', '“You hypocrites!” the Lord replied. “Does not each of you on the Sabbath untie his ox or donkey from the stall and lead it to water?'),
('LUK', 13, 16, 'LUK.13.16', 'Then should not this daughter of Abraham, whom Satan has kept bound for eighteen long years, be released from her bondage on the Sabbath day?”'),
('LUK', 13, 17, 'LUK.13.17', 'When Jesus said this, all His adversaries were humiliated. And the whole crowd rejoiced at all the glorious things He was doing.'),
('LUK', 13, 18, 'LUK.13.18', 'Then Jesus asked, “What is the kingdom of God like? To what can I compare it?'),
('LUK', 13, 19, 'LUK.13.19', 'It is like a mustard seed that a man tossed into his garden. It grew and became a tree, and the birds of the air nested in its branches.”'),
('LUK', 13, 20, 'LUK.13.20', 'Again He asked, “To what can I compare the kingdom of God?'),
('LUK', 13, 21, 'LUK.13.21', 'It is like leaven that a woman took and mixed into three measures of flour, until all of it was leavened.”'),
('LUK', 13, 22, 'LUK.13.22', 'Then Jesus traveled throughout the towns and villages, teaching as He made His way toward Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 13, 23, 'LUK.13.23', '“Lord,” someone asked Him, “will only a few people be saved?” Jesus answered,'),
('LUK', 13, 24, 'LUK.13.24', '“Make every effort to enter through the narrow door. For many, I tell you, will try to enter and will not be able.'),
('LUK', 13, 25, 'LUK.13.25', 'After the master of the house gets up and shuts the door, you will stand outside knocking and saying, ‘Lord, open the door for us.’ But he will reply, ‘I do not know where you are from.’'),
('LUK', 13, 26, 'LUK.13.26', 'Then you will say, ‘We ate and drank with you, and you taught in our streets.’'),
('LUK', 13, 27, 'LUK.13.27', 'And he will answer, ‘I tell you, I do not know where you are from. Depart from me, all you evildoers.’'),
('LUK', 13, 28, 'LUK.13.28', 'There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth when you see Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and all the prophets in the kingdom of God, but you yourselves are thrown out.'),
('LUK', 13, 29, 'LUK.13.29', 'People will come from east and west and north and south, and will recline at the table in the kingdom of God.'),
('LUK', 13, 30, 'LUK.13.30', 'And indeed, some who are last will be first, and some who are first will be last.”'),
('LUK', 13, 31, 'LUK.13.31', 'At that very hour, some Pharisees came to Jesus and told Him, “Leave this place and get away, because Herod wants to kill You.”'),
('LUK', 13, 32, 'LUK.13.32', 'But Jesus replied, “Go tell that fox, ‘Look, I will keep driving out demons and healing people today and tomorrow, and on the third day I will reach My goal.’'),
('LUK', 13, 33, 'LUK.13.33', 'Nevertheless, I must keep going today and tomorrow and the next day, for it is not admissible for a prophet to perish outside of Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 13, 34, 'LUK.13.34', 'O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those sent to her, how often I have longed to gather your children together as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, but you were unwilling!'),
('LUK', 13, 35, 'LUK.13.35', 'Look, your house is left to you desolate. And I tell you that you will not see Me again until you say, ‘Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord.’”'),
('LUK', 14, 1, 'LUK.14.1', 'One Sabbath, Jesus went to eat in the home of a leading Pharisee, and those in attendance were watching Him closely.'),
('LUK', 14, 2, 'LUK.14.2', 'Right there before Him was a man with dropsy.'),
('LUK', 14, 3, 'LUK.14.3', 'So Jesus asked the experts in the law and the Pharisees, “Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath or not?”'),
('LUK', 14, 4, 'LUK.14.4', 'But they remained silent. Then Jesus took hold of the man, healed him, and sent him on his way.'),
('LUK', 14, 5, 'LUK.14.5', 'And He asked them, “Which of you whose son or ox falls into a pit on the Sabbath day will not immediately pull him out?”'),
('LUK', 14, 6, 'LUK.14.6', 'And they were unable to answer these questions.'),
('LUK', 14, 7, 'LUK.14.7', 'When Jesus noticed how the guests chose the places of honor, He told them a parable:'),
('LUK', 14, 8, 'LUK.14.8', '“When you are invited to a wedding banquet, do not sit in the place of honor, in case someone more distinguished than you has been invited.'),
('LUK', 14, 9, 'LUK.14.9', 'Then the host who invited both of you will come and tell you, ‘Give this man your seat.’ And in humiliation, you will have to take the last place.'),
('LUK', 14, 10, 'LUK.14.10', 'But when you are invited, go and sit in the last place, so that your host will come and tell you, ‘Friend, move up to a better place.’ Then you will be honored in front of everyone at the table with you.'),
('LUK', 14, 11, 'LUK.14.11', 'For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, and the one who humbles himself will be exalted.”'),
('LUK', 14, 12, 'LUK.14.12', 'Then Jesus said to the man who had invited Him, “When you host a dinner or a banquet, do not invite your friends or brothers or relatives or rich neighbors. Otherwise, they may invite you in return, and you will be repaid.'),
('LUK', 14, 13, 'LUK.14.13', 'But when you host a banquet, invite the poor, the crippled, the lame, and the blind,'),
('LUK', 14, 14, 'LUK.14.14', 'and you will be blessed. Since they cannot repay you, you will be repaid at the resurrection of the righteous.”'),
('LUK', 14, 15, 'LUK.14.15', 'When one of those reclining with Him heard this, he said to Jesus, “Blessed is everyone who will eat at the feast in the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 14, 16, 'LUK.14.16', 'But Jesus replied, “A certain man prepared a great banquet and invited many guests.'),
('LUK', 14, 17, 'LUK.14.17', 'When it was time for the banquet, he sent his servant to tell those who had been invited, ‘Come, for everything is now ready.’'),
('LUK', 14, 18, 'LUK.14.18', 'But one after another they all began to make excuses. The first one said, ‘I have bought a field, and I need to go see it. Please excuse me.’'),
('LUK', 14, 19, 'LUK.14.19', 'Another said, ‘I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I am going to try them out. Please excuse me.’'),
('LUK', 14, 20, 'LUK.14.20', 'Still another said, ‘I have married a wife, so I cannot come.’'),
('LUK', 14, 21, 'LUK.14.21', 'The servant returned and reported all this to his master. Then the owner of the house became angry and said to his servant, ‘Go out quickly into the streets and alleys of the city, and bring in the poor, the crippled, the blind, and the lame.’'),
('LUK', 14, 22, 'LUK.14.22', '‘Sir,’ the servant replied, ‘what you ordered has been done, and there is still room.’'),
('LUK', 14, 23, 'LUK.14.23', 'So the master told his servant, ‘Go out to the highways and hedges and compel them to come in, so that my house will be full.'),
('LUK', 14, 24, 'LUK.14.24', 'For I tell you, not one of those men who were invited will taste my banquet.’”'),
('LUK', 14, 25, 'LUK.14.25', 'Now large crowds were traveling with Jesus, and He turned and said to them,'),
('LUK', 14, 26, 'LUK.14.26', '“If anyone comes to Me and does not hate his father and mother and wife and children and brothers and sisters—yes, even his own life—he cannot be My disciple.'),
('LUK', 14, 27, 'LUK.14.27', 'And whoever does not carry his cross and follow Me cannot be My disciple.'),
('LUK', 14, 28, 'LUK.14.28', 'Which of you, wishing to build a tower, does not first sit down and count the cost to see if he has the resources to complete it?'),
('LUK', 14, 29, 'LUK.14.29', 'Otherwise, if he lays the foundation and is unable to finish the work, everyone who sees it will ridicule him,'),
('LUK', 14, 30, 'LUK.14.30', 'saying, ‘This man could not finish what he started to build.’'),
('LUK', 14, 31, 'LUK.14.31', 'Or what king on his way to war with another king will not first sit down and consider whether he can engage with ten thousand men the one coming against him with twenty thousand?'),
('LUK', 14, 32, 'LUK.14.32', 'And if he is unable, he will send a delegation while the other king is still far off, to ask for terms of peace.'),
('LUK', 14, 33, 'LUK.14.33', 'In the same way, any one of you who does not give up everything he has cannot be My disciple.'),
('LUK', 14, 34, 'LUK.14.34', 'Salt is good, but if the salt loses its savor, with what will it be seasoned?'),
('LUK', 14, 35, 'LUK.14.35', 'It is fit neither for the soil nor for the manure pile, and it is thrown out. He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”'),
('LUK', 15, 1, 'LUK.15.1', 'Now all the tax collectors and sinners were gathering around to listen to Jesus.'),
('LUK', 15, 2, 'LUK.15.2', 'So the Pharisees and scribes began to grumble: “This man welcomes sinners and eats with them.”'),
('LUK', 15, 3, 'LUK.15.3', 'Then Jesus told them this parable:'),
('LUK', 15, 4, 'LUK.15.4', '“What man among you, if he has a hundred sheep and loses one of them, does not leave the ninety-nine in the pasture and go after the one that is lost, until he finds it?'),
('LUK', 15, 5, 'LUK.15.5', 'And when he finds it, he joyfully puts it on his shoulders,'),
('LUK', 15, 6, 'LUK.15.6', 'comes home, and calls together his friends and neighbors to tell them, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my lost sheep!’'),
('LUK', 15, 7, 'LUK.15.7', 'I tell you that in the same way there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous ones who do not need to repent.'),
('LUK', 15, 8, 'LUK.15.8', 'Or what woman who has ten silver coins and loses one of them does not light a lamp, sweep her house, and search carefully until she finds it?'),
('LUK', 15, 9, 'LUK.15.9', 'And when she finds it, she calls together her friends and neighbors to say, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my lost coin.’'),
('LUK', 15, 10, 'LUK.15.10', 'In the same way, I tell you, there is joy in the presence of God’s angels over one sinner who repents.”'),
('LUK', 15, 11, 'LUK.15.11', 'Then Jesus said, “There was a man who had two sons.'),
('LUK', 15, 12, 'LUK.15.12', 'The younger son said to him, ‘Father, give me my share of the estate.’ So he divided his property between them.'),
('LUK', 15, 13, 'LUK.15.13', 'After a few days, the younger son got everything together and journeyed to a distant country, where he squandered his wealth in wild living.'),
('LUK', 15, 14, 'LUK.15.14', 'After he had spent all he had, a severe famine swept through that country, and he began to be in need.'),
('LUK', 15, 15, 'LUK.15.15', 'So he went and hired himself out to a citizen of that country, who sent him into his fields to feed the pigs.'),
('LUK', 15, 16, 'LUK.15.16', 'He longed to fill his belly with the pods the pigs were eating, but no one would give him a thing.'),
('LUK', 15, 17, 'LUK.15.17', 'Finally he came to his senses and said, ‘How many of my father’s hired servants have plenty of food, but here I am, starving to death!'),
('LUK', 15, 18, 'LUK.15.18', 'I will get up and go back to my father and say to him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you.'),
('LUK', 15, 19, 'LUK.15.19', 'I am no longer worthy to be called your son. Make me like one of your hired servants.”’'),
('LUK', 15, 20, 'LUK.15.20', 'So he got up and went to his father. But while he was still in the distance, his father saw him and was filled with compassion. He ran to his son, embraced him, and kissed him.'),
('LUK', 15, 21, 'LUK.15.21', 'The son declared, ‘Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you. I am no longer worthy to be called your son.’'),
('LUK', 15, 22, 'LUK.15.22', 'But the father said to his servants, ‘Quick! Bring the best robe and put it on him. Put a ring on his finger and sandals on his feet.'),
('LUK', 15, 23, 'LUK.15.23', 'Bring the fattened calf and kill it. Let us feast and celebrate.'),
('LUK', 15, 24, 'LUK.15.24', 'For this son of mine was dead and is alive again! He was lost and is found!’ So they began to celebrate.'),
('LUK', 15, 25, 'LUK.15.25', 'Meanwhile the older son was in the field, and as he approached the house, he heard music and dancing.'),
('LUK', 15, 26, 'LUK.15.26', 'So he called one of the servants and asked what was going on.'),
('LUK', 15, 27, 'LUK.15.27', '‘Your brother has returned,’ he said, ‘and your father has killed the fattened calf, because he has him back safe and sound.’'),
('LUK', 15, 28, 'LUK.15.28', 'The older son became angry and refused to go in. So his father came out and pleaded with him.'),
('LUK', 15, 29, 'LUK.15.29', 'But he answered his father, ‘Look, all these years I have served you and never disobeyed a commandment of yours. Yet you never gave me even a young goat so I could celebrate with my friends.'),
('LUK', 15, 30, 'LUK.15.30', 'But when this son of yours returns from squandering your wealth with prostitutes, you kill the fattened calf for him!’'),
('LUK', 15, 31, 'LUK.15.31', '‘Son, you are always with me,’ the father said, ‘and all that is mine is yours.'),
('LUK', 15, 32, 'LUK.15.32', 'But it was fitting to celebrate and be glad, because this brother of yours was dead and is alive again; he was lost and is found.’”'),
('LUK', 16, 1, 'LUK.16.1', 'Jesus also said to His disciples, “There was a rich man whose manager was accused of wasting his possessions.'),
('LUK', 16, 2, 'LUK.16.2', 'So he called him in to ask, ‘What is this I hear about you? Turn in an account of your management, for you cannot be manager any longer.’'),
('LUK', 16, 3, 'LUK.16.3', 'The manager said to himself, ‘What shall I do, now that my master is taking away my position? I am too weak to dig and too ashamed to beg.'),
('LUK', 16, 4, 'LUK.16.4', 'I know what I will do so that after my removal from management, people will welcome me into their homes.’'),
('LUK', 16, 5, 'LUK.16.5', 'And he called in each one of his master’s debtors. ‘How much do you owe my master?’ he asked the first.'),
('LUK', 16, 6, 'LUK.16.6', '‘A hundred measures of olive oil,’ he answered. ‘Take your bill,’ said the manager, ‘sit down quickly, and write fifty.’'),
('LUK', 16, 7, 'LUK.16.7', 'Then he asked another, ‘And how much do you owe?’ ‘A hundred measures of wheat,’ he replied. ‘Take your bill and write eighty,’ he told him.'),
('LUK', 16, 8, 'LUK.16.8', 'The master commended the dishonest manager because he had acted shrewdly. For the sons of this age are more shrewd in dealing with their own kind than are the sons of light.'),
('LUK', 16, 9, 'LUK.16.9', 'I tell you, use worldly wealth to make friends for yourselves so that when it is gone, they will welcome you into eternal dwellings.'),
('LUK', 16, 10, 'LUK.16.10', 'Whoever is faithful with very little will also be faithful with much, and whoever is dishonest with very little will also be dishonest with much.'),
('LUK', 16, 11, 'LUK.16.11', 'So if you have not been faithful with worldly wealth, who will entrust you with true riches?'),
('LUK', 16, 12, 'LUK.16.12', 'And if you have not been faithful with the belongings of another, who will give you belongings of your own?'),
('LUK', 16, 13, 'LUK.16.13', 'No servant can serve two masters. Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money.”'),
('LUK', 16, 14, 'LUK.16.14', 'The Pharisees, who were lovers of money, heard all of this and were scoffing at Jesus.'),
('LUK', 16, 15, 'LUK.16.15', 'So He said to them, “You are the ones who justify yourselves before men, but God knows your hearts. For what is prized among men is detestable before God.'),
('LUK', 16, 16, 'LUK.16.16', 'The Law and the Prophets were proclaimed until John. Since that time, the gospel of the kingdom of God is being preached, and everyone is forcing his way into it.'),
('LUK', 16, 17, 'LUK.16.17', 'But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for a single stroke of a pen to drop out of the Law.'),
('LUK', 16, 18, 'LUK.16.18', 'Anyone who divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery, and he who marries a divorced woman commits adultery.'),
('LUK', 16, 19, 'LUK.16.19', 'Now there was a rich man dressed in purple and fine linen, who lived each day in joyous splendor.'),
('LUK', 16, 20, 'LUK.16.20', 'And a beggar named Lazarus lay at his gate, covered with sores'),
('LUK', 16, 21, 'LUK.16.21', 'and longing to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man’s table. Even the dogs came and licked his sores.'),
('LUK', 16, 22, 'LUK.16.22', 'One day the beggar died and was carried by the angels to Abraham’s side. And the rich man also died and was buried.'),
('LUK', 16, 23, 'LUK.16.23', 'In Hades, where he was in torment, he looked up and saw Abraham from afar, with Lazarus by his side.'),
('LUK', 16, 24, 'LUK.16.24', 'So he cried out, ‘Father Abraham, have mercy on me and send Lazarus to dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue. For I am in agony in this fire.’'),
('LUK', 16, 25, 'LUK.16.25', 'But Abraham answered, ‘Child, remember that during your lifetime you received your good things, while Lazarus received bad things. But now he is comforted here, while you are in agony.'),
('LUK', 16, 26, 'LUK.16.26', 'And besides all this, a great chasm has been fixed between us and you, so that even those who wish cannot cross from here to you, nor can anyone cross from there to us.’'),
('LUK', 16, 27, 'LUK.16.27', '‘Then I beg you, father,’ he said, ‘send Lazarus to my father’s house,'),
('LUK', 16, 28, 'LUK.16.28', 'for I have five brothers. Let him warn them, so that they will not also end up in this place of torment.’'),
('LUK', 16, 29, 'LUK.16.29', 'But Abraham replied, ‘They have Moses and the Prophets; let your brothers listen to them.’'),
('LUK', 16, 30, 'LUK.16.30', '‘No, father Abraham,’ he said, ‘but if someone is sent to them from the dead, they will repent.’'),
('LUK', 16, 31, 'LUK.16.31', 'Then Abraham said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from the dead.’”'),
('LUK', 17, 1, 'LUK.17.1', 'Jesus said to His disciples, “It is inevitable that stumbling blocks will come, but woe to the one through whom they come!'),
('LUK', 17, 2, 'LUK.17.2', 'It would be better for him to have a millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea than to cause one of these little ones to stumble.'),
('LUK', 17, 3, 'LUK.17.3', 'Watch yourselves. If your brother sins, rebuke him; and if he repents, forgive him.'),
('LUK', 17, 4, 'LUK.17.4', 'Even if he sins against you seven times in a day, and seven times returns to say, ‘I repent,’ you must forgive him.”'),
('LUK', 17, 5, 'LUK.17.5', 'The apostles said to the Lord, “Increase our faith!”'),
('LUK', 17, 6, 'LUK.17.6', 'And the Lord answered, “If you have faith the size of a mustard seed, you can say to this mulberry tree, ‘Be uprooted and planted in the sea,’ and it will obey you.'),
('LUK', 17, 7, 'LUK.17.7', 'Which of you whose servant comes in from plowing or shepherding in the field will say to him, ‘Come at once and sit down to eat’?'),
('LUK', 17, 8, 'LUK.17.8', 'Instead, won’t he tell him, ‘Prepare my meal and dress yourself to serve me while I eat and drink, and afterward you may eat and drink’?'),
('LUK', 17, 9, 'LUK.17.9', 'Does he thank the servant because he did what he was told?'),
('LUK', 17, 10, 'LUK.17.10', 'So you also, when you have done everything commanded of you, should say, ‘We are unworthy servants; we have only done our duty.’”'),
('LUK', 17, 11, 'LUK.17.11', 'While Jesus was on His way to Jerusalem, He was passing between Samaria and Galilee.'),
('LUK', 17, 12, 'LUK.17.12', 'As He entered one of the villages, He was met by ten lepers. They stood at a distance'),
('LUK', 17, 13, 'LUK.17.13', 'and raised their voices, shouting, “Jesus, Master, have mercy on us!”'),
('LUK', 17, 14, 'LUK.17.14', 'When Jesus saw them, He said, “Go, show yourselves to the priests.” And as they were on their way, they were cleansed.'),
('LUK', 17, 15, 'LUK.17.15', 'When one of them saw that he was healed, he came back, praising God in a loud voice.'),
('LUK', 17, 16, 'LUK.17.16', 'He fell facedown at Jesus’ feet in thanksgiving to Him—and he was a Samaritan.'),
('LUK', 17, 17, 'LUK.17.17', '“Were not all ten cleansed?” Jesus asked. “Where then are the other nine?'),
('LUK', 17, 18, 'LUK.17.18', 'Was no one found except this foreigner to return and give glory to God?”'),
('LUK', 17, 19, 'LUK.17.19', 'Then Jesus said to him, “Rise and go; your faith has made you well!”'),
('LUK', 17, 20, 'LUK.17.20', 'When asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, Jesus replied, “The kingdom of God will not come with observable signs.'),
('LUK', 17, 21, 'LUK.17.21', 'Nor will people say, ‘Look, here it is,’ or ‘There it is.’ For you see, the kingdom of God is in your midst.”'),
('LUK', 17, 22, 'LUK.17.22', 'Then He said to the disciples, “The time is coming when you will long to see one of the days of the Son of Man, but you will not see it.'),
('LUK', 17, 23, 'LUK.17.23', 'People will tell you, ‘Look, there He is!’ or ‘Look, here He is!’ Do not go out or chase after them.'),
('LUK', 17, 24, 'LUK.17.24', 'For just as the lightning flashes and lights up the sky from one end to the other, so will be the Son of Man in His day.'),
('LUK', 17, 25, 'LUK.17.25', 'But first He must suffer many things and be rejected by this generation.'),
('LUK', 17, 26, 'LUK.17.26', 'Just as it was in the days of Noah, so also will it be in the days of the Son of Man:'),
('LUK', 17, 27, 'LUK.17.27', 'People were eating and drinking, marrying and being given in marriage, up to the day Noah entered the ark. Then the flood came and destroyed them all.'),
('LUK', 17, 28, 'LUK.17.28', 'It was the same in the days of Lot: People were eating and drinking, buying and selling, planting and building.'),
('LUK', 17, 29, 'LUK.17.29', 'But on the day Lot left Sodom, fire and sulfur rained down from heaven and destroyed them all.'),
('LUK', 17, 30, 'LUK.17.30', 'It will be just like that on the day the Son of Man is revealed.'),
('LUK', 17, 31, 'LUK.17.31', 'On that day, let no one on the housetop come down to retrieve his possessions. Likewise, let no one in the field return for anything he has left behind.'),
('LUK', 17, 32, 'LUK.17.32', 'Remember Lot’s wife!'),
('LUK', 17, 33, 'LUK.17.33', 'Whoever tries to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life will preserve it.'),
('LUK', 17, 34, 'LUK.17.34', 'I tell you, on that night two people will be in one bed: one will be taken and the other left.'),
('LUK', 17, 35, 'LUK.17.35', 'Two women will be grinding grain together: one will be taken and the other left.”'),
('LUK', 17, 37, 'LUK.17.37', '“Where, Lord?” they asked. Jesus answered, “Wherever there is a carcass, there the vultures will gather.”'),
('LUK', 18, 1, 'LUK.18.1', 'Then Jesus told them a parable about their need to pray at all times and not lose heart:'),
('LUK', 18, 2, 'LUK.18.2', '“In a certain town there was a judge who neither feared God nor respected men.'),
('LUK', 18, 3, 'LUK.18.3', 'And there was a widow in that town who kept appealing to him, ‘Give me justice against my adversary.’'),
('LUK', 18, 4, 'LUK.18.4', 'For a while he refused, but later he said to himself, ‘Though I neither fear God nor respect men,'),
('LUK', 18, 5, 'LUK.18.5', 'yet because this widow keeps pestering me, I will give her justice. Otherwise, she will wear me out with her perpetual requests.’”'),
('LUK', 18, 6, 'LUK.18.6', 'And the Lord said, “Listen to the words of the unjust judge.'),
('LUK', 18, 7, 'LUK.18.7', 'Will not God bring about justice for His elect who cry out to Him day and night? Will He delay in helping them?'),
('LUK', 18, 8, 'LUK.18.8', 'I tell you, He will promptly carry out justice on their behalf. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, will He find faith on earth?”'),
('LUK', 18, 9, 'LUK.18.9', 'To some who trusted in their own righteousness and viewed others with contempt, He also told this parable:'),
('LUK', 18, 10, 'LUK.18.10', '“Two men went up to the temple to pray. One was a Pharisee and the other a tax collector.'),
('LUK', 18, 11, 'LUK.18.11', 'The Pharisee stood by himself and prayed, ‘God, I thank You that I am not like other men—swindlers, evildoers, adulterers—or even like this tax collector.'),
('LUK', 18, 12, 'LUK.18.12', 'I fast twice a week and pay tithes of all that I acquire.’'),
('LUK', 18, 13, 'LUK.18.13', 'But the tax collector stood at a distance, unwilling even to lift up his eyes to heaven. Instead, he beat his breast and said, ‘God, have mercy on me, a sinner!’'),
('LUK', 18, 14, 'LUK.18.14', 'I tell you, this man, rather than the Pharisee, went home justified. For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but the one who humbles himself will be exalted.”'),
('LUK', 18, 15, 'LUK.18.15', 'Now people were even bringing their babies to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them. And when the disciples saw this, they rebuked those who brought them.'),
('LUK', 18, 16, 'LUK.18.16', 'But Jesus called the children to Him and said, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.'),
('LUK', 18, 17, 'LUK.18.17', 'Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”'),
('LUK', 18, 18, 'LUK.18.18', 'Then a certain ruler asked Him, “Good Teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?”'),
('LUK', 18, 19, 'LUK.18.19', '“Why do you call Me good?” Jesus replied. “No one is good except God alone.'),
('LUK', 18, 20, 'LUK.18.20', 'You know the commandments: ‘Do not commit adultery, do not murder, do not steal, do not bear false witness, honor your father and mother.’”'),
('LUK', 18, 21, 'LUK.18.21', '“All these I have kept from my youth,” he said.'),
('LUK', 18, 22, 'LUK.18.22', 'On hearing this, Jesus told him, “You still lack one thing: Sell everything you own and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”'),
('LUK', 18, 23, 'LUK.18.23', 'But when the ruler heard this, he became very sad, because he was extremely wealthy.'),
('LUK', 18, 24, 'LUK.18.24', 'Seeing the man’s sadness, Jesus said, “How hard it is for the rich to enter the kingdom of God!'),
('LUK', 18, 25, 'LUK.18.25', 'Indeed, it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 18, 26, 'LUK.18.26', 'Those who heard this asked, “Who then can be saved?”'),
('LUK', 18, 27, 'LUK.18.27', 'But Jesus said, “What is impossible with man is possible with God.”'),
('LUK', 18, 28, 'LUK.18.28', '“Look,” said Peter, “we have left all we had to follow You.”'),
('LUK', 18, 29, 'LUK.18.29', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “no one who has left home or wife or brothers or parents or children for the sake of the kingdom of God'),
('LUK', 18, 30, 'LUK.18.30', 'will fail to receive many times more in this age—and in the age to come, eternal life.”'),
('LUK', 18, 31, 'LUK.18.31', 'Then Jesus took the Twelve aside and said to them, “Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and everything the prophets have written about the Son of Man will be fulfilled.'),
('LUK', 18, 32, 'LUK.18.32', 'He will be delivered over to the Gentiles and will be mocked and insulted and spit upon.'),
('LUK', 18, 33, 'LUK.18.33', 'They will flog Him and kill Him, and on the third day He will rise again.”'),
('LUK', 18, 34, 'LUK.18.34', 'But the disciples did not understand any of these things. The meaning was hidden from them, and they did not comprehend what He was saying.'),
('LUK', 18, 35, 'LUK.18.35', 'As Jesus drew near to Jericho, a blind man was sitting beside the road, begging.'),
('LUK', 18, 36, 'LUK.18.36', 'When he heard the crowd going by, he asked what was happening.'),
('LUK', 18, 37, 'LUK.18.37', '“Jesus of Nazareth is passing by,” they told him.'),
('LUK', 18, 38, 'LUK.18.38', 'So he called out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”'),
('LUK', 18, 39, 'LUK.18.39', 'Those who led the way admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”'),
('LUK', 18, 40, 'LUK.18.40', 'Jesus stopped and directed that the man be brought to Him. When he had come near, Jesus asked him,'),
('LUK', 18, 41, 'LUK.18.41', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” “Lord,” he said, “let me see again.”'),
('LUK', 18, 42, 'LUK.18.42', '“Receive your sight!” Jesus replied. “Your faith has healed you.”'),
('LUK', 18, 43, 'LUK.18.43', 'Immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus, glorifying God. And all the people, when they saw it, gave praise to God.'),
('LUK', 19, 1, 'LUK.19.1', 'Then Jesus entered Jericho and was passing through.'),
('LUK', 19, 2, 'LUK.19.2', 'And there was a man named Zacchaeus, a chief tax collector, who was very wealthy.'),
('LUK', 19, 3, 'LUK.19.3', 'He was trying to see who Jesus was, but could not see over the crowd because he was small in stature.'),
('LUK', 19, 4, 'LUK.19.4', 'So he ran on ahead and climbed a sycamore tree to see Him, since Jesus was about to pass that way.'),
('LUK', 19, 5, 'LUK.19.5', 'When Jesus came to that place, He looked up and said, “Zacchaeus, hurry down, for I must stay at your house today.”'),
('LUK', 19, 6, 'LUK.19.6', 'So Zacchaeus hurried down and welcomed Him joyfully.'),
('LUK', 19, 7, 'LUK.19.7', 'And all who saw this began to grumble, saying, “He has gone to be the guest of a sinful man!”'),
('LUK', 19, 8, 'LUK.19.8', 'But Zacchaeus stood up and said to the Lord, “Look, Lord, half of my possessions I give to the poor, and if I have cheated anyone, I will repay it fourfold.”'),
('LUK', 19, 9, 'LUK.19.9', 'Jesus said to him, “Today salvation has come to this house, because this man too is a son of Abraham.'),
('LUK', 19, 10, 'LUK.19.10', 'For the Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.”'),
('LUK', 19, 11, 'LUK.19.11', 'While the people were listening to this, Jesus proceeded to tell them a parable, because He was near Jerusalem and they thought the kingdom of God would appear imminently.'),
('LUK', 19, 12, 'LUK.19.12', 'So He said, “A man of noble birth went to a distant country to lay claim to his kingship and then return.'),
('LUK', 19, 13, 'LUK.19.13', 'Beforehand, he called ten of his servants and gave them ten minas. ‘Conduct business with this until I return,’ he said.'),
('LUK', 19, 14, 'LUK.19.14', 'But his subjects hated him and sent a delegation after him to say, ‘We do not want this man to rule over us.’'),
('LUK', 19, 15, 'LUK.19.15', 'When he returned from procuring his kingship, he summoned the servants to whom he had given the money, to find out what each one had earned.'),
('LUK', 19, 16, 'LUK.19.16', 'The first servant came forward and said, ‘Master, your mina has produced ten more minas.’'),
('LUK', 19, 17, 'LUK.19.17', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good servant! Because you have been faithful in a very small matter, you shall have authority over ten cities.’'),
('LUK', 19, 18, 'LUK.19.18', 'The second servant came and said, ‘Master, your mina has made five minas.’'),
('LUK', 19, 19, 'LUK.19.19', 'And to this one he said, ‘You shall have authority over five cities.’'),
('LUK', 19, 20, 'LUK.19.20', 'Then another servant came and said, ‘Master, here is your mina, which I have laid away in a piece of cloth.'),
('LUK', 19, 21, 'LUK.19.21', 'For I was afraid of you, because you are a harsh man. You withdraw what you did not deposit and reap what you did not sow.’'),
('LUK', 19, 22, 'LUK.19.22', 'His master replied, ‘You wicked servant, I will judge you by your own words. So you knew that I am a harsh man, withdrawing what I did not deposit and reaping what I did not sow?'),
('LUK', 19, 23, 'LUK.19.23', 'Why then did you not deposit my money in the bank, and upon my return I could have collected it with interest?’'),
('LUK', 19, 24, 'LUK.19.24', 'Then he told those standing by, ‘Take the mina from him and give it to the one who has ten minas.’'),
('LUK', 19, 25, 'LUK.19.25', '‘Master,’ they said, ‘he already has ten!’'),
('LUK', 19, 26, 'LUK.19.26', 'He replied, ‘I tell you that everyone who has will be given more; but the one who does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.'),
('LUK', 19, 27, 'LUK.19.27', 'And these enemies of mine who were unwilling for me to rule over them, bring them here and slay them in front of me.’”'),
('LUK', 19, 28, 'LUK.19.28', 'After Jesus had said this, He went on ahead, going up to Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 19, 29, 'LUK.19.29', 'As He approached Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, He sent out two of His disciples,'),
('LUK', 19, 30, 'LUK.19.30', 'saying, “Go into the village ahead of you, and as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there, on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.'),
('LUK', 19, 31, 'LUK.19.31', 'If anyone asks, ‘Why are you untying it?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it.’”'),
('LUK', 19, 32, 'LUK.19.32', 'So those who were sent went out and found it just as Jesus had told them.'),
('LUK', 19, 33, 'LUK.19.33', 'As they were untying the colt, its owners asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”'),
('LUK', 19, 34, 'LUK.19.34', '“The Lord needs it,” they answered.'),
('LUK', 19, 35, 'LUK.19.35', 'Then they led the colt to Jesus, threw their cloaks over it, and put Jesus on it.'),
('LUK', 19, 36, 'LUK.19.36', 'As He rode along, the people spread their cloaks on the road.'),
('LUK', 19, 37, 'LUK.19.37', 'And as He approached the descent from the Mount of Olives, the whole multitude of disciples began to praise God joyfully in a loud voice for all the miracles they had seen:'),
('LUK', 19, 38, 'LUK.19.38', '“Blessed is the King who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Peace in heaven and glory in the highest!”'),
('LUK', 19, 39, 'LUK.19.39', 'But some of the Pharisees in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, rebuke Your disciples!”'),
('LUK', 19, 40, 'LUK.19.40', '“I tell you,” He answered, “if they remain silent, the very stones will cry out.”'),
('LUK', 19, 41, 'LUK.19.41', 'As Jesus approached Jerusalem and saw the city, He wept over it'),
('LUK', 19, 42, 'LUK.19.42', 'and said, “If only you had known on this day what would bring you peace! But now it is hidden from your eyes.'),
('LUK', 19, 43, 'LUK.19.43', 'For the days will come upon you when your enemies will barricade you and surround you and hem you in on every side.'),
('LUK', 19, 44, 'LUK.19.44', 'They will level you to the ground—you and the children within your walls. They will not leave one stone on another, because you did not recognize the time of your visitation from God.”'),
('LUK', 19, 45, 'LUK.19.45', 'Then Jesus entered the temple courts and began to drive out those who were selling there.'),
('LUK', 19, 46, 'LUK.19.46', 'He declared to them, “It is written: ‘My house will be a house of prayer.’ But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”'),
('LUK', 19, 47, 'LUK.19.47', 'Jesus was teaching at the temple every day, but the chief priests, scribes, and leaders of the people were intent on killing Him.'),
('LUK', 19, 48, 'LUK.19.48', 'Yet they could not find a way to do so, because all the people hung on His words.'),
('LUK', 20, 1, 'LUK.20.1', 'One day as Jesus was teaching the people in the temple courts and proclaiming the gospel, the chief priests and scribes, together with the elders, came up to Him.'),
('LUK', 20, 2, 'LUK.20.2', '“Tell us,” they said, “by what authority are You doing these things, and who gave You this authority?”'),
('LUK', 20, 3, 'LUK.20.3', '“I will also ask you a question,” Jesus replied. “Tell Me:'),
('LUK', 20, 4, 'LUK.20.4', 'John’s baptism—was it from heaven, or from men?”'),
('LUK', 20, 5, 'LUK.20.5', 'They deliberated among themselves and said, “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why did you not believe him?’'),
('LUK', 20, 6, 'LUK.20.6', 'But if we say, ‘From men,’ all the people will stone us, for they are convinced that John was a prophet.”'),
('LUK', 20, 7, 'LUK.20.7', 'So they answered that they did not know where it was from.'),
('LUK', 20, 8, 'LUK.20.8', 'And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”'),
('LUK', 20, 9, 'LUK.20.9', 'Then He proceeded to tell the people this parable: “A man planted a vineyard, rented it out to some tenants, and went away for a long time.'),
('LUK', 20, 10, 'LUK.20.10', 'At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard. But the tenants beat the servant and sent him away empty-handed.'),
('LUK', 20, 11, 'LUK.20.11', 'So he sent another servant, but they beat him and treated him shamefully, sending him away empty-handed.'),
('LUK', 20, 12, 'LUK.20.12', 'Then he sent a third, but they wounded him and threw him out.'),
('LUK', 20, 13, 'LUK.20.13', '‘What shall I do?’ asked the owner of the vineyard. ‘I will send my beloved son. Perhaps they will respect him.’'),
('LUK', 20, 14, 'LUK.20.14', 'But when the tenants saw the son, they discussed it among themselves and said, ‘This is the heir. Let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’'),
('LUK', 20, 15, 'LUK.20.15', 'So they threw him out of the vineyard and killed him. What then will the owner of the vineyard do to them?'),
('LUK', 20, 16, 'LUK.20.16', 'He will come and kill those tenants and give the vineyard to others.” And when the people heard this, they said, “May such a thing never happen!”'),
('LUK', 20, 17, 'LUK.20.17', 'But Jesus looked directly at them and said, “Then what is the meaning of that which is written: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone’?'),
('LUK', 20, 18, 'LUK.20.18', 'Everyone who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces, but he on whom it falls will be crushed.”'),
('LUK', 20, 19, 'LUK.20.19', 'When the scribes and chief priests realized that Jesus had spoken this parable against them, they sought to arrest Him that very hour. But they were afraid of the people.'),
('LUK', 20, 20, 'LUK.20.20', 'So they watched Him closely and sent spies who pretended to be sincere. They were hoping to catch Him in His words in order to hand Him over to the rule and authority of the governor.'),
('LUK', 20, 21, 'LUK.20.21', '“Teacher,” they inquired, “we know that You speak and teach correctly. You show no partiality but teach the way of God in accordance with the truth.'),
('LUK', 20, 22, 'LUK.20.22', 'Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to Caesar or not?”'),
('LUK', 20, 23, 'LUK.20.23', 'But Jesus saw through their duplicity and said to them,'),
('LUK', 20, 24, 'LUK.20.24', '“Show Me a denarius. Whose image and inscription are on it?” “Caesar’s,” they answered.'),
('LUK', 20, 25, 'LUK.20.25', 'So Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.”'),
('LUK', 20, 26, 'LUK.20.26', 'And they were unable to trap Him in His words before the people. And amazed at His answer, they fell silent.'),
('LUK', 20, 27, 'LUK.20.27', 'Then some of the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to question Him.'),
('LUK', 20, 28, 'LUK.20.28', '“Teacher,” they said, “Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies and leaves a wife but no children, the man is to marry his brother’s widow and raise up offspring for him.'),
('LUK', 20, 29, 'LUK.20.29', 'Now there were seven brothers. The first one married a wife but died childless.'),
('LUK', 20, 30, 'LUK.20.30', 'Then the second'),
('LUK', 20, 31, 'LUK.20.31', 'and the third married the widow, and in the same way all seven died, leaving no children.'),
('LUK', 20, 32, 'LUK.20.32', 'And last of all, the woman died.'),
('LUK', 20, 33, 'LUK.20.33', 'So then, in the resurrection, whose wife will she be? For all seven were married to her.”'),
('LUK', 20, 34, 'LUK.20.34', 'Jesus answered, “The sons of this age marry and are given in marriage.'),
('LUK', 20, 35, 'LUK.20.35', 'But those who are considered worthy to share in the age to come and in the resurrection from the dead will neither marry nor be given in marriage.'),
('LUK', 20, 36, 'LUK.20.36', 'In fact, they can no longer die, because they are like the angels. And since they are sons of the resurrection, they are sons of God.'),
('LUK', 20, 37, 'LUK.20.37', 'Even Moses demonstrates that the dead are raised, in the passage about the burning bush. For he calls the Lord ‘the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.’'),
('LUK', 20, 38, 'LUK.20.38', 'He is not the God of the dead, but of the living, for to Him all are alive.”'),
('LUK', 20, 39, 'LUK.20.39', 'Some of the scribes answered, “Teacher, You have spoken well!”'),
('LUK', 20, 40, 'LUK.20.40', 'And they did not dare to question Him any further.'),
('LUK', 20, 41, 'LUK.20.41', 'Then Jesus declared, “How can it be said that the Christ is the Son of David?'),
('LUK', 20, 42, 'LUK.20.42', 'For David himself says in the book of Psalms: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand'),
('LUK', 20, 43, 'LUK.20.43', 'until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”’'),
('LUK', 20, 44, 'LUK.20.44', 'Thus David calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be David’s son?”'),
('LUK', 20, 45, 'LUK.20.45', 'In the hearing of all the people, Jesus said to His disciples,'),
('LUK', 20, 46, 'LUK.20.46', '“Beware of the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, and they love the greetings in the marketplaces, the chief seats in the synagogues, and the places of honor at banquets.'),
('LUK', 20, 47, 'LUK.20.47', 'They defraud widows of their houses, and for a show make lengthy prayers. These men will receive greater condemnation.”'),
('LUK', 21, 1, 'LUK.21.1', 'Then Jesus looked up and saw the rich putting their gifts into the treasury,'),
('LUK', 21, 2, 'LUK.21.2', 'and He saw a poor widow put in two small copper coins.'),
('LUK', 21, 3, 'LUK.21.3', '“Truly I tell you,” He said, “this poor widow has put in more than all the others.'),
('LUK', 21, 4, 'LUK.21.4', 'For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”'),
('LUK', 21, 5, 'LUK.21.5', 'As some of the disciples were remarking how the temple was adorned with beautiful stones and consecrated gifts, Jesus said,'),
('LUK', 21, 6, 'LUK.21.6', '“As for what you see here, the time will come when not one stone will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”'),
('LUK', 21, 7, 'LUK.21.7', '“Teacher,” they asked, “when will these things happen? And what will be the sign that they are about to take place?”'),
('LUK', 21, 8, 'LUK.21.8', 'Jesus answered, “See to it that you are not deceived. For many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am He,’ and, ‘The time is near.’ Do not follow them.'),
('LUK', 21, 9, 'LUK.21.9', 'When you hear of wars and rebellions, do not be alarmed. These things must happen first, but the end is not imminent.”'),
('LUK', 21, 10, 'LUK.21.10', 'Then He told them, “Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom.'),
('LUK', 21, 11, 'LUK.21.11', 'There will be great earthquakes, famines, and pestilences in various places, along with fearful sights and great signs from heaven.'),
('LUK', 21, 12, 'LUK.21.12', 'But before all this, they will seize you and persecute you. On account of My name they will deliver you to the synagogues and prisons, and they will bring you before kings and governors.'),
('LUK', 21, 13, 'LUK.21.13', 'This will be your opportunity to serve as witnesses.'),
('LUK', 21, 14, 'LUK.21.14', 'So make up your mind not to worry beforehand how to defend yourselves.'),
('LUK', 21, 15, 'LUK.21.15', 'For I will give you speech and wisdom that none of your adversaries will be able to resist or contradict.'),
('LUK', 21, 16, 'LUK.21.16', 'You will be betrayed even by parents and brothers and relatives and friends, and some of you will be put to death.'),
('LUK', 21, 17, 'LUK.21.17', 'And you will be hated by everyone because of My name.'),
('LUK', 21, 18, 'LUK.21.18', 'Yet not even a hair of your head will perish.'),
('LUK', 21, 19, 'LUK.21.19', 'By your patient endurance you will gain your souls.'),
('LUK', 21, 20, 'LUK.21.20', 'But when you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, you will know that her desolation is near.'),
('LUK', 21, 21, 'LUK.21.21', 'Then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains, let those in the city get out, and let those in the country stay out of the city.'),
('LUK', 21, 22, 'LUK.21.22', 'For these are the days of vengeance, to fulfill all that is written.'),
('LUK', 21, 23, 'LUK.21.23', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers! For there will be great distress upon the land and wrath against this people.'),
('LUK', 21, 24, 'LUK.21.24', 'They will fall by the edge of the sword and be led captive into all the nations. And Jerusalem will be trodden down by the Gentiles, until the times of the Gentiles are fulfilled.'),
('LUK', 21, 25, 'LUK.21.25', 'There will be signs in the sun and moon and stars, and on the earth dismay among the nations, bewildered by the roaring of the sea and the surging of the waves.'),
('LUK', 21, 26, 'LUK.21.26', 'Men will faint from fear and anxiety over what is coming upon the earth, for the powers of the heavens will be shaken.'),
('LUK', 21, 27, 'LUK.21.27', 'At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in a cloud with power and great glory.'),
('LUK', 21, 28, 'LUK.21.28', 'When these things begin to happen, stand up and lift up your heads, because your redemption is drawing near.”'),
('LUK', 21, 29, 'LUK.21.29', 'Then Jesus told them a parable: “Look at the fig tree and all the trees.'),
('LUK', 21, 30, 'LUK.21.30', 'When they sprout leaves, you can see for yourselves and know that summer is near.'),
('LUK', 21, 31, 'LUK.21.31', 'So also, when you see these things happening, know that the kingdom of God is near.'),
('LUK', 21, 32, 'LUK.21.32', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.'),
('LUK', 21, 33, 'LUK.21.33', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.'),
('LUK', 21, 34, 'LUK.21.34', 'But watch yourselves, or your hearts will be weighed down by dissipation, drunkenness, and the worries of life—and that day will spring upon you suddenly like a snare.'),
('LUK', 21, 35, 'LUK.21.35', 'For it will come upon all who dwell on the face of all the earth.'),
('LUK', 21, 36, 'LUK.21.36', 'So keep watch at all times, and pray that you may have the strength to escape all that is about to happen and to stand before the Son of Man.”'),
('LUK', 21, 37, 'LUK.21.37', 'Every day Jesus taught at the temple, but every evening He went out to spend the night on the Mount of Olives.'),
('LUK', 21, 38, 'LUK.21.38', 'And early in the morning all the people would come to hear Him at the temple.'),
('LUK', 22, 1, 'LUK.22.1', 'Now the Feast of Unleavened Bread, called the Passover, was approaching,'),
('LUK', 22, 2, 'LUK.22.2', 'and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a way to put Jesus to death, for they feared the people.'),
('LUK', 22, 3, 'LUK.22.3', 'Then Satan entered Judas Iscariot, who was one of the Twelve.'),
('LUK', 22, 4, 'LUK.22.4', 'And Judas went to discuss with the chief priests and temple officers how he might betray Jesus to them.'),
('LUK', 22, 5, 'LUK.22.5', 'They were delighted and agreed to give him money.'),
('LUK', 22, 6, 'LUK.22.6', 'Judas consented, and began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus to them in the absence of a crowd.'),
('LUK', 22, 7, 'LUK.22.7', 'Then came the day of Unleavened Bread on which the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed.'),
('LUK', 22, 8, 'LUK.22.8', 'Jesus sent Peter and John, saying, “Go and make preparations for us to eat the Passover.”'),
('LUK', 22, 9, 'LUK.22.9', '“Where do You want us to prepare it?” they asked.'),
('LUK', 22, 10, 'LUK.22.10', 'He answered, “When you enter the city, a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him to the house he enters,'),
('LUK', 22, 11, 'LUK.22.11', 'and say to the owner of that house, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’'),
('LUK', 22, 12, 'LUK.22.12', 'And he will show you a large upper room, already furnished. Make preparations there.”'),
('LUK', 22, 13, 'LUK.22.13', 'So they went and found it just as Jesus had told them. And they prepared the Passover.'),
('LUK', 22, 14, 'LUK.22.14', 'When the hour had come, Jesus reclined at the table with His apostles.'),
('LUK', 22, 15, 'LUK.22.15', 'And He said to them, “I have eagerly desired to eat this Passover with you before My suffering.'),
('LUK', 22, 16, 'LUK.22.16', 'For I tell you that I will not eat it again until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.”'),
('LUK', 22, 17, 'LUK.22.17', 'After taking the cup, He gave thanks and said, “Take this and divide it among yourselves.'),
('LUK', 22, 18, 'LUK.22.18', 'For I tell you that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine from now on until the kingdom of God comes.”'),
('LUK', 22, 19, 'LUK.22.19', 'And He took the bread, gave thanks and broke it, and gave it to them, saying, “This is My body, given for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”'),
('LUK', 22, 20, 'LUK.22.20', 'In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood, which is poured out for you.'),
('LUK', 22, 21, 'LUK.22.21', 'Look! The hand of My betrayer is with Mine on the table.'),
('LUK', 22, 22, 'LUK.22.22', 'Indeed, the Son of Man will go as it has been determined, but woe to that man who betrays Him.”'),
('LUK', 22, 23, 'LUK.22.23', 'Then they began to question among themselves which of them was going to do this.'),
('LUK', 22, 24, 'LUK.22.24', 'A dispute also arose among the disciples as to which of them should be considered the greatest.'),
('LUK', 22, 25, 'LUK.22.25', 'So Jesus declared, “The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those in authority over them call themselves benefactors.'),
('LUK', 22, 26, 'LUK.22.26', 'But you shall not be like them. Instead, the greatest among you should be like the youngest, and the one who leads like the one who serves.'),
('LUK', 22, 27, 'LUK.22.27', 'For who is greater, the one who reclines at the table or the one who serves? Is it not the one who reclines? But I am among you as one who serves.'),
('LUK', 22, 28, 'LUK.22.28', 'You are the ones who have stood by Me in My trials.'),
('LUK', 22, 29, 'LUK.22.29', 'And I bestow on you a kingdom, just as My Father has bestowed one on Me,'),
('LUK', 22, 30, 'LUK.22.30', 'so that you may eat and drink at My table in My kingdom and sit on thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.'),
('LUK', 22, 31, 'LUK.22.31', 'Simon, Simon, Satan has asked to sift all of you like wheat.'),
('LUK', 22, 32, 'LUK.22.32', 'But I have prayed for you, Simon, that your faith will not fail. And when you have turned back, strengthen your brothers.”'),
('LUK', 22, 33, 'LUK.22.33', '“Lord,” said Peter, “I am ready to go with You even to prison and to death.”'),
('LUK', 22, 34, 'LUK.22.34', 'But Jesus replied, “I tell you, Peter, the rooster will not crow today until you have denied three times that you know Me.”'),
('LUK', 22, 35, 'LUK.22.35', 'Then Jesus asked them, “When I sent you out without purse or bag or sandals, did you lack anything?” “Nothing,” they answered.'),
('LUK', 22, 36, 'LUK.22.36', '“Now, however,” He told them, “the one with a purse should take it, and likewise a bag; and the one without a sword should sell his cloak and buy one.'),
('LUK', 22, 37, 'LUK.22.37', 'For I tell you that this Scripture must be fulfilled in Me: ‘And He was numbered with the transgressors.’ For what is written about Me is reaching its fulfillment.”'),
('LUK', 22, 38, 'LUK.22.38', 'So they said, “Look, Lord, here are two swords.” “That is enough,” He answered.'),
('LUK', 22, 39, 'LUK.22.39', 'Jesus went out as usual to the Mount of Olives, and the disciples followed Him.'),
('LUK', 22, 40, 'LUK.22.40', 'When He came to the place, He told them, “Pray that you will not enter into temptation.”'),
('LUK', 22, 41, 'LUK.22.41', 'And He withdrew about a stone’s throw beyond them, where He knelt down and prayed,'),
('LUK', 22, 42, 'LUK.22.42', '“Father, if You are willing, take this cup from Me. Yet not My will, but Yours be done.”'),
('LUK', 22, 43, 'LUK.22.43', 'Then an angel from heaven appeared to Him and strengthened Him.'),
('LUK', 22, 44, 'LUK.22.44', 'And in His anguish, He prayed more earnestly, and His sweat became like drops of blood falling to the ground.'),
('LUK', 22, 45, 'LUK.22.45', 'When Jesus rose from prayer and returned to the disciples, He found them asleep, exhausted from sorrow.'),
('LUK', 22, 46, 'LUK.22.46', '“Why are you sleeping?” He asked. “Get up and pray so that you will not enter into temptation.”'),
('LUK', 22, 47, 'LUK.22.47', 'While He was still speaking, a crowd arrived, led by the man called Judas, one of the Twelve. He approached Jesus to kiss Him.'),
('LUK', 22, 48, 'LUK.22.48', 'But Jesus asked him, “Judas, are you betraying the Son of Man with a kiss?”'),
('LUK', 22, 49, 'LUK.22.49', 'Those around Jesus saw what was about to happen and said, “Lord, should we strike with our swords?”'),
('LUK', 22, 50, 'LUK.22.50', 'And one of them struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear.'),
('LUK', 22, 51, 'LUK.22.51', 'But Jesus answered, “No more of this!” And He touched the man’s ear and healed him.'),
('LUK', 22, 52, 'LUK.22.52', 'Then Jesus said to the chief priests, temple officers, and elders who had come for Him, “Have you come out with swords and clubs as you would against an outlaw?'),
('LUK', 22, 53, 'LUK.22.53', 'Every day I was with you in the temple courts, and you did not lay a hand on Me. But this hour belongs to you and to the power of darkness.”'),
('LUK', 22, 54, 'LUK.22.54', 'Then they seized Jesus, led Him away, and took Him into the house of the high priest. And Peter followed at a distance.'),
('LUK', 22, 55, 'LUK.22.55', 'When those present had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and sat down together, Peter sat down among them.'),
('LUK', 22, 56, 'LUK.22.56', 'A servant girl saw him seated in the firelight and looked intently at him. “This man also was with Him,” she said.'),
('LUK', 22, 57, 'LUK.22.57', 'But Peter denied it. “Woman, I do not know Him,” he said.'),
('LUK', 22, 58, 'LUK.22.58', 'A short time later, someone else saw him and said, “You also are one of them.” But Peter said, “Man, I am not.”'),
('LUK', 22, 59, 'LUK.22.59', 'About an hour later, another man insisted, “Certainly this man was with Him, for he too is a Galilean.”'),
('LUK', 22, 60, 'LUK.22.60', '“Man, I do not know what you are talking about,” Peter replied. And immediately, while he was still speaking, the rooster crowed.'),
('LUK', 22, 61, 'LUK.22.61', 'And the Lord turned and looked at Peter. Then Peter remembered the word that the Lord had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows today, you will deny Me three times.”'),
('LUK', 22, 62, 'LUK.22.62', 'And he went outside and wept bitterly.'),
('LUK', 22, 63, 'LUK.22.63', 'The men who were holding Jesus began to mock Him and beat Him.'),
('LUK', 22, 64, 'LUK.22.64', 'They blindfolded Him and kept demanding, “Prophesy! Who hit You?”'),
('LUK', 22, 65, 'LUK.22.65', 'And they said many other blasphemous things against Him.'),
('LUK', 22, 66, 'LUK.22.66', 'At daybreak the council of the elders of the people, both the chief priests and scribes, met together. They led Jesus into their Sanhedrin and said,'),
('LUK', 22, 67, 'LUK.22.67', '“If You are the Christ, tell us.” Jesus answered, “If I tell you, you will not believe.'),
('LUK', 22, 68, 'LUK.22.68', 'And if I ask you a question, you will not answer.'),
('LUK', 22, 69, 'LUK.22.69', 'But from now on the Son of Man will be seated at the right hand of the power of God.”'),
('LUK', 22, 70, 'LUK.22.70', 'So they all asked, “Are You then the Son of God?” He replied, “You say that I am.”'),
('LUK', 22, 71, 'LUK.22.71', '“Why do we need any more testimony?” they declared. “We have heard it for ourselves from His own lips.”'),
('LUK', 23, 1, 'LUK.23.1', 'Then the whole council rose and led Jesus away to Pilate.'),
('LUK', 23, 2, 'LUK.23.2', 'And they began to accuse Him, saying, “We found this man subverting our nation, forbidding payment of taxes to Caesar, and proclaiming Himself to be Christ, a King.”'),
('LUK', 23, 3, 'LUK.23.3', 'So Pilate asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.'),
('LUK', 23, 4, 'LUK.23.4', 'Then Pilate said to the chief priests and the crowds, “I find no basis for a charge against this man.”'),
('LUK', 23, 5, 'LUK.23.5', 'But they kept insisting, “He stirs up the people all over Judea with His teaching. He began in Galilee and has come all the way here.”'),
('LUK', 23, 6, 'LUK.23.6', 'When Pilate heard this, he asked if the man was a Galilean.'),
('LUK', 23, 7, 'LUK.23.7', 'And learning that Jesus was under Herod’s jurisdiction, he sent Him to Herod, who himself was in Jerusalem at that time.'),
('LUK', 23, 8, 'LUK.23.8', 'When Herod saw Jesus, he was greatly pleased. He had wanted to see Him for a long time, because he had heard about Him and was hoping to see Him perform a miracle.'),
('LUK', 23, 9, 'LUK.23.9', 'Herod questioned Jesus at great length, but He gave no answer.'),
('LUK', 23, 10, 'LUK.23.10', 'Meanwhile, the chief priests and scribes stood there, vehemently accusing Him.'),
('LUK', 23, 11, 'LUK.23.11', 'And even Herod and his soldiers ridiculed and mocked Him. Dressing Him in a fine robe, they sent Him back to Pilate.'),
('LUK', 23, 12, 'LUK.23.12', 'That day Herod and Pilate became friends; before this time they had been enemies.'),
('LUK', 23, 13, 'LUK.23.13', 'Then Pilate called together the chief priests, the rulers, and the people,'),
('LUK', 23, 14, 'LUK.23.14', 'and said to them, “You brought me this man as one who was inciting the people to rebellion. I have examined Him here in your presence and found Him not guilty of your charges against Him.'),
('LUK', 23, 15, 'LUK.23.15', 'Neither has Herod, for he sent Him back to us. As you can see, He has done nothing deserving of death.'),
('LUK', 23, 16, 'LUK.23.16', 'Therefore I will punish Him and release Him.”'),
('LUK', 23, 18, 'LUK.23.18', 'But they all cried out in unison: “Away with this man! Release Barabbas to us!”'),
('LUK', 23, 19, 'LUK.23.19', '(Barabbas had been imprisoned for an insurrection in the city, and for murder.)'),
('LUK', 23, 20, 'LUK.23.20', 'Wanting to release Jesus, Pilate addressed them again,'),
('LUK', 23, 21, 'LUK.23.21', 'but they kept shouting, “Crucify Him! Crucify Him!”'),
('LUK', 23, 22, 'LUK.23.22', 'A third time he said to them, “What evil has this man done? I have found in Him no offense worthy of death. So after I punish Him, I will release Him.”'),
('LUK', 23, 23, 'LUK.23.23', 'But they were insistent, demanding with loud voices for Jesus to be crucified. And their clamor prevailed.'),
('LUK', 23, 24, 'LUK.23.24', 'So Pilate sentenced that their demand be met.'),
('LUK', 23, 25, 'LUK.23.25', 'As they had requested, he released the one imprisoned for insurrection and murder, and he handed Jesus over to their will.'),
('LUK', 23, 26, 'LUK.23.26', 'As the soldiers led Him away, they seized Simon of Cyrene on his way in from the country, and they put the cross on him to carry behind Jesus.'),
('LUK', 23, 27, 'LUK.23.27', 'A great number of people followed Him, including women who kept mourning and wailing for Him.'),
('LUK', 23, 28, 'LUK.23.28', 'But Jesus turned to them and said, “Daughters of Jerusalem, do not weep for Me, but weep for yourselves and for your children.'),
('LUK', 23, 29, 'LUK.23.29', 'Look, the days are coming when people will say, ‘Blessed are the barren women, the wombs that never bore, and breasts that never nursed!’'),
('LUK', 23, 30, 'LUK.23.30', 'At that time ‘they will say to the mountains, “Fall on us!” and to the hills, “Cover us!”’'),
('LUK', 23, 31, 'LUK.23.31', 'For if men do these things while the tree is green, what will happen when it is dry?”'),
('LUK', 23, 32, 'LUK.23.32', 'Two others, who were criminals, were also led away to be executed with Jesus.'),
('LUK', 23, 33, 'LUK.23.33', 'When they came to the place called The Skull, they crucified Him there, along with the criminals, one on His right and the other on His left.'),
('LUK', 23, 34, 'LUK.23.34', 'Then Jesus said, “Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing.” And they divided up His garments by casting lots.'),
('LUK', 23, 35, 'LUK.23.35', 'The people stood watching, and the rulers sneered at Him, saying, “He saved others; let Him save Himself if He is the Christ of God, the Chosen One.”'),
('LUK', 23, 36, 'LUK.23.36', 'The soldiers also mocked Him and came up to offer Him sour wine.'),
('LUK', 23, 37, 'LUK.23.37', '“If You are the King of the Jews,” they said, “save Yourself!”'),
('LUK', 23, 38, 'LUK.23.38', 'Above Him was posted an inscription: THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.'),
('LUK', 23, 39, 'LUK.23.39', 'One of the criminals who hung there heaped abuse on Him. “Are You not the Christ?” he said. “Save Yourself and us!”'),
('LUK', 23, 40, 'LUK.23.40', 'But the other one rebuked him, saying, “Do you not even fear God, since you are under the same judgment?'),
('LUK', 23, 41, 'LUK.23.41', 'We are punished justly, for we are receiving what our actions deserve. But this man has done nothing wrong.”'),
('LUK', 23, 42, 'LUK.23.42', 'Then he said, “Jesus, remember me when You come into Your kingdom!”'),
('LUK', 23, 43, 'LUK.23.43', 'And Jesus said to him, “Truly I tell you, today you will be with Me in Paradise.”'),
('LUK', 23, 44, 'LUK.23.44', 'It was now about the sixth hour, and darkness came over all the land until the ninth hour.'),
('LUK', 23, 45, 'LUK.23.45', 'The sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was torn down the middle.'),
('LUK', 23, 46, 'LUK.23.46', 'Then Jesus called out in a loud voice, “Father, into Your hands I commit My Spirit.” And when He had said this, He breathed His last.'),
('LUK', 23, 47, 'LUK.23.47', 'When the centurion saw what had happened, he gave glory to God, saying, “Surely this was a righteous man.”'),
('LUK', 23, 48, 'LUK.23.48', 'And when all the people who had gathered for this spectacle saw what had happened, they returned home beating their breasts.'),
('LUK', 23, 49, 'LUK.23.49', 'But all those who knew Jesus, including the women who had followed Him from Galilee, stood at a distance watching these things.'),
('LUK', 23, 50, 'LUK.23.50', 'Now there was a Council member named Joseph, a good and righteous man,'),
('LUK', 23, 51, 'LUK.23.51', 'who had not consented to their decision or action. He was from the Judean town of Arimathea and was waiting for the kingdom of God.'),
('LUK', 23, 52, 'LUK.23.52', 'He went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus.'),
('LUK', 23, 53, 'LUK.23.53', 'Then he took it down, wrapped it in a linen cloth, and placed it in a tomb cut into the rock, where no one had yet been laid.'),
('LUK', 23, 54, 'LUK.23.54', 'It was Preparation Day, and the Sabbath was beginning.'),
('LUK', 23, 55, 'LUK.23.55', 'The women who had come with Jesus from Galilee followed, and they saw the tomb and how His body was placed.'),
('LUK', 23, 56, 'LUK.23.56', 'Then they returned to prepare spices and perfumes. And they rested on the Sabbath, according to the commandment.'),
('LUK', 24, 1, 'LUK.24.1', 'On the first day of the week, very early in the morning, the women came to the tomb, bringing the spices they had prepared.'),
('LUK', 24, 2, 'LUK.24.2', 'They found the stone rolled away from the tomb,'),
('LUK', 24, 3, 'LUK.24.3', 'but when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.'),
('LUK', 24, 4, 'LUK.24.4', 'While they were puzzling over this, suddenly two men in radiant apparel stood beside them.'),
('LUK', 24, 5, 'LUK.24.5', 'As the women bowed their faces to the ground in terror, the two men asked them, “Why do you look for the living among the dead?'),
('LUK', 24, 6, 'LUK.24.6', 'He is not here; He has risen! Remember how He told you while He was still in Galilee:'),
('LUK', 24, 7, 'LUK.24.7', '‘The Son of Man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and on the third day rise again.’”'),
('LUK', 24, 8, 'LUK.24.8', 'Then they remembered His words.'),
('LUK', 24, 9, 'LUK.24.9', 'And when they returned from the tomb, they reported all these things to the Eleven and to all the others.'),
('LUK', 24, 10, 'LUK.24.10', 'It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the mother of James, and the other women with them who told this to the apostles.'),
('LUK', 24, 11, 'LUK.24.11', 'But their words seemed like nonsense to them, and they did not believe the women.'),
('LUK', 24, 12, 'LUK.24.12', 'Peter, however, got up and ran to the tomb. And after bending down and seeing only the linen cloths, he went away, wondering to himself what had happened.'),
('LUK', 24, 13, 'LUK.24.13', 'That same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles from Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 24, 14, 'LUK.24.14', 'They were talking with each other about everything that had happened.'),
('LUK', 24, 15, 'LUK.24.15', 'And as they talked and deliberated, Jesus Himself came up and walked along with them.'),
('LUK', 24, 16, 'LUK.24.16', 'But their eyes were kept from recognizing Him.'),
('LUK', 24, 17, 'LUK.24.17', 'He asked them, “What are you discussing so intently as you walk along?” They stood still, with sadness on their faces.'),
('LUK', 24, 18, 'LUK.24.18', 'One of them, named Cleopas, asked Him, “Are You the only visitor to Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in recent days?”'),
('LUK', 24, 19, 'LUK.24.19', '“What things?” He asked. “The events involving Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. “This man was a prophet, powerful in speech and action before God and all the people.'),
('LUK', 24, 20, 'LUK.24.20', 'Our chief priests and rulers delivered Him up to the sentence of death, and they crucified Him.'),
('LUK', 24, 21, 'LUK.24.21', 'But we were hoping He was the One who would redeem Israel. And besides all this, it is the third day since these things took place.'),
('LUK', 24, 22, 'LUK.24.22', 'Furthermore, some of our women astounded us. They were at the tomb early this morning,'),
('LUK', 24, 23, 'LUK.24.23', 'but they did not find His body. They came and told us they had seen a vision of angels, who said that Jesus was alive.'),
('LUK', 24, 24, 'LUK.24.24', 'Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had described. But Him they did not see.”'),
('LUK', 24, 25, 'LUK.24.25', 'Then Jesus said to them, “O foolish ones, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken!'),
('LUK', 24, 26, 'LUK.24.26', 'Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things and then to enter His glory?”'),
('LUK', 24, 27, 'LUK.24.27', 'And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what was written in all the Scriptures about Himself.'),
('LUK', 24, 28, 'LUK.24.28', 'As they approached the village where they were headed, He seemed to be going farther.'),
('LUK', 24, 29, 'LUK.24.29', 'But they pleaded with Him, “Stay with us, for it is nearly evening and the day is almost over.” So He went in to stay with them.'),
('LUK', 24, 30, 'LUK.24.30', 'While He was reclining at the table with them, He took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to them.'),
('LUK', 24, 31, 'LUK.24.31', 'Then their eyes were opened and they recognized Jesus—and He disappeared from their sight.'),
('LUK', 24, 32, 'LUK.24.32', 'They asked each other, “Were not our hearts burning within us as He spoke with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?”'),
('LUK', 24, 33, 'LUK.24.33', 'And they got up that very hour and returned to Jerusalem. There they found the Eleven and those with them, gathered together'),
('LUK', 24, 34, 'LUK.24.34', 'and saying, “The Lord has indeed risen and has appeared to Simon!”'),
('LUK', 24, 35, 'LUK.24.35', 'Then the two told what had happened on the road, and how they had recognized Jesus in the breaking of the bread.'),
('LUK', 24, 36, 'LUK.24.36', 'While they were describing these events, Jesus Himself stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”'),
('LUK', 24, 37, 'LUK.24.37', 'But they were startled and frightened, thinking they had seen a spirit.'),
('LUK', 24, 38, 'LUK.24.38', '“Why are you troubled,” Jesus asked, “and why do doubts arise in your hearts?'),
('LUK', 24, 39, 'LUK.24.39', 'Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself. Touch Me and see—for a spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.”'),
('LUK', 24, 40, 'LUK.24.40', 'And when He had said this, He showed them His hands and feet.'),
('LUK', 24, 41, 'LUK.24.41', 'While they were still in disbelief because of their joy and amazement, He asked them, “Do you have anything here to eat?”'),
('LUK', 24, 42, 'LUK.24.42', 'So they gave Him a piece of broiled fish,'),
('LUK', 24, 43, 'LUK.24.43', 'and He took it and ate it in front of them.'),
('LUK', 24, 44, 'LUK.24.44', 'Jesus said to them, “These are the words I spoke to you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that is written about Me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and the Psalms.”'),
('LUK', 24, 45, 'LUK.24.45', 'Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures.'),
('LUK', 24, 46, 'LUK.24.46', 'And He told them, “This is what is written: The Christ will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day,'),
('LUK', 24, 47, 'LUK.24.47', 'and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem.'),
('LUK', 24, 48, 'LUK.24.48', 'You are witnesses of these things.'),
('LUK', 24, 49, 'LUK.24.49', 'And behold, I am sending the promise of My Father upon you. But remain in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.”'),
('LUK', 24, 50, 'LUK.24.50', 'When Jesus had led them out as far as Bethany, He lifted up His hands and blessed them.'),
('LUK', 24, 51, 'LUK.24.51', 'While He was blessing them, He left them and was carried up into heaven.'),
('LUK', 24, 52, 'LUK.24.52', 'And they worshiped Him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,'),
('LUK', 24, 53, 'LUK.24.53', 'praising God continually in the temple.'),
('JHN', 1, 1, 'JHN.1.1', 'In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.'),
('JHN', 1, 2, 'JHN.1.2', 'He was with God in the beginning.'),
('JHN', 1, 3, 'JHN.1.3', 'Through Him all things were made, and without Him nothing was made that has been made.'),
('JHN', 1, 4, 'JHN.1.4', 'In Him was life, and that life was the light of men.'),
('JHN', 1, 5, 'JHN.1.5', 'The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.'),
('JHN', 1, 6, 'JHN.1.6', 'There came a man who was sent from God. His name was John.'),
('JHN', 1, 7, 'JHN.1.7', 'He came as a witness to testify about the Light, so that through him everyone might believe.'),
('JHN', 1, 8, 'JHN.1.8', 'He himself was not the Light, but he came to testify about the Light.'),
('JHN', 1, 9, 'JHN.1.9', 'The true Light, who gives light to everyone, was coming into the world.'),
('JHN', 1, 10, 'JHN.1.10', 'He was in the world, and though the world was made through Him, the world did not recognize Him.'),
('JHN', 1, 11, 'JHN.1.11', 'He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him.'),
('JHN', 1, 12, 'JHN.1.12', 'But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God—'),
('JHN', 1, 13, 'JHN.1.13', 'children born not of blood, nor of the desire or will of man, but born of God.'),
('JHN', 1, 14, 'JHN.1.14', 'The Word became flesh and made His dwelling among us. We have seen His glory, the glory of the one and only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.'),
('JHN', 1, 15, 'JHN.1.15', 'John testified concerning Him. He cried out, saying, “This is He of whom I said, ‘He who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’”'),
('JHN', 1, 16, 'JHN.1.16', 'From His fullness we have all received grace upon grace.'),
('JHN', 1, 17, 'JHN.1.17', 'For the law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus Christ.'),
('JHN', 1, 18, 'JHN.1.18', 'No one has ever seen God, but the one and only Son, who is Himself God and is at the Father’s side, has made Him known.'),
('JHN', 1, 19, 'JHN.1.19', 'And this was John’s testimony when the Jews of Jerusalem sent priests and Levites to ask him, “Who are you?”'),
('JHN', 1, 20, 'JHN.1.20', 'He did not refuse to confess, but openly declared, “I am not the Christ.”'),
('JHN', 1, 21, 'JHN.1.21', '“Then who are you?” they inquired. “Are you Elijah?” He said, “I am not.” “Are you the Prophet?” He answered, “No.”'),
('JHN', 1, 22, 'JHN.1.22', 'So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?”'),
('JHN', 1, 23, 'JHN.1.23', 'John replied in the words of Isaiah the prophet: “I am a voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way for the Lord.’”'),
('JHN', 1, 24, 'JHN.1.24', 'Then the Pharisees who had been sent'),
('JHN', 1, 25, 'JHN.1.25', 'asked him, “Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?”'),
('JHN', 1, 26, 'JHN.1.26', '“I baptize with water,” John replied, “but among you stands One you do not know.'),
('JHN', 1, 27, 'JHN.1.27', 'He is the One who comes after me, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.”'),
('JHN', 1, 28, 'JHN.1.28', 'All this happened at Bethany beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing.'),
('JHN', 1, 29, 'JHN.1.29', 'The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him and said, “Look, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!'),
('JHN', 1, 30, 'JHN.1.30', 'This is He of whom I said, ‘A man who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’'),
('JHN', 1, 31, 'JHN.1.31', 'I myself did not know Him, but the reason I came baptizing with water was that He might be revealed to Israel.”'),
('JHN', 1, 32, 'JHN.1.32', 'Then John testified, “I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove and resting on Him.'),
('JHN', 1, 33, 'JHN.1.33', 'I myself did not know Him, but the One who sent me to baptize with water told me, ‘The man on whom you see the Spirit descend and rest is He who will baptize with the Holy Spirit.’'),
('JHN', 1, 34, 'JHN.1.34', 'I have seen and testified that this is the Son of God.”'),
('JHN', 1, 35, 'JHN.1.35', 'The next day John was there again with two of his disciples.'),
('JHN', 1, 36, 'JHN.1.36', 'When he saw Jesus walking by, he said, “Look, the Lamb of God!”'),
('JHN', 1, 37, 'JHN.1.37', 'And when the two disciples heard him say this, they followed Jesus.'),
('JHN', 1, 38, 'JHN.1.38', 'Jesus turned and saw them following. “What do you want?” He asked. They said to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”'),
('JHN', 1, 39, 'JHN.1.39', '“Come and see,” He replied. So they went and saw where He was staying, and spent that day with Him. It was about the tenth hour.'),
('JHN', 1, 40, 'JHN.1.40', 'Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, was one of the two who heard John’s testimony and followed Jesus.'),
('JHN', 1, 41, 'JHN.1.41', 'He first found his brother Simon and told him, “We have found the Messiah” (which is translated as Christ).'),
('JHN', 1, 42, 'JHN.1.42', 'Andrew brought him to Jesus, who looked at him and said, “You are Simon son of John. You will be called Cephas” (which is translated as Peter).'),
('JHN', 1, 43, 'JHN.1.43', 'The next day Jesus decided to set out for Galilee. Finding Philip, He told him, “Follow Me.”'),
('JHN', 1, 44, 'JHN.1.44', 'Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the same town as Andrew and Peter.'),
('JHN', 1, 45, 'JHN.1.45', 'Philip found Nathanael and told him, “We have found the One Moses wrote about in the Law, the One the prophets foretold—Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.”'),
('JHN', 1, 46, 'JHN.1.46', '“Can anything good come from Nazareth?” Nathanael asked. “Come and see,” said Philip.'),
('JHN', 1, 47, 'JHN.1.47', 'When Jesus saw Nathanael approaching, He said of him, “Here is a true Israelite, in whom there is no deceit.”'),
('JHN', 1, 48, 'JHN.1.48', '“How do You know me?” Nathanael asked. Jesus replied, “Before Philip called you, I saw you under the fig tree.”'),
('JHN', 1, 49, 'JHN.1.49', '“Rabbi,” Nathanael answered, “You are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!”'),
('JHN', 1, 50, 'JHN.1.50', 'Jesus said to him, “Do you believe just because I told you I saw you under the fig tree? You will see greater things than these.”'),
('JHN', 1, 51, 'JHN.1.51', 'Then He declared, “Truly, truly, I tell you, you will all see heaven open and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man.”'),
('JHN', 2, 1, 'JHN.2.1', 'On the third day a wedding took place at Cana in Galilee. Jesus’ mother was there,'),
('JHN', 2, 2, 'JHN.2.2', 'and Jesus and His disciples had also been invited to the wedding.'),
('JHN', 2, 3, 'JHN.2.3', 'When the wine ran out, Jesus’ mother said to Him, “They have no more wine.”'),
('JHN', 2, 4, 'JHN.2.4', '“Woman, what is that to you and to Me?” Jesus replied. “My hour has not yet come.”'),
('JHN', 2, 5, 'JHN.2.5', 'His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever He tells you.”'),
('JHN', 2, 6, 'JHN.2.6', 'Now six stone water jars had been set there for the Jewish rites of purification. Each could hold from twenty to thirty gallons.'),
('JHN', 2, 7, 'JHN.2.7', 'Jesus told the servants, “Fill the jars with water.” So they filled them to the brim.'),
('JHN', 2, 8, 'JHN.2.8', '“Now draw some out,” He said, “and take it to the master of the banquet.” They did so,'),
('JHN', 2, 9, 'JHN.2.9', 'and the master of the banquet tasted the water that had been turned into wine. He did not know where it was from, but the servants who had drawn the water knew. Then he called the bridegroom aside'),
('JHN', 2, 10, 'JHN.2.10', 'and said, “Everyone serves the fine wine first, and then the cheap wine after the guests are drunk. But you have saved the fine wine until now!”'),
('JHN', 2, 11, 'JHN.2.11', 'Jesus performed this, the first of His signs, at Cana in Galilee. He thus revealed His glory, and His disciples believed in Him.'),
('JHN', 2, 12, 'JHN.2.12', 'After this, He went down to Capernaum with His mother and brothers and His disciples, and they stayed there a few days.'),
('JHN', 2, 13, 'JHN.2.13', 'When the Jewish Passover was near, Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
('JHN', 2, 14, 'JHN.2.14', 'In the temple courts He found men selling cattle, sheep, and doves, and money changers seated at their tables.'),
('JHN', 2, 15, 'JHN.2.15', 'So He made a whip out of cords and drove all from the temple courts, both sheep and cattle. He poured out the coins of the money changers and overturned their tables.'),
('JHN', 2, 16, 'JHN.2.16', 'To those selling doves He said, “Get these out of here! How dare you turn My Father’s house into a marketplace!”'),
('JHN', 2, 17, 'JHN.2.17', 'His disciples remembered that it is written: “Zeal for Your house will consume Me.”'),
('JHN', 2, 18, 'JHN.2.18', 'On account of this, the Jews demanded, “What sign can You show us to prove Your authority to do these things?”'),
('JHN', 2, 19, 'JHN.2.19', 'Jesus answered, “Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up again.”'),
('JHN', 2, 20, 'JHN.2.20', '“This temple took forty-six years to build,” the Jews replied, “and You are going to raise it up in three days?”'),
('JHN', 2, 21, 'JHN.2.21', 'But Jesus was speaking about the temple of His body.'),
('JHN', 2, 22, 'JHN.2.22', 'After He was raised from the dead, His disciples remembered that He had said this. Then they believed the Scripture and the word that Jesus had spoken.'),
('JHN', 2, 23, 'JHN.2.23', 'While He was in Jerusalem at the Passover Feast, many people saw the signs He was doing and believed in His name.'),
('JHN', 2, 24, 'JHN.2.24', 'But Jesus did not entrust Himself to them, for He knew them all.'),
('JHN', 2, 25, 'JHN.2.25', 'He did not need any testimony about man, for He knew what was in a man.'),
('JHN', 3, 1, 'JHN.3.1', 'Now there was a man of the Pharisees named Nicodemus, a leader of the Jews.'),
('JHN', 3, 2, 'JHN.3.2', 'He came to Jesus at night and said, “Rabbi, we know that You are a teacher who has come from God. For no one could perform the signs You are doing if God were not with him.”'),
('JHN', 3, 3, 'JHN.3.3', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can see the kingdom of God unless he is born again.”'),
('JHN', 3, 4, 'JHN.3.4', '“How can a man be born when he is old?” Nicodemus asked. “Can he enter his mother’s womb a second time to be born?”'),
('JHN', 3, 5, 'JHN.3.5', 'Jesus answered, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can enter the kingdom of God unless he is born of water and the Spirit.'),
('JHN', 3, 6, 'JHN.3.6', 'Flesh is born of flesh, but spirit is born of the Spirit.'),
('JHN', 3, 7, 'JHN.3.7', 'Do not be amazed that I said, ‘You must be born again.’'),
('JHN', 3, 8, 'JHN.3.8', 'The wind blows where it wishes. You hear its sound, but you do not know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.”'),
('JHN', 3, 9, 'JHN.3.9', '“How can this be?” Nicodemus asked.'),
('JHN', 3, 10, 'JHN.3.10', '“You are Israel’s teacher,” said Jesus, “and you do not understand these things?'),
('JHN', 3, 11, 'JHN.3.11', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, we speak of what we know, and we testify to what we have seen, and yet you people do not accept our testimony.'),
('JHN', 3, 12, 'JHN.3.12', 'If I have told you about earthly things and you do not believe, how will you believe if I tell you about heavenly things?'),
('JHN', 3, 13, 'JHN.3.13', 'No one has ascended into heaven except the One who descended from heaven—the Son of Man.'),
('JHN', 3, 14, 'JHN.3.14', 'Just as Moses lifted up the snake in the wilderness, so the Son of Man must be lifted up,'),
('JHN', 3, 15, 'JHN.3.15', 'that everyone who believes in Him may have eternal life.'),
('JHN', 3, 16, 'JHN.3.16', 'For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.'),
('JHN', 3, 17, 'JHN.3.17', 'For God did not send His Son into the world to condemn the world, but to save the world through Him.'),
('JHN', 3, 18, 'JHN.3.18', 'Whoever believes in Him is not condemned, but whoever does not believe has already been condemned, because he has not believed in the name of God’s one and only Son.'),
('JHN', 3, 19, 'JHN.3.19', 'And this is the verdict: The Light has come into the world, but men loved the darkness rather than the Light because their deeds were evil.'),
('JHN', 3, 20, 'JHN.3.20', 'Everyone who does evil hates the Light, and does not come into the Light for fear that his deeds will be exposed.'),
('JHN', 3, 21, 'JHN.3.21', 'But whoever practices the truth comes into the Light, so that it may be seen clearly that what he has done has been accomplished in God.”'),
('JHN', 3, 22, 'JHN.3.22', 'After this, Jesus and His disciples went into the Judean countryside, where He spent some time with them and baptized.'),
('JHN', 3, 23, 'JHN.3.23', 'Now John was also baptizing at Aenon near Salim, because the water was plentiful there, and people kept coming to be baptized.'),
('JHN', 3, 24, 'JHN.3.24', '(For John had not yet been thrown into prison.)'),
('JHN', 3, 25, 'JHN.3.25', 'Then a dispute arose between John’s disciples and a certain Jew over the issue of ceremonial washing.'),
('JHN', 3, 26, 'JHN.3.26', 'So John’s disciples came to him and said, “Look, Rabbi, the One who was with you beyond the Jordan, the One you testified about—He is baptizing, and everyone is going to Him.”'),
('JHN', 3, 27, 'JHN.3.27', 'John replied, “A man can receive only what is given him from heaven.'),
('JHN', 3, 28, 'JHN.3.28', 'You yourselves can testify that I said, ‘I am not the Christ, but am sent ahead of Him.’'),
('JHN', 3, 29, 'JHN.3.29', 'The bride belongs to the bridegroom. The friend of the bridegroom stands and listens for him, and is overjoyed to hear the bridegroom’s voice. That joy is mine, and it is now complete.'),
('JHN', 3, 30, 'JHN.3.30', 'He must increase; I must decrease.'),
('JHN', 3, 31, 'JHN.3.31', 'The One who comes from above is above all. The one who is from the earth belongs to the earth and speaks as one from the earth. The One who comes from heaven is above all.'),
('JHN', 3, 32, 'JHN.3.32', 'He testifies to what He has seen and heard, yet no one accepts His testimony.'),
('JHN', 3, 33, 'JHN.3.33', 'Whoever accepts His testimony has certified that God is truthful.'),
('JHN', 3, 34, 'JHN.3.34', 'For the One whom God has sent speaks the words of God, for God gives the Spirit without limit.'),
('JHN', 3, 35, 'JHN.3.35', 'The Father loves the Son and has placed all things in His hands.'),
('JHN', 3, 36, 'JHN.3.36', 'Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. Whoever rejects the Son will not see life. Instead, the wrath of God remains on him.”'),
('JHN', 4, 1, 'JHN.4.1', 'When Jesus realized that the Pharisees were aware He was gaining and baptizing more disciples than John'),
('JHN', 4, 2, 'JHN.4.2', '(although it was not Jesus who baptized, but His disciples),'),
('JHN', 4, 3, 'JHN.4.3', 'He left Judea and returned to Galilee.'),
('JHN', 4, 4, 'JHN.4.4', 'Now He had to pass through Samaria.'),
('JHN', 4, 5, 'JHN.4.5', 'So He came to a town of Samaria called Sychar, near the plot of ground that Jacob had given to his son Joseph.'),
('JHN', 4, 6, 'JHN.4.6', 'Since Jacob’s well was there, Jesus, weary from His journey, sat down by the well. It was about the sixth hour.'),
('JHN', 4, 7, 'JHN.4.7', 'When a Samaritan woman came to draw water, Jesus said to her, “Give Me a drink.”'),
('JHN', 4, 8, 'JHN.4.8', '(His disciples had gone into the town to buy food.)'),
('JHN', 4, 9, 'JHN.4.9', '“You are a Jew,” said the woman. “How can You ask for a drink from me, a Samaritan woman?” (For Jews do not associate with Samaritans.)'),
('JHN', 4, 10, 'JHN.4.10', 'Jesus answered, “If you knew the gift of God and who is asking you for a drink, you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water.”'),
('JHN', 4, 11, 'JHN.4.11', '“Sir,” the woman replied, “You have nothing to draw with and the well is deep. Where then will You get this living water?'),
('JHN', 4, 12, 'JHN.4.12', 'Are You greater than our father Jacob, who gave us this well and drank from it himself, as did his sons and his livestock?”'),
('JHN', 4, 13, 'JHN.4.13', 'Jesus said to her, “Everyone who drinks this water will be thirsty again.'),
('JHN', 4, 14, 'JHN.4.14', 'But whoever drinks the water I give him will never thirst. Indeed, the water I give him will become in him a fount of water springing up to eternal life.”'),
('JHN', 4, 15, 'JHN.4.15', 'The woman said to Him, “Sir, give me this water so that I will not get thirsty and have to keep coming here to draw water.”'),
('JHN', 4, 16, 'JHN.4.16', 'Jesus told her, “Go, call your husband and come back.”'),
('JHN', 4, 17, 'JHN.4.17', '“I have no husband,” the woman replied. Jesus said to her, “You are correct to say that you have no husband.'),
('JHN', 4, 18, 'JHN.4.18', 'In fact, you have had five husbands, and the man you now have is not your husband. You have spoken truthfully.”'),
('JHN', 4, 19, 'JHN.4.19', '“Sir,” the woman said, “I see that You are a prophet.'),
('JHN', 4, 20, 'JHN.4.20', 'Our fathers worshiped on this mountain, but you Jews say that the place where one must worship is in Jerusalem.”'),
('JHN', 4, 21, 'JHN.4.21', '“Believe Me, woman,” Jesus replied, “a time is coming when you will worship the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.'),
('JHN', 4, 22, 'JHN.4.22', 'You worship what you do not know; we worship what we do know, for salvation is from the Jews.'),
('JHN', 4, 23, 'JHN.4.23', 'But a time is coming and has now come when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and in truth, for the Father is seeking such as these to worship Him.'),
('JHN', 4, 24, 'JHN.4.24', 'God is Spirit, and His worshipers must worship Him in spirit and in truth.”'),
('JHN', 4, 25, 'JHN.4.25', 'The woman said, “I know that Messiah” (called Christ) “is coming. When He comes, He will explain everything to us.”'),
('JHN', 4, 26, 'JHN.4.26', 'Jesus answered, “I who speak to you am He.”'),
('JHN', 4, 27, 'JHN.4.27', 'Just then His disciples returned and were surprised that He was speaking with a woman. But no one asked Him, “What do You want from her?” or “Why are You talking with her?”'),
('JHN', 4, 28, 'JHN.4.28', 'Then the woman left her water jar, went back into the town, and said to the people,'),
('JHN', 4, 29, 'JHN.4.29', '“Come, see a man who told me everything I ever did. Could this be the Christ?”'),
('JHN', 4, 30, 'JHN.4.30', 'So they left the town and made their way toward Jesus.'),
('JHN', 4, 31, 'JHN.4.31', 'Meanwhile the disciples urged Him, “Rabbi, eat something.”'),
('JHN', 4, 32, 'JHN.4.32', 'But He told them, “I have food to eat that you know nothing about.”'),
('JHN', 4, 33, 'JHN.4.33', 'So the disciples asked one another, “Could someone have brought Him food?”'),
('JHN', 4, 34, 'JHN.4.34', 'Jesus explained, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me and to finish His work.'),
('JHN', 4, 35, 'JHN.4.35', 'Do you not say, ‘There are still four months until the harvest’? I tell you, lift up your eyes and look at the fields, for they are ripe for harvest.'),
('JHN', 4, 36, 'JHN.4.36', 'Already the reaper draws his wages and gathers a crop for eternal life, so that the sower and the reaper may rejoice together.'),
('JHN', 4, 37, 'JHN.4.37', 'For in this case the saying ‘One sows and another reaps’ is true.'),
('JHN', 4, 38, 'JHN.4.38', 'I sent you to reap what you have not worked for; others have done the hard work, and now you have taken up their labor.”'),
('JHN', 4, 39, 'JHN.4.39', 'Many of the Samaritans from that town believed in Jesus because of the woman’s testimony, “He told me everything I ever did.”'),
('JHN', 4, 40, 'JHN.4.40', 'So when the Samaritans came to Him, they asked Him to stay with them, and He stayed two days.'),
('JHN', 4, 41, 'JHN.4.41', 'And many more believed because of His message.'),
('JHN', 4, 42, 'JHN.4.42', 'They said to the woman, “We now believe not only because of your words; we have heard for ourselves, and we know that this man truly is the Savior of the world.”'),
('JHN', 4, 43, 'JHN.4.43', 'After two days, Jesus left for Galilee.'),
('JHN', 4, 44, 'JHN.4.44', 'Now He Himself had testified that a prophet has no honor in his own hometown.'),
('JHN', 4, 45, 'JHN.4.45', 'Yet when He arrived, the Galileans welcomed Him. They had seen all the great things He had done in Jerusalem at the feast, for they had gone there as well.'),
('JHN', 4, 46, 'JHN.4.46', 'So once again He came to Cana in Galilee, where He had turned the water into wine. And there was a royal official whose son lay sick at Capernaum.'),
('JHN', 4, 47, 'JHN.4.47', 'When he heard that Jesus had come from Judea to Galilee, he went and begged Him to come down and heal his son, who was about to die.'),
('JHN', 4, 48, 'JHN.4.48', 'Jesus said to him, “Unless you people see signs and wonders, you will never believe.”'),
('JHN', 4, 49, 'JHN.4.49', '“Sir,” the official said, “come down before my child dies.”'),
('JHN', 4, 50, 'JHN.4.50', '“Go,” said Jesus. “Your son will live.” The man took Jesus at His word and departed.'),
('JHN', 4, 51, 'JHN.4.51', 'And while he was still on the way, his servants met him with the news that his boy was alive.'),
('JHN', 4, 52, 'JHN.4.52', 'So he inquired as to the hour when his son had recovered, and they told him, “The fever left him yesterday at the seventh hour.”'),
('JHN', 4, 53, 'JHN.4.53', 'Then the father realized that this was the very hour in which Jesus had told him, “Your son will live.” And he and all his household believed.'),
('JHN', 4, 54, 'JHN.4.54', 'This was now the second sign that Jesus performed after coming from Judea into Galilee.'),
('JHN', 5, 1, 'JHN.5.1', 'Some time later there was a feast of the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
('JHN', 5, 2, 'JHN.5.2', 'Now there is in Jerusalem near the Sheep Gate a pool with five covered colonnades, which in Hebrew is called Bethesda.'),
('JHN', 5, 3, 'JHN.5.3', 'On these walkways lay a great number of the sick, the blind, the lame, and the paralyzed.'),
('JHN', 5, 5, 'JHN.5.5', 'One man there had been an invalid for thirty-eight years.'),
('JHN', 5, 6, 'JHN.5.6', 'When Jesus saw him lying there and realized that he had spent a long time in this condition, He asked him, “Do you want to get well?”'),
('JHN', 5, 7, 'JHN.5.7', '“Sir,” the invalid replied, “I have no one to help me into the pool when the water is stirred. While I am on my way, someone else goes in before me.”'),
('JHN', 5, 8, 'JHN.5.8', 'Then Jesus told him, “Get up, pick up your mat, and walk.”'),
('JHN', 5, 9, 'JHN.5.9', 'Immediately the man was made well, and he picked up his mat and began to walk. Now this happened on the Sabbath day,'),
('JHN', 5, 10, 'JHN.5.10', 'so the Jews said to the man who had been healed, “This is the Sabbath! It is unlawful for you to carry your mat.”'),
('JHN', 5, 11, 'JHN.5.11', 'But he answered, “The man who made me well told me, ‘Pick up your mat and walk.’”'),
('JHN', 5, 12, 'JHN.5.12', '“Who is this man who told you to pick it up and walk?” they asked.'),
('JHN', 5, 13, 'JHN.5.13', 'But the man who was healed did not know who it was, for Jesus had slipped away while the crowd was there.'),
('JHN', 5, 14, 'JHN.5.14', 'Afterward, Jesus found the man at the temple and said to him, “See, you have been made well. Stop sinning, or something worse may happen to you.”'),
('JHN', 5, 15, 'JHN.5.15', 'And the man went away and told the Jews that it was Jesus who had made him well.'),
('JHN', 5, 16, 'JHN.5.16', 'Now because Jesus was doing these things on the Sabbath, the Jews began to persecute Him.'),
('JHN', 5, 17, 'JHN.5.17', 'But Jesus answered them, “To this very day My Father is at His work, and I too am working.”'),
('JHN', 5, 18, 'JHN.5.18', 'Because of this, the Jews tried all the harder to kill Him. Not only was He breaking the Sabbath, but He was even calling God His own Father, making Himself equal with God.'),
('JHN', 5, 19, 'JHN.5.19', 'So Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, the Son can do nothing by Himself, unless He sees the Father doing it. For whatever the Father does, the Son also does.'),
('JHN', 5, 20, 'JHN.5.20', 'The Father loves the Son and shows Him all He does. And to your amazement, He will show Him even greater works than these.'),
('JHN', 5, 21, 'JHN.5.21', 'For just as the Father raises the dead and gives them life, so also the Son gives life to whom He wishes.'),
('JHN', 5, 22, 'JHN.5.22', 'Furthermore, the Father judges no one, but has assigned all judgment to the Son,'),
('JHN', 5, 23, 'JHN.5.23', 'so that all may honor the Son just as they honor the Father. Whoever does not honor the Son does not honor the Father who sent Him.'),
('JHN', 5, 24, 'JHN.5.24', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever hears My word and believes Him who sent Me has eternal life and will not come under judgment. Indeed, he has crossed over from death to life.'),
('JHN', 5, 25, 'JHN.5.25', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, the hour is coming and has now come when the dead will hear the voice of the Son of God, and those who hear will live.'),
('JHN', 5, 26, 'JHN.5.26', 'For as the Father has life in Himself, so also He has granted the Son to have life in Himself.'),
('JHN', 5, 27, 'JHN.5.27', 'And He has given Him authority to execute judgment, because He is the Son of Man.'),
('JHN', 5, 28, 'JHN.5.28', 'Do not be amazed at this, for the hour is coming when all who are in their graves will hear His voice'),
('JHN', 5, 29, 'JHN.5.29', 'and come out—those who have done good to the resurrection of life, and those who have done evil to the resurrection of judgment.'),
('JHN', 5, 30, 'JHN.5.30', 'I can do nothing by Myself; I judge only as I hear. And My judgment is just, because I do not seek My own will, but the will of Him who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 5, 31, 'JHN.5.31', 'If I testify about Myself, My testimony is not valid.'),
('JHN', 5, 32, 'JHN.5.32', 'There is another who testifies about Me, and I know that His testimony about Me is valid.'),
('JHN', 5, 33, 'JHN.5.33', 'You have sent to John, and he has testified to the truth.'),
('JHN', 5, 34, 'JHN.5.34', 'Even though I do not accept human testimony, I say these things so that you may be saved.'),
('JHN', 5, 35, 'JHN.5.35', 'John was a lamp that burned and gave light, and you were willing for a season to bask in his light.'),
('JHN', 5, 36, 'JHN.5.36', 'But I have testimony more substantial than that of John. For the works that the Father has given Me to accomplish—the very works I am doing—testify about Me that the Father has sent Me.'),
('JHN', 5, 37, 'JHN.5.37', 'And the Father who sent Me has Himself testified about Me. You have never heard His voice nor seen His form,'),
('JHN', 5, 38, 'JHN.5.38', 'nor does His word abide in you, because you do not believe the One He sent.'),
('JHN', 5, 39, 'JHN.5.39', 'You pore over the Scriptures because you presume that by them you possess eternal life. These are the very words that testify about Me,'),
('JHN', 5, 40, 'JHN.5.40', 'yet you refuse to come to Me to have life.'),
('JHN', 5, 41, 'JHN.5.41', 'I do not accept glory from men,'),
('JHN', 5, 42, 'JHN.5.42', 'but I know you, that you do not have the love of God within you.'),
('JHN', 5, 43, 'JHN.5.43', 'I have come in My Father’s name, and you have not received Me; but if someone else comes in his own name, you will receive him.'),
('JHN', 5, 44, 'JHN.5.44', 'How can you believe if you accept glory from one another, yet do not seek the glory that comes from the only God?'),
('JHN', 5, 45, 'JHN.5.45', 'Do not think that I will accuse you before the Father. Your accuser is Moses, in whom you have put your hope.'),
('JHN', 5, 46, 'JHN.5.46', 'If you had believed Moses, you would believe Me, because he wrote about Me.'),
('JHN', 5, 47, 'JHN.5.47', 'But since you do not believe what he wrote, how will you believe what I say?”'),
('JHN', 6, 1, 'JHN.6.1', 'After this, Jesus crossed to the other side of the Sea of Galilee (that is, the Sea of Tiberias).'),
('JHN', 6, 2, 'JHN.6.2', 'A large crowd followed Him because they saw the signs He was performing on the sick.'),
('JHN', 6, 3, 'JHN.6.3', 'Then Jesus went up on the mountain and sat down with His disciples.'),
('JHN', 6, 4, 'JHN.6.4', 'Now the Jewish Feast of the Passover was near.'),
('JHN', 6, 5, 'JHN.6.5', 'When Jesus looked up and saw a large crowd coming toward Him, He said to Philip, “Where can we buy bread for these people to eat?”'),
('JHN', 6, 6, 'JHN.6.6', 'But He was asking this to test him, for He knew what He was about to do.'),
('JHN', 6, 7, 'JHN.6.7', 'Philip answered, “Two hundred denarii would not buy enough bread for each of them to have a small piece.”'),
('JHN', 6, 8, 'JHN.6.8', 'One of His disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, said to Him,'),
('JHN', 6, 9, 'JHN.6.9', '“Here is a boy with five barley loaves and two small fish. But what difference will these make among so many?”'),
('JHN', 6, 10, 'JHN.6.10', '“Have the people sit down,” Jesus said. Now there was plenty of grass in that place, so the men sat down, about five thousand of them.'),
('JHN', 6, 11, 'JHN.6.11', 'Then Jesus took the loaves and the fish, gave thanks, and distributed to those who were seated as much as they wanted.'),
('JHN', 6, 12, 'JHN.6.12', 'And when everyone was full, He said to His disciples, “Gather the pieces that are left over, so that nothing will be wasted.”'),
('JHN', 6, 13, 'JHN.6.13', 'So they collected them and filled twelve baskets with the pieces of the five barley loaves left over by those who had eaten.'),
('JHN', 6, 14, 'JHN.6.14', 'When the people saw the sign that Jesus had performed, they began to say, “Truly this is the Prophet who is to come into the world.”'),
('JHN', 6, 15, 'JHN.6.15', 'Then Jesus, realizing that they were about to come and make Him king by force, withdrew again to a mountain by Himself.'),
('JHN', 6, 16, 'JHN.6.16', 'When evening came, His disciples went down to the sea,'),
('JHN', 6, 17, 'JHN.6.17', 'got into a boat, and started across the sea to Capernaum. It was already dark, and Jesus had not yet gone out to them.'),
('JHN', 6, 18, 'JHN.6.18', 'A strong wind was blowing, and the sea grew agitated.'),
('JHN', 6, 19, 'JHN.6.19', 'When they had rowed about three or four miles, they saw Jesus approaching the boat, walking on the sea—and they were terrified.'),
('JHN', 6, 20, 'JHN.6.20', 'But Jesus spoke up: “It is I; do not be afraid.”'),
('JHN', 6, 21, 'JHN.6.21', 'Then they were willing to take Him into the boat, and at once the boat reached the shore where they were heading.'),
('JHN', 6, 22, 'JHN.6.22', 'The next day, the crowd that had remained on the other side of the sea realized that only one boat had been there, and that Jesus had not boarded it with His disciples, but they had gone away alone.'),
('JHN', 6, 23, 'JHN.6.23', 'However, some boats from Tiberias landed near the place where the people had eaten the bread after the Lord had given thanks.'),
('JHN', 6, 24, 'JHN.6.24', 'So when the crowd saw that neither Jesus nor His disciples were there, they got into the boats and went to Capernaum to look for Him.'),
('JHN', 6, 25, 'JHN.6.25', 'When they found Him on the other side of the sea, they asked Him, “Rabbi, when did You get here?”'),
('JHN', 6, 26, 'JHN.6.26', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it is not because you saw these signs that you are looking for Me, but because you ate the loaves and had your fill.'),
('JHN', 6, 27, 'JHN.6.27', 'Do not work for food that perishes, but for food that endures to eternal life, which the Son of Man will give you. For on Him God the Father has placed His seal of approval.”'),
('JHN', 6, 28, 'JHN.6.28', 'Then they inquired, “What must we do to perform the works of God?”'),
('JHN', 6, 29, 'JHN.6.29', 'Jesus replied, “The work of God is this: to believe in the One He has sent.”'),
('JHN', 6, 30, 'JHN.6.30', 'So they asked Him, “What sign then will You perform, so that we may see it and believe You? What will You do?'),
('JHN', 6, 31, 'JHN.6.31', 'Our fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, as it is written: ‘He gave them bread from heaven to eat.’”'),
('JHN', 6, 32, 'JHN.6.32', 'Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it was not Moses who gave you the bread from heaven, but it is My Father who gives you the true bread from heaven.'),
('JHN', 6, 33, 'JHN.6.33', 'For the bread of God is He who comes down from heaven and gives life to the world.”'),
('JHN', 6, 34, 'JHN.6.34', '“Sir,” they said, “give us this bread at all times.”'),
('JHN', 6, 35, 'JHN.6.35', 'Jesus answered, “I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to Me will never hunger, and whoever believes in Me will never thirst.'),
('JHN', 6, 36, 'JHN.6.36', 'But as I stated, you have seen Me and still you do not believe.'),
('JHN', 6, 37, 'JHN.6.37', 'Everyone the Father gives Me will come to Me, and the one who comes to Me I will never drive away.'),
('JHN', 6, 38, 'JHN.6.38', 'For I have come down from heaven, not to do My own will, but to do the will of Him who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 6, 39, 'JHN.6.39', 'And this is the will of Him who sent Me, that I shall lose none of those He has given Me, but raise them up at the last day.'),
('JHN', 6, 40, 'JHN.6.40', 'For it is My Father’s will that everyone who looks to the Son and believes in Him shall have eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.”'),
('JHN', 6, 41, 'JHN.6.41', 'At this, the Jews began to grumble about Jesus because He had said, “I am the bread that came down from heaven.”'),
('JHN', 6, 42, 'JHN.6.42', 'They were asking, “Is this not Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then can He say, ‘I have come down from heaven’?”'),
('JHN', 6, 43, 'JHN.6.43', '“Stop grumbling among yourselves,” Jesus replied.'),
('JHN', 6, 44, 'JHN.6.44', '“No one can come to Me unless the Father who sent Me draws him, and I will raise him up at the last day.'),
('JHN', 6, 45, 'JHN.6.45', 'It is written in the Prophets: ‘And they will all be taught by God.’ Everyone who has heard the Father and learned from Him comes to Me—'),
('JHN', 6, 46, 'JHN.6.46', 'not that anyone has seen the Father except the One who is from God; only He has seen the Father.'),
('JHN', 6, 47, 'JHN.6.47', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, he who believes has eternal life.'),
('JHN', 6, 48, 'JHN.6.48', 'I am the bread of life.'),
('JHN', 6, 49, 'JHN.6.49', 'Your fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, yet they died.'),
('JHN', 6, 50, 'JHN.6.50', 'This is the bread that comes down from heaven, so that anyone may eat of it and not die.'),
('JHN', 6, 51, 'JHN.6.51', 'I am the living bread that came down from heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever. And this bread, which I will give for the life of the world, is My flesh.”'),
('JHN', 6, 52, 'JHN.6.52', 'At this, the Jews began to argue among themselves, “How can this man give us His flesh to eat?”'),
('JHN', 6, 53, 'JHN.6.53', 'So Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, unless you eat the flesh and drink the blood of the Son of Man, you have no life in you.'),
('JHN', 6, 54, 'JHN.6.54', 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood has eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.'),
('JHN', 6, 55, 'JHN.6.55', 'For My flesh is real food, and My blood is real drink.'),
('JHN', 6, 56, 'JHN.6.56', 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood remains in Me, and I in him.'),
('JHN', 6, 57, 'JHN.6.57', 'Just as the living Father sent Me and I live because of the Father, so also the one who feeds on Me will live because of Me.'),
('JHN', 6, 58, 'JHN.6.58', 'This is the bread that came down from heaven. Unlike your fathers, who ate the manna and died, the one who eats this bread will live forever.”'),
('JHN', 6, 59, 'JHN.6.59', 'Jesus said this while teaching in the synagogue in Capernaum.'),
('JHN', 6, 60, 'JHN.6.60', 'On hearing it, many of His disciples said, “This is a difficult teaching. Who can accept it?”'),
('JHN', 6, 61, 'JHN.6.61', 'Aware that His disciples were grumbling about this teaching, Jesus asked them, “Does this offend you?'),
('JHN', 6, 62, 'JHN.6.62', 'Then what will happen if you see the Son of Man ascend to where He was before?'),
('JHN', 6, 63, 'JHN.6.63', 'The Spirit gives life; the flesh profits nothing. The words I have spoken to you are spirit and they are life.'),
('JHN', 6, 64, 'JHN.6.64', 'However, there are some of you who do not believe.” (For Jesus had known from the beginning which of them did not believe and who would betray Him.)'),
('JHN', 6, 65, 'JHN.6.65', 'Then Jesus said, “This is why I told you that no one can come to Me unless the Father has granted it to him.”'),
('JHN', 6, 66, 'JHN.6.66', 'From that time on many of His disciples turned back and no longer walked with Him.'),
('JHN', 6, 67, 'JHN.6.67', 'So Jesus asked the Twelve, “Do you want to leave too?”'),
('JHN', 6, 68, 'JHN.6.68', 'Simon Peter replied, “Lord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life.'),
('JHN', 6, 69, 'JHN.6.69', 'We believe and know that You are the Holy One of God.”'),
('JHN', 6, 70, 'JHN.6.70', 'Jesus answered them, “Have I not chosen you, the Twelve? Yet one of you is a devil!”'),
('JHN', 6, 71, 'JHN.6.71', 'He was speaking about Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot. For although Judas was one of the Twelve, he was later to betray Jesus.'),
('JHN', 7, 1, 'JHN.7.1', 'After this, Jesus traveled throughout Galilee. He did not want to travel in Judea, because the Jews there were trying to kill Him.'),
('JHN', 7, 2, 'JHN.7.2', 'However, the Jewish Feast of Tabernacles was near.'),
('JHN', 7, 3, 'JHN.7.3', 'So Jesus’ brothers said to Him, “Leave here and go to Judea, so that Your disciples there may see the works You are doing.'),
('JHN', 7, 4, 'JHN.7.4', 'For no one who wants to be known publicly acts in secret. Since You are doing these things, show Yourself to the world.”'),
('JHN', 7, 5, 'JHN.7.5', 'For even His own brothers did not believe in Him.'),
('JHN', 7, 6, 'JHN.7.6', 'Therefore Jesus told them, “Although your time is always at hand, My time has not yet come.'),
('JHN', 7, 7, 'JHN.7.7', 'The world cannot hate you, but it hates Me, because I testify that its works are evil.'),
('JHN', 7, 8, 'JHN.7.8', 'Go up to the feast on your own. I am not going up to this feast, because My time has not yet come.”'),
('JHN', 7, 9, 'JHN.7.9', 'Having said this, Jesus remained in Galilee.'),
('JHN', 7, 10, 'JHN.7.10', 'But after His brothers had gone up to the feast, He also went—not publicly, but in secret.'),
('JHN', 7, 11, 'JHN.7.11', 'So the Jews were looking for Him at the feast and asking, “Where is He?”'),
('JHN', 7, 12, 'JHN.7.12', 'Many in the crowds were whispering about Him. Some said, “He is a good man.” But others replied, “No, He deceives the people.”'),
('JHN', 7, 13, 'JHN.7.13', 'Yet no one would speak publicly about Him for fear of the Jews.'),
('JHN', 7, 14, 'JHN.7.14', 'About halfway through the feast, Jesus went up to the temple courts and began to teach.'),
('JHN', 7, 15, 'JHN.7.15', 'The Jews were amazed and asked, “How did this man attain such learning without having studied?”'),
('JHN', 7, 16, 'JHN.7.16', '“My teaching is not My own,” Jesus replied. “It comes from Him who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 7, 17, 'JHN.7.17', 'If anyone desires to do His will, he will know whether My teaching is from God or whether I speak on My own.'),
('JHN', 7, 18, 'JHN.7.18', 'He who speaks on his own authority seeks his own glory, but He who seeks the glory of the One who sent Him is a man of truth; in Him there is no falsehood.'),
('JHN', 7, 19, 'JHN.7.19', 'Has not Moses given you the law? Yet not one of you keeps it. Why are you trying to kill Me?”'),
('JHN', 7, 20, 'JHN.7.20', '“You have a demon,” the crowd replied. “Who is trying to kill You?”'),
('JHN', 7, 21, 'JHN.7.21', 'Jesus answered them, “I did one miracle, and you are all amazed.'),
('JHN', 7, 22, 'JHN.7.22', 'But because Moses gave you circumcision, you circumcise a boy on the Sabbath (not that it is from Moses, but from the patriarchs.)'),
('JHN', 7, 23, 'JHN.7.23', 'If a boy can be circumcised on the Sabbath so that the law of Moses will not be broken, why are you angry with Me for making the whole man well on the Sabbath?'),
('JHN', 7, 24, 'JHN.7.24', 'Stop judging by outward appearances, and start judging justly.”'),
('JHN', 7, 25, 'JHN.7.25', 'Then some of the people of Jerusalem began to say, “Isn’t this the man they are trying to kill?'),
('JHN', 7, 26, 'JHN.7.26', 'Yet here He is, speaking publicly, and they are not saying anything to Him. Have the rulers truly recognized that this is the Christ?'),
('JHN', 7, 27, 'JHN.7.27', 'But we know where this man is from. When the Christ comes, no one will know where He is from.”'),
('JHN', 7, 28, 'JHN.7.28', 'Then Jesus, still teaching in the temple courts, cried out, “You know Me, and you know where I am from. I have not come of My own accord, but He who sent Me is true. You do not know Him,'),
('JHN', 7, 29, 'JHN.7.29', 'but I know Him, because I am from Him and He sent Me.”'),
('JHN', 7, 30, 'JHN.7.30', 'So they tried to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him, because His hour had not yet come.'),
('JHN', 7, 31, 'JHN.7.31', 'Many in the crowd, however, believed in Him and said, “When the Christ comes, will He perform more signs than this man?”'),
('JHN', 7, 32, 'JHN.7.32', 'When the Pharisees heard the crowd whispering these things about Jesus, they and the chief priests sent officers to arrest Him.'),
('JHN', 7, 33, 'JHN.7.33', 'So Jesus said, “I am with you only a little while longer, and then I am going to the One who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 7, 34, 'JHN.7.34', 'You will look for Me, but you will not find Me; and where I am, you cannot come.”'),
('JHN', 7, 35, 'JHN.7.35', 'At this, the Jews said to one another, “Where does He intend to go that we will not find Him? Will He go where the Jews are dispersed among the Greeks, and teach the Greeks?'),
('JHN', 7, 36, 'JHN.7.36', 'What does He mean by saying, ‘You will look for Me, but you will not find Me,’ and, ‘Where I am, you cannot come’?”'),
('JHN', 7, 37, 'JHN.7.37', 'On the last and greatest day of the feast, Jesus stood up and called out in a loud voice, “If anyone is thirsty, let him come to Me and drink.'),
('JHN', 7, 38, 'JHN.7.38', 'Whoever believes in Me, as the Scripture has said: ‘Streams of living water will flow from within him.’”'),
('JHN', 7, 39, 'JHN.7.39', 'He was speaking about the Spirit, whom those who believed in Him were later to receive. For the Spirit had not yet been given, because Jesus had not yet been glorified.'),
('JHN', 7, 40, 'JHN.7.40', 'On hearing these words, some of the people said, “This is truly the Prophet.”'),
('JHN', 7, 41, 'JHN.7.41', 'Others declared, “This is the Christ.” But still others asked, “How can the Christ come from Galilee?'),
('JHN', 7, 42, 'JHN.7.42', 'Doesn’t the Scripture say that the Christ will come from the line of David and from Bethlehem, the village where David lived?”'),
('JHN', 7, 43, 'JHN.7.43', 'So there was division in the crowd because of Jesus.'),
('JHN', 7, 44, 'JHN.7.44', 'Some of them wanted to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him.'),
('JHN', 7, 45, 'JHN.7.45', 'Then the officers returned to the chief priests and Pharisees, who asked them, “Why didn’t you bring Him in?”'),
('JHN', 7, 46, 'JHN.7.46', '“Never has anyone spoken like this man!” the officers answered.'),
('JHN', 7, 47, 'JHN.7.47', '“Have you also been deceived?” replied the Pharisees.'),
('JHN', 7, 48, 'JHN.7.48', '“Have any of the rulers or Pharisees believed in Him?'),
('JHN', 7, 49, 'JHN.7.49', 'But this crowd that does not know the law—they are under a curse.”'),
('JHN', 7, 50, 'JHN.7.50', 'Nicodemus, who had gone to Jesus earlier and who himself was one of them, asked,'),
('JHN', 7, 51, 'JHN.7.51', '“Does our law convict a man without first hearing from him to determine what he has done?”'),
('JHN', 7, 52, 'JHN.7.52', '“Aren’t you also from Galilee?” they replied. “Look into it, and you will see that no prophet comes out of Galilee.”'),
('JHN', 7, 53, 'JHN.7.53', 'Then each went to his own home.'),
('JHN', 8, 1, 'JHN.8.1', 'But Jesus went to the Mount of Olives.'),
('JHN', 8, 2, 'JHN.8.2', 'Early in the morning He went back into the temple courts. All the people came to Him, and He sat down to teach them.'),
('JHN', 8, 3, 'JHN.8.3', 'The scribes and Pharisees, however, brought to Him a woman caught in adultery. They made her stand before them'),
('JHN', 8, 4, 'JHN.8.4', 'and said, “Teacher, this woman was caught in the act of adultery.'),
('JHN', 8, 5, 'JHN.8.5', 'In the Law Moses commanded us to stone such a woman. So what do You say?”'),
('JHN', 8, 6, 'JHN.8.6', 'They said this to test Him, in order to have a basis for accusing Him. But Jesus bent down and began to write on the ground with His finger.'),
('JHN', 8, 7, 'JHN.8.7', 'When they continued to question Him, He straightened up and said to them, “Let him who is without sin among you be the first to cast a stone at her.”'),
('JHN', 8, 8, 'JHN.8.8', 'And again He bent down and wrote on the ground.'),
('JHN', 8, 9, 'JHN.8.9', 'When they heard this, they began to go away one by one, beginning with the older ones, until only Jesus was left, with the woman standing there.'),
('JHN', 8, 10, 'JHN.8.10', 'Then Jesus straightened up and asked her, “Woman, where are your accusers? Has no one condemned you?”'),
('JHN', 8, 11, 'JHN.8.11', '“No one, Lord,” she answered. “Then neither do I condemn you,” Jesus declared. “Now go and sin no more.”'),
('JHN', 8, 12, 'JHN.8.12', 'Once again, Jesus spoke to the people and said, “I am the light of the world. Whoever follows Me will never walk in the darkness, but will have the light of life.”'),
('JHN', 8, 13, 'JHN.8.13', 'So the Pharisees said to Him, “You are testifying about Yourself; Your testimony is not valid.”'),
('JHN', 8, 14, 'JHN.8.14', 'Jesus replied, “Even if I testify about Myself, My testimony is valid, because I know where I came from and where I am going. But you do not know where I came from or where I am going.'),
('JHN', 8, 15, 'JHN.8.15', 'You judge according to the flesh; I judge no one.'),
('JHN', 8, 16, 'JHN.8.16', 'But even if I do judge, My judgment is true, because I am not alone; I am with the Father who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 8, 17, 'JHN.8.17', 'Even in your own Law it is written that the testimony of two men is valid.'),
('JHN', 8, 18, 'JHN.8.18', 'I am One who testifies about Myself, and the Father, who sent Me, also testifies about Me.”'),
('JHN', 8, 19, 'JHN.8.19', '“Where is Your Father?” they asked Him. “You do not know Me or My Father,” Jesus answered. “If you knew Me, you would know My Father as well.”'),
('JHN', 8, 20, 'JHN.8.20', 'He spoke these words while teaching in the temple courts, near the treasury. Yet no one seized Him, because His hour had not yet come.'),
('JHN', 8, 21, 'JHN.8.21', 'Again He said to them, “I am going away, and you will look for Me, but you will die in your sin. Where I am going, you cannot come.”'),
('JHN', 8, 22, 'JHN.8.22', 'So the Jews began to ask, “Will He kill Himself, since He says, ‘Where I am going, you cannot come’?”'),
('JHN', 8, 23, 'JHN.8.23', 'Then He told them, “You are from below; I am from above. You are of this world; I am not of this world.'),
('JHN', 8, 24, 'JHN.8.24', 'That is why I told you that you would die in your sins. For unless you believe that I am He, you will die in your sins.”'),
('JHN', 8, 25, 'JHN.8.25', '“Who are You?” they asked. “Just what I have been telling you from the beginning,” Jesus replied.'),
('JHN', 8, 26, 'JHN.8.26', '“I have much to say about you and much to judge. But the One who sent Me is truthful, and what I have heard from Him, I tell the world.”'),
('JHN', 8, 27, 'JHN.8.27', 'They did not understand that He was telling them about the Father.'),
('JHN', 8, 28, 'JHN.8.28', 'So Jesus said, “When you have lifted up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am He, and that I do nothing on My own, but speak exactly what the Father has taught Me.'),
('JHN', 8, 29, 'JHN.8.29', 'He who sent Me is with Me. He has not left Me alone, because I always do what pleases Him.”'),
('JHN', 8, 30, 'JHN.8.30', 'As Jesus spoke these things, many believed in Him.'),
('JHN', 8, 31, 'JHN.8.31', 'So He said to the Jews who had believed Him, “If you continue in My word, you are truly My disciples.'),
('JHN', 8, 32, 'JHN.8.32', 'Then you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.”'),
('JHN', 8, 33, 'JHN.8.33', '“We are Abraham’s descendants,” they answered. “We have never been slaves to anyone. How can You say we will be set free?”'),
('JHN', 8, 34, 'JHN.8.34', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, everyone who sins is a slave to sin.'),
('JHN', 8, 35, 'JHN.8.35', 'A slave does not remain in the house forever, but a son remains forever.'),
('JHN', 8, 36, 'JHN.8.36', 'So if the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed.'),
('JHN', 8, 37, 'JHN.8.37', 'I know you are Abraham’s descendants, but you are trying to kill Me because My word has no place within you.'),
('JHN', 8, 38, 'JHN.8.38', 'I speak of what I have seen in the presence of the Father, and you do what you have heard from your father.”'),
('JHN', 8, 39, 'JHN.8.39', '“Abraham is our father,” they replied. “If you were children of Abraham,” said Jesus, “you would do the works of Abraham.'),
('JHN', 8, 40, 'JHN.8.40', 'But now you are trying to kill Me, a man who has told you the truth that I heard from God. Abraham never did such a thing.'),
('JHN', 8, 41, 'JHN.8.41', 'You are doing the works of your father.” “We are not illegitimate children,” they declared. “Our only Father is God Himself.”'),
('JHN', 8, 42, 'JHN.8.42', 'Jesus said to them, “If God were your Father, you would love Me, for I have come here from God. I have not come on My own, but He sent Me.'),
('JHN', 8, 43, 'JHN.8.43', 'Why do you not understand what I am saying? It is because you are unable to accept My message.'),
('JHN', 8, 44, 'JHN.8.44', 'You belong to your father, the devil, and you want to carry out his desires. He was a murderer from the beginning, refusing to uphold the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he lies, he speaks his native language, because he is a liar and the father of lies.'),
('JHN', 8, 45, 'JHN.8.45', 'But because I speak the truth, you do not believe Me!'),
('JHN', 8, 46, 'JHN.8.46', 'Which of you can prove Me guilty of sin? If I speak the truth, why do you not believe Me?'),
('JHN', 8, 47, 'JHN.8.47', 'Whoever belongs to God hears the words of God. The reason you do not hear is that you do not belong to God.”'),
('JHN', 8, 48, 'JHN.8.48', 'The Jews answered Him, “Are we not right to say that You are a Samaritan and You have a demon?”'),
('JHN', 8, 49, 'JHN.8.49', '“I do not have a demon,” Jesus replied, “but I honor My Father, and you dishonor Me.'),
('JHN', 8, 50, 'JHN.8.50', 'I do not seek My own glory. There is One who seeks it, and He is the Judge.'),
('JHN', 8, 51, 'JHN.8.51', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, if anyone keeps My word, he will never see death.”'),
('JHN', 8, 52, 'JHN.8.52', '“Now we know that You have a demon!” declared the Jews. “Abraham died, and so did the prophets, yet You say that anyone who keeps Your word will never taste death.'),
('JHN', 8, 53, 'JHN.8.53', 'Are You greater than our father Abraham? He died, as did the prophets. Who do You claim to be?”'),
('JHN', 8, 54, 'JHN.8.54', 'Jesus answered, “If I glorify Myself, My glory means nothing. The One who glorifies Me is My Father, of whom you say, ‘He is our God.’'),
('JHN', 8, 55, 'JHN.8.55', 'You do not know Him, but I know Him. If I said I did not know Him, I would be a liar like you. But I do know Him, and I keep His word.'),
('JHN', 8, 56, 'JHN.8.56', 'Your father Abraham rejoiced that he would see My day. He saw it and was glad.”'),
('JHN', 8, 57, 'JHN.8.57', 'Then the Jews said to Him, “You are not yet fifty years old, and You have seen Abraham?”'),
('JHN', 8, 58, 'JHN.8.58', '“Truly, truly, I tell you,” Jesus declared, “before Abraham was born, I am!”'),
('JHN', 8, 59, 'JHN.8.59', 'At this, they picked up stones to throw at Him. But Jesus was hidden and went out of the temple area.'),
('JHN', 9, 1, 'JHN.9.1', 'Now as Jesus was passing by, He saw a man blind from birth,'),
('JHN', 9, 2, 'JHN.9.2', 'and His disciples asked Him, “Rabbi, who sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?”'),
('JHN', 9, 3, 'JHN.9.3', 'Jesus answered, “Neither this man nor his parents sinned, but this happened so that the works of God would be displayed in him.'),
('JHN', 9, 4, 'JHN.9.4', 'While it is daytime, we must do the works of Him who sent Me. Night is coming, when no one can work.'),
('JHN', 9, 5, 'JHN.9.5', 'While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.”'),
('JHN', 9, 6, 'JHN.9.6', 'When Jesus had said this, He spit on the ground, made some mud, and applied it to the man’s eyes.'),
('JHN', 9, 7, 'JHN.9.7', 'Then He told him, “Go, wash in the Pool of Siloam” (which means “Sent”). So the man went and washed, and came back seeing.'),
('JHN', 9, 8, 'JHN.9.8', 'At this, his neighbors and those who had formerly seen him begging began to ask, “Isn’t this the man who used to sit and beg?”'),
('JHN', 9, 9, 'JHN.9.9', 'Some claimed that he was, but others said, “No, he just looks like him.” But the man kept saying, “I am the one.”'),
('JHN', 9, 10, 'JHN.9.10', '“How then were your eyes opened?” they asked.'),
('JHN', 9, 11, 'JHN.9.11', 'He answered, “The man they call Jesus made some mud and anointed my eyes, and He told me to go to Siloam and wash. So I went and washed and received my sight.”'),
('JHN', 9, 12, 'JHN.9.12', '“Where is He?” they asked. “I do not know,” he answered.'),
('JHN', 9, 13, 'JHN.9.13', 'They brought to the Pharisees the man who had been blind.'),
('JHN', 9, 14, 'JHN.9.14', 'Now the day on which Jesus had made the mud and opened his eyes was a Sabbath.'),
('JHN', 9, 15, 'JHN.9.15', 'So the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight. The man answered, “He put mud on my eyes, and I washed, and now I can see.”'),
('JHN', 9, 16, 'JHN.9.16', 'Because of this, some of the Pharisees said, “This man is not from God, for He does not keep the Sabbath.” But others said, “How can a sinful man perform such signs?” And there was division among them.'),
('JHN', 9, 17, 'JHN.9.17', 'So once again they asked the man who had been blind, “What do you say about Him, since it was your eyes He opened?” “He is a prophet,” the man replied.'),
('JHN', 9, 18, 'JHN.9.18', 'The Jews still did not believe that the man had been blind and had received his sight until they summoned his parents'),
('JHN', 9, 19, 'JHN.9.19', 'and asked, “Is this your son, the one you say was born blind? So how is it that he can now see?”'),
('JHN', 9, 20, 'JHN.9.20', 'His parents answered, “We know he is our son, and we know he was born blind.'),
('JHN', 9, 21, 'JHN.9.21', 'But how he can now see or who opened his eyes, we do not know. Ask him. He is old enough to speak for himself.”'),
('JHN', 9, 22, 'JHN.9.22', 'His parents said this because they were afraid of the Jews. For the Jews had already determined that anyone who confessed Jesus as the Christ would be put out of the synagogue.'),
('JHN', 9, 23, 'JHN.9.23', 'That was why his parents said, “He is old enough. Ask him.”'),
('JHN', 9, 24, 'JHN.9.24', 'So a second time they called for the man who had been blind and said, “Give glory to God! We know that this man is a sinner.”'),
('JHN', 9, 25, 'JHN.9.25', 'He answered, “Whether He is a sinner I do not know. There is one thing I do know: I was blind, but now I see!”'),
('JHN', 9, 26, 'JHN.9.26', '“What did He do to you?” they asked. “How did He open your eyes?”'),
('JHN', 9, 27, 'JHN.9.27', 'He replied, “I already told you, and you did not listen. Why do you want to hear it again? Do you also want to become His disciples?”'),
('JHN', 9, 28, 'JHN.9.28', 'Then they heaped insults on him and said, “You are His disciple; we are disciples of Moses.'),
('JHN', 9, 29, 'JHN.9.29', 'We know that God spoke to Moses, but we do not know where this man is from.”'),
('JHN', 9, 30, 'JHN.9.30', '“That is remarkable indeed!” the man said. “You do not know where He is from, and yet He opened my eyes.'),
('JHN', 9, 31, 'JHN.9.31', 'We know that God does not listen to sinners, but He does listen to the one who worships Him and does His will.'),
('JHN', 9, 32, 'JHN.9.32', 'Never before has anyone heard of opening the eyes of a man born blind.'),
('JHN', 9, 33, 'JHN.9.33', 'If this man were not from God, He could do no such thing.”'),
('JHN', 9, 34, 'JHN.9.34', 'They replied, “You were born in utter sin, and you are instructing us?” And they threw him out.'),
('JHN', 9, 35, 'JHN.9.35', 'When Jesus heard that they had thrown him out, He found the man and said, “Do you believe in the Son of Man?”'),
('JHN', 9, 36, 'JHN.9.36', '“Who is He, Sir?” he replied. “Tell me so that I may believe in Him.”'),
('JHN', 9, 37, 'JHN.9.37', '“You have already seen Him,” Jesus answered. “He is the One speaking with you.”'),
('JHN', 9, 38, 'JHN.9.38', '“Lord, I believe,” he said. And he worshiped Jesus.'),
('JHN', 9, 39, 'JHN.9.39', 'Then Jesus declared, “For judgment I have come into this world, so that the blind may see and those who see may become blind.”'),
('JHN', 9, 40, 'JHN.9.40', 'Some of the Pharisees who were with Him heard this, and they asked Him, “Are we blind too?”'),
('JHN', 9, 41, 'JHN.9.41', '“If you were blind,” Jesus replied, “you would not be guilty of sin. But since you claim you can see, your guilt remains.”'),
('JHN', 10, 1, 'JHN.10.1', '“Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever does not enter the sheepfold by the gate, but climbs in some other way, is a thief and a robber.'),
('JHN', 10, 2, 'JHN.10.2', 'But the one who enters by the gate is the shepherd of the sheep.'),
('JHN', 10, 3, 'JHN.10.3', 'The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep listen for his voice. He calls his own sheep by name and leads them out.'),
('JHN', 10, 4, 'JHN.10.4', 'When he has brought out all his own, he goes on ahead of them, and his sheep follow him because they know his voice.'),
('JHN', 10, 5, 'JHN.10.5', 'But they will never follow a stranger; in fact, they will flee from him because they do not recognize his voice.”'),
('JHN', 10, 6, 'JHN.10.6', 'Jesus spoke to them using this illustration, but they did not understand what He was telling them.'),
('JHN', 10, 7, 'JHN.10.7', 'So He said to them again, “Truly, truly, I tell you, I am the gate for the sheep.'),
('JHN', 10, 8, 'JHN.10.8', 'All who came before Me were thieves and robbers, but the sheep did not listen to them.'),
('JHN', 10, 9, 'JHN.10.9', 'I am the gate. If anyone enters through Me, he will be saved. He will come in and go out and find pasture.'),
('JHN', 10, 10, 'JHN.10.10', 'The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy. I have come that they may have life, and have it in all its fullness.'),
('JHN', 10, 11, 'JHN.10.11', 'I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down His life for the sheep.'),
('JHN', 10, 12, 'JHN.10.12', 'The hired hand is not the shepherd, and the sheep are not his own. When he sees the wolf coming, he abandons the sheep and runs away. Then the wolf pounces on them and scatters the flock.'),
('JHN', 10, 13, 'JHN.10.13', 'The man runs away because he is a hired servant and is unconcerned for the sheep.'),
('JHN', 10, 14, 'JHN.10.14', 'I am the good shepherd. I know My sheep and My sheep know Me,'),
('JHN', 10, 15, 'JHN.10.15', 'just as the Father knows Me and I know the Father. And I lay down My life for the sheep.'),
('JHN', 10, 16, 'JHN.10.16', 'I have other sheep that are not of this fold. I must bring them in as well, and they will listen to My voice. Then there will be one flock and one shepherd.'),
('JHN', 10, 17, 'JHN.10.17', 'The reason the Father loves Me is that I lay down My life in order to take it up again.'),
('JHN', 10, 18, 'JHN.10.18', 'No one takes it from Me, but I lay it down of My own accord. I have authority to lay it down and authority to take it up again. This charge I have received from My Father.”'),
('JHN', 10, 19, 'JHN.10.19', 'Again there was division among the Jews because of Jesus’ message.'),
('JHN', 10, 20, 'JHN.10.20', 'Many of them said, “He is demon-possessed and insane. Why would you listen to Him?”'),
('JHN', 10, 21, 'JHN.10.21', 'But others replied, “These are not the words of a man possessed by a demon. Can a demon open the eyes of the blind?”'),
('JHN', 10, 22, 'JHN.10.22', 'At that time the Feast of Dedication took place in Jerusalem. It was winter,'),
('JHN', 10, 23, 'JHN.10.23', 'and Jesus was walking in the temple courts in Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
('JHN', 10, 24, 'JHN.10.24', 'So the Jews gathered around Him and demanded, “How long will You keep us in suspense? If You are the Christ, tell us plainly.”'),
('JHN', 10, 25, 'JHN.10.25', '“I already told you,” Jesus replied, “but you did not believe. The works I do in My Father’s name testify on My behalf.'),
('JHN', 10, 26, 'JHN.10.26', 'But because you are not My sheep, you refuse to believe.'),
('JHN', 10, 27, 'JHN.10.27', 'My sheep listen to My voice; I know them, and they follow Me.'),
('JHN', 10, 28, 'JHN.10.28', 'I give them eternal life, and they will never perish. No one can snatch them out of My hand.'),
('JHN', 10, 29, 'JHN.10.29', 'My Father who has given them to Me is greater than all. No one can snatch them out of My Father’s hand.'),
('JHN', 10, 30, 'JHN.10.30', 'I and the Father are one.”'),
('JHN', 10, 31, 'JHN.10.31', 'At this, the Jews again picked up stones to stone Him.'),
('JHN', 10, 32, 'JHN.10.32', 'But Jesus responded, “I have shown you many good works from the Father. For which of these do you stone Me?”'),
('JHN', 10, 33, 'JHN.10.33', '“We are not stoning You for any good work,” said the Jews, “but for blasphemy, because You, who are a man, make Yourself out to be God.”'),
('JHN', 10, 34, 'JHN.10.34', 'Jesus replied, “Is it not written in your Law: ‘I have said you are gods’?'),
('JHN', 10, 35, 'JHN.10.35', 'If he called them gods to whom the word of God came—and the Scripture cannot be broken—'),
('JHN', 10, 36, 'JHN.10.36', 'then what about the One whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world? How then can you accuse Me of blasphemy for stating that I am the Son of God?'),
('JHN', 10, 37, 'JHN.10.37', 'If I am not doing the works of My Father, then do not believe Me.'),
('JHN', 10, 38, 'JHN.10.38', 'But if I am doing them, even though you do not believe Me, believe the works themselves, so that you may know and understand that the Father is in Me, and I am in the Father.”'),
('JHN', 10, 39, 'JHN.10.39', 'At this, they tried again to seize Him, but He escaped their grasp.'),
('JHN', 10, 40, 'JHN.10.40', 'Then Jesus went back across the Jordan to the place where John had first been baptizing, and He stayed there.'),
('JHN', 10, 41, 'JHN.10.41', 'Many came to Him and said, “Although John never performed a sign, everything he said about this man was true.”'),
('JHN', 10, 42, 'JHN.10.42', 'And many in that place believed in Jesus.'),
('JHN', 11, 1, 'JHN.11.1', 'At this time a man named Lazarus was sick. He lived in Bethany, the village of Mary and her sister Martha.'),
('JHN', 11, 2, 'JHN.11.2', '(Mary, whose brother Lazarus was sick, was to anoint the Lord with perfume and wipe His feet with her hair.)'),
('JHN', 11, 3, 'JHN.11.3', 'So the sisters sent word to Jesus, “Lord, the one You love is sick.”'),
('JHN', 11, 4, 'JHN.11.4', 'When Jesus heard this, He said, “This sickness will not end in death. No, it is for the glory of God, so that the Son of God may be glorified through it.”'),
('JHN', 11, 5, 'JHN.11.5', 'Now Jesus loved Martha and her sister and Lazarus.'),
('JHN', 11, 6, 'JHN.11.6', 'So on hearing that Lazarus was sick, He stayed where He was for two days,'),
('JHN', 11, 7, 'JHN.11.7', 'and then He said to the disciples, “Let us go back to Judea.”'),
('JHN', 11, 8, 'JHN.11.8', '“Rabbi,” they replied, “the Jews just tried to stone You, and You are going back there?”'),
('JHN', 11, 9, 'JHN.11.9', 'Jesus answered, “Are there not twelve hours of daylight? If anyone walks in the daytime, he will not stumble, because he sees by the light of this world.'),
('JHN', 11, 10, 'JHN.11.10', 'But if anyone walks at night, he will stumble, because he has no light.”'),
('JHN', 11, 11, 'JHN.11.11', 'After He had said this, He told them, “Our friend Lazarus has fallen asleep, but I am going there to wake him up.”'),
('JHN', 11, 12, 'JHN.11.12', 'His disciples replied, “Lord, if he is sleeping, he will get better.”'),
('JHN', 11, 13, 'JHN.11.13', 'They thought that Jesus was talking about actual sleep, but He was speaking about the death of Lazarus.'),
('JHN', 11, 14, 'JHN.11.14', 'So Jesus told them plainly, “Lazarus is dead,'),
('JHN', 11, 15, 'JHN.11.15', 'and for your sake I am glad I was not there, so that you may believe. But let us go to him.”'),
('JHN', 11, 16, 'JHN.11.16', 'Then Thomas called Didymus said to his fellow disciples, “Let us also go, so that we may die with Him.”'),
('JHN', 11, 17, 'JHN.11.17', 'When Jesus arrived, He found that Lazarus had already spent four days in the tomb.'),
('JHN', 11, 18, 'JHN.11.18', 'Now Bethany was near Jerusalem, a little less than two miles away,'),
('JHN', 11, 19, 'JHN.11.19', 'and many of the Jews had come to Martha and Mary to console them in the loss of their brother.'),
('JHN', 11, 20, 'JHN.11.20', 'So when Martha heard that Jesus was coming, she went out to meet Him, but Mary stayed at home.'),
('JHN', 11, 21, 'JHN.11.21', 'Martha said to Jesus, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.'),
('JHN', 11, 22, 'JHN.11.22', 'But even now I know that God will give You whatever You ask of Him.”'),
('JHN', 11, 23, 'JHN.11.23', '“Your brother will rise again,” Jesus told her.'),
('JHN', 11, 24, 'JHN.11.24', 'Martha replied, “I know that he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day.”'),
('JHN', 11, 25, 'JHN.11.25', 'Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. Whoever believes in Me will live, even though he dies.'),
('JHN', 11, 26, 'JHN.11.26', 'And everyone who lives and believes in Me will never die. Do you believe this?”'),
('JHN', 11, 27, 'JHN.11.27', '“Yes, Lord,” she answered, “I believe that You are the Christ, the Son of God, who was to come into the world.”'),
('JHN', 11, 28, 'JHN.11.28', 'After Martha had said this, she went back and called her sister Mary aside to tell her, “The Teacher is here and is asking for you.”'),
('JHN', 11, 29, 'JHN.11.29', 'And when Mary heard this, she got up quickly and went to Him.'),
('JHN', 11, 30, 'JHN.11.30', 'Now Jesus had not yet entered the village, but was still at the place where Martha had met Him.'),
('JHN', 11, 31, 'JHN.11.31', 'When the Jews who were in the house consoling Mary saw how quickly she got up and went out, they followed her, supposing she was going to the tomb to mourn there.'),
('JHN', 11, 32, 'JHN.11.32', 'When Mary came to Jesus and saw Him, she fell at His feet and said, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.”'),
('JHN', 11, 33, 'JHN.11.33', 'When Jesus saw her weeping, and the Jews who had come with her also weeping, He was deeply moved in spirit and troubled.'),
('JHN', 11, 34, 'JHN.11.34', '“Where have you put him?” He asked. “Come and see, Lord,” they answered.'),
('JHN', 11, 35, 'JHN.11.35', 'Jesus wept.'),
('JHN', 11, 36, 'JHN.11.36', 'Then the Jews said, “See how He loved him!”'),
('JHN', 11, 37, 'JHN.11.37', 'But some of them asked, “Could not this man who opened the eyes of the blind also have kept Lazarus from dying?”'),
('JHN', 11, 38, 'JHN.11.38', 'Jesus, once again deeply moved, came to the tomb. It was a cave with a stone laid across the entrance.'),
('JHN', 11, 39, 'JHN.11.39', '“Take away the stone,” Jesus said. “Lord, by now he stinks,” said Martha, the sister of the dead man. “It has already been four days.”'),
('JHN', 11, 40, 'JHN.11.40', 'Jesus replied, “Did I not tell you that if you believed, you would see the glory of God?”'),
('JHN', 11, 41, 'JHN.11.41', 'So they took away the stone. Then Jesus lifted His eyes upward and said, “Father, I thank You that You have heard Me.'),
('JHN', 11, 42, 'JHN.11.42', 'I knew that You always hear Me, but I say this for the benefit of the people standing here, so they may believe that You sent Me.”'),
('JHN', 11, 43, 'JHN.11.43', 'After Jesus had said this, He called out in a loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!”'),
('JHN', 11, 44, 'JHN.11.44', 'The man who had been dead came out with his hands and feet bound in strips of linen, and his face wrapped in a cloth. “Unwrap him and let him go,” Jesus told them.'),
('JHN', 11, 45, 'JHN.11.45', 'Therefore many of the Jews who had come to Mary, and had seen what Jesus did, believed in Him.'),
('JHN', 11, 46, 'JHN.11.46', 'But some of them went to the Pharisees and told them what Jesus had done.'),
('JHN', 11, 47, 'JHN.11.47', 'Then the chief priests and Pharisees convened the Sanhedrin and said, “What are we to do? This man is performing many signs.'),
('JHN', 11, 48, 'JHN.11.48', 'If we let Him go on like this, everyone will believe in Him, and then the Romans will come and take away both our place and our nation.”'),
('JHN', 11, 49, 'JHN.11.49', 'But one of them, named Caiaphas, who was high priest that year, said to them, “You know nothing at all!'),
('JHN', 11, 50, 'JHN.11.50', 'You do not realize that it is better for you that one man die for the people than that the whole nation perish.”'),
('JHN', 11, 51, 'JHN.11.51', 'Caiaphas did not say this on his own. Instead, as high priest that year, he was prophesying that Jesus would die for the nation,'),
('JHN', 11, 52, 'JHN.11.52', 'and not only for the nation, but also for the scattered children of God, to gather them together into one.'),
('JHN', 11, 53, 'JHN.11.53', 'So from that day on they plotted to kill Him.'),
('JHN', 11, 54, 'JHN.11.54', 'As a result, Jesus no longer went about publicly among the Jews, but He withdrew to a town called Ephraim in an area near the wilderness. And He stayed there with the disciples.'),
('JHN', 11, 55, 'JHN.11.55', 'Now the Jewish Passover was near, and many people went up from the country to Jerusalem to purify themselves before the Passover.'),
('JHN', 11, 56, 'JHN.11.56', 'They kept looking for Jesus and asking one another as they stood in the temple courts, “What do you think? Will He come to the feast at all?”'),
('JHN', 11, 57, 'JHN.11.57', 'But the chief priests and Pharisees had given orders that anyone who knew where He was must report it, so that they could arrest Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 1, 'JHN.12.1', 'Six days before the Passover, Jesus came to Bethany, the hometown of Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.'),
('JHN', 12, 2, 'JHN.12.2', 'So they hosted a dinner for Jesus there. Martha served, and Lazarus was among those reclining at the table with Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 3, 'JHN.12.3', 'Then Mary took about a pint of expensive perfume, made of pure nard, and she anointed Jesus’ feet and wiped them with her hair. And the house was filled with the fragrance of the perfume.'),
('JHN', 12, 4, 'JHN.12.4', 'But one of His disciples, Judas Iscariot, who was going to betray Him, asked,'),
('JHN', 12, 5, 'JHN.12.5', '“Why wasn’t this perfume sold for three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor?”'),
('JHN', 12, 6, 'JHN.12.6', 'Judas did not say this because he cared about the poor, but because he was a thief. As keeper of the money bag, he used to take from what was put into it.'),
('JHN', 12, 7, 'JHN.12.7', '“Leave her alone,” Jesus replied. “She has kept this perfume in preparation for the day of My burial.'),
('JHN', 12, 8, 'JHN.12.8', 'The poor you will always have with you, but you will not always have Me.”'),
('JHN', 12, 9, 'JHN.12.9', 'Meanwhile a large crowd of Jews learned that Jesus was there. And they came not only because of Him, but also to see Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.'),
('JHN', 12, 10, 'JHN.12.10', 'So the chief priests made plans to kill Lazarus as well,'),
('JHN', 12, 11, 'JHN.12.11', 'for on account of him many of the Jews were deserting them and believing in Jesus.'),
('JHN', 12, 12, 'JHN.12.12', 'The next day the great crowd that had come to the feast heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem.'),
('JHN', 12, 13, 'JHN.12.13', 'They took palm branches and went out to meet Him, shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Blessed is the King of Israel!”'),
('JHN', 12, 14, 'JHN.12.14', 'Finding a young donkey, Jesus sat on it, as it is written:'),
('JHN', 12, 15, 'JHN.12.15', '“Do not be afraid, O Daughter of Zion. See, your King is coming, seated on the colt of a donkey.”'),
('JHN', 12, 16, 'JHN.12.16', 'At first His disciples did not understand these things, but after Jesus was glorified they remembered what had been done to Him, and they realized that these very things had also been written about Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 17, 'JHN.12.17', 'Meanwhile, many people who had been with Jesus when He called Lazarus from the tomb and raised him from the dead continued to testify.'),
('JHN', 12, 18, 'JHN.12.18', 'That is also why the crowd went out to meet Him, because they heard that He had performed this sign.'),
('JHN', 12, 19, 'JHN.12.19', 'Then the Pharisees said to one another, “You can see that this is doing you no good. Look how the whole world has gone after Him!”'),
('JHN', 12, 20, 'JHN.12.20', 'Now there were some Greeks among those who went up to worship at the feast.'),
('JHN', 12, 21, 'JHN.12.21', 'They came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida in Galilee, and requested of him, “Sir, we want to see Jesus.”'),
('JHN', 12, 22, 'JHN.12.22', 'Philip relayed this appeal to Andrew, and both of them went and told Jesus.'),
('JHN', 12, 23, 'JHN.12.23', 'But Jesus replied, “The hour has come for the Son of Man to be glorified.'),
('JHN', 12, 24, 'JHN.12.24', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, unless a kernel of wheat falls to the ground and dies, it remains only a seed. But if it dies, it bears much fruit.'),
('JHN', 12, 25, 'JHN.12.25', 'Whoever loves his life will lose it, but whoever hates his life in this world will keep it for eternal life.'),
('JHN', 12, 26, 'JHN.12.26', 'If anyone serves Me, he must follow Me; and where I am, My servant will be as well. If anyone serves Me, the Father will honor him.'),
('JHN', 12, 27, 'JHN.12.27', 'Now My soul is troubled, and what shall I say? ‘Father, save Me from this hour’? No, it is for this purpose that I have come to this hour.'),
('JHN', 12, 28, 'JHN.12.28', 'Father, glorify Your name!” Then a voice came from heaven: “I have glorified it, and I will glorify it again.”'),
('JHN', 12, 29, 'JHN.12.29', 'The crowd standing there heard it and said that it had thundered. Others said that an angel had spoken to Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 30, 'JHN.12.30', 'In response, Jesus said, “This voice was not for My benefit, but yours.'),
('JHN', 12, 31, 'JHN.12.31', 'Now judgment is upon this world; now the prince of this world will be cast out.'),
('JHN', 12, 32, 'JHN.12.32', 'And I, when I am lifted up from the earth, will draw everyone to Myself.”'),
('JHN', 12, 33, 'JHN.12.33', 'He said this to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.'),
('JHN', 12, 34, 'JHN.12.34', 'The crowd replied, “We have heard from the Law that the Christ will remain forever. So how can You say that the Son of Man must be lifted up? Who is this Son of Man?”'),
('JHN', 12, 35, 'JHN.12.35', 'Then Jesus told them, “For a little while longer, the Light will be among you. Walk while you have the Light, so that darkness will not overtake you. The one who walks in the darkness does not know where he is going.'),
('JHN', 12, 36, 'JHN.12.36', 'While you have the Light, believe in the Light, so that you may become sons of light.” After Jesus had spoken these things, He went away and was hidden from them.'),
('JHN', 12, 37, 'JHN.12.37', 'Although Jesus had performed so many signs in their presence, they still did not believe in Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 38, 'JHN.12.38', 'This was to fulfill the word of Isaiah the prophet: “Lord, who has believed our message? And to whom has the arm of the Lord been revealed?”'),
('JHN', 12, 39, 'JHN.12.39', 'For this reason they were unable to believe. For again, Isaiah says:'),
('JHN', 12, 40, 'JHN.12.40', '“He has blinded their eyes and hardened their hearts, so that they cannot see with their eyes, and understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.”'),
('JHN', 12, 41, 'JHN.12.41', 'Isaiah said these things because he saw Jesus’ glory and spoke about Him.'),
('JHN', 12, 42, 'JHN.12.42', 'Nevertheless, many of the leaders believed in Him. But because of the Pharisees they did not confess Him, for fear that they would be put out of the synagogue.'),
('JHN', 12, 43, 'JHN.12.43', 'For they loved praise from men more than praise from God.'),
('JHN', 12, 44, 'JHN.12.44', 'Then Jesus cried out, “Whoever believes in Me does not believe in Me alone, but in the One who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 12, 45, 'JHN.12.45', 'And whoever sees Me sees the One who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 12, 46, 'JHN.12.46', 'I have come into the world as a light, so that no one who believes in Me should remain in darkness.'),
('JHN', 12, 47, 'JHN.12.47', 'As for anyone who hears My words and does not keep them, I do not judge him. For I have not come to judge the world, but to save the world.'),
('JHN', 12, 48, 'JHN.12.48', 'There is a judge for the one who rejects Me and does not receive My words: The word that I have spoken will judge him on the last day.'),
('JHN', 12, 49, 'JHN.12.49', 'I have not spoken on My own, but the Father who sent Me has commanded Me what to say and how to say it.'),
('JHN', 12, 50, 'JHN.12.50', 'And I know that His command leads to eternal life. So I speak exactly what the Father has told Me to say.”'),
('JHN', 13, 1, 'JHN.13.1', 'It was now just before the Passover Feast, and Jesus knew that His hour had come to leave this world and return to the Father. Having loved His own who were in the world, He loved them to the very end.'),
('JHN', 13, 2, 'JHN.13.2', 'The evening meal was underway, and the devil had already put into the heart of Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, to betray Jesus.'),
('JHN', 13, 3, 'JHN.13.3', 'Jesus knew that the Father had delivered all things into His hands, and that He had come from God and was returning to God.'),
('JHN', 13, 4, 'JHN.13.4', 'So He got up from the supper, laid aside His outer garments, and wrapped a towel around His waist.'),
('JHN', 13, 5, 'JHN.13.5', 'After that, He poured water into a basin and began to wash the disciples’ feet and dry them with the towel that was around Him.'),
('JHN', 13, 6, 'JHN.13.6', 'He came to Simon Peter, who asked Him, “Lord, are You going to wash my feet?”'),
('JHN', 13, 7, 'JHN.13.7', 'Jesus replied, “You do not realize now what I am doing, but later you will understand.”'),
('JHN', 13, 8, 'JHN.13.8', '“Never shall You wash my feet!” Peter told Him. Jesus answered, “Unless I wash you, you have no part with Me.”'),
('JHN', 13, 9, 'JHN.13.9', '“Then, Lord,” Simon Peter replied, “not only my feet, but my hands and my head as well!”'),
('JHN', 13, 10, 'JHN.13.10', 'Jesus told him, “Whoever has already bathed needs only to wash his feet, and he will be completely clean. And you are clean, though not all of you.”'),
('JHN', 13, 11, 'JHN.13.11', 'For He knew who would betray Him. That is why He said, “Not all of you are clean.”'),
('JHN', 13, 12, 'JHN.13.12', 'When Jesus had washed their feet and put on His outer garments, He reclined with them again and asked, “Do you know what I have done for you?'),
('JHN', 13, 13, 'JHN.13.13', 'You call Me Teacher and Lord, and rightly so, because I am.'),
('JHN', 13, 14, 'JHN.13.14', 'So if I, your Lord and Teacher, have washed your feet, you also should wash one another’s feet.'),
('JHN', 13, 15, 'JHN.13.15', 'I have set you an example so that you should do as I have done for you.'),
('JHN', 13, 16, 'JHN.13.16', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, no servant is greater than his master, nor is a messenger greater than the one who sent him.'),
('JHN', 13, 17, 'JHN.13.17', 'If you know these things, you will be blessed if you do them.'),
('JHN', 13, 18, 'JHN.13.18', 'I am not speaking about all of you; I know whom I have chosen. But this is to fulfill the Scripture: ‘The one who shares My bread has lifted up his heel against Me.’'),
('JHN', 13, 19, 'JHN.13.19', 'I am telling you now before it happens, so that when it comes to pass, you will believe that I am He.'),
('JHN', 13, 20, 'JHN.13.20', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever receives the one I send receives Me, and whoever receives Me receives the One who sent Me.”'),
('JHN', 13, 21, 'JHN.13.21', 'After Jesus had said this, He became troubled in spirit and testified, “Truly, truly, I tell you, one of you will betray Me.”'),
('JHN', 13, 22, 'JHN.13.22', 'The disciples looked at one another, perplexed as to which of them He meant.'),
('JHN', 13, 23, 'JHN.13.23', 'One of His disciples, the one whom Jesus loved, was reclining at His side.'),
('JHN', 13, 24, 'JHN.13.24', 'So Simon Peter motioned to him to ask Jesus which one He was talking about.'),
('JHN', 13, 25, 'JHN.13.25', 'Leaning back against Jesus, he asked, “Lord, who is it?”'),
('JHN', 13, 26, 'JHN.13.26', 'Jesus answered, “It is the one to whom I give this morsel after I have dipped it.” Then He dipped the morsel and gave it to Judas son of Simon Iscariot.'),
('JHN', 13, 27, 'JHN.13.27', 'And when Judas had taken the morsel, Satan entered into him. Then Jesus said to Judas, “What you are about to do, do quickly.”'),
('JHN', 13, 28, 'JHN.13.28', 'But no one at the table knew why Jesus had said this to him.'),
('JHN', 13, 29, 'JHN.13.29', 'Since Judas kept the money bag, some thought that Jesus was telling him to buy what was needed for the feast, or to give something to the poor.'),
('JHN', 13, 30, 'JHN.13.30', 'As soon as he had received the morsel, Judas went out into the night.'),
('JHN', 13, 31, 'JHN.13.31', 'When Judas had gone out, Jesus said, “Now the Son of Man is glorified, and God is glorified in Him.'),
('JHN', 13, 32, 'JHN.13.32', 'If God is glorified in Him, God will also glorify the Son in Himself—and will glorify Him at once.'),
('JHN', 13, 33, 'JHN.13.33', 'Little children, I am with you only a little while longer. You will look for Me, and as I said to the Jews, so now I say to you: ‘Where I am going, you cannot come.’'),
('JHN', 13, 34, 'JHN.13.34', 'A new commandment I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you also must love one another.'),
('JHN', 13, 35, 'JHN.13.35', 'By this everyone will know that you are My disciples, if you love one another.”'),
('JHN', 13, 36, 'JHN.13.36', '“Lord, where are You going?” Simon Peter asked. Jesus answered, “Where I am going, you cannot follow Me now, but you will follow later.”'),
('JHN', 13, 37, 'JHN.13.37', '“Lord,” said Peter, “why can’t I follow You now? I will lay down my life for You.”'),
('JHN', 13, 38, 'JHN.13.38', '“Will you lay down your life for Me?” Jesus replied. “Truly, truly, I tell you, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.'),
('JHN', 14, 1, 'JHN.14.1', '“Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe in Me as well.'),
('JHN', 14, 2, 'JHN.14.2', 'In My Father’s house are many rooms. If it were not so, would I have told you that I am going there to prepare a place for you?'),
('JHN', 14, 3, 'JHN.14.3', 'And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come back and welcome you into My presence, so that you also may be where I am.'),
('JHN', 14, 4, 'JHN.14.4', 'You know the way to the place where I am going.”'),
('JHN', 14, 5, 'JHN.14.5', '“Lord,” said Thomas, “we do not know where You are going, so how can we know the way?”'),
('JHN', 14, 6, 'JHN.14.6', 'Jesus answered, “I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.'),
('JHN', 14, 7, 'JHN.14.7', 'If you had known Me, you would know My Father as well. From now on you do know Him and have seen Him.”'),
('JHN', 14, 8, 'JHN.14.8', 'Philip said to Him, “Lord, show us the Father, and that will be enough for us.”'),
('JHN', 14, 9, 'JHN.14.9', 'Jesus replied, “Philip, I have been with you all this time, and still you do not know Me? Anyone who has seen Me has seen the Father. How can you say, ‘Show us the Father’?'),
('JHN', 14, 10, 'JHN.14.10', 'Do you not believe that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me? The words I say to you, I do not speak on My own. Instead, it is the Father dwelling in Me, performing His works.'),
('JHN', 14, 11, 'JHN.14.11', 'Believe Me that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me—or at least believe on account of the works themselves.'),
('JHN', 14, 12, 'JHN.14.12', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever believes in Me will also do the works that I am doing. He will do even greater things than these, because I am going to the Father.'),
('JHN', 14, 13, 'JHN.14.13', 'And I will do whatever you ask in My name, so that the Father may be glorified in the Son.'),
('JHN', 14, 14, 'JHN.14.14', 'If you ask Me for anything in My name, I will do it.'),
('JHN', 14, 15, 'JHN.14.15', 'If you love Me, you will keep My commandments.'),
('JHN', 14, 16, 'JHN.14.16', 'And I will ask the Father, and He will give you another Advocate to be with you forever—'),
('JHN', 14, 17, 'JHN.14.17', 'the Spirit of truth. The world cannot receive Him, because it neither sees Him nor knows Him. But you do know Him, for He abides with you and will be in you.'),
('JHN', 14, 18, 'JHN.14.18', 'I will not leave you as orphans; I will come to you.'),
('JHN', 14, 19, 'JHN.14.19', 'In a little while the world will see Me no more, but you will see Me. Because I live, you also will live.'),
('JHN', 14, 20, 'JHN.14.20', 'On that day you will know that I am in My Father, and you are in Me, and I am in you.'),
('JHN', 14, 21, 'JHN.14.21', 'Whoever has My commandments and keeps them is the one who loves Me. The one who loves Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and reveal Myself to him.”'),
('JHN', 14, 22, 'JHN.14.22', 'Judas (not Iscariot) asked Him, “Lord, why are You going to reveal Yourself to us and not to the world?”'),
('JHN', 14, 23, 'JHN.14.23', 'Jesus replied, “If anyone loves Me, he will keep My word. My Father will love him, and We will come to him and make Our home with him.'),
('JHN', 14, 24, 'JHN.14.24', 'Whoever does not love Me does not keep My words. The word that you hear is not My own, but it is from the Father who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 14, 25, 'JHN.14.25', 'All this I have spoken to you while I am still with you.'),
('JHN', 14, 26, 'JHN.14.26', 'But the Advocate, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My name, will teach you all things and will remind you of everything I have told you.'),
('JHN', 14, 27, 'JHN.14.27', 'Peace I leave with you; My peace I give to you. I do not give to you as the world gives. Do not let your hearts be troubled; do not be afraid.'),
('JHN', 14, 28, 'JHN.14.28', 'You heard Me say, ‘I am going away, and I am coming back to you.’ If you loved Me, you would rejoice that I am going to the Father, because the Father is greater than I.'),
('JHN', 14, 29, 'JHN.14.29', 'And now I have told you before it happens, so that when it does happen, you will believe.'),
('JHN', 14, 30, 'JHN.14.30', 'I will not speak with you much longer, for the prince of this world is coming, and he has no claim on Me.'),
('JHN', 14, 31, 'JHN.14.31', 'But I do exactly what the Father has commanded Me, so that the world may know that I love the Father. Get up! Let us go on from here.'),
('JHN', 15, 1, 'JHN.15.1', '“I am the true vine, and My Father is the keeper of the vineyard.'),
('JHN', 15, 2, 'JHN.15.2', 'He cuts off every branch in Me that bears no fruit, and every branch that does bear fruit, He prunes to make it even more fruitful.'),
('JHN', 15, 3, 'JHN.15.3', 'You are already clean because of the word I have spoken to you.'),
('JHN', 15, 4, 'JHN.15.4', 'Remain in Me, and I will remain in you. Just as no branch can bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, neither can you bear fruit unless you remain in Me.'),
('JHN', 15, 5, 'JHN.15.5', 'I am the vine and you are the branches. The one who remains in Me, and I in him, will bear much fruit. For apart from Me you can do nothing.'),
('JHN', 15, 6, 'JHN.15.6', 'If anyone does not remain in Me, he is like a branch that is thrown away and withers. Such branches are gathered up, thrown into the fire, and burned.'),
('JHN', 15, 7, 'JHN.15.7', 'If you remain in Me and My words remain in you, ask whatever you wish, and it will be done for you.'),
('JHN', 15, 8, 'JHN.15.8', 'This is to My Father’s glory, that you bear much fruit, proving yourselves to be My disciples.'),
('JHN', 15, 9, 'JHN.15.9', 'As the Father has loved Me, so have I loved you. Remain in My love.'),
('JHN', 15, 10, 'JHN.15.10', 'If you keep My commandments, you will remain in My love, just as I have kept My Father’s commandments and remain in His love.'),
('JHN', 15, 11, 'JHN.15.11', 'I have told you these things so that My joy may be in you and your joy may be complete.'),
('JHN', 15, 12, 'JHN.15.12', 'This is My commandment, that you love one another as I have loved you.'),
('JHN', 15, 13, 'JHN.15.13', 'Greater love has no one than this, that he lay down his life for his friends.'),
('JHN', 15, 14, 'JHN.15.14', 'You are My friends if you do what I command you.'),
('JHN', 15, 15, 'JHN.15.15', 'No longer do I call you servants, for a servant does not understand what his master is doing. But I have called you friends, because everything I have learned from My Father I have made known to you.'),
('JHN', 15, 16, 'JHN.15.16', 'You did not choose Me, but I chose you. And I appointed you to go and bear fruit—fruit that will remain—so that whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.'),
('JHN', 15, 17, 'JHN.15.17', 'This is My command to you: Love one another.'),
('JHN', 15, 18, 'JHN.15.18', 'If the world hates you, understand that it hated Me first.'),
('JHN', 15, 19, 'JHN.15.19', 'If you were of the world, it would love you as its own. Instead, the world hates you, because you are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world.'),
('JHN', 15, 20, 'JHN.15.20', 'Remember the word that I spoke to you: ‘No servant is greater than his master.’ If they persecuted Me, they will persecute you as well; if they kept My word, they will keep yours as well.'),
('JHN', 15, 21, 'JHN.15.21', 'But they will treat you like this because of My name, since they do not know the One who sent Me.'),
('JHN', 15, 22, 'JHN.15.22', 'If I had not come and spoken to them, they would not be guilty of sin. Now, however, they have no excuse for their sin.'),
('JHN', 15, 23, 'JHN.15.23', 'Whoever hates Me hates My Father as well.'),
('JHN', 15, 24, 'JHN.15.24', 'If I had not done among them the works that no one else did, they would not be guilty of sin; but now they have seen and hated both Me and My Father.'),
('JHN', 15, 25, 'JHN.15.25', 'But this is to fulfill what is written in their Law: ‘They hated Me without reason.’'),
('JHN', 15, 26, 'JHN.15.26', 'When the Advocate comes, whom I will send to you from the Father—the Spirit of truth who proceeds from the Father—He will testify about Me.'),
('JHN', 15, 27, 'JHN.15.27', 'And you also must testify, because you have been with Me from the beginning.'),
('JHN', 16, 1, 'JHN.16.1', '“I have told you these things so that you will not fall away.'),
('JHN', 16, 2, 'JHN.16.2', 'They will put you out of the synagogues. In fact, a time is coming when anyone who kills you will think he is offering a service to God.'),
('JHN', 16, 3, 'JHN.16.3', 'They will do these things because they have not known the Father or Me.'),
('JHN', 16, 4, 'JHN.16.4', 'But I have told you these things so that when their hour comes, you will remember that I told you about them. I did not tell you these things from the beginning, because I was with you.'),
('JHN', 16, 5, 'JHN.16.5', 'Now, however, I am going to Him who sent Me; yet none of you asks Me, ‘Where are You going?’'),
('JHN', 16, 6, 'JHN.16.6', 'Instead, your hearts are filled with sorrow because I have told you these things.'),
('JHN', 16, 7, 'JHN.16.7', 'But I tell you the truth, it is for your benefit that I am going away. Unless I go away, the Advocate will not come to you; but if I go, I will send Him to you.'),
('JHN', 16, 8, 'JHN.16.8', 'And when He comes, He will convict the world in regard to sin and righteousness and judgment:'),
('JHN', 16, 9, 'JHN.16.9', 'in regard to sin, because they do not believe in Me;'),
('JHN', 16, 10, 'JHN.16.10', 'in regard to righteousness, because I am going to the Father and you will no longer see Me;'),
('JHN', 16, 11, 'JHN.16.11', 'and in regard to judgment, because the prince of this world has been condemned.'),
('JHN', 16, 12, 'JHN.16.12', 'I still have much to tell you, but you cannot yet bear to hear it.'),
('JHN', 16, 13, 'JHN.16.13', 'However, when the Spirit of truth comes, He will guide you into all truth. For He will not speak on His own, but He will speak what He hears, and He will declare to you what is to come.'),
('JHN', 16, 14, 'JHN.16.14', 'He will glorify Me by taking from what is Mine and disclosing it to you.'),
('JHN', 16, 15, 'JHN.16.15', 'Everything that belongs to the Father is Mine. That is why I said that the Spirit will take from what is Mine and disclose it to you.'),
('JHN', 16, 16, 'JHN.16.16', 'In a little while you will see Me no more, and then after a little while you will see Me.”'),
('JHN', 16, 17, 'JHN.16.17', 'Then some of His disciples asked one another, “Why is He telling us, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’ and ‘Because I am going to the Father’?”'),
('JHN', 16, 18, 'JHN.16.18', 'They kept asking, “Why is He saying, ‘a little while’? We do not understand what He is saying.”'),
('JHN', 16, 19, 'JHN.16.19', 'Aware that they wanted to question Him, Jesus said to them, “Are you asking one another why I said, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’?'),
('JHN', 16, 20, 'JHN.16.20', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, you will weep and wail while the world rejoices. You will grieve, but your grief will turn to joy.'),
('JHN', 16, 21, 'JHN.16.21', 'A woman has pain in childbirth because her time has come; but when she brings forth her child, she forgets her anguish because of her joy that a child has been born into the world.'),
('JHN', 16, 22, 'JHN.16.22', 'So also you have sorrow now, but I will see you again and your hearts will rejoice, and no one will take away your joy.'),
('JHN', 16, 23, 'JHN.16.23', 'In that day you will no longer ask Me anything. Truly, truly, I tell you, whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.'),
('JHN', 16, 24, 'JHN.16.24', 'Until now you have not asked for anything in My name. Ask and you will receive, so that your joy may be complete.'),
('JHN', 16, 25, 'JHN.16.25', 'I have spoken these things to you in figures of speech. An hour is coming when I will no longer speak to you this way, but will tell you plainly about the Father.'),
('JHN', 16, 26, 'JHN.16.26', 'In that day you will ask in My name. I am not saying that I will ask the Father on your behalf.'),
('JHN', 16, 27, 'JHN.16.27', 'For the Father Himself loves you, because you have loved Me and have believed that I came from God.'),
('JHN', 16, 28, 'JHN.16.28', 'I came from the Father and entered the world. In turn, I will leave the world and go to the Father.”'),
('JHN', 16, 29, 'JHN.16.29', 'His disciples said, “See, now You are speaking plainly and without figures of speech.'),
('JHN', 16, 30, 'JHN.16.30', 'Now we understand that You know all things and that You have no need for anyone to question You. Because of this, we believe that You came from God.”'),
('JHN', 16, 31, 'JHN.16.31', '“Do you finally believe?” Jesus replied.'),
('JHN', 16, 32, 'JHN.16.32', '“Look, an hour is coming and has already come when you will be scattered, each to his own home, and you will leave Me all alone. Yet I am not alone, because the Father is with Me.'),
('JHN', 16, 33, 'JHN.16.33', 'I have told you these things so that in Me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take courage; I have overcome the world!”'),
('JHN', 17, 1, 'JHN.17.1', 'When Jesus had spoken these things, He lifted up His eyes to heaven and said, “Father, the hour has come. Glorify Your Son, that Your Son may glorify You.'),
('JHN', 17, 2, 'JHN.17.2', 'For You granted Him authority over all people, so that He may give eternal life to all those You have given Him.'),
('JHN', 17, 3, 'JHN.17.3', 'Now this is eternal life, that they may know You, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom You have sent.'),
('JHN', 17, 4, 'JHN.17.4', 'I have glorified You on earth by accomplishing the work You gave Me to do.'),
('JHN', 17, 5, 'JHN.17.5', 'And now, Father, glorify Me in Your presence with the glory I had with You before the world existed.'),
('JHN', 17, 6, 'JHN.17.6', 'I have revealed Your name to those You have given Me out of the world. They were Yours; You gave them to Me, and they have kept Your word.'),
('JHN', 17, 7, 'JHN.17.7', 'Now they know that everything You have given Me comes from You.'),
('JHN', 17, 8, 'JHN.17.8', 'For I have given them the words You gave Me, and they have received them. They knew with certainty that I came from You, and they believed that You sent Me.'),
('JHN', 17, 9, 'JHN.17.9', 'I ask on their behalf. I do not ask on behalf of the world, but on behalf of those You have given Me; for they are Yours.'),
('JHN', 17, 10, 'JHN.17.10', 'All I have is Yours, and all You have is Mine; and in them I have been glorified.'),
('JHN', 17, 11, 'JHN.17.11', 'I will no longer be in the world, but they are in the world, and I am coming to You. Holy Father, protect them by Your name, the name You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one.'),
('JHN', 17, 12, 'JHN.17.12', 'While I was with them, I protected and preserved them by Your name, the name You gave Me. Not one of them has been lost, except the son of destruction, so that the Scripture would be fulfilled.'),
('JHN', 17, 13, 'JHN.17.13', 'But now I am coming to You; and I am saying these things while I am in the world, so that they may have My joy fulfilled within them.'),
('JHN', 17, 14, 'JHN.17.14', 'I have given them Your word and the world has hated them. For they are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.'),
('JHN', 17, 15, 'JHN.17.15', 'I am not asking that You take them out of the world, but that You keep them from the evil one.'),
('JHN', 17, 16, 'JHN.17.16', 'They are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.'),
('JHN', 17, 17, 'JHN.17.17', 'Sanctify them by the truth; Your word is truth.'),
('JHN', 17, 18, 'JHN.17.18', 'As You sent Me into the world, I have also sent them into the world.'),
('JHN', 17, 19, 'JHN.17.19', 'For them I sanctify Myself, so that they too may be sanctified by the truth.'),
('JHN', 17, 20, 'JHN.17.20', 'I am not asking on behalf of them alone, but also on behalf of those who will believe in Me through their message,'),
('JHN', 17, 21, 'JHN.17.21', 'that all of them may be one, as You, Father, are in Me, and I am in You. May they also be in Us, so that the world may believe that You sent Me.'),
('JHN', 17, 22, 'JHN.17.22', 'I have given them the glory You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one—'),
('JHN', 17, 23, 'JHN.17.23', 'I in them and You in Me—that they may be perfectly united, so that the world may know that You sent Me and have loved them just as You have loved Me.'),
('JHN', 17, 24, 'JHN.17.24', 'Father, I want those You have given Me to be with Me where I am, that they may see the glory You gave Me because You loved Me before the foundation of the world.'),
('JHN', 17, 25, 'JHN.17.25', 'Righteous Father, although the world has not known You, I know You, and they know that You sent Me.'),
('JHN', 17, 26, 'JHN.17.26', 'And I have made Your name known to them and will continue to make it known, so that the love You have for Me may be in them, and I in them.”'),
('JHN', 18, 1, 'JHN.18.1', 'After Jesus had spoken these words, He went out with His disciples across the Kidron Valley, where they entered a garden.'),
('JHN', 18, 2, 'JHN.18.2', 'Now Judas His betrayer also knew the place, because Jesus had often met there with His disciples.'),
('JHN', 18, 3, 'JHN.18.3', 'So Judas brought a band of soldiers and officers from the chief priests and Pharisees. They arrived at the garden carrying lanterns, torches, and weapons.'),
('JHN', 18, 4, 'JHN.18.4', 'Jesus, knowing all that was coming upon Him, stepped forward and asked them, “Whom are you seeking?”'),
('JHN', 18, 5, 'JHN.18.5', '“Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. Jesus said, “I am He.” And Judas His betrayer was standing there with them.'),
('JHN', 18, 6, 'JHN.18.6', 'When Jesus said, “I am He,” they drew back and fell to the ground.'),
('JHN', 18, 7, 'JHN.18.7', 'So He asked them again, “Whom are you seeking?” “Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered.'),
('JHN', 18, 8, 'JHN.18.8', '“I told you that I am He,” Jesus replied. “So if you are looking for Me, let these men go.”'),
('JHN', 18, 9, 'JHN.18.9', 'This was to fulfill the word He had spoken: “I have not lost one of those You have given Me.”'),
('JHN', 18, 10, 'JHN.18.10', 'Then Simon Peter drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear. The servant’s name was Malchus.'),
('JHN', 18, 11, 'JHN.18.11', '“Put your sword back in its sheath!” Jesus said to Peter. “Shall I not drink the cup the Father has given Me?”'),
('JHN', 18, 12, 'JHN.18.12', 'Then the band of soldiers, with its commander and the officers of the Jews, arrested Jesus and bound Him.'),
('JHN', 18, 13, 'JHN.18.13', 'They brought Him first to Annas, who was the father-in-law of Caiaphas, the high priest that year.'),
('JHN', 18, 14, 'JHN.18.14', 'Caiaphas was the one who had advised the Jews that it would be better if one man died for the people.'),
('JHN', 18, 15, 'JHN.18.15', 'Now Simon Peter and another disciple were following Jesus. Since that disciple was known to the high priest, he also went with Jesus into the courtyard of the high priest.'),
('JHN', 18, 16, 'JHN.18.16', 'But Peter stood outside at the door. Then the disciple who was known to the high priest went out and spoke to the doorkeeper, and brought Peter in.'),
('JHN', 18, 17, 'JHN.18.17', 'At this, the servant girl watching the door said to Peter, “Aren’t you also one of this man’s disciples?” “I am not,” he answered.'),
('JHN', 18, 18, 'JHN.18.18', 'Because it was cold, the servants and officers were standing around a charcoal fire they had made to keep warm. And Peter was also standing with them, warming himself.'),
('JHN', 18, 19, 'JHN.18.19', 'Meanwhile, the high priest questioned Jesus about His disciples and His teaching.'),
('JHN', 18, 20, 'JHN.18.20', '“I have spoken openly to the world,” Jesus answered. “I always taught in the synagogues and at the temple, where all the Jews come together. I said nothing in secret.'),
('JHN', 18, 21, 'JHN.18.21', 'Why are you asking Me? Ask those who heard My message. Surely they know what I said.”'),
('JHN', 18, 22, 'JHN.18.22', 'When Jesus had said this, one of the officers standing nearby slapped Him in the face and said, “Is this how You answer the high priest?”'),
('JHN', 18, 23, 'JHN.18.23', 'Jesus replied, “If I said something wrong, testify as to what was wrong. But if I spoke correctly, why did you strike Me?”'),
('JHN', 18, 24, 'JHN.18.24', 'Then Annas sent Him, still bound, to Caiaphas the high priest.'),
('JHN', 18, 25, 'JHN.18.25', 'Simon Peter was still standing and warming himself. So they asked him, “Aren’t you also one of His disciples?” He denied it and said, “I am not.”'),
('JHN', 18, 26, 'JHN.18.26', 'One of the high priest’s servants, a relative of the man whose ear Peter had cut off, asked, “Didn’t I see you with Him in the garden?”'),
('JHN', 18, 27, 'JHN.18.27', 'Peter denied it once more, and immediately a rooster crowed.'),
('JHN', 18, 28, 'JHN.18.28', 'Then they led Jesus away from Caiaphas into the Praetorium. By now it was early morning, and the Jews did not enter the Praetorium, to avoid being defiled and unable to eat the Passover.'),
('JHN', 18, 29, 'JHN.18.29', 'So Pilate went out to them and asked, “What accusation are you bringing against this man?”'),
('JHN', 18, 30, 'JHN.18.30', '“If He were not a criminal,” they replied, “we would not have handed Him over to you.”'),
('JHN', 18, 31, 'JHN.18.31', '“You take Him and judge Him by your own law,” Pilate told them. “We are not permitted to execute anyone,” the Jews replied.'),
('JHN', 18, 32, 'JHN.18.32', 'This was to fulfill the word that Jesus had spoken to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.'),
('JHN', 18, 33, 'JHN.18.33', 'Pilate went back into the Praetorium, summoned Jesus, and asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?”'),
('JHN', 18, 34, 'JHN.18.34', '“Are you saying this on your own,” Jesus asked, “or did others tell you about Me?”'),
('JHN', 18, 35, 'JHN.18.35', '“Am I a Jew?” Pilate replied. “Your own people and chief priests handed You over to me. What have You done?”'),
('JHN', 18, 36, 'JHN.18.36', 'Jesus answered, “My kingdom is not of this world; if it were, My servants would fight to prevent My arrest by the Jews. But now My kingdom is not of this realm.”'),
('JHN', 18, 37, 'JHN.18.37', '“Then You are a king!” Pilate said. “You say that I am a king,” Jesus answered. “For this reason I was born and have come into the world, to testify to the truth. Everyone who belongs to the truth listens to My voice.”'),
('JHN', 18, 38, 'JHN.18.38', '“What is truth?” Pilate asked. And having said this, he went out again to the Jews and told them, “I find no basis for a charge against Him.'),
('JHN', 18, 39, 'JHN.18.39', 'But it is your custom that I release to you one prisoner at the Passover. So then, do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?”'),
('JHN', 18, 40, 'JHN.18.40', '“Not this man,” they shouted, “but Barabbas!” (Now Barabbas was an insurrectionist.)'),
('JHN', 19, 1, 'JHN.19.1', 'Then Pilate took Jesus and had Him flogged.'),
('JHN', 19, 2, 'JHN.19.2', 'The soldiers twisted together a crown of thorns, set it on His head, and dressed Him in a purple robe.'),
('JHN', 19, 3, 'JHN.19.3', 'And they went up to Him again and again, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!” and slapping Him in the face.'),
('JHN', 19, 4, 'JHN.19.4', 'Once again Pilate came out and said to the Jews, “Look, I am bringing Him out to you to let you know that I find no basis for a charge against Him.”'),
('JHN', 19, 5, 'JHN.19.5', 'When Jesus came out wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe, Pilate said to them, “Here is the man!”'),
('JHN', 19, 6, 'JHN.19.6', 'As soon as the chief priests and officers saw Him, they shouted, “Crucify Him! Crucify Him!” “You take Him and crucify Him,” Pilate replied, “for I find no basis for a charge against Him.”'),
('JHN', 19, 7, 'JHN.19.7', '“We have a law,” answered the Jews, “and according to that law He must die, because He declared Himself to be the Son of God.”'),
('JHN', 19, 8, 'JHN.19.8', 'When Pilate heard this statement, he was even more afraid,'),
('JHN', 19, 9, 'JHN.19.9', 'and he went back into the Praetorium. “Where are You from?” he asked. But Jesus gave no answer.'),
('JHN', 19, 10, 'JHN.19.10', 'So Pilate said to Him, “Do You refuse to speak to me? Do You not know that I have authority to release You and authority to crucify You?”'),
('JHN', 19, 11, 'JHN.19.11', 'Jesus answered, “You would have no authority over Me if it were not given to you from above. Therefore the one who handed Me over to you is guilty of greater sin.”'),
('JHN', 19, 12, 'JHN.19.12', 'From then on, Pilate tried to release Him, but the Jews kept shouting, “If you release this man, you are no friend of Caesar. Anyone who declares himself a king is defying Caesar.”'),
('JHN', 19, 13, 'JHN.19.13', 'When Pilate heard these words, he brought Jesus out and sat on the judgment seat at a place called the Stone Pavement, which in Hebrew is Gabbatha.'),
('JHN', 19, 14, 'JHN.19.14', 'It was the day of Preparation for the Passover, about the sixth hour. And Pilate said to the Jews, “Here is your King!”'),
('JHN', 19, 15, 'JHN.19.15', 'At this, they shouted, “Away with Him! Away with Him! Crucify Him!” “Shall I crucify your King?” Pilate asked. “We have no king but Caesar,” replied the chief priests.'),
('JHN', 19, 16, 'JHN.19.16', 'Then Pilate handed Jesus over to be crucified, and the soldiers took Him away.'),
('JHN', 19, 17, 'JHN.19.17', 'Carrying His own cross, He went out to The Place of the Skull, which in Hebrew is called Golgotha.'),
('JHN', 19, 18, 'JHN.19.18', 'There they crucified Him, and with Him two others, one on each side, with Jesus in the middle.'),
('JHN', 19, 19, 'JHN.19.19', 'Pilate also had a notice posted on the cross. It read: JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.'),
('JHN', 19, 20, 'JHN.19.20', 'Many of the Jews read this sign, because the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city, and it was written in Hebrew, Latin, and Greek.'),
('JHN', 19, 21, 'JHN.19.21', 'So the chief priests of the Jews said to Pilate, “Do not write, ‘The King of the Jews,’ but only that He said, ‘I am the King of the Jews.’”'),
('JHN', 19, 22, 'JHN.19.22', 'Pilate answered, “What I have written, I have written.”'),
('JHN', 19, 23, 'JHN.19.23', 'When the soldiers had crucified Jesus, they divided His garments into four parts, one for each soldier, with the tunic remaining. It was seamless, woven in one piece from top to bottom.'),
('JHN', 19, 24, 'JHN.19.24', 'So they said to one another, “Let us not tear it. Instead, let us cast lots to see who will get it.” This was to fulfill the Scripture: “They divided My garments among them, and cast lots for My clothing.” So that is what the soldiers did.'),
('JHN', 19, 25, 'JHN.19.25', 'Near the cross of Jesus stood His mother and her sister, as well as Mary the wife of Clopas and Mary Magdalene.'),
('JHN', 19, 26, 'JHN.19.26', 'When Jesus saw His mother and the disciple whom He loved standing nearby, He said to His mother, “Woman, here is your son.”'),
('JHN', 19, 27, 'JHN.19.27', 'Then He said to the disciple, “Here is your mother.” So from that hour, this disciple took her into his home.'),
('JHN', 19, 28, 'JHN.19.28', 'After this, knowing that everything had now been accomplished, and to fulfill the Scripture, Jesus said, “I am thirsty.”'),
('JHN', 19, 29, 'JHN.19.29', 'A jar of sour wine was sitting there. So they soaked a sponge in the wine, put it on a stalk of hyssop, and lifted it to His mouth.'),
('JHN', 19, 30, 'JHN.19.30', 'When Jesus had received the sour wine, He said, “It is finished.” And bowing His head, He yielded up His spirit.'),
('JHN', 19, 31, 'JHN.19.31', 'It was the day of Preparation, and the next day was a High Sabbath. In order that the bodies would not remain on the cross during the Sabbath, the Jews asked Pilate to have the legs broken and the bodies removed.'),
('JHN', 19, 32, 'JHN.19.32', 'So the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first man who had been crucified with Jesus, and those of the other.'),
('JHN', 19, 33, 'JHN.19.33', 'But when they came to Jesus and saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs.'),
('JHN', 19, 34, 'JHN.19.34', 'Instead, one of the soldiers pierced His side with a spear, and immediately blood and water flowed out.'),
('JHN', 19, 35, 'JHN.19.35', 'The one who saw it has testified to this, and his testimony is true. He knows that he is telling the truth, so that you also may believe.'),
('JHN', 19, 36, 'JHN.19.36', 'Now these things happened so that the Scripture would be fulfilled: “Not one of His bones will be broken.”'),
('JHN', 19, 37, 'JHN.19.37', 'And, as another Scripture says: “They will look on the One they have pierced.”'),
('JHN', 19, 38, 'JHN.19.38', 'Afterward, Joseph of Arimathea, who was a disciple of Jesus (but secretly for fear of the Jews), asked Pilate to let him remove the body of Jesus. Pilate gave him permission, so he came and removed His body.'),
('JHN', 19, 39, 'JHN.19.39', 'Nicodemus, who had previously come to Jesus at night, also brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about seventy-five pounds.'),
('JHN', 19, 40, 'JHN.19.40', 'So they took the body of Jesus and wrapped it in linen cloths with the spices, according to the Jewish burial custom.'),
('JHN', 19, 41, 'JHN.19.41', 'Now there was a garden in the place where Jesus was crucified, and in the garden a new tomb in which no one had yet been laid.'),
('JHN', 19, 42, 'JHN.19.42', 'And because it was the Jewish day of Preparation and the tomb was nearby, they placed Jesus there.'),
('JHN', 20, 1, 'JHN.20.1', 'Early on the first day of the week, while it was still dark, Mary Magdalene went to the tomb and saw that the stone had been removed from the entrance.'),
('JHN', 20, 2, 'JHN.20.2', 'So she came running to Simon Peter and the other disciple, the one whom Jesus loved. “They have taken the Lord out of the tomb,” she said, “and we do not know where they have put Him!”'),
('JHN', 20, 3, 'JHN.20.3', 'Then Peter and the other disciple set out for the tomb.'),
('JHN', 20, 4, 'JHN.20.4', 'The two were running together, but the other disciple outran Peter and reached the tomb first.'),
('JHN', 20, 5, 'JHN.20.5', 'He bent down and looked in at the linen cloths lying there, but he did not go in.'),
('JHN', 20, 6, 'JHN.20.6', 'Simon Peter arrived just after him. He entered the tomb and saw the linen cloths lying there.'),
('JHN', 20, 7, 'JHN.20.7', 'The cloth that had been around Jesus’ head was rolled up, lying separate from the linen cloths.'),
('JHN', 20, 8, 'JHN.20.8', 'Then the other disciple, who had reached the tomb first, also went in. And he saw and believed.'),
('JHN', 20, 9, 'JHN.20.9', 'For they still did not understand from the Scripture that Jesus had to rise from the dead.'),
('JHN', 20, 10, 'JHN.20.10', 'Then the disciples returned to their homes.'),
('JHN', 20, 11, 'JHN.20.11', 'But Mary stood outside the tomb weeping. And as she wept, she bent down to look into the tomb,'),
('JHN', 20, 12, 'JHN.20.12', 'and she saw two angels in white sitting where the body of Jesus had lain, one at the head and the other at the feet.'),
('JHN', 20, 13, 'JHN.20.13', '“Woman, why are you weeping?” they asked. “Because they have taken my Lord away,” she said, “and I do not know where they have put Him.”'),
('JHN', 20, 14, 'JHN.20.14', 'When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing there. But she did not recognize that it was Jesus.'),
('JHN', 20, 15, 'JHN.20.15', '“Woman, why are you weeping?” Jesus asked. “Whom are you seeking?” Thinking He was the gardener, she said, “Sir, if you have carried Him off, tell me where you have put Him, and I will get Him.”'),
('JHN', 20, 16, 'JHN.20.16', 'Jesus said to her, “Mary.” She turned and said to Him in Hebrew, “Rabboni!” (which means “Teacher”).'),
('JHN', 20, 17, 'JHN.20.17', '“Do not cling to Me,” Jesus said, “for I have not yet ascended to the Father. But go and tell My brothers, ‘I am ascending to My Father and your Father, to My God and your God.’”'),
('JHN', 20, 18, 'JHN.20.18', 'Mary Magdalene went and announced to the disciples, “I have seen the Lord!” And she told them what He had said to her.'),
('JHN', 20, 19, 'JHN.20.19', 'It was the first day of the week, and that very evening, while the disciples were together with the doors locked for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood among them. “Peace be with you!” He said to them.'),
('JHN', 20, 20, 'JHN.20.20', 'After He had said this, He showed them His hands and His side. The disciples rejoiced when they saw the Lord.'),
('JHN', 20, 21, 'JHN.20.21', 'Again Jesus said to them, “Peace be with you. As the Father has sent Me, so also I am sending you.”'),
('JHN', 20, 22, 'JHN.20.22', 'When He had said this, He breathed on them and said, “Receive the Holy Spirit.'),
('JHN', 20, 23, 'JHN.20.23', 'If you forgive anyone his sins, they are forgiven; if you withhold forgiveness from anyone, it is withheld.”'),
('JHN', 20, 24, 'JHN.20.24', 'Now Thomas called Didymus, one of the Twelve, was not with the disciples when Jesus came.'),
('JHN', 20, 25, 'JHN.20.25', 'So the other disciples told him, “We have seen the Lord!” But he replied, “Unless I see the nail marks in His hands, and put my finger where the nails have been, and put my hand into His side, I will never believe.”'),
('JHN', 20, 26, 'JHN.20.26', 'Eight days later, His disciples were once again inside with the doors locked, and Thomas was with them. Jesus came and stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”'),
('JHN', 20, 27, 'JHN.20.27', 'Then Jesus said to Thomas, “Put your finger here and look at My hands. Reach out your hand and put it into My side. Stop doubting and believe.”'),
('JHN', 20, 28, 'JHN.20.28', 'Thomas replied, “My Lord and my God!”'),
('JHN', 20, 29, 'JHN.20.29', 'Jesus said to him, “Because you have seen Me, you have believed; blessed are those who have not seen and yet have believed.”'),
('JHN', 20, 30, 'JHN.20.30', 'Jesus performed many other signs in the presence of His disciples, which are not written in this book.'),
('JHN', 20, 31, 'JHN.20.31', 'But these are written so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that by believing you may have life in His name.'),
('JHN', 21, 1, 'JHN.21.1', 'Later, by the Sea of Tiberias, Jesus again revealed Himself to the disciples. He made Himself known in this way:'),
('JHN', 21, 2, 'JHN.21.2', 'Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael from Cana in Galilee, the sons of Zebedee, and two other disciples were together.'),
('JHN', 21, 3, 'JHN.21.3', 'Simon Peter told them, “I am going fishing.” “We will go with you,” they said. So they went out and got into the boat, but caught nothing that night.'),
('JHN', 21, 4, 'JHN.21.4', 'Early in the morning, Jesus stood on the shore, but the disciples did not recognize that it was Jesus.'),
('JHN', 21, 5, 'JHN.21.5', 'So He called out to them, “Children, do you have any fish?” “No,” they answered.'),
('JHN', 21, 6, 'JHN.21.6', 'He told them, “Cast the net on the right side of the boat, and you will find some.” So they cast it there, and they were unable to haul it in because of the great number of fish.'),
('JHN', 21, 7, 'JHN.21.7', 'Then the disciple whom Jesus loved said to Peter, “It is the Lord!” As soon as Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he put on his outer garment (for he had removed it) and jumped into the sea.'),
('JHN', 21, 8, 'JHN.21.8', 'The other disciples came ashore in the boat. They dragged in the net full of fish, for they were not far from land, only about a hundred yards.'),
('JHN', 21, 9, 'JHN.21.9', 'When they landed, they saw a charcoal fire there with fish on it, and some bread.'),
('JHN', 21, 10, 'JHN.21.10', 'Jesus told them, “Bring some of the fish you have just caught.”'),
('JHN', 21, 11, 'JHN.21.11', 'So Simon Peter went aboard and dragged the net ashore. It was full of large fish, 153, but even with so many, the net was not torn.'),
('JHN', 21, 12, 'JHN.21.12', '“Come, have breakfast,” Jesus said to them. None of the disciples dared to ask Him, “Who are You?” They knew it was the Lord.'),
('JHN', 21, 13, 'JHN.21.13', 'Jesus came and took the bread and gave it to them, and He did the same with the fish.'),
('JHN', 21, 14, 'JHN.21.14', 'This was now the third time that Jesus appeared to the disciples after He was raised from the dead.'),
('JHN', 21, 15, 'JHN.21.15', 'When they had finished eating, Jesus asked Simon Peter, “Simon son of John, do you love Me more than these?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus replied, “Feed My lambs.”'),
('JHN', 21, 16, 'JHN.21.16', 'Jesus asked a second time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus told him, “Shepherd My sheep.”'),
('JHN', 21, 17, 'JHN.21.17', 'Jesus asked a third time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” Peter was deeply hurt that Jesus had asked him a third time, “Do you love Me?” “Lord, You know all things,” he replied. “You know I love You.” Jesus said to him, “Feed My sheep.'),
('JHN', 21, 18, 'JHN.21.18', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, when you were young, you dressed yourself and walked where you wanted; but when you are old, you will stretch out your hands, and someone else will dress you and lead you where you do not want to go.”'),
('JHN', 21, 19, 'JHN.21.19', 'Jesus said this to indicate the kind of death by which Peter would glorify God. And after He had said this, He told him, “Follow Me.”'),
('JHN', 21, 20, 'JHN.21.20', 'Peter turned and saw the disciple whom Jesus loved following them. He was the one who had leaned back against Jesus at the supper to ask, “Lord, who is going to betray You?”'),
('JHN', 21, 21, 'JHN.21.21', 'When Peter saw him, he asked, “Lord, what about him?”'),
('JHN', 21, 22, 'JHN.21.22', 'Jesus answered, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you? You follow Me!”'),
('JHN', 21, 23, 'JHN.21.23', 'Because of this, the rumor spread among the brothers that this disciple would not die. However, Jesus did not say that he would not die, but only, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you?”'),
('JHN', 21, 24, 'JHN.21.24', 'This is the disciple who testifies to these things and who has written them down. And we know that his testimony is true.'),
('JHN', 21, 25, 'JHN.21.25', 'There are many more things that Jesus did. If all of them were written down, I suppose that not even the world itself would have space for the books that would be written.'),
('ACT', 1, 1, 'ACT.1.1', 'In my first book, O Theophilus, I wrote about all that Jesus began to do and to teach,'),
('ACT', 1, 2, 'ACT.1.2', 'until the day He was taken up to heaven, after giving instructions through the Holy Spirit to the apostles He had chosen.'),
('ACT', 1, 3, 'ACT.1.3', 'After His suffering, He presented Himself to them with many convincing proofs that He was alive. He appeared to them over a span of forty days and spoke about the kingdom of God.'),
('ACT', 1, 4, 'ACT.1.4', 'And while they were gathered together, He commanded them: “Do not leave Jerusalem, but wait for the gift the Father promised, which you have heard Me discuss.'),
('ACT', 1, 5, 'ACT.1.5', 'For John baptized with water, but in a few days you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.”'),
('ACT', 1, 6, 'ACT.1.6', 'So when they came together, they asked Him, “Lord, will You at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?”'),
('ACT', 1, 7, 'ACT.1.7', 'Jesus replied, “It is not for you to know times or seasons that the Father has fixed by His own authority.'),
('ACT', 1, 8, 'ACT.1.8', 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes upon you, and you will be My witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.”'),
('ACT', 1, 9, 'ACT.1.9', 'After He had said this, they watched as He was taken up, and a cloud hid Him from their sight.'),
('ACT', 1, 10, 'ACT.1.10', 'They were looking intently into the sky as He was going, when suddenly two men dressed in white stood beside them.'),
('ACT', 1, 11, 'ACT.1.11', '“Men of Galilee,” they said, “why do you stand here looking into the sky? This same Jesus, who has been taken from you into heaven, will come back in the same way you have seen Him go into heaven.”'),
('ACT', 1, 12, 'ACT.1.12', 'Then they returned to Jerusalem from the Mount of Olives, which is near the city, a Sabbath day’s journey away.'),
('ACT', 1, 13, 'ACT.1.13', 'When they arrived, they went to the upper room where they were staying: Peter and John, James and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas son of James.'),
('ACT', 1, 14, 'ACT.1.14', 'With one accord they all continued in prayer, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers.'),
('ACT', 1, 15, 'ACT.1.15', 'In those days Peter stood up among the brothers (a gathering of about a hundred and twenty) and said,'),
('ACT', 1, 16, 'ACT.1.16', '“Brothers, the Scripture had to be fulfilled that the Holy Spirit foretold through the mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide for those who arrested Jesus.'),
('ACT', 1, 17, 'ACT.1.17', 'He was one of our number and shared in this ministry.”'),
('ACT', 1, 18, 'ACT.1.18', '(Now with the reward for his wickedness Judas bought a field; there he fell headlong and burst open in the middle, and all his intestines spilled out.'),
('ACT', 1, 19, 'ACT.1.19', 'This became known to all who lived in Jerusalem, so they called that field in their own language Akeldama, that is, Field of Blood.)'),
('ACT', 1, 20, 'ACT.1.20', '“For it is written in the book of Psalms: ‘May his place be deserted; let there be no one to dwell in it,’ and, ‘May another take his position.’'),
('ACT', 1, 21, 'ACT.1.21', 'Therefore it is necessary to choose one of the men who have accompanied us the whole time the Lord Jesus went in and out among us,'),
('ACT', 1, 22, 'ACT.1.22', 'beginning from John’s baptism until the day Jesus was taken up from us. For one of these must become a witness with us of His resurrection.”'),
('ACT', 1, 23, 'ACT.1.23', 'So they proposed two men: Joseph called Barsabbas (also known as Justus) and Matthias.'),
('ACT', 1, 24, 'ACT.1.24', 'And they prayed, “Lord, You know everyone’s heart. Show us which of these two You have chosen'),
('ACT', 1, 25, 'ACT.1.25', 'to take up this ministry and apostleship, which Judas abandoned to go to his rightful place.”'),
('ACT', 1, 26, 'ACT.1.26', 'Then they cast lots, and the lot fell to Matthias. So he was added to the eleven apostles.'),
('ACT', 2, 1, 'ACT.2.1', 'When the day of Pentecost came, they were all together in one place.'),
('ACT', 2, 2, 'ACT.2.2', 'Suddenly a sound like a mighty rushing wind came from heaven and filled the whole house where they were sitting.'),
('ACT', 2, 3, 'ACT.2.3', 'They saw tongues like flames of fire that separated and came to rest on each of them.'),
('ACT', 2, 4, 'ACT.2.4', 'And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit enabled them.'),
('ACT', 2, 5, 'ACT.2.5', 'Now there were dwelling in Jerusalem God-fearing Jews from every nation under heaven.'),
('ACT', 2, 6, 'ACT.2.6', 'And when this sound rang out, a crowd came together in bewilderment, because each one heard them speaking his own language.'),
('ACT', 2, 7, 'ACT.2.7', 'Astounded and amazed, they asked, “Are not all these who are speaking Galileans?'),
('ACT', 2, 8, 'ACT.2.8', 'How is it then that each of us hears them in his own native language?'),
('ACT', 2, 9, 'ACT.2.9', 'Parthians, Medes, and Elamites; residents of Mesopotamia, Judea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,'),
('ACT', 2, 10, 'ACT.2.10', 'Phrygia and Pamphylia, Egypt and the parts of Libya near Cyrene; visitors from Rome,'),
('ACT', 2, 11, 'ACT.2.11', 'both Jews and converts to Judaism; Cretans and Arabs—we hear them declaring the wonders of God in our own tongues!”'),
('ACT', 2, 12, 'ACT.2.12', 'Astounded and perplexed, they asked one another, “What does this mean?”'),
('ACT', 2, 13, 'ACT.2.13', 'But others mocked them and said, “They are drunk on new wine!”'),
('ACT', 2, 14, 'ACT.2.14', 'Then Peter stood up with the Eleven, lifted up his voice, and addressed the crowd: “Men of Judea and all who dwell in Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen carefully to my words.'),
('ACT', 2, 15, 'ACT.2.15', 'These men are not drunk, as you suppose. It is only the third hour of the day!'),
('ACT', 2, 16, 'ACT.2.16', 'No, this is what was spoken by the prophet Joel:'),
('ACT', 2, 17, 'ACT.2.17', '‘In the last days, God says, I will pour out My Spirit on all people. Your sons and daughters will prophesy, your young men will see visions, your old men will dream dreams.'),
('ACT', 2, 18, 'ACT.2.18', 'Even on My menservants and maidservants I will pour out My Spirit in those days, and they will prophesy.'),
('ACT', 2, 19, 'ACT.2.19', 'I will show wonders in the heavens above and signs on the earth below, blood and fire and billows of smoke.'),
('ACT', 2, 20, 'ACT.2.20', 'The sun will be turned to darkness, and the moon to blood, before the coming of the great and glorious Day of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 2, 21, 'ACT.2.21', 'And everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.’'),
('ACT', 2, 22, 'ACT.2.22', 'Men of Israel, listen to this message: Jesus of Nazareth was a man certified by God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs, which God did among you through Him, as you yourselves know.'),
('ACT', 2, 23, 'ACT.2.23', 'He was delivered up by God’s set plan and foreknowledge, and you, by the hands of the lawless, put Him to death by nailing Him to the cross.'),
('ACT', 2, 24, 'ACT.2.24', 'But God raised Him from the dead, releasing Him from the agony of death, because it was impossible for death to keep Him in its grip.'),
('ACT', 2, 25, 'ACT.2.25', 'David says about Him: ‘I saw the Lord always before me; because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.'),
('ACT', 2, 26, 'ACT.2.26', 'Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will dwell in hope,'),
('ACT', 2, 27, 'ACT.2.27', 'because You will not abandon my soul to Hades, nor will You let Your Holy One see decay.'),
('ACT', 2, 28, 'ACT.2.28', 'You have made known to me the paths of life; You will fill me with joy in Your presence.’'),
('ACT', 2, 29, 'ACT.2.29', 'Brothers, I can tell you with confidence that the patriarch David died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day.'),
('ACT', 2, 30, 'ACT.2.30', 'But he was a prophet and knew that God had promised him on oath that He would place one of his descendants on his throne.'),
('ACT', 2, 31, 'ACT.2.31', 'Foreseeing this, David spoke about the resurrection of the Christ, that He was not abandoned to Hades, nor did His body see decay.'),
('ACT', 2, 32, 'ACT.2.32', 'God has raised this Jesus to life, to which we are all witnesses.'),
('ACT', 2, 33, 'ACT.2.33', 'Exalted, then, to the right hand of God, He has received from the Father the promised Holy Spirit and has poured out what you now see and hear.'),
('ACT', 2, 34, 'ACT.2.34', 'For David did not ascend into heaven, but he himself says: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand'),
('ACT', 2, 35, 'ACT.2.35', 'until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”’'),
('ACT', 2, 36, 'ACT.2.36', 'Therefore let all Israel know with certainty that God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Christ!”'),
('ACT', 2, 37, 'ACT.2.37', 'When the people heard this, they were cut to the heart and asked Peter and the other apostles, “Brothers, what shall we do?”'),
('ACT', 2, 38, 'ACT.2.38', 'Peter replied, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.'),
('ACT', 2, 39, 'ACT.2.39', 'This promise belongs to you and your children and to all who are far off—to all whom the Lord our God will call to Himself.”'),
('ACT', 2, 40, 'ACT.2.40', 'With many other words he testified, and he urged them, “Be saved from this corrupt generation.”'),
('ACT', 2, 41, 'ACT.2.41', 'Those who embraced his message were baptized, and about three thousand were added to the believers that day.'),
('ACT', 2, 42, 'ACT.2.42', 'They devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching and to the fellowship, to the breaking of bread and to prayer.'),
('ACT', 2, 43, 'ACT.2.43', 'A sense of awe came over everyone, and the apostles performed many wonders and signs.'),
('ACT', 2, 44, 'ACT.2.44', 'All the believers were together and had everything in common.'),
('ACT', 2, 45, 'ACT.2.45', 'Selling their possessions and goods, they shared with anyone who was in need.'),
('ACT', 2, 46, 'ACT.2.46', 'With one accord they continued to meet daily in the temple courts and to break bread from house to house, sharing their meals with gladness and sincerity of heart,'),
('ACT', 2, 47, 'ACT.2.47', 'praising God and enjoying the favor of all the people. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved.'),
('ACT', 3, 1, 'ACT.3.1', 'One afternoon Peter and John were going up to the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth hour.'),
('ACT', 3, 2, 'ACT.3.2', 'And a man who was lame from birth was being carried to the temple gate called Beautiful, where he was put every day to beg from those entering the temple courts.'),
('ACT', 3, 3, 'ACT.3.3', 'When he saw Peter and John about to enter, he asked them for money.'),
('ACT', 3, 4, 'ACT.3.4', 'Peter looked directly at him, as did John. “Look at us!” said Peter.'),
('ACT', 3, 5, 'ACT.3.5', 'So the man gave them his attention, expecting to receive something from them.'),
('ACT', 3, 6, 'ACT.3.6', 'But Peter said, “Silver or gold I do not have, but what I have I give you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!”'),
('ACT', 3, 7, 'ACT.3.7', 'Taking him by the right hand, Peter helped him up, and at once the man’s feet and ankles were made strong.'),
('ACT', 3, 8, 'ACT.3.8', 'He sprang to his feet and began to walk. Then he went with them into the temple courts, walking and leaping and praising God.'),
('ACT', 3, 9, 'ACT.3.9', 'When all the people saw him walking and praising God,'),
('ACT', 3, 10, 'ACT.3.10', 'they recognized him as the man who used to sit begging at the Beautiful Gate of the temple, and they were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him.'),
('ACT', 3, 11, 'ACT.3.11', 'While the man clung to Peter and John, all the people were astonished and ran to them in the walkway called Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
('ACT', 3, 12, 'ACT.3.12', 'And when Peter saw this, he addressed the people: “Men of Israel, why are you surprised by this? Why do you stare at us as if by our own power or godliness we had made this man walk?'),
('ACT', 3, 13, 'ACT.3.13', 'The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified His servant Jesus. You handed Him over and rejected Him before Pilate, even though he had decided to release Him.'),
('ACT', 3, 14, 'ACT.3.14', 'You rejected the Holy and Righteous One and asked that a murderer be released to you.'),
('ACT', 3, 15, 'ACT.3.15', 'You killed the Author of life, but God raised Him from the dead, and we are witnesses of this fact.'),
('ACT', 3, 16, 'ACT.3.16', 'By faith in the name of Jesus, this man whom you see and know has been made strong. It is Jesus’ name and the faith that comes through Him that has given him this complete healing in your presence.'),
('ACT', 3, 17, 'ACT.3.17', 'And now, brothers, I know that you acted in ignorance, as did your leaders.'),
('ACT', 3, 18, 'ACT.3.18', 'But in this way God has fulfilled what He foretold through all the prophets, saying that His Christ would suffer.'),
('ACT', 3, 19, 'ACT.3.19', 'Repent, then, and turn back, so that your sins may be wiped away,'),
('ACT', 3, 20, 'ACT.3.20', 'that times of refreshing may come from the presence of the Lord, and that He may send Jesus, the Christ, who has been appointed for you.'),
('ACT', 3, 21, 'ACT.3.21', 'Heaven must take Him in until the time comes for the restoration of all things, which God announced long ago through His holy prophets.'),
('ACT', 3, 22, 'ACT.3.22', 'For Moses said, ‘The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers. You must listen to Him in everything He tells you.'),
('ACT', 3, 23, 'ACT.3.23', 'Everyone who does not listen to Him will be completely cut off from among his people.’'),
('ACT', 3, 24, 'ACT.3.24', 'Indeed, all the prophets from Samuel on, as many as have spoken, have proclaimed these days.'),
('ACT', 3, 25, 'ACT.3.25', 'And you are sons of the prophets and of the covenant God made with your fathers when He said to Abraham, ‘Through your offspring all the families of the earth will be blessed.’'),
('ACT', 3, 26, 'ACT.3.26', 'When God raised up His Servant, He sent Him first to you to bless you by turning each of you from your wicked ways.”'),
('ACT', 4, 1, 'ACT.4.1', 'While Peter and John were speaking to the people, the priests and the captain of the temple guard and the Sadducees came up to them,'),
('ACT', 4, 2, 'ACT.4.2', 'greatly disturbed that they were teaching the people and proclaiming in Jesus the resurrection of the dead.'),
('ACT', 4, 3, 'ACT.4.3', 'They seized Peter and John, and because it was evening, they put them in custody until the next day.'),
('ACT', 4, 4, 'ACT.4.4', 'But many who heard the message believed, and the number of men grew to about five thousand.'),
('ACT', 4, 5, 'ACT.4.5', 'The next day the rulers, elders, and scribes assembled in Jerusalem,'),
('ACT', 4, 6, 'ACT.4.6', 'along with Annas the high priest, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and many others from the high priest’s family.'),
('ACT', 4, 7, 'ACT.4.7', 'They had Peter and John brought in and began to question them: “By what power or what name did you do this?”'),
('ACT', 4, 8, 'ACT.4.8', 'Then Peter, filled with the Holy Spirit, said to them, “Rulers and elders of the people!'),
('ACT', 4, 9, 'ACT.4.9', 'If we are being examined today about a kind service to a man who was lame, to determine how he was healed,'),
('ACT', 4, 10, 'ACT.4.10', 'then let this be known to all of you and to all the people of Israel: It is by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified but whom God raised from the dead, that this man stands before you healed.'),
('ACT', 4, 11, 'ACT.4.11', 'This Jesus is ‘the stone you builders rejected, which has become the cornerstone.’'),
('ACT', 4, 12, 'ACT.4.12', 'Salvation exists in no one else, for there is no other name under heaven given to men by which we must be saved.”'),
('ACT', 4, 13, 'ACT.4.13', 'When they saw the boldness of Peter and John and realized that they were unschooled, ordinary men, they marveled and took note that these men had been with Jesus.'),
('ACT', 4, 14, 'ACT.4.14', 'And seeing the man who had been healed standing there with them, they had nothing to say in response.'),
('ACT', 4, 15, 'ACT.4.15', 'So they ordered them to leave the Sanhedrin and then conferred together.'),
('ACT', 4, 16, 'ACT.4.16', '“What shall we do with these men?” they asked. “It is clear to everyone living in Jerusalem that a remarkable miracle has occurred through them, and we cannot deny it.'),
('ACT', 4, 17, 'ACT.4.17', 'But to keep this message from spreading any further among the people, we must warn them not to speak to anyone in this name.”'),
('ACT', 4, 18, 'ACT.4.18', 'Then they called them in again and commanded them not to speak or teach at all in the name of Jesus.'),
('ACT', 4, 19, 'ACT.4.19', 'But Peter and John replied, “Judge for yourselves whether it is right in God’s sight to listen to you rather than God.'),
('ACT', 4, 20, 'ACT.4.20', 'For we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.”'),
('ACT', 4, 21, 'ACT.4.21', 'After further threats they let them go. They could not find a way to punish them, because all the people were glorifying God for what had happened.'),
('ACT', 4, 22, 'ACT.4.22', 'For the man who was miraculously healed was over forty years old.'),
('ACT', 4, 23, 'ACT.4.23', 'On their release, Peter and John returned to their own people and reported everything that the chief priests and elders had said to them.'),
('ACT', 4, 24, 'ACT.4.24', 'When the believers heard this, they lifted up their voices to God with one accord. “Sovereign Lord,” they said, “You made the heaven and the earth and the sea and everything in them.'),
('ACT', 4, 25, 'ACT.4.25', 'You spoke by the Holy Spirit through the mouth of Your servant, our father David: ‘Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?'),
('ACT', 4, 26, 'ACT.4.26', 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together against the Lord and against His Anointed One.’'),
('ACT', 4, 27, 'ACT.4.27', 'In fact, this is the very city where Herod and Pontius Pilate conspired with the Gentiles and the people of Israel against Your holy servant Jesus, whom You anointed.'),
('ACT', 4, 28, 'ACT.4.28', 'They carried out what Your hand and will had decided beforehand would happen.'),
('ACT', 4, 29, 'ACT.4.29', 'And now, Lord, consider their threats, and enable Your servants to speak Your word with complete boldness,'),
('ACT', 4, 30, 'ACT.4.30', 'as You stretch out Your hand to heal and perform signs and wonders through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.”'),
('ACT', 4, 31, 'ACT.4.31', 'After they had prayed, their meeting place was shaken, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and spoke the word of God boldly.'),
('ACT', 4, 32, 'ACT.4.32', 'The multitude of believers was one in heart and soul. No one claimed that any of his possessions was his own, but they shared everything they owned.'),
('ACT', 4, 33, 'ACT.4.33', 'With great power the apostles continued to give their testimony about the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. And abundant grace was upon them all.'),
('ACT', 4, 34, 'ACT.4.34', 'There were no needy ones among them, because those who owned lands or houses would sell their property, bring the proceeds from the sales,'),
('ACT', 4, 35, 'ACT.4.35', 'and lay them at the apostles’ feet for distribution to anyone as he had need.'),
('ACT', 4, 36, 'ACT.4.36', 'Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas (meaning Son of Encouragement),'),
('ACT', 4, 37, 'ACT.4.37', 'sold a field he owned, brought the money, and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
('ACT', 5, 1, 'ACT.5.1', 'Now a man named Ananias, together with his wife Sapphira, also sold a piece of property.'),
('ACT', 5, 2, 'ACT.5.2', 'With his wife’s full knowledge, he kept back some of the proceeds for himself, but brought a portion and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
('ACT', 5, 3, 'ACT.5.3', 'Then Peter said, “Ananias, how is it that Satan has filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and withhold some of the proceeds from the land?'),
('ACT', 5, 4, 'ACT.5.4', 'Did it not belong to you before it was sold? And after it was sold, was it not at your disposal? How could you conceive such a deed in your heart? You have not lied to men, but to God!”'),
('ACT', 5, 5, 'ACT.5.5', 'On hearing these words, Ananias fell down and died. And great fear came over all who heard what had happened.'),
('ACT', 5, 6, 'ACT.5.6', 'Then the young men stepped forward, wrapped up his body, and carried him out and buried him.'),
('ACT', 5, 7, 'ACT.5.7', 'About three hours later his wife also came in, unaware of what had happened.'),
('ACT', 5, 8, 'ACT.5.8', '“Tell me,” said Peter, “is this the price you and your husband got for the land?” “Yes,” she answered, “that is the price.”'),
('ACT', 5, 9, 'ACT.5.9', '“How could you agree to test the Spirit of the Lord?” Peter replied. “Look, the feet of the men who buried your husband are at the door, and they will carry you out also.”'),
('ACT', 5, 10, 'ACT.5.10', 'At that instant she fell down at his feet and died. Then the young men came in and, finding her dead, carried her out and buried her beside her husband.'),
('ACT', 5, 11, 'ACT.5.11', 'And great fear came over the whole church and all who heard about these events.'),
('ACT', 5, 12, 'ACT.5.12', 'The apostles performed many signs and wonders among the people, and with one accord the believers gathered together in Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
('ACT', 5, 13, 'ACT.5.13', 'Although the people regarded them highly, no one else dared to join them.'),
('ACT', 5, 14, 'ACT.5.14', 'Yet more and more believers were brought to the Lord—large numbers of both men and women.'),
('ACT', 5, 15, 'ACT.5.15', 'As a result, people brought the sick into the streets and laid them on cots and mats, so that at least Peter’s shadow might fall on some of them as he passed by.'),
('ACT', 5, 16, 'ACT.5.16', 'Crowds also gathered from the towns around Jerusalem, bringing the sick and those tormented by unclean spirits, and all of them were healed.'),
('ACT', 5, 17, 'ACT.5.17', 'Then the high priest and all his associates, who belonged to the party of the Sadducees, were filled with jealousy. They went out'),
('ACT', 5, 18, 'ACT.5.18', 'and arrested the apostles and put them in the public jail.'),
('ACT', 5, 19, 'ACT.5.19', 'But during the night an angel of the Lord opened the doors of the jail and brought them out, saying,'),
('ACT', 5, 20, 'ACT.5.20', '“Go, stand in the temple courts and tell the people the full message of this new life.”'),
('ACT', 5, 21, 'ACT.5.21', 'At daybreak the apostles entered the temple courts as they had been told and began to teach the people. When the high priest and his associates arrived, they convened the Sanhedrin—the full assembly of the elders of Israel—and sent to the jail for the apostles.'),
('ACT', 5, 22, 'ACT.5.22', 'But on arriving at the jail, the officers did not find them there. So they returned with the report:'),
('ACT', 5, 23, 'ACT.5.23', '“We found the jail securely locked, with the guards posted at the doors; but when we opened them, we found no one inside.”'),
('ACT', 5, 24, 'ACT.5.24', 'When the captain of the temple guard and the chief priests heard this account, they were perplexed as to what was happening.'),
('ACT', 5, 25, 'ACT.5.25', 'Then someone came in and announced, “Look, the men you put in jail are standing in the temple courts teaching the people!”'),
('ACT', 5, 26, 'ACT.5.26', 'At that point, the captain went with the officers and brought the apostles—but not by force, for fear the people would stone them.'),
('ACT', 5, 27, 'ACT.5.27', 'They brought them in and made them stand before the Sanhedrin, where the high priest interrogated them.'),
('ACT', 5, 28, 'ACT.5.28', '“We gave you strict orders not to teach in this name,” he said. “Yet you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching and are determined to make us responsible for this man’s blood.”'),
('ACT', 5, 29, 'ACT.5.29', 'But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men.'),
('ACT', 5, 30, 'ACT.5.30', 'The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you had killed by hanging Him on a tree.'),
('ACT', 5, 31, 'ACT.5.31', 'God exalted Him to His right hand as Prince and Savior, in order to grant repentance and forgiveness of sins to Israel.'),
('ACT', 5, 32, 'ACT.5.32', 'We are witnesses of these things, and so is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey Him.”'),
('ACT', 5, 33, 'ACT.5.33', 'When the Council members heard this, they were enraged, and they resolved to put the apostles to death.'),
('ACT', 5, 34, 'ACT.5.34', 'But a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law who was honored by all the people, stood up in the Sanhedrin and ordered that the men be put outside for a short time.'),
('ACT', 5, 35, 'ACT.5.35', '“Men of Israel,” he said, “consider carefully what you are about to do to these men.'),
('ACT', 5, 36, 'ACT.5.36', 'Some time ago Theudas rose up, claiming to be somebody, and about four hundred men joined him. He was killed, all his followers were dispersed, and it all came to nothing.'),
('ACT', 5, 37, 'ACT.5.37', 'After him, Judas the Galilean appeared in the days of the census and drew away people after him. He too perished, and all his followers were scattered.'),
('ACT', 5, 38, 'ACT.5.38', 'So in the present case I advise you: Leave these men alone. Let them go! For if their purpose or endeavor is of human origin, it will fail.'),
('ACT', 5, 39, 'ACT.5.39', 'But if it is from God, you will not be able to stop them. You may even find yourselves fighting against God.”'),
('ACT', 5, 40, 'ACT.5.40', 'At this, they yielded to Gamaliel. They called the apostles in and had them flogged. Then they ordered them not to speak in the name of Jesus, and released them.'),
('ACT', 5, 41, 'ACT.5.41', 'The apostles left the Sanhedrin, rejoicing that they had been counted worthy of suffering disgrace for the Name.'),
('ACT', 5, 42, 'ACT.5.42', 'Every day, in the temple courts and from house to house, they did not stop teaching and proclaiming the good news that Jesus is the Christ.'),
('ACT', 6, 1, 'ACT.6.1', 'In those days when the disciples were increasing in number, the Grecian Jews among them began to grumble against the Hebraic Jews because their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution of food.'),
('ACT', 6, 2, 'ACT.6.2', 'So the Twelve summoned all the disciples and said, “It is unacceptable for us to neglect the word of God in order to wait on tables.'),
('ACT', 6, 3, 'ACT.6.3', 'Therefore, brothers, select from among you seven men confirmed to be full of the Spirit and wisdom. We will assign this responsibility to them'),
('ACT', 6, 4, 'ACT.6.4', 'and will devote ourselves to prayer and to the ministry of the word.”'),
('ACT', 6, 5, 'ACT.6.5', 'This proposal pleased the whole group. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit, as well as Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolas from Antioch, a convert to Judaism.'),
('ACT', 6, 6, 'ACT.6.6', 'They presented these seven to the apostles, who prayed and laid their hands on them.'),
('ACT', 6, 7, 'ACT.6.7', 'So the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith.'),
('ACT', 6, 8, 'ACT.6.8', 'Now Stephen, who was full of grace and power, was performing great wonders and signs among the people.'),
('ACT', 6, 9, 'ACT.6.9', 'But resistance arose from what was called the Synagogue of the Freedmen, including Cyrenians, Alexandrians, and men from the provinces of Cilicia and Asia. They disputed with Stephen,'),
('ACT', 6, 10, 'ACT.6.10', 'but they could not stand up to his wisdom or the Spirit by whom he spoke.'),
('ACT', 6, 11, 'ACT.6.11', 'Then they prompted some men to say, “We heard Stephen speak words of blasphemy against Moses and against God.”'),
('ACT', 6, 12, 'ACT.6.12', 'So they stirred up the people, elders, and scribes and confronted Stephen. They seized him and brought him before the Sanhedrin,'),
('ACT', 6, 13, 'ACT.6.13', 'where they presented false witnesses who said, “This man never stops speaking against this holy place and against the law.'),
('ACT', 6, 14, 'ACT.6.14', 'For we have heard him say that Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place and change the customs that Moses handed down to us.”'),
('ACT', 6, 15, 'ACT.6.15', 'All who were sitting in the Sanhedrin looked intently at Stephen, and they saw that his face was like the face of an angel.'),
('ACT', 7, 1, 'ACT.7.1', 'Then the high priest asked Stephen, “Are these charges true?”'),
('ACT', 7, 2, 'ACT.7.2', 'And Stephen declared: “Brothers and fathers, listen to me! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham while he was still in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,'),
('ACT', 7, 3, 'ACT.7.3', 'and told him, ‘Leave your country and your kindred and go to the land I will show you.’'),
('ACT', 7, 4, 'ACT.7.4', 'So Abraham left the land of the Chaldeans and settled in Haran. After his father died, God brought him out of that place and into this land where you are now living.'),
('ACT', 7, 5, 'ACT.7.5', 'He gave him no inheritance here, not even a foot of ground. But God promised to give possession of the land to Abraham and his descendants, even though he did not yet have a child.'),
('ACT', 7, 6, 'ACT.7.6', 'God told him that his descendants would be foreigners in a strange land, and that they would be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years.'),
('ACT', 7, 7, 'ACT.7.7', '‘But I will punish the nation that enslaves them,’ God said, ‘and afterward they will come forth and worship Me in this place.’'),
('ACT', 7, 8, 'ACT.7.8', 'Then God gave Abraham the covenant of circumcision, and Abraham became the father of Isaac and circumcised him on the eighth day. And Isaac became the father of Jacob, and Jacob of the twelve patriarchs.'),
('ACT', 7, 9, 'ACT.7.9', 'Because the patriarchs were jealous of Joseph, they sold him as a slave into Egypt. But God was with him'),
('ACT', 7, 10, 'ACT.7.10', 'and rescued him from all his troubles. He granted Joseph favor and wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king of Egypt, who appointed him ruler over Egypt and all his household.'),
('ACT', 7, 11, 'ACT.7.11', 'Then famine and great suffering swept across Egypt and Canaan, and our fathers could not find food.'),
('ACT', 7, 12, 'ACT.7.12', 'When Jacob heard that there was grain in Egypt, he sent our fathers on their first visit.'),
('ACT', 7, 13, 'ACT.7.13', 'On their second visit, Joseph revealed his identity to his brothers, and his family became known to Pharaoh.'),
('ACT', 7, 14, 'ACT.7.14', 'Then Joseph sent for his father Jacob and all his relatives, seventy-five in all.'),
('ACT', 7, 15, 'ACT.7.15', 'So Jacob went down to Egypt, where he and our fathers died.'),
('ACT', 7, 16, 'ACT.7.16', 'Their bones were carried back to Shechem and placed in the tomb that Abraham had bought from the sons of Hamor at Shechem for a price he paid in silver.'),
('ACT', 7, 17, 'ACT.7.17', 'As the time drew near for God to fulfill His promise to Abraham, our people in Egypt increased greatly in number.'),
('ACT', 7, 18, 'ACT.7.18', 'Then another king, who knew nothing of Joseph, arose over Egypt.'),
('ACT', 7, 19, 'ACT.7.19', 'He exploited our people and oppressed our fathers, forcing them to abandon their infants so they would die.'),
('ACT', 7, 20, 'ACT.7.20', 'At that time Moses was born, and he was beautiful in the sight of God. For three months he was nurtured in his father’s house.'),
('ACT', 7, 21, 'ACT.7.21', 'When he was set outside, Pharaoh’s daughter took him and brought him up as her own son.'),
('ACT', 7, 22, 'ACT.7.22', 'So Moses was educated in all the wisdom of the Egyptians and was powerful in speech and action.'),
('ACT', 7, 23, 'ACT.7.23', 'When Moses was forty years old, he decided to visit his brothers, the children of Israel.'),
('ACT', 7, 24, 'ACT.7.24', 'And when he saw one of them being mistreated, Moses went to his defense and avenged him by striking down the Egyptian who was oppressing him.'),
('ACT', 7, 25, 'ACT.7.25', 'He assumed his brothers would understand that God was using him to deliver them, but they did not.'),
('ACT', 7, 26, 'ACT.7.26', 'The next day he came upon two Israelites who were fighting, and he tried to reconcile them, saying, ‘Men, you are brothers. Why are you mistreating each other?’'),
('ACT', 7, 27, 'ACT.7.27', 'But the man who was abusing his neighbor pushed Moses aside and said, ‘Who made you ruler and judge over us?'),
('ACT', 7, 28, 'ACT.7.28', 'Do you want to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?’'),
('ACT', 7, 29, 'ACT.7.29', 'At this remark, Moses fled to the land of Midian, where he lived as a foreigner and had two sons.'),
('ACT', 7, 30, 'ACT.7.30', 'After forty years had passed, an angel appeared to Moses in the flames of a burning bush in the desert near Mount Sinai.'),
('ACT', 7, 31, 'ACT.7.31', 'When Moses saw it, he marveled at the sight. As he approached to look more closely, the voice of the Lord came to him:'),
('ACT', 7, 32, 'ACT.7.32', '‘I am the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.’ Moses trembled with fear and did not dare to look.'),
('ACT', 7, 33, 'ACT.7.33', 'Then the Lord said to him, ‘Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground.'),
('ACT', 7, 34, 'ACT.7.34', 'I have indeed seen the oppression of My people in Egypt. I have heard their groaning and have come down to deliver them. Now come, I will send you back to Egypt.’'),
('ACT', 7, 35, 'ACT.7.35', 'This Moses, whom they had rejected with the words, ‘Who made you ruler and judge?’ is the one whom God sent to be their ruler and redeemer through the angel who appeared to him in the bush.'),
('ACT', 7, 36, 'ACT.7.36', 'He led them out and performed wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, at the Red Sea, and for forty years in the wilderness.'),
('ACT', 7, 37, 'ACT.7.37', 'This is the same Moses who told the Israelites, ‘God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers.’'),
('ACT', 7, 38, 'ACT.7.38', 'He was in the assembly in the wilderness with the angel who spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and with our fathers. And he received living words to pass on to us.'),
('ACT', 7, 39, 'ACT.7.39', 'But our fathers refused to obey him. Instead, they rejected him and in their hearts turned back to Egypt.'),
('ACT', 7, 40, 'ACT.7.40', 'They said to Aaron, ‘Make us gods who will go before us! As for this Moses who led us out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what has happened to him.’'),
('ACT', 7, 41, 'ACT.7.41', 'At that time they made a calf and offered a sacrifice to the idol, rejoicing in the works of their hands.'),
('ACT', 7, 42, 'ACT.7.42', 'But God turned away from them and gave them over to the worship of the host of heaven, as it is written in the book of the prophets: ‘Did you bring Me sacrifices and offerings forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?'),
('ACT', 7, 43, 'ACT.7.43', 'You have taken along the tabernacle of Molech and the star of your god Rephan, the idols you made to worship. Therefore I will send you into exile beyond Babylon.’'),
('ACT', 7, 44, 'ACT.7.44', 'Our fathers had the tabernacle of the Testimony with them in the wilderness. It was constructed exactly as God had directed Moses, according to the pattern he had seen.'),
('ACT', 7, 45, 'ACT.7.45', 'And our fathers who received it brought it in with Joshua when they dispossessed the nations God drove out before them. It remained until the time of David,'),
('ACT', 7, 46, 'ACT.7.46', 'who found favor in the sight of God and asked to provide a dwelling place for the God of Jacob.'),
('ACT', 7, 47, 'ACT.7.47', 'But it was Solomon who built the house for Him.'),
('ACT', 7, 48, 'ACT.7.48', 'However, the Most High does not dwell in houses made by human hands. As the prophet says:'),
('ACT', 7, 49, 'ACT.7.49', '‘Heaven is My throne and the earth is My footstool. What kind of house will you build for Me, says the Lord, or where will My place of repose be?'),
('ACT', 7, 50, 'ACT.7.50', 'Has not My hand made all these things?’'),
('ACT', 7, 51, 'ACT.7.51', 'You stiff-necked people with uncircumcised hearts and ears! You always resist the Holy Spirit, just as your fathers did.'),
('ACT', 7, 52, 'ACT.7.52', 'Which of the prophets did your fathers fail to persecute? They even killed those who foretold the coming of the Righteous One. And now you are His betrayers and murderers—'),
('ACT', 7, 53, 'ACT.7.53', 'you who received the law ordained by angels, yet have not kept it.”'),
('ACT', 7, 54, 'ACT.7.54', 'On hearing this, the members of the Sanhedrin were enraged, and they gnashed their teeth at him.'),
('ACT', 7, 55, 'ACT.7.55', 'But Stephen, full of the Holy Spirit, looked intently into heaven and saw the glory of God and Jesus standing at the right hand of God.'),
('ACT', 7, 56, 'ACT.7.56', '“Look,” he said, “I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God.”'),
('ACT', 7, 57, 'ACT.7.57', 'At this they covered their ears, cried out in a loud voice, and rushed together at him.'),
('ACT', 7, 58, 'ACT.7.58', 'They dragged him out of the city and began to stone him. Meanwhile the witnesses laid their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul.'),
('ACT', 7, 59, 'ACT.7.59', 'While they were stoning him, Stephen appealed, “Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.”'),
('ACT', 7, 60, 'ACT.7.60', 'Falling on his knees, he cried out in a loud voice, “Lord, do not hold this sin against them.” And when he had said this, he fell asleep.'),
('ACT', 8, 1, 'ACT.8.1', 'And Saul was there, giving approval to Stephen’s death. On that day a great persecution broke out against the church in Jerusalem, and all except the apostles were scattered throughout Judea and Samaria.'),
('ACT', 8, 2, 'ACT.8.2', 'God-fearing men buried Stephen and mourned deeply over him.'),
('ACT', 8, 3, 'ACT.8.3', 'But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women and put them in prison.'),
('ACT', 8, 4, 'ACT.8.4', 'Those who had been scattered preached the word wherever they went.'),
('ACT', 8, 5, 'ACT.8.5', 'Philip went down to a city in Samaria and proclaimed the Christ to them.'),
('ACT', 8, 6, 'ACT.8.6', 'The crowds all paid close attention to Philip’s message and to the signs they saw him perform.'),
('ACT', 8, 7, 'ACT.8.7', 'With loud shrieks, unclean spirits came out of many who were possessed, and many of the paralyzed and lame were healed.'),
('ACT', 8, 8, 'ACT.8.8', 'So there was great joy in that city.'),
('ACT', 8, 9, 'ACT.8.9', 'Prior to that time, a man named Simon had practiced sorcery in the city and astounded the people of Samaria. He claimed to be someone great,'),
('ACT', 8, 10, 'ACT.8.10', 'and all the people, from the least to the greatest, heeded his words and said, “This man is the divine power called the Great Power.”'),
('ACT', 8, 11, 'ACT.8.11', 'They paid close attention to him because he had astounded them for a long time with his sorcery.'),
('ACT', 8, 12, 'ACT.8.12', 'But when they believed Philip as he preached the gospel of the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women.'),
('ACT', 8, 13, 'ACT.8.13', 'Even Simon himself believed and was baptized. He followed Philip closely and was astounded by the great signs and miracles he observed.'),
('ACT', 8, 14, 'ACT.8.14', 'When the apostles in Jerusalem heard that Samaria had received the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them.'),
('ACT', 8, 15, 'ACT.8.15', 'On their arrival, they prayed for them to receive the Holy Spirit.'),
('ACT', 8, 16, 'ACT.8.16', 'For the Holy Spirit had not yet fallen upon any of them; they had simply been baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.'),
('ACT', 8, 17, 'ACT.8.17', 'Then Peter and John laid their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.'),
('ACT', 8, 18, 'ACT.8.18', 'When Simon saw that the Spirit was given through the laying on of the apostles’ hands, he offered them money.'),
('ACT', 8, 19, 'ACT.8.19', '“Give me this power as well,” he said, “so that everyone on whom I lay my hands may receive the Holy Spirit.”'),
('ACT', 8, 20, 'ACT.8.20', 'But Peter replied, “May your silver perish with you, because you thought you could buy the gift of God with money!'),
('ACT', 8, 21, 'ACT.8.21', 'You have no part or share in our ministry, because your heart is not right before God.'),
('ACT', 8, 22, 'ACT.8.22', 'Repent, therefore, of your wickedness, and pray to the Lord. Perhaps He will forgive you for the intent of your heart.'),
('ACT', 8, 23, 'ACT.8.23', 'For I see that you are poisoned by bitterness and captive to iniquity.”'),
('ACT', 8, 24, 'ACT.8.24', 'Then Simon answered, “Pray to the Lord for me, so that nothing you have said may happen to me.”'),
('ACT', 8, 25, 'ACT.8.25', 'And after Peter and John had testified and spoken the word of the Lord, they returned to Jerusalem, preaching the gospel in many of the Samaritan villages.'),
('ACT', 8, 26, 'ACT.8.26', 'Now an angel of the Lord said to Philip, “Get up and go south to the desert road that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza.”'),
('ACT', 8, 27, 'ACT.8.27', 'So he started out, and on his way he met an Ethiopian eunuch, a court official in charge of the entire treasury of Candace, queen of the Ethiopians. He had gone to Jerusalem to worship,'),
('ACT', 8, 28, 'ACT.8.28', 'and on his return was sitting in his chariot reading Isaiah the prophet.'),
('ACT', 8, 29, 'ACT.8.29', 'The Spirit said to Philip, “Go over to that chariot and stay by it.”'),
('ACT', 8, 30, 'ACT.8.30', 'So Philip ran up and heard the man reading Isaiah the prophet. “Do you understand what you are reading?” Philip asked.'),
('ACT', 8, 31, 'ACT.8.31', '“How can I,” he said, “unless someone guides me?” And he invited Philip to come up and sit with him.'),
('ACT', 8, 32, 'ACT.8.32', 'The eunuch was reading this passage of Scripture: “He was led like a sheep to the slaughter, and as a lamb before the shearer is silent, so He did not open His mouth.'),
('ACT', 8, 33, 'ACT.8.33', 'In His humiliation He was deprived of justice. Who can recount His descendants? For His life was removed from the earth.”'),
('ACT', 8, 34, 'ACT.8.34', '“Tell me,” said the eunuch, “who is the prophet talking about, himself or someone else?”'),
('ACT', 8, 35, 'ACT.8.35', 'Then Philip began with this very Scripture and told him the good news about Jesus.'),
('ACT', 8, 36, 'ACT.8.36', 'As they traveled along the road and came to some water, the eunuch said, “Look, here is water! What is there to prevent me from being baptized?”'),
('ACT', 8, 38, 'ACT.8.38', 'And he gave orders to stop the chariot. Then both Philip and the eunuch went down into the water, and Philip baptized him.'),
('ACT', 8, 39, 'ACT.8.39', 'When they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord carried Philip away, and the eunuch saw him no more, but went on his way rejoicing.'),
('ACT', 8, 40, 'ACT.8.40', 'But Philip appeared at Azotus and traveled through that region, preaching the gospel in all the towns until he came to Caesarea.'),
('ACT', 9, 1, 'ACT.9.1', 'Meanwhile, Saul was still breathing out murderous threats against the disciples of the Lord. He approached the high priest'),
('ACT', 9, 2, 'ACT.9.2', 'and requested letters to the synagogues in Damascus, so that if he found any men or women belonging to the Way, he could bring them as prisoners to Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 9, 3, 'ACT.9.3', 'As Saul drew near to Damascus on his journey, suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him.'),
('ACT', 9, 4, 'ACT.9.4', 'He fell to the ground and heard a voice say to him, “Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”'),
('ACT', 9, 5, 'ACT.9.5', '“Who are You, Lord?” Saul asked. “I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,” He replied.'),
('ACT', 9, 6, 'ACT.9.6', '“Now get up and go into the city, and you will be told what you must do.”'),
('ACT', 9, 7, 'ACT.9.7', 'The men traveling with Saul stood there speechless. They heard the voice but did not see anyone.'),
('ACT', 9, 8, 'ACT.9.8', 'Saul got up from the ground, but when he opened his eyes he could not see a thing. So they led him by the hand into Damascus.'),
('ACT', 9, 9, 'ACT.9.9', 'For three days he was without sight, and he did not eat or drink anything.'),
('ACT', 9, 10, 'ACT.9.10', 'In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord spoke to him in a vision, “Ananias!” “Here I am, Lord,” he answered.'),
('ACT', 9, 11, 'ACT.9.11', '“Get up!” the Lord told him. “Go to the house of Judas on Straight Street and ask for a man from Tarsus named Saul, for he is praying.'),
('ACT', 9, 12, 'ACT.9.12', 'In a vision he has seen a man named Ananias come and place his hands on him to restore his sight.”'),
('ACT', 9, 13, 'ACT.9.13', 'But Ananias answered, “Lord, many people have told me about this man and all the harm he has done to Your saints in Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 9, 14, 'ACT.9.14', 'And now he is here with authority from the chief priests to arrest all who call on Your name.”'),
('ACT', 9, 15, 'ACT.9.15', '“Go!” said the Lord. “This man is My chosen instrument to carry My name before the Gentiles and their kings, and before the people of Israel.'),
('ACT', 9, 16, 'ACT.9.16', 'I will show him how much he must suffer for My name.”'),
('ACT', 9, 17, 'ACT.9.17', 'So Ananias went to the house, and when he arrived, he placed his hands on Saul. “Brother Saul,” he said, “the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road as you were coming here, has sent me so that you may see again and be filled with the Holy Spirit.”'),
('ACT', 9, 18, 'ACT.9.18', 'At that instant, something like scales fell from Saul’s eyes, and his sight was restored. He got up and was baptized,'),
('ACT', 9, 19, 'ACT.9.19', 'and after taking some food, he regained his strength. And he spent several days with the disciples in Damascus.'),
('ACT', 9, 20, 'ACT.9.20', 'Saul promptly began to proclaim Jesus in the synagogues, declaring, “He is the Son of God.”'),
('ACT', 9, 21, 'ACT.9.21', 'All who heard him were astounded and asked, “Isn’t this the man who wreaked havoc in Jerusalem on those who call on this name? And hasn’t he come here to take them as prisoners to the chief priests?”'),
('ACT', 9, 22, 'ACT.9.22', 'But Saul was empowered all the more, and he confounded the Jews living in Damascus by proving that Jesus is the Christ.'),
('ACT', 9, 23, 'ACT.9.23', 'After many days had passed, the Jews conspired to kill him,'),
('ACT', 9, 24, 'ACT.9.24', 'but Saul learned of their plot. Day and night they watched the city gates in order to kill him.'),
('ACT', 9, 25, 'ACT.9.25', 'One night, however, his disciples took him and lowered him in a basket through a window in the wall.'),
('ACT', 9, 26, 'ACT.9.26', 'When Saul arrived in Jerusalem, he tried to join the disciples, but they were all afraid of him, not believing that he was a disciple.'),
('ACT', 9, 27, 'ACT.9.27', 'Then Barnabas brought him to the apostles and described how Saul had seen the Lord, who had spoken to him on the road to Damascus, and how Saul had spoken boldly in that city in the name of Jesus.'),
('ACT', 9, 28, 'ACT.9.28', 'So Saul stayed with them, moving about freely in Jerusalem and speaking boldly in the name of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 9, 29, 'ACT.9.29', 'He talked and debated with the Grecian Jews, but they tried to kill him.'),
('ACT', 9, 30, 'ACT.9.30', 'When the brothers learned of this, they took him down to Caesarea and sent him off to Tarsus.'),
('ACT', 9, 31, 'ACT.9.31', 'Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria experienced a time of peace. It grew in strength and numbers, living in the fear of the Lord and the encouragement of the Holy Spirit.'),
('ACT', 9, 32, 'ACT.9.32', 'As Peter traveled throughout the area, he went to visit the saints in Lydda.'),
('ACT', 9, 33, 'ACT.9.33', 'There he found a man named Aeneas who had been paralyzed and bedridden for eight years.'),
('ACT', 9, 34, 'ACT.9.34', '“Aeneas,” Peter said to him, “Jesus Christ heals you! Get up and put away your mat.” Immediately Aeneas got up,'),
('ACT', 9, 35, 'ACT.9.35', 'and all who lived in Lydda and Sharon saw him and turned to the Lord.'),
('ACT', 9, 36, 'ACT.9.36', 'In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (which is translated as Dorcas), who was always occupied with works of kindness and charity.'),
('ACT', 9, 37, 'ACT.9.37', 'At that time, however, she became sick and died, and her body was washed and placed in an upper room.'),
('ACT', 9, 38, 'ACT.9.38', 'Since Lydda was near Joppa, the disciples, hearing that Peter was there, sent two men to urge him, “Come to us without delay.”'),
('ACT', 9, 39, 'ACT.9.39', 'So Peter got up and went with them. On his arrival, they took him to the upper room. All the widows stood around him, weeping and showing him the tunics and other clothing that Dorcas had made while she was still with them.'),
('ACT', 9, 40, 'ACT.9.40', 'Then Peter sent them all out of the room. He knelt down and prayed, and turning toward her body, he said, “Tabitha, get up!” She opened her eyes, and seeing Peter, she sat up.'),
('ACT', 9, 41, 'ACT.9.41', 'Peter took her by the hand and helped her up. Then he called the saints and widows and presented her to them alive.'),
('ACT', 9, 42, 'ACT.9.42', 'This became known all over Joppa, and many people believed in the Lord.'),
('ACT', 9, 43, 'ACT.9.43', 'And Peter stayed for several days in Joppa with a tanner named Simon.'),
('ACT', 10, 1, 'ACT.10.1', 'At Caesarea there was a man named Cornelius, a centurion in what was called the Italian Regiment.'),
('ACT', 10, 2, 'ACT.10.2', 'He and all his household were devout and God-fearing. He gave generously to the people and prayed to God regularly.'),
('ACT', 10, 3, 'ACT.10.3', 'One day at about the ninth hour, he had a clear vision of an angel of God who came to him and said, “Cornelius!”'),
('ACT', 10, 4, 'ACT.10.4', 'Cornelius stared at him in fear and asked, “What is it, Lord?” The angel answered, “Your prayers and gifts to the poor have ascended as a memorial offering before God.'),
('ACT', 10, 5, 'ACT.10.5', 'Now send men to Joppa to call for a man named Simon who is called Peter.'),
('ACT', 10, 6, 'ACT.10.6', 'He is staying with Simon the tanner, whose house is by the sea.”'),
('ACT', 10, 7, 'ACT.10.7', 'When the angel who spoke to him had gone, Cornelius called two of his servants and a devout soldier from among his attendants.'),
('ACT', 10, 8, 'ACT.10.8', 'He explained what had happened and sent them to Joppa.'),
('ACT', 10, 9, 'ACT.10.9', 'The next day at about the sixth hour, as the men were approaching the city on their journey, Peter went up on the roof to pray.'),
('ACT', 10, 10, 'ACT.10.10', 'He became hungry and wanted something to eat, but while the meal was being prepared, he fell into a trance.'),
('ACT', 10, 11, 'ACT.10.11', 'He saw heaven open and something like a large sheet being let down to earth by its four corners.'),
('ACT', 10, 12, 'ACT.10.12', 'It contained all kinds of four-footed animals and reptiles of the earth, as well as birds of the air.'),
('ACT', 10, 13, 'ACT.10.13', 'Then a voice said to him: “Get up, Peter, kill and eat!”'),
('ACT', 10, 14, 'ACT.10.14', '“No, Lord!” Peter answered. “I have never eaten anything impure or unclean.”'),
('ACT', 10, 15, 'ACT.10.15', 'The voice spoke to him a second time: “Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.”'),
('ACT', 10, 16, 'ACT.10.16', 'This happened three times, and all at once the sheet was taken back up into heaven.'),
('ACT', 10, 17, 'ACT.10.17', 'While Peter was puzzling over the meaning of the vision, the men sent by Cornelius found Simon’s house and approached the gate.'),
('ACT', 10, 18, 'ACT.10.18', 'They called out to ask if Simon called Peter was staying there.'),
('ACT', 10, 19, 'ACT.10.19', 'As Peter continued to reflect on the vision, the Spirit said to him, “Behold, three men are looking for you.'),
('ACT', 10, 20, 'ACT.10.20', 'So get up! Go downstairs and accompany them without hesitation, because I have sent them.”'),
('ACT', 10, 21, 'ACT.10.21', 'So Peter went down to the men and said, “Here am I, the one you are looking for. Why have you come?”'),
('ACT', 10, 22, 'ACT.10.22', '“Cornelius the centurion has sent us,” they said. “He is a righteous and God-fearing man with a good reputation among the whole Jewish nation. A holy angel instructed him to request your presence in his home so he could hear a message from you.”'),
('ACT', 10, 23, 'ACT.10.23', 'So Peter invited them in as his guests. And the next day he got ready and went with them, accompanied by some of the brothers from Joppa.'),
('ACT', 10, 24, 'ACT.10.24', 'The following day he arrived in Caesarea, where Cornelius was expecting them and had called together his relatives and close friends.'),
('ACT', 10, 25, 'ACT.10.25', 'As Peter was about to enter, Cornelius met him and fell at his feet to worship him.'),
('ACT', 10, 26, 'ACT.10.26', 'But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”'),
('ACT', 10, 27, 'ACT.10.27', 'As Peter talked with him, he went inside and found many people gathered together.'),
('ACT', 10, 28, 'ACT.10.28', 'He said to them, “You know how unlawful it is for a Jew to associate with a foreigner or visit him. But God has shown me that I should not call any man impure or unclean.'),
('ACT', 10, 29, 'ACT.10.29', 'So when I was invited, I came without objection. I ask, then, why have you sent for me?”'),
('ACT', 10, 30, 'ACT.10.30', 'Cornelius answered: “Four days ago I was in my house praying at this, the ninth hour. Suddenly a man in radiant clothing stood before me'),
('ACT', 10, 31, 'ACT.10.31', 'and said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer has been heard, and your gifts to the poor have been remembered before God.'),
('ACT', 10, 32, 'ACT.10.32', 'Therefore send to Joppa for Simon, who is called Peter. He is a guest in the home of Simon the tanner, by the sea.’'),
('ACT', 10, 33, 'ACT.10.33', 'So I sent for you immediately, and you were kind enough to come. Now then, we are all here in the presence of God to listen to everything the Lord has instructed you to tell us.”'),
('ACT', 10, 34, 'ACT.10.34', 'Then Peter began to speak: “I now truly understand that God does not show favoritism,'),
('ACT', 10, 35, 'ACT.10.35', 'but welcomes those from every nation who fear Him and do what is right.'),
('ACT', 10, 36, 'ACT.10.36', 'He has sent this message to the people of Israel, proclaiming the gospel of peace through Jesus Christ, who is Lord of all.'),
('ACT', 10, 37, 'ACT.10.37', 'You yourselves know what has happened throughout Judea, beginning in Galilee with the baptism that John proclaimed:'),
('ACT', 10, 38, 'ACT.10.38', 'how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, and how Jesus went around doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, because God was with Him.'),
('ACT', 10, 39, 'ACT.10.39', 'We are witnesses of all that He did, both in the land of the Jews and in Jerusalem. And although they put Him to death by hanging Him on a tree,'),
('ACT', 10, 40, 'ACT.10.40', 'God raised Him up on the third day and caused Him to be seen—'),
('ACT', 10, 41, 'ACT.10.41', 'not by all the people, but by the witnesses God had chosen beforehand, by us who ate and drank with Him after He rose from the dead.'),
('ACT', 10, 42, 'ACT.10.42', 'And He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that He is the One appointed by God to judge the living and the dead.'),
('ACT', 10, 43, 'ACT.10.43', 'All the prophets testify about Him that everyone who believes in Him receives forgiveness of sins through His name.”'),
('ACT', 10, 44, 'ACT.10.44', 'While Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon all who heard his message.'),
('ACT', 10, 45, 'ACT.10.45', 'All the circumcised believers who had accompanied Peter were astounded that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on the Gentiles.'),
('ACT', 10, 46, 'ACT.10.46', 'For they heard them speaking in tongues and exalting God. Then Peter said,'),
('ACT', 10, 47, 'ACT.10.47', '“Can anyone withhold the water to baptize these people? They have received the Holy Spirit just as we have!”'),
('ACT', 10, 48, 'ACT.10.48', 'So he ordered that they be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ. Then they asked him to stay for a few days.'),
('ACT', 11, 1, 'ACT.11.1', 'The apostles and brothers throughout Judea soon heard that the Gentiles also had received the word of God.'),
('ACT', 11, 2, 'ACT.11.2', 'So when Peter went up to Jerusalem, the circumcised believers took issue with him'),
('ACT', 11, 3, 'ACT.11.3', 'and said, “You visited uncircumcised men and ate with them.”'),
('ACT', 11, 4, 'ACT.11.4', 'But Peter began and explained to them the whole sequence of events:'),
('ACT', 11, 5, 'ACT.11.5', '“I was in the city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision of something like a large sheet being let down from heaven by its four corners, and it came right down to me.'),
('ACT', 11, 6, 'ACT.11.6', 'I looked at it closely and saw four-footed animals of the earth, wild beasts, reptiles, and birds of the air.'),
('ACT', 11, 7, 'ACT.11.7', 'Then I heard a voice saying to me, ‘Get up, Peter, kill and eat.’'),
('ACT', 11, 8, 'ACT.11.8', '‘No, Lord,’ I said, ‘for nothing impure or unclean has ever entered my mouth.’'),
('ACT', 11, 9, 'ACT.11.9', 'But the voice spoke from heaven a second time, ‘Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.’'),
('ACT', 11, 10, 'ACT.11.10', 'This happened three times, and everything was drawn back up into heaven.'),
('ACT', 11, 11, 'ACT.11.11', 'Just then three men sent to me from Caesarea stopped at the house where I was staying.'),
('ACT', 11, 12, 'ACT.11.12', 'The Spirit told me to accompany them without hesitation. These six brothers also went with me, and we entered the man’s home.'),
('ACT', 11, 13, 'ACT.11.13', 'He told us how he had seen an angel standing in his house and saying, ‘Send to Joppa for Simon who is called Peter.'),
('ACT', 11, 14, 'ACT.11.14', 'He will convey to you a message by which you and all your household will be saved.’'),
('ACT', 11, 15, 'ACT.11.15', 'As I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, just as He had fallen upon us at the beginning.'),
('ACT', 11, 16, 'ACT.11.16', 'Then I remembered the word of the Lord, how He said, ‘John baptized with water, but you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.’'),
('ACT', 11, 17, 'ACT.11.17', 'So if God gave them the same gift He gave us who believed in the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I to hinder the work of God?”'),
('ACT', 11, 18, 'ACT.11.18', 'When they heard this, they had no further objections, and they glorified God, saying, “So then, God has granted even the Gentiles repentance unto life.”'),
('ACT', 11, 19, 'ACT.11.19', 'Meanwhile those scattered by the persecution that began with Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, speaking the message only to Jews.'),
('ACT', 11, 20, 'ACT.11.20', 'But some of them, men from Cyprus and Cyrene, went to Antioch and began speaking to the Greeks as well, proclaiming the good news about the Lord Jesus.'),
('ACT', 11, 21, 'ACT.11.21', 'The hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number of people believed and turned to the Lord.'),
('ACT', 11, 22, 'ACT.11.22', 'When news of this reached the ears of the church in Jerusalem, they sent Barnabas to Antioch.'),
('ACT', 11, 23, 'ACT.11.23', 'When he arrived and saw the grace of God, he rejoiced and encouraged them all to abide in the Lord with all their hearts.'),
('ACT', 11, 24, 'ACT.11.24', 'Barnabas was a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and faith, and a great number of people were brought to the Lord.'),
('ACT', 11, 25, 'ACT.11.25', 'Then Barnabas went to Tarsus to look for Saul,'),
('ACT', 11, 26, 'ACT.11.26', 'and when he found him, he brought him back to Antioch. So for a full year they met together with the church and taught large numbers of people. The disciples were first called Christians at Antioch.'),
('ACT', 11, 27, 'ACT.11.27', 'In those days some prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch.'),
('ACT', 11, 28, 'ACT.11.28', 'One of them named Agabus stood up and predicted through the Spirit that a great famine would sweep across the whole world. (This happened under Claudius.)'),
('ACT', 11, 29, 'ACT.11.29', 'So the disciples, each according to his ability, decided to send relief to the brothers living in Judea.'),
('ACT', 11, 30, 'ACT.11.30', 'This they did, sending their gifts to the elders with Barnabas and Saul.'),
('ACT', 12, 1, 'ACT.12.1', 'About that time, King Herod reached out to harm some who belonged to the church.'),
('ACT', 12, 2, 'ACT.12.2', 'He had James, the brother of John, put to death with the sword.'),
('ACT', 12, 3, 'ACT.12.3', 'And seeing that this pleased the Jews, Herod proceeded to seize Peter during the Feast of Unleavened Bread.'),
('ACT', 12, 4, 'ACT.12.4', 'He arrested him and put him in prison, handing him over to be guarded by four squads of four soldiers each. Herod intended to bring him out to the people after the Passover.'),
('ACT', 12, 5, 'ACT.12.5', 'So Peter was kept in prison, but the church was fervently praying to God for him.'),
('ACT', 12, 6, 'ACT.12.6', 'On the night before Herod was to bring him to trial, Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains, with sentries standing guard at the entrance to the prison.'),
('ACT', 12, 7, 'ACT.12.7', 'Suddenly an angel of the Lord appeared and a light shone in the cell. He tapped Peter on the side and woke him up, saying, “Get up quickly.” And the chains fell off his wrists.'),
('ACT', 12, 8, 'ACT.12.8', '“Get dressed and put on your sandals,” said the angel. Peter did so, and the angel told him, “Wrap your cloak around you and follow me.”'),
('ACT', 12, 9, 'ACT.12.9', 'So Peter followed him out, but he was unaware that what the angel was doing was real. He thought he was only seeing a vision.'),
('ACT', 12, 10, 'ACT.12.10', 'They passed the first and second guards and came to the iron gate leading to the city, which opened for them by itself. When they had gone outside and walked the length of one block, the angel suddenly left him.'),
('ACT', 12, 11, 'ACT.12.11', 'Then Peter came to himself and said, “Now I know for sure that the Lord has sent His angel and rescued me from Herod’s grasp and from everything the Jewish people were anticipating.”'),
('ACT', 12, 12, 'ACT.12.12', 'And when he had realized this, he went to the house of Mary the mother of John, also called Mark, where many people had gathered together and were praying.'),
('ACT', 12, 13, 'ACT.12.13', 'He knocked at the outer gate, and a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer it.'),
('ACT', 12, 14, 'ACT.12.14', 'When she recognized Peter’s voice, she was so overjoyed that she forgot to open the gate, but ran inside and announced, “Peter is standing at the gate!”'),
('ACT', 12, 15, 'ACT.12.15', '“You are out of your mind,” they told her. But when she kept insisting it was so, they said, “It must be his angel.”'),
('ACT', 12, 16, 'ACT.12.16', 'But Peter kept on knocking, and when they opened the door and saw him, they were astounded.'),
('ACT', 12, 17, 'ACT.12.17', 'Peter motioned with his hand for silence, and he described how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. “Send word to James and to the brothers,” he said, and he left for another place.'),
('ACT', 12, 18, 'ACT.12.18', 'At daybreak there was no small commotion among the soldiers as to what had become of Peter.'),
('ACT', 12, 19, 'ACT.12.19', 'After Herod had searched for him unsuccessfully, he examined the guards and ordered that they be executed. Then he went down from Judea to Caesarea and spent some time there.'),
('ACT', 12, 20, 'ACT.12.20', 'Now Herod was in a furious dispute with the people of Tyre and Sidon, and they convened before him. Having secured the support of Blastus, the king’s chamberlain, they asked for peace, because their region depended on the king’s country for food.'),
('ACT', 12, 21, 'ACT.12.21', 'On the appointed day, Herod donned his royal robes, sat on his throne, and addressed the people.'),
('ACT', 12, 22, 'ACT.12.22', 'And they began to shout, “This is the voice of a god, not a man!”'),
('ACT', 12, 23, 'ACT.12.23', 'Immediately, because Herod did not give glory to God, an angel of the Lord struck him down, and he was eaten by worms and died.'),
('ACT', 12, 24, 'ACT.12.24', 'But the word of God continued to spread and multiply.'),
('ACT', 12, 25, 'ACT.12.25', 'When Barnabas and Saul had fulfilled their mission to Jerusalem, they returned, bringing with them John, also called Mark.'),
('ACT', 13, 1, 'ACT.13.1', 'Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen (who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch), and Saul.'),
('ACT', 13, 2, 'ACT.13.2', 'While they were worshiping the Lord and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, “Set apart for Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them.”'),
('ACT', 13, 3, 'ACT.13.3', 'And after they had fasted and prayed, they laid their hands on them and sent them off.'),
('ACT', 13, 4, 'ACT.13.4', 'So Barnabas and Saul, sent forth by the Holy Spirit, went down to Seleucia and sailed from there to Cyprus.'),
('ACT', 13, 5, 'ACT.13.5', 'When they arrived at Salamis, they proclaimed the word of God in the Jewish synagogues. And John was with them as their helper.'),
('ACT', 13, 6, 'ACT.13.6', 'They traveled through the whole island as far as Paphos, where they found a Jewish sorcerer and false prophet named Bar-Jesus,'),
('ACT', 13, 7, 'ACT.13.7', 'an attendant of the proconsul, Sergius Paulus. The proconsul, a man of intelligence, summoned Barnabas and Saul because he wanted to hear the word of God.'),
('ACT', 13, 8, 'ACT.13.8', 'But Elymas the sorcerer (for that is what his name means) opposed them and tried to turn the proconsul from the faith.'),
('ACT', 13, 9, 'ACT.13.9', 'Then Saul, who was also called Paul, filled with the Holy Spirit, looked directly at Elymas'),
('ACT', 13, 10, 'ACT.13.10', 'and said, “O child of the devil and enemy of all righteousness, you are full of all kinds of deceit and trickery! Will you never stop perverting the straight ways of the Lord?'),
('ACT', 13, 11, 'ACT.13.11', 'Now look, the hand of the Lord is against you, and for a time you will be blind and unable to see the light of the sun.” Immediately mist and darkness came over him, and he groped about, seeking someone to lead him by the hand.'),
('ACT', 13, 12, 'ACT.13.12', 'When the proconsul saw what had happened, he believed, for he was astonished at the teaching about the Lord.'),
('ACT', 13, 13, 'ACT.13.13', 'After setting sail from Paphos, Paul and his companions came to Perga in Pamphylia, where John left them to return to Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 13, 14, 'ACT.13.14', 'And from Perga, they traveled inland to Pisidian Antioch, where they entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and sat down.'),
('ACT', 13, 15, 'ACT.13.15', 'After the reading from the Law and the Prophets, the synagogue leaders sent word to them: “Brothers, if you have a word of encouragement for the people, please speak.”'),
('ACT', 13, 16, 'ACT.13.16', 'Paul stood up, motioned with his hand, and began to speak: “Men of Israel and you Gentiles who fear God, listen to me!'),
('ACT', 13, 17, 'ACT.13.17', 'The God of the people of Israel chose our fathers. He made them into a great people during their stay in Egypt, and with an uplifted arm He led them out of that land.'),
('ACT', 13, 18, 'ACT.13.18', 'He endured their conduct for about forty years in the wilderness.'),
('ACT', 13, 19, 'ACT.13.19', 'And having vanquished seven nations in Canaan, He gave their land to His people as an inheritance.'),
('ACT', 13, 20, 'ACT.13.20', 'All this took about 450 years. After this, God gave them judges until the time of Samuel the prophet.'),
('ACT', 13, 21, 'ACT.13.21', 'Then the people asked for a king, and God gave them Saul son of Kish, from the tribe of Benjamin, who ruled forty years.'),
('ACT', 13, 22, 'ACT.13.22', 'After removing Saul, He raised up David as their king and testified about him: ‘I have found David son of Jesse a man after My own heart; he will carry out My will in its entirety.’'),
('ACT', 13, 23, 'ACT.13.23', 'From the descendants of this man, God has brought to Israel the Savior Jesus, as He promised.'),
('ACT', 13, 24, 'ACT.13.24', 'Before the arrival of Jesus, John preached a baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel.'),
('ACT', 13, 25, 'ACT.13.25', 'As John was completing his course, he said, ‘Who do you suppose I am? I am not that One. But there is One coming after me whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.’'),
('ACT', 13, 26, 'ACT.13.26', 'Brothers, children of Abraham, and you Gentiles who fear God, it is to us that this message of salvation has been sent.'),
('ACT', 13, 27, 'ACT.13.27', 'The people of Jerusalem and their rulers did not recognize Jesus, yet in condemning Him they fulfilled the words of the prophets that are read every Sabbath.'),
('ACT', 13, 28, 'ACT.13.28', 'And though they found no ground for a death sentence, they asked Pilate to have Him executed.'),
('ACT', 13, 29, 'ACT.13.29', 'When they had carried out all that was written about Him, they took Him down from the tree and laid Him in a tomb.'),
('ACT', 13, 30, 'ACT.13.30', 'But God raised Him from the dead,'),
('ACT', 13, 31, 'ACT.13.31', 'and for many days He was seen by those who had accompanied Him from Galilee to Jerusalem. They are now His witnesses to our people.'),
('ACT', 13, 32, 'ACT.13.32', 'And now we proclaim to you the good news: What God promised our fathers'),
('ACT', 13, 33, 'ACT.13.33', 'He has fulfilled for us, their children, by raising up Jesus. As it is written in the second Psalm: ‘You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.’'),
('ACT', 13, 34, 'ACT.13.34', 'In fact, God raised Him from the dead, never to see decay. As He has said: ‘I will give you the holy and sure blessings promised to David.’'),
('ACT', 13, 35, 'ACT.13.35', 'So also, He says in another Psalm: ‘You will not let Your Holy One see decay.’'),
('ACT', 13, 36, 'ACT.13.36', 'For when David had served God’s purpose in his own generation, he fell asleep. His body was buried with his fathers and saw decay.'),
('ACT', 13, 37, 'ACT.13.37', 'But the One whom God raised from the dead did not see decay.'),
('ACT', 13, 38, 'ACT.13.38', 'Therefore let it be known to you, brothers, that through Jesus the forgiveness of sins is proclaimed to you.'),
('ACT', 13, 39, 'ACT.13.39', 'Through Him everyone who believes is justified from everything from which you could not be justified by the law of Moses.'),
('ACT', 13, 40, 'ACT.13.40', 'Watch out, then, that what was spoken by the prophets does not happen to you:'),
('ACT', 13, 41, 'ACT.13.41', '‘Look, you scoffers, wonder and perish! For I am doing a work in your days that you would never believe, even if someone told you.’”'),
('ACT', 13, 42, 'ACT.13.42', 'As Paul and Barnabas were leaving the synagogue, the people urged them to continue this message on the next Sabbath.'),
('ACT', 13, 43, 'ACT.13.43', 'After the synagogue was dismissed, many of the Jews and devout converts to Judaism followed Paul and Barnabas, who spoke to them and urged them to continue in the grace of God.'),
('ACT', 13, 44, 'ACT.13.44', 'On the following Sabbath, nearly the whole city gathered to hear the word of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 13, 45, 'ACT.13.45', 'But when the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and they blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying.'),
('ACT', 13, 46, 'ACT.13.46', 'Then Paul and Barnabas answered them boldly: “It was necessary to speak the word of God to you first. But since you reject it and do not consider yourselves worthy of eternal life, we now turn to the Gentiles.'),
('ACT', 13, 47, 'ACT.13.47', 'For this is what the Lord has commanded us: ‘I have made you a light for the Gentiles, to bring salvation to the ends of the earth.’”'),
('ACT', 13, 48, 'ACT.13.48', 'When the Gentiles heard this, they rejoiced and glorified the word of the Lord, and all who were appointed for eternal life believed.'),
('ACT', 13, 49, 'ACT.13.49', 'And the word of the Lord spread throughout that region.'),
('ACT', 13, 50, 'ACT.13.50', 'The Jews, however, incited the religious women of prominence and the leading men of the city. They stirred up persecution against Paul and Barnabas and drove them out of their district.'),
('ACT', 13, 51, 'ACT.13.51', 'So they shook the dust off their feet in protest against them and went to Iconium.'),
('ACT', 13, 52, 'ACT.13.52', 'And the disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Spirit.'),
('ACT', 14, 1, 'ACT.14.1', 'At Iconium, Paul and Barnabas went as usual into the Jewish synagogue, where they spoke so well that a great number of Jews and Greeks believed.'),
('ACT', 14, 2, 'ACT.14.2', 'But the unbelieving Jews stirred up the Gentiles and poisoned their minds against the brothers.'),
('ACT', 14, 3, 'ACT.14.3', 'So Paul and Barnabas spent considerable time there, speaking boldly for the Lord, who affirmed the message of His grace by enabling them to perform signs and wonders.'),
('ACT', 14, 4, 'ACT.14.4', 'The people of the city were divided. Some sided with the Jews, and others with the apostles.'),
('ACT', 14, 5, 'ACT.14.5', 'But when the Gentiles and Jews, together with their rulers, set out to mistreat and stone them,'),
('ACT', 14, 6, 'ACT.14.6', 'they found out about it and fled to the Lycaonian cities of Lystra and Derbe and to the surrounding region,'),
('ACT', 14, 7, 'ACT.14.7', 'where they continued to preach the gospel.'),
('ACT', 14, 8, 'ACT.14.8', 'In Lystra there sat a man crippled in his feet, who was lame from birth and had never walked.'),
('ACT', 14, 9, 'ACT.14.9', 'This man was listening to the words of Paul, who looked intently at him and saw that he had faith to be healed.'),
('ACT', 14, 10, 'ACT.14.10', 'In a loud voice Paul called out, “Stand up on your feet!” And the man jumped up and began to walk.'),
('ACT', 14, 11, 'ACT.14.11', 'When the crowds saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voices in the Lycaonian language: “The gods have come down to us in human form!”'),
('ACT', 14, 12, 'ACT.14.12', 'Barnabas they called Zeus, and Paul they called Hermes, because he was the chief speaker.'),
('ACT', 14, 13, 'ACT.14.13', 'The priest of Zeus, whose temple was just outside the city, brought bulls and wreaths to the city gates, hoping to offer a sacrifice along with the crowds.'),
('ACT', 14, 14, 'ACT.14.14', 'But when the apostles Barnabas and Paul found out about this, they tore their clothes and rushed into the crowd, shouting,'),
('ACT', 14, 15, 'ACT.14.15', '“Men, why are you doing this? We too are only men, human like you. We are bringing you good news that you should turn from these worthless things to the living God, who made heaven and earth and sea and everything in them.'),
('ACT', 14, 16, 'ACT.14.16', 'In past generations, He let all nations go their own way.'),
('ACT', 14, 17, 'ACT.14.17', 'Yet He has not left Himself without testimony to His goodness: He gives you rain from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your hearts with food and gladness.”'),
('ACT', 14, 18, 'ACT.14.18', 'Even with these words, Paul and Barnabas could hardly stop the crowds from sacrificing to them.'),
('ACT', 14, 19, 'ACT.14.19', 'Then some Jews arrived from Antioch and Iconium and won over the crowds. They stoned Paul and dragged him outside the city, presuming he was dead.'),
('ACT', 14, 20, 'ACT.14.20', 'But after the disciples had gathered around him, he got up and went back into the city. And the next day he left with Barnabas for Derbe.'),
('ACT', 14, 21, 'ACT.14.21', 'They preached the gospel to that city and made many disciples. Then they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch,'),
('ACT', 14, 22, 'ACT.14.22', 'strengthening the souls of the disciples and encouraging them to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” they said.'),
('ACT', 14, 23, 'ACT.14.23', 'Paul and Barnabas appointed elders for them in each church, praying and fasting as they entrusted them to the Lord, in whom they had believed.'),
('ACT', 14, 24, 'ACT.14.24', 'After passing through Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia.'),
('ACT', 14, 25, 'ACT.14.25', 'And when they had spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia.'),
('ACT', 14, 26, 'ACT.14.26', 'From Attalia they sailed to Antioch, where they had been commended to the grace of God for the work they had just completed.'),
('ACT', 14, 27, 'ACT.14.27', 'When they arrived, they gathered the church together and reported all that God had done through them, and how He had opened the door of faith to the Gentiles.'),
('ACT', 14, 28, 'ACT.14.28', 'And they spent a long time there with the disciples.'),
('ACT', 15, 1, 'ACT.15.1', 'Then some men came down from Judea and were teaching the brothers, “Unless you are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you cannot be saved.”'),
('ACT', 15, 2, 'ACT.15.2', 'And after engaging these men in sharp debate, Paul and Barnabas were appointed, along with some other believers, to go up to Jerusalem to see the apostles and elders about this question.'),
('ACT', 15, 3, 'ACT.15.3', 'Sent on their way by the church, they passed through Phoenicia and Samaria, recounting the conversion of the Gentiles and bringing great joy to all the brothers.'),
('ACT', 15, 4, 'ACT.15.4', 'On their arrival in Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church and apostles and elders, to whom they reported all that God had done through them.'),
('ACT', 15, 5, 'ACT.15.5', 'But some believers from the party of the Pharisees stood up and declared, “The Gentiles must be circumcised and required to obey the law of Moses.”'),
('ACT', 15, 6, 'ACT.15.6', 'So the apostles and elders met to look into this matter.'),
('ACT', 15, 7, 'ACT.15.7', 'After much discussion, Peter got up and said to them, “Brothers, you know that in the early days God made a choice among you that the Gentiles would hear from my lips the message of the gospel and believe.'),
('ACT', 15, 8, 'ACT.15.8', 'And God, who knows the heart, showed His approval by giving the Holy Spirit to them, just as He did to us.'),
('ACT', 15, 9, 'ACT.15.9', 'He made no distinction between us and them, for He cleansed their hearts by faith.'),
('ACT', 15, 10, 'ACT.15.10', 'Now then, why do you test God by placing on the necks of the disciples a yoke that neither we nor our fathers have been able to bear?'),
('ACT', 15, 11, 'ACT.15.11', 'On the contrary, we believe it is through the grace of the Lord Jesus that we are saved, just as they are.”'),
('ACT', 15, 12, 'ACT.15.12', 'The whole assembly fell silent as they listened to Barnabas and Paul describing the signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles through them.'),
('ACT', 15, 13, 'ACT.15.13', 'When they had finished speaking, James declared, “Brothers, listen to me!'),
('ACT', 15, 14, 'ACT.15.14', 'Simon has told us how God first visited the Gentiles to take from them a people to be His own.'),
('ACT', 15, 15, 'ACT.15.15', 'The words of the prophets agree with this, as it is written:'),
('ACT', 15, 16, 'ACT.15.16', '‘After this I will return and rebuild the fallen tent of David. Its ruins I will rebuild, and I will restore it,'),
('ACT', 15, 17, 'ACT.15.17', 'so that the remnant of men may seek the Lord, and all the Gentiles who are called by My name, says the Lord who does these things'),
('ACT', 15, 18, 'ACT.15.18', 'that have been known for ages.’'),
('ACT', 15, 19, 'ACT.15.19', 'It is my judgment, therefore, that we should not cause trouble for the Gentiles who are turning to God.'),
('ACT', 15, 20, 'ACT.15.20', 'Instead, we should write and tell them to abstain from food polluted by idols, from sexual immorality, from the meat of strangled animals, and from blood.'),
('ACT', 15, 21, 'ACT.15.21', 'For Moses has been proclaimed in every city from ancient times and is read in the synagogues on every Sabbath.”'),
('ACT', 15, 22, 'ACT.15.22', 'Then the apostles and elders, with the whole church, decided to select men from among them to send to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas. They chose Judas called Barsabbas and Silas, two leaders among the brothers,'),
('ACT', 15, 23, 'ACT.15.23', 'and sent them with this letter: The apostles and the elders, your brothers, To the brothers among the Gentiles in Antioch, Syria, and Cilicia: Greetings.'),
('ACT', 15, 24, 'ACT.15.24', 'It has come to our attention that some went out from us without our authorization and unsettled you, troubling your minds by what they said.'),
('ACT', 15, 25, 'ACT.15.25', 'So we all agreed to choose men to send to you along with our beloved Barnabas and Paul,'),
('ACT', 15, 26, 'ACT.15.26', 'men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('ACT', 15, 27, 'ACT.15.27', 'Therefore we are sending Judas and Silas to tell you in person the same things we are writing.'),
('ACT', 15, 28, 'ACT.15.28', 'It seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to us not to burden you with anything beyond these essential requirements:'),
('ACT', 15, 29, 'ACT.15.29', 'You must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality. You will do well to avoid these things. Farewell.'),
('ACT', 15, 30, 'ACT.15.30', 'So the men were sent off and went down to Antioch, where they assembled the congregation and delivered the letter.'),
('ACT', 15, 31, 'ACT.15.31', 'When the people read it, they rejoiced at its encouraging message.'),
('ACT', 15, 32, 'ACT.15.32', 'Judas and Silas, who themselves were prophets, said much to encourage and strengthen the brothers.'),
('ACT', 15, 33, 'ACT.15.33', 'After spending some time there, they were sent off by the brothers in peace to return to those who had sent them.'),
('ACT', 15, 35, 'ACT.15.35', 'But Paul and Barnabas remained at Antioch, along with many others, teaching and preaching the word of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 15, 36, 'ACT.15.36', 'Some time later Paul said to Barnabas, “Let us go back and visit the brothers in every town where we proclaimed the word of the Lord, to see how they are doing.”'),
('ACT', 15, 37, 'ACT.15.37', 'Barnabas wanted to take John, also called Mark.'),
('ACT', 15, 38, 'ACT.15.38', 'But Paul thought it best not to take him, because he had deserted them in Pamphylia and had not accompanied them in the work.'),
('ACT', 15, 39, 'ACT.15.39', 'Their disagreement was so sharp that they parted company. Barnabas took Mark and sailed for Cyprus,'),
('ACT', 15, 40, 'ACT.15.40', 'but Paul chose Silas and left, commended by the brothers to the grace of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 15, 41, 'ACT.15.41', 'And he traveled through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches.'),
('ACT', 16, 1, 'ACT.16.1', 'Paul came to Derbe and then to Lystra, where he found a disciple named Timothy, the son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father.'),
('ACT', 16, 2, 'ACT.16.2', 'The brothers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of him.'),
('ACT', 16, 3, 'ACT.16.3', 'Paul wanted Timothy to accompany him, so he took him and circumcised him on account of the Jews in that area, for they all knew that his father was a Greek.'),
('ACT', 16, 4, 'ACT.16.4', 'As they went from town to town, they delivered the decisions handed down by the apostles and elders in Jerusalem for the people to obey.'),
('ACT', 16, 5, 'ACT.16.5', 'So the churches were strengthened in the faith and grew daily in numbers.'),
('ACT', 16, 6, 'ACT.16.6', 'After the Holy Spirit had prevented them from speaking the word in the province of Asia, they traveled through the region of Phrygia and Galatia.'),
('ACT', 16, 7, 'ACT.16.7', 'And when they came to the border of Mysia, they tried to enter Bithynia, but the Spirit of Jesus would not permit them.'),
('ACT', 16, 8, 'ACT.16.8', 'So they passed by Mysia and went down to Troas.'),
('ACT', 16, 9, 'ACT.16.9', 'During the night, Paul had a vision of a man of Macedonia standing and pleading with him, “Come over to Macedonia and help us.”'),
('ACT', 16, 10, 'ACT.16.10', 'As soon as Paul had seen the vision, we got ready to leave for Macedonia, concluding that God had called us to preach the gospel to them.'),
('ACT', 16, 11, 'ACT.16.11', 'We sailed from Troas straight to Samothrace, and the following day on to Neapolis.'),
('ACT', 16, 12, 'ACT.16.12', 'From there we went to the Roman colony of Philippi, the leading city of that district of Macedonia. And we stayed there several days.'),
('ACT', 16, 13, 'ACT.16.13', 'On the Sabbath we went outside the city gate along the river, where it was customary to find a place of prayer. After sitting down, we spoke to the women who had gathered there.'),
('ACT', 16, 14, 'ACT.16.14', 'Among those listening was a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, who was a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul’s message.'),
('ACT', 16, 15, 'ACT.16.15', 'And when she and her household had been baptized, she urged us, “If you consider me a believer in the Lord, come and stay at my house.” And she persuaded us.'),
('ACT', 16, 16, 'ACT.16.16', 'One day as we were going to the place of prayer, we were met by a slave girl with a spirit of divination, who earned a large income for her masters by fortune-telling.'),
('ACT', 16, 17, 'ACT.16.17', 'This girl followed Paul and the rest of us, shouting, “These men are servants of the Most High God, who are proclaiming to you the way of salvation!”'),
('ACT', 16, 18, 'ACT.16.18', 'She continued this for many days. Eventually Paul grew so aggravated that he turned and said to the spirit, “In the name of Jesus Christ I command you to come out of her!” And the spirit left her at that very moment.'),
('ACT', 16, 19, 'ACT.16.19', 'When the girl’s owners saw that their hope of making money was gone, they seized Paul and Silas and dragged them before the authorities in the marketplace.'),
('ACT', 16, 20, 'ACT.16.20', 'They brought them to the magistrates and said, “These men are Jews and are throwing our city into turmoil'),
('ACT', 16, 21, 'ACT.16.21', 'by promoting customs that are unlawful for us Romans to adopt or practice.”'),
('ACT', 16, 22, 'ACT.16.22', 'The crowd joined in the attack against Paul and Silas, and the magistrates ordered that they be stripped and beaten with rods.'),
('ACT', 16, 23, 'ACT.16.23', 'And after striking them with many blows, they threw them into prison and ordered the jailer to guard them securely.'),
('ACT', 16, 24, 'ACT.16.24', 'On receiving this order, he placed them in the inner cell and fastened their feet in the stocks.'),
('ACT', 16, 25, 'ACT.16.25', 'About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them.'),
('ACT', 16, 26, 'ACT.16.26', 'Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyone’s chains came loose.'),
('ACT', 16, 27, 'ACT.16.27', 'When the jailer woke up and saw the prison doors open, he drew his sword and was about to kill himself, presuming that the prisoners had escaped.'),
('ACT', 16, 28, 'ACT.16.28', 'But Paul called out in a loud voice, “Do not harm yourself! We are all here!”'),
('ACT', 16, 29, 'ACT.16.29', 'Calling for lights, the jailer rushed in and fell trembling before Paul and Silas.'),
('ACT', 16, 30, 'ACT.16.30', 'Then he brought them out and asked, “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?”'),
('ACT', 16, 31, 'ACT.16.31', 'They replied, “Believe in the Lord Jesus and you will be saved, you and your household.”'),
('ACT', 16, 32, 'ACT.16.32', 'Then Paul and Silas spoke the word of the Lord to him and to everyone in his house.'),
('ACT', 16, 33, 'ACT.16.33', 'At that hour of the night, the jailer took them and washed their wounds. And without delay, he and all his household were baptized.'),
('ACT', 16, 34, 'ACT.16.34', 'Then he brought them into his home and set a meal before them. So he and all his household rejoiced that they had come to believe in God.'),
('ACT', 16, 35, 'ACT.16.35', 'When daylight came, the magistrates sent their officers with the order: “Release those men.”'),
('ACT', 16, 36, 'ACT.16.36', 'The jailer informed Paul: “The magistrates have sent orders to release you. Now you may go on your way in peace.”'),
('ACT', 16, 37, 'ACT.16.37', 'But Paul said to the officers, “They beat us publicly without a trial and threw us into prison, even though we are Roman citizens. And now do they want to send us away secretly? Absolutely not! Let them come themselves and escort us out!”'),
('ACT', 16, 38, 'ACT.16.38', 'So the officers relayed this message to the magistrates, who were alarmed to hear that Paul and Silas were Roman citizens.'),
('ACT', 16, 39, 'ACT.16.39', 'They came to appease them and led them out, requesting that they leave the city.'),
('ACT', 16, 40, 'ACT.16.40', 'After Paul and Silas came out of the prison, they went to Lydia’s house to see the brothers and encourage them. Then they left the city.'),
('ACT', 17, 1, 'ACT.17.1', 'When they had passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a Jewish synagogue.'),
('ACT', 17, 2, 'ACT.17.2', 'As was his custom, Paul went into the synagogue, and on three Sabbaths he reasoned with them from the Scriptures,'),
('ACT', 17, 3, 'ACT.17.3', 'explaining and proving that the Christ had to suffer and rise from the dead. “This Jesus I am proclaiming to you is the Christ,” he declared.'),
('ACT', 17, 4, 'ACT.17.4', 'Some of the Jews were persuaded and joined Paul and Silas, along with a large number of God-fearing Greeks and quite a few leading women.'),
('ACT', 17, 5, 'ACT.17.5', 'The Jews, however, became jealous. So they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, and sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jason’s house in search of Paul and Silas, hoping to bring them out to the people.'),
('ACT', 17, 6, 'ACT.17.6', 'But when they could not find them, they dragged Jason and some other brothers before the city officials, shouting, “These men who have turned the world upside down have now come here,'),
('ACT', 17, 7, 'ACT.17.7', 'and Jason has welcomed them into his home. They are all defying Caesar’s decrees, saying that there is another king, named Jesus!”'),
('ACT', 17, 8, 'ACT.17.8', 'On hearing this, the crowd and city officials were greatly disturbed.'),
('ACT', 17, 9, 'ACT.17.9', 'And they collected bond from Jason and the others and then released them.'),
('ACT', 17, 10, 'ACT.17.10', 'As soon as night had fallen, the brothers sent Paul and Silas away to Berea. On arriving there, they went into the Jewish synagogue.'),
('ACT', 17, 11, 'ACT.17.11', 'Now the Bereans were more noble-minded than the Thessalonians, for they received the message with great eagerness and examined the Scriptures every day to see if these teachings were true.'),
('ACT', 17, 12, 'ACT.17.12', 'As a result, many of them believed, along with quite a few prominent Greek women and men.'),
('ACT', 17, 13, 'ACT.17.13', 'But when the Jews from Thessalonica learned that Paul was also proclaiming the word of God in Berea, they went there themselves to incite and agitate the crowds.'),
('ACT', 17, 14, 'ACT.17.14', 'The brothers immediately sent Paul to the coast, but Silas and Timothy remained in Berea.'),
('ACT', 17, 15, 'ACT.17.15', 'Those who escorted Paul brought him to Athens and then returned with instructions for Silas and Timothy to join him as soon as possible.'),
('ACT', 17, 16, 'ACT.17.16', 'While Paul was waiting for them in Athens, he was deeply disturbed in his spirit to see that the city was full of idols.'),
('ACT', 17, 17, 'ACT.17.17', 'So he reasoned in the synagogue with the Jews and God-fearing Gentiles, and in the marketplace with those he met each day.'),
('ACT', 17, 18, 'ACT.17.18', 'Some Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also began to debate with him. Some of them asked, “What is this babbler trying to say?” Others said, “He seems to be advocating foreign gods.” They said this because Paul was proclaiming the good news of Jesus and the resurrection.'),
('ACT', 17, 19, 'ACT.17.19', 'So they took Paul and brought him to the Areopagus, where they asked him, “May we know what this new teaching is that you are presenting?'),
('ACT', 17, 20, 'ACT.17.20', 'For you are bringing some strange notions to our ears, and we want to know what they mean.”'),
('ACT', 17, 21, 'ACT.17.21', 'Now all the Athenians and foreigners who lived there spent their time doing nothing more than hearing and articulating new ideas.'),
('ACT', 17, 22, 'ACT.17.22', 'Then Paul stood up in the meeting of the Areopagus and said, “Men of Athens, I see that in every way you are very religious.'),
('ACT', 17, 23, 'ACT.17.23', 'For as I walked around and examined your objects of worship, I even found an altar with this inscription: TO AN UNKNOWN GOD. Therefore what you worship as something unknown, I now proclaim to you.'),
('ACT', 17, 24, 'ACT.17.24', 'The God who made the world and everything in it is the Lord of heaven and earth and does not live in temples made by human hands.'),
('ACT', 17, 25, 'ACT.17.25', 'Nor is He served by human hands, as if He needed anything, because He Himself gives everyone life and breath and everything else.'),
('ACT', 17, 26, 'ACT.17.26', 'From one man He made every nation of men, that they should inhabit the whole earth; and He determined their appointed times and the boundaries of their lands.'),
('ACT', 17, 27, 'ACT.17.27', 'God intended that they would seek Him and perhaps reach out for Him and find Him, though He is not far from each one of us.'),
('ACT', 17, 28, 'ACT.17.28', '‘For in Him we live and move and have our being.’ As some of your own poets have said, ‘We are His offspring.’'),
('ACT', 17, 29, 'ACT.17.29', 'Therefore, being offspring of God, we should not think that the Divine Being is like gold or silver or stone, an image formed by man’s skill and imagination.'),
('ACT', 17, 30, 'ACT.17.30', 'Although God overlooked the ignorance of earlier times, He now commands all people everywhere to repent.'),
('ACT', 17, 31, 'ACT.17.31', 'For He has set a day when He will judge the world with justice by the Man He has appointed. He has given proof of this to everyone by raising Him from the dead.”'),
('ACT', 17, 32, 'ACT.17.32', 'When they heard about the resurrection of the dead, some began to mock him, but others said, “We want to hear you again on this topic.”'),
('ACT', 17, 33, 'ACT.17.33', 'At that, Paul left the Areopagus.'),
('ACT', 17, 34, 'ACT.17.34', 'But some joined him and believed, including Dionysius the Areopagite, a woman named Damaris, and others who were with them.'),
('ACT', 18, 1, 'ACT.18.1', 'After this, Paul left Athens and went to Corinth.'),
('ACT', 18, 2, 'ACT.18.2', 'There he found a Jew named Aquila, a native of Pontus, who had recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla because Claudius had ordered all the Jews to leave Rome. Paul went to visit them,'),
('ACT', 18, 3, 'ACT.18.3', 'and he stayed and worked with them because they were tentmakers by trade, just as he was.'),
('ACT', 18, 4, 'ACT.18.4', 'Every Sabbath he reasoned in the synagogue, trying to persuade Jews and Greeks alike.'),
('ACT', 18, 5, 'ACT.18.5', 'And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.'),
('ACT', 18, 6, 'ACT.18.6', 'But when they opposed and insulted him, he shook out his garments and told them, “Your blood be on your own heads! I am innocent of it. From now on I will go to the Gentiles.”'),
('ACT', 18, 7, 'ACT.18.7', 'So Paul left the synagogue and went next door to the house of Titus Justus, a worshiper of God.'),
('ACT', 18, 8, 'ACT.18.8', 'Crispus, the synagogue leader, and his whole household believed in the Lord. And many of the Corinthians who heard the message believed and were baptized.'),
('ACT', 18, 9, 'ACT.18.9', 'One night the Lord spoke to Paul in a vision: “Do not be afraid; keep on speaking; do not be silent.'),
('ACT', 18, 10, 'ACT.18.10', 'For I am with you and no one will lay a hand on you, because I have many people in this city.”'),
('ACT', 18, 11, 'ACT.18.11', 'So Paul stayed for a year and a half, teaching the word of God among the Corinthians.'),
('ACT', 18, 12, 'ACT.18.12', 'While Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews coordinated an attack on Paul and brought him before the judgment seat.'),
('ACT', 18, 13, 'ACT.18.13', '“This man is persuading the people to worship God in ways contrary to the law,” they said.'),
('ACT', 18, 14, 'ACT.18.14', 'But just as Paul was about to speak, Gallio told the Jews, “If this matter involved a wrongdoing or vicious crime, O Jews, it would be reasonable for me to hear your complaint.'),
('ACT', 18, 15, 'ACT.18.15', 'But since it is a dispute about words and names and your own law, settle it yourselves. I refuse to be a judge of such things.”'),
('ACT', 18, 16, 'ACT.18.16', 'And he drove them away from the judgment seat.'),
('ACT', 18, 17, 'ACT.18.17', 'At this, the crowd seized Sosthenes the synagogue leader and beat him in front of the judgment seat. But none of this was of concern to Gallio.'),
('ACT', 18, 18, 'ACT.18.18', 'Paul remained in Corinth for quite some time before saying goodbye to the brothers. He had his head shaved in Cenchrea to keep a vow he had made, and then he sailed for Syria, accompanied by Priscilla and Aquila.'),
('ACT', 18, 19, 'ACT.18.19', 'When they reached Ephesus, Paul left Priscilla and Aquila. He himself went into the synagogue there and reasoned with the Jews.'),
('ACT', 18, 20, 'ACT.18.20', 'When they asked him to stay for a while longer, he declined.'),
('ACT', 18, 21, 'ACT.18.21', 'But as he left, he said, “I will come back to you if God is willing.” And he set sail from Ephesus.'),
('ACT', 18, 22, 'ACT.18.22', 'When Paul had landed at Caesarea, he went up and greeted the church at Jerusalem. Then he went down to Antioch.'),
('ACT', 18, 23, 'ACT.18.23', 'After Paul had spent some time in Antioch, he traveled from place to place throughout the region of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples.'),
('ACT', 18, 24, 'ACT.18.24', 'Meanwhile a Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria, came to Ephesus. He was an eloquent man, well versed in the Scriptures.'),
('ACT', 18, 25, 'ACT.18.25', 'He had been instructed in the way of the Lord and was fervent in spirit. He spoke and taught accurately about Jesus, though he knew only the baptism of John.'),
('ACT', 18, 26, 'ACT.18.26', 'And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. When Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him aside and explained to him the way of God more accurately.'),
('ACT', 18, 27, 'ACT.18.27', 'When Apollos resolved to cross over to Achaia, the brothers encouraged him and wrote to the disciples there to welcome him. On his arrival, he was a great help to those who by grace had believed.'),
('ACT', 18, 28, 'ACT.18.28', 'For he powerfully refuted the Jews in public debate, proving from the Scriptures that Jesus is the Christ.'),
('ACT', 19, 1, 'ACT.19.1', 'While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul passed through the interior and came to Ephesus. There he found some disciples'),
('ACT', 19, 2, 'ACT.19.2', 'and asked them, “Did you receive the Holy Spirit when you became believers?” “No,” they answered, “we have not even heard that there is a Holy Spirit.”'),
('ACT', 19, 3, 'ACT.19.3', '“Into what, then, were you baptized?” Paul asked. “The baptism of John,” they replied.'),
('ACT', 19, 4, 'ACT.19.4', 'Paul explained: “John’s baptism was a baptism of repentance. He told the people to believe in the One coming after him, that is, in Jesus.”'),
('ACT', 19, 5, 'ACT.19.5', 'On hearing this, they were baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.'),
('ACT', 19, 6, 'ACT.19.6', 'And when Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they spoke in tongues and prophesied.'),
('ACT', 19, 7, 'ACT.19.7', 'There were about twelve men in all.'),
('ACT', 19, 8, 'ACT.19.8', 'Then Paul went into the synagogue and spoke boldly there for three months, arguing persuasively about the kingdom of God.'),
('ACT', 19, 9, 'ACT.19.9', 'But when some of them stubbornly refused to believe and publicly maligned the Way, Paul took his disciples and left the synagogue to conduct daily discussions in the lecture hall of Tyrannus.'),
('ACT', 19, 10, 'ACT.19.10', 'This continued for two years, so that everyone who lived in the province of Asia, Jews and Greeks alike, heard the word of the Lord.'),
('ACT', 19, 11, 'ACT.19.11', 'God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul,'),
('ACT', 19, 12, 'ACT.19.12', 'so that even handkerchiefs and aprons that had touched him were taken to the sick, and the diseases and evil spirits left them.'),
('ACT', 19, 13, 'ACT.19.13', 'Now there were some itinerant Jewish exorcists who tried to invoke the name of the Lord Jesus over those with evil spirits. They would say, “I command you by Jesus, whom Paul proclaims.”'),
('ACT', 19, 14, 'ACT.19.14', 'Seven sons of Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, were doing this.'),
('ACT', 19, 15, 'ACT.19.15', 'But one day the evil spirit responded, “Jesus I know, and I know about Paul, but who are you?”'),
('ACT', 19, 16, 'ACT.19.16', 'Then the man with the evil spirit jumped on them and overpowered them all. The attack was so violent that they ran out of the house naked and wounded.'),
('ACT', 19, 17, 'ACT.19.17', 'This became known to all the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus, and fear came over all of them. So the name of the Lord Jesus was held in high honor.'),
('ACT', 19, 18, 'ACT.19.18', 'Many who had believed now came forward, confessing and disclosing their deeds.'),
('ACT', 19, 19, 'ACT.19.19', 'And a number of those who had practiced magic arts brought their books and burned them in front of everyone. When the value of the books was calculated, the total came to fifty thousand drachmas.'),
('ACT', 19, 20, 'ACT.19.20', 'So the word of the Lord powerfully continued to spread and prevail.'),
('ACT', 19, 21, 'ACT.19.21', 'After these things had happened, Paul resolved in the Spirit to go to Jerusalem, passing through Macedonia and Achaia. “After I have been there,” he said, “I must see Rome as well.”'),
('ACT', 19, 22, 'ACT.19.22', 'He sent two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, to Macedonia, while he stayed for a time in the province of Asia.'),
('ACT', 19, 23, 'ACT.19.23', 'About that time there arose a great disturbance about the Way.'),
('ACT', 19, 24, 'ACT.19.24', 'It began with a silversmith named Demetrius who made silver shrines of Artemis, bringing much business to the craftsmen.'),
('ACT', 19, 25, 'ACT.19.25', 'Demetrius assembled the craftsmen, along with the workmen in related trades. “Men,” he said, “you know that this business is our source of prosperity.'),
('ACT', 19, 26, 'ACT.19.26', 'And you can see and hear that not only in Ephesus, but in nearly the whole province of Asia, this Paul has persuaded a great number of people to turn away. He says that man-made gods are no gods at all.'),
('ACT', 19, 27, 'ACT.19.27', 'There is danger not only that our business will fall into disrepute, but also that the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be discredited and her majesty deposed—she who is worshiped by all the province of Asia and the whole world.”'),
('ACT', 19, 28, 'ACT.19.28', 'When the men heard this, they were enraged and began shouting, “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”'),
('ACT', 19, 29, 'ACT.19.29', 'Soon the whole city was in disarray. They rushed together into the theatre, dragging with them Gaius and Aristarchus, Paul’s traveling companions from Macedonia.'),
('ACT', 19, 30, 'ACT.19.30', 'Paul wanted to go before the assembly, but the disciples would not allow him.'),
('ACT', 19, 31, 'ACT.19.31', 'Even some of Paul’s friends who were officials of the province of Asia sent word to him, begging him not to venture into the theatre.'),
('ACT', 19, 32, 'ACT.19.32', 'Meanwhile the assembly was in turmoil. Some were shouting one thing and some another, and most of them did not even know why they were there.'),
('ACT', 19, 33, 'ACT.19.33', 'The Jews in the crowd pushed Alexander forward to explain himself, and he motioned for silence so he could make his defense to the people.'),
('ACT', 19, 34, 'ACT.19.34', 'But when they realized that he was a Jew, they all shouted in unison for about two hours: “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”'),
('ACT', 19, 35, 'ACT.19.35', 'Finally the city clerk quieted the crowd and declared, “Men of Ephesus, doesn’t everyone know that the city of Ephesus is guardian of the temple of the great Artemis and of her image, which fell from heaven?'),
('ACT', 19, 36, 'ACT.19.36', 'Since these things are undeniable, you ought to be calm and not do anything rash.'),
('ACT', 19, 37, 'ACT.19.37', 'For you have brought these men here, though they have neither robbed our temple nor blasphemed our goddess.'),
('ACT', 19, 38, 'ACT.19.38', 'So if Demetrius and his fellow craftsmen have a complaint against anyone, the courts are open and proconsuls are available. Let them bring charges against one another there.'),
('ACT', 19, 39, 'ACT.19.39', 'But if you are seeking anything beyond this, it must be settled in a legal assembly.'),
('ACT', 19, 40, 'ACT.19.40', 'For we are in jeopardy of being charged with rioting for today’s events, and we have no justification to account for this commotion.”'),
('ACT', 19, 41, 'ACT.19.41', 'After he had said this, he dismissed the assembly.'),
('ACT', 20, 1, 'ACT.20.1', 'When the uproar had ended, Paul sent for the disciples. And after encouraging them, he said goodbye to them and left for Macedonia.'),
('ACT', 20, 2, 'ACT.20.2', 'After traveling through that area and speaking many words of encouragement, he arrived in Greece,'),
('ACT', 20, 3, 'ACT.20.3', 'where he stayed three months. And when the Jews formed a plot against him as he was about to sail for Syria, he decided to go back through Macedonia.'),
('ACT', 20, 4, 'ACT.20.4', 'Paul was accompanied by Sopater son of Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from the province of Asia.'),
('ACT', 20, 5, 'ACT.20.5', 'These men went on ahead and waited for us in Troas.'),
('ACT', 20, 6, 'ACT.20.6', 'And after the Feast of Unleavened Bread, we sailed from Philippi, and five days later we rejoined them in Troas, where we stayed seven days.'),
('ACT', 20, 7, 'ACT.20.7', 'On the first day of the week we came together to break bread. Since Paul was ready to leave the next day, he talked to them and kept on speaking until midnight.'),
('ACT', 20, 8, 'ACT.20.8', 'Now there were many lamps in the upper room where we were gathered.'),
('ACT', 20, 9, 'ACT.20.9', 'And a certain young man named Eutychus, seated in the window, was sinking into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and on. When he was sound asleep, he fell from the third story and was picked up dead.'),
('ACT', 20, 10, 'ACT.20.10', 'But Paul went down, threw himself on the young man, and embraced him. “Do not be alarmed!” he said. “He is still alive!”'),
('ACT', 20, 11, 'ACT.20.11', 'Then Paul went back upstairs, broke bread, and ate. And after speaking until daybreak, he departed.'),
('ACT', 20, 12, 'ACT.20.12', 'And the people were greatly relieved to take the boy home alive.'),
('ACT', 20, 13, 'ACT.20.13', 'We went on ahead to the ship and sailed to Assos, where we were to take Paul aboard. He had arranged this because he was going there on foot.'),
('ACT', 20, 14, 'ACT.20.14', 'And when he met us at Assos, we took him aboard and went on to Mitylene.'),
('ACT', 20, 15, 'ACT.20.15', 'Sailing on from there, we arrived the next day opposite Chios. The day after that we arrived at Samos, and on the following day we came to Miletus.'),
('ACT', 20, 16, 'ACT.20.16', 'Paul had decided to sail past Ephesus to avoid spending time in the province of Asia, because he was in a hurry to reach Jerusalem, if possible, by the day of Pentecost.'),
('ACT', 20, 17, 'ACT.20.17', 'From Miletus, Paul sent to Ephesus for the elders of the church.'),
('ACT', 20, 18, 'ACT.20.18', 'When they came to him, he said, “You know how I lived the whole time I was with you, from the first day I arrived in the province of Asia.'),
('ACT', 20, 19, 'ACT.20.19', 'I served the Lord with great humility and with tears, especially in the trials that came upon me through the plots of the Jews.'),
('ACT', 20, 20, 'ACT.20.20', 'I did not shrink back from declaring anything that was helpful to you as I taught you publicly and from house to house,'),
('ACT', 20, 21, 'ACT.20.21', 'testifying to Jews and Greeks alike about repentance to God and faith in our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('ACT', 20, 22, 'ACT.20.22', 'And now, compelled by the Spirit, I am going to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there.'),
('ACT', 20, 23, 'ACT.20.23', 'I only know that in town after town the Holy Spirit warns me that chains and afflictions await me.'),
('ACT', 20, 24, 'ACT.20.24', 'But I consider my life of no value to me, if only I may finish my course and complete the ministry I have received from the Lord Jesus—the ministry of testifying to the good news of God’s grace.'),
('ACT', 20, 25, 'ACT.20.25', 'Now I know that none of you among whom I have preached the kingdom will see my face again.'),
('ACT', 20, 26, 'ACT.20.26', 'Therefore I testify to you this day that I am innocent of the blood of all men.'),
('ACT', 20, 27, 'ACT.20.27', 'For I did not shrink back from declaring to you the whole will of God.'),
('ACT', 20, 28, 'ACT.20.28', 'Keep watch over yourselves and the entire flock of which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers. Be shepherds of the church of God, which He purchased with His own blood.'),
('ACT', 20, 29, 'ACT.20.29', 'I know that after my departure, savage wolves will come in among you and will not spare the flock.'),
('ACT', 20, 30, 'ACT.20.30', 'Even from your own number, men will rise up and distort the truth to draw away disciples after them.'),
('ACT', 20, 31, 'ACT.20.31', 'Therefore be alert and remember that for three years I never stopped warning each of you night and day with tears.'),
('ACT', 20, 32, 'ACT.20.32', 'And now I commit you to God and to the word of His grace, which can build you up and give you an inheritance among all who are sanctified.'),
('ACT', 20, 33, 'ACT.20.33', 'I have not coveted anyone’s silver or gold or clothing.'),
('ACT', 20, 34, 'ACT.20.34', 'You yourselves know that these hands of mine have ministered to my own needs and those of my companions.'),
('ACT', 20, 35, 'ACT.20.35', 'In everything, I showed you that by this kind of hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words of the Lord Jesus Himself: ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’”'),
('ACT', 20, 36, 'ACT.20.36', 'When Paul had said this, he knelt down with all of them and prayed.'),
('ACT', 20, 37, 'ACT.20.37', 'They all wept openly as they embraced Paul and kissed him.'),
('ACT', 20, 38, 'ACT.20.38', 'They were especially grieved by his statement that they would never see his face again. Then they accompanied him to the ship.'),
('ACT', 21, 1, 'ACT.21.1', 'After we had torn ourselves away from them, we sailed directly to Cos, and the next day on to Rhodes, and from there to Patara.'),
('ACT', 21, 2, 'ACT.21.2', 'Finding a ship crossing over to Phoenicia, we boarded it and set sail.'),
('ACT', 21, 3, 'ACT.21.3', 'After sighting Cyprus and passing south of it, we sailed on to Syria and landed at Tyre, where the ship was to unload its cargo.'),
('ACT', 21, 4, 'ACT.21.4', 'We sought out the disciples in Tyre and stayed with them seven days. Through the Spirit they kept telling Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 21, 5, 'ACT.21.5', 'But when our time there had ended, we set out on our journey. All the disciples, with their wives and children, accompanied us out of the city and knelt down on the beach to pray with us.'),
('ACT', 21, 6, 'ACT.21.6', 'And after we had said our farewells, we went aboard the ship, and they returned home.'),
('ACT', 21, 7, 'ACT.21.7', 'When we had finished our voyage from Tyre, we landed at Ptolemais, where we greeted the brothers and stayed with them for a day.'),
('ACT', 21, 8, 'ACT.21.8', 'Leaving the next day, we went on to Caesarea and stayed at the home of Philip the evangelist, who was one of the Seven.'),
('ACT', 21, 9, 'ACT.21.9', 'He had four unmarried daughters who prophesied.'),
('ACT', 21, 10, 'ACT.21.10', 'After we had been there several days, a prophet named Agabus came down from Judea.'),
('ACT', 21, 11, 'ACT.21.11', 'Coming over to us, he took Paul’s belt, bound his own feet and hands, and said, “The Holy Spirit says: ‘In this way the Jews of Jerusalem will bind the owner of this belt and hand him over to the Gentiles.’”'),
('ACT', 21, 12, 'ACT.21.12', 'When we heard this, we and the people there pleaded with Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 21, 13, 'ACT.21.13', 'Then Paul answered, “Why are you weeping and breaking my heart? I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die in Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.”'),
('ACT', 21, 14, 'ACT.21.14', 'When he would not be dissuaded, we quieted down and said, “The Lord’s will be done.”'),
('ACT', 21, 15, 'ACT.21.15', 'After these days, we packed up and went on to Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 21, 16, 'ACT.21.16', 'Some of the disciples from Caesarea accompanied us, and they took us to stay at the home of Mnason the Cypriot, an early disciple.'),
('ACT', 21, 17, 'ACT.21.17', 'When we arrived in Jerusalem, the brothers welcomed us joyfully.'),
('ACT', 21, 18, 'ACT.21.18', 'The next day Paul went in with us to see James, and all the elders were present.'),
('ACT', 21, 19, 'ACT.21.19', 'Paul greeted them and recounted one by one the things that God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry.'),
('ACT', 21, 20, 'ACT.21.20', 'When they heard this, they glorified God. Then they said to Paul, “You see, brother, how many thousands of Jews have believed, and all of them are zealous for the law.'),
('ACT', 21, 21, 'ACT.21.21', 'But they are under the impression that you teach all the Jews who live among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, telling them not to circumcise their children or observe our customs.'),
('ACT', 21, 22, 'ACT.21.22', 'What then should we do? They will certainly hear that you have come.'),
('ACT', 21, 23, 'ACT.21.23', 'Therefore do what we advise you. There are four men with us who have taken a vow.'),
('ACT', 21, 24, 'ACT.21.24', 'Take these men, purify yourself along with them, and pay their expenses so they can have their heads shaved. Then everyone will know that there is no truth to these rumors about you, but that you also live in obedience to the law.'),
('ACT', 21, 25, 'ACT.21.25', 'As for the Gentile believers, we have written to them our decision that they must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality.”'),
('ACT', 21, 26, 'ACT.21.26', 'So the next day Paul took the men and purified himself along with them. Then he entered the temple to give notice of the date when their purification would be complete and the offering would be made for each of them.'),
('ACT', 21, 27, 'ACT.21.27', 'When the seven days were almost over, some Jews from the province of Asia saw Paul at the temple. They stirred up the whole crowd and seized him,'),
('ACT', 21, 28, 'ACT.21.28', 'crying out, “Men of Israel, help us! This is the man who teaches everyone everywhere against our people and against our law and against this place. Furthermore, he has brought Greeks into the temple and defiled this holy place.”'),
('ACT', 21, 29, 'ACT.21.29', 'For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, and they assumed that Paul had brought him into the temple.'),
('ACT', 21, 30, 'ACT.21.30', 'The whole city was stirred up, and the people rushed together. They seized Paul and dragged him out of the temple, and at once the gates were shut.'),
('ACT', 21, 31, 'ACT.21.31', 'While they were trying to kill him, the commander of the Roman regiment received a report that all Jerusalem was in turmoil.'),
('ACT', 21, 32, 'ACT.21.32', 'Immediately he took some soldiers and centurions and ran down to the crowd. When the people saw the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul.'),
('ACT', 21, 33, 'ACT.21.33', 'The commander came up and arrested Paul, ordering that he be bound with two chains. Then he asked who he was and what he had done.'),
('ACT', 21, 34, 'ACT.21.34', 'Some in the crowd were shouting one thing, and some another. And since the commander could not get at the truth because of the uproar, he ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks.'),
('ACT', 21, 35, 'ACT.21.35', 'When Paul reached the steps, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob.'),
('ACT', 21, 36, 'ACT.21.36', 'For the crowd that followed him kept shouting, “Away with him!”'),
('ACT', 21, 37, 'ACT.21.37', 'As they were about to take Paul into the barracks, he asked the commander, “May I say something to you?” “Do you speak Greek?” he replied.'),
('ACT', 21, 38, 'ACT.21.38', '“Aren’t you the Egyptian who incited a rebellion some time ago and led four thousand members of the Assassins into the wilderness?”'),
('ACT', 21, 39, 'ACT.21.39', 'But Paul answered, “I am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no ordinary city. Now I beg you to allow me to speak to the people.”'),
('ACT', 21, 40, 'ACT.21.40', 'Having received permission, Paul stood on the steps and motioned to the crowd. A great hush came over the crowd, and he addressed them in Hebrew:'),
('ACT', 22, 1, 'ACT.22.1', '“Brothers and fathers, listen now to my defense before you.”'),
('ACT', 22, 2, 'ACT.22.2', 'When they heard him speak to them in Hebrew, they became even more quiet. Then Paul declared,'),
('ACT', 22, 3, 'ACT.22.3', '“I am a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but raised in this city. I was educated at the feet of Gamaliel in strict conformity to the law of our fathers. I was just as zealous for God as any of you are today.'),
('ACT', 22, 4, 'ACT.22.4', 'I persecuted this Way even to the death, detaining both men and women and throwing them into prison,'),
('ACT', 22, 5, 'ACT.22.5', 'as the high priest and the whole Council can testify about me. I even obtained letters from them to their brothers in Damascus, and I was on my way to apprehend these people and bring them to Jerusalem to be punished.'),
('ACT', 22, 6, 'ACT.22.6', 'About noon as I was approaching Damascus, suddenly a bright light from heaven flashed around me.'),
('ACT', 22, 7, 'ACT.22.7', 'I fell to the ground and heard a voice say to me, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?’'),
('ACT', 22, 8, 'ACT.22.8', '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting,’ He replied.'),
('ACT', 22, 9, 'ACT.22.9', 'My companions saw the light, but they could not understand the voice of the One speaking to me.'),
('ACT', 22, 10, 'ACT.22.10', 'Then I asked, ‘What should I do, Lord?’ ‘Get up and go into Damascus,’ He told me. ‘There you will be told all that you have been appointed to do.’'),
('ACT', 22, 11, 'ACT.22.11', 'Because the brilliance of the light had blinded me, my companions led me by the hand into Damascus.'),
('ACT', 22, 12, 'ACT.22.12', 'There a man named Ananias, a devout observer of the law who was highly regarded by all the Jews living there,'),
('ACT', 22, 13, 'ACT.22.13', 'came and stood beside me. ‘Brother Saul,’ he said, ‘receive your sight.’ And at that moment I could see him.'),
('ACT', 22, 14, 'ACT.22.14', 'Then he said, ‘The God of our fathers has appointed you to know His will and to see the Righteous One and to hear His voice.'),
('ACT', 22, 15, 'ACT.22.15', 'You will be His witness to everyone of what you have seen and heard.'),
('ACT', 22, 16, 'ACT.22.16', 'And now what are you waiting for? Get up, be baptized, and wash your sins away, calling on His name.’'),
('ACT', 22, 17, 'ACT.22.17', 'Later, when I had returned to Jerusalem and was praying at the temple, I fell into a trance'),
('ACT', 22, 18, 'ACT.22.18', 'and saw the Lord saying to me, ‘Hurry! Leave Jerusalem quickly, because the people here will not accept your testimony about Me.’'),
('ACT', 22, 19, 'ACT.22.19', '‘Lord,’ I answered, ‘they know very well that in one synagogue after another I imprisoned and beat those who believed in You.'),
('ACT', 22, 20, 'ACT.22.20', 'And when the blood of Your witness Stephen was shed, I stood there giving my approval and watching over the garments of those who killed him.’'),
('ACT', 22, 21, 'ACT.22.21', 'Then He said to me, ‘Go! I will send you far away to the Gentiles.’”'),
('ACT', 22, 22, 'ACT.22.22', 'The crowd listened to Paul until he made this statement. Then they lifted up their voices and shouted, “Rid the earth of him! He is not fit to live!”'),
('ACT', 22, 23, 'ACT.22.23', 'As they were shouting and throwing off their cloaks and tossing dust into the air,'),
('ACT', 22, 24, 'ACT.22.24', 'the commander ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks. He directed that Paul be flogged and interrogated to determine the reason for this outcry against him.'),
('ACT', 22, 25, 'ACT.22.25', 'But as they stretched him out to strap him down, Paul said to the centurion standing there, “Is it lawful for you to flog a Roman citizen without a trial?”'),
('ACT', 22, 26, 'ACT.22.26', 'On hearing this, the centurion went and reported it to the commander. “What are you going to do?” he said. “This man is a Roman citizen.”'),
('ACT', 22, 27, 'ACT.22.27', 'The commander went to Paul and asked, “Tell me, are you a Roman citizen?” “Yes,” he answered.'),
('ACT', 22, 28, 'ACT.22.28', '“I paid a high price for my citizenship,” said the commander. “But I was born a citizen,” Paul replied.'),
('ACT', 22, 29, 'ACT.22.29', 'At once those who were about to interrogate Paul stepped back, and the commander himself was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen in chains.'),
('ACT', 22, 30, 'ACT.22.30', 'The next day the commander, wanting to learn the real reason Paul was accused by the Jews, released him and ordered the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin to assemble. Then he brought Paul down and had him stand before them.'),
('ACT', 23, 1, 'ACT.23.1', 'Paul looked directly at the Sanhedrin and said, “Brothers, I have conducted myself before God in all good conscience to this day.”'),
('ACT', 23, 2, 'ACT.23.2', 'At this, the high priest Ananias ordered those standing near Paul to strike him on the mouth.'),
('ACT', 23, 3, 'ACT.23.3', 'Then Paul said to him, “God will strike you, you whitewashed wall! You sit here to judge me according to the law, yet you yourself violate the law by commanding that I be struck.”'),
('ACT', 23, 4, 'ACT.23.4', 'But those standing nearby said, “How dare you insult the high priest of God!”'),
('ACT', 23, 5, 'ACT.23.5', '“Brothers,” Paul replied, “I was not aware that he was the high priest, for it is written: ‘Do not speak evil about the ruler of your people.’”'),
('ACT', 23, 6, 'ACT.23.6', 'Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and the others Pharisees, called out in the Sanhedrin, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee. It is because of my hope in the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial.”'),
('ACT', 23, 7, 'ACT.23.7', 'As soon as he had said this, a dispute broke out between the Pharisees and Sadducees, and the assembly was divided.'),
('ACT', 23, 8, 'ACT.23.8', 'For the Sadducees say that there is neither a resurrection nor angels nor spirits, but the Pharisees acknowledge them all.'),
('ACT', 23, 9, 'ACT.23.9', 'A great clamor arose, and some scribes from the party of the Pharisees got up and contended sharply, “We find nothing wrong with this man. What if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?”'),
('ACT', 23, 10, 'ACT.23.10', 'The dispute grew so violent that the commander was afraid they would tear Paul to pieces. He ordered the soldiers to go down and remove him by force and bring him into the barracks.'),
('ACT', 23, 11, 'ACT.23.11', 'The following night the Lord stood near Paul and said, “Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so also you must testify in Rome.”'),
('ACT', 23, 12, 'ACT.23.12', 'When daylight came, the Jews formed a conspiracy and bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they had killed Paul.'),
('ACT', 23, 13, 'ACT.23.13', 'More than forty of them were involved in this plot.'),
('ACT', 23, 14, 'ACT.23.14', 'They went to the chief priests and elders and said, “We have bound ourselves with a solemn oath not to eat anything until we have killed Paul.'),
('ACT', 23, 15, 'ACT.23.15', 'Now then, you and the Sanhedrin petition the commander to bring him down to you on the pretext of examining his case more carefully. We are ready to kill him on the way.”'),
('ACT', 23, 16, 'ACT.23.16', 'But when the son of Paul’s sister heard about the plot, he went into the barracks and told Paul.'),
('ACT', 23, 17, 'ACT.23.17', 'Then Paul called one of the centurions and said, “Take this young man to the commander; he has something to tell him.”'),
('ACT', 23, 18, 'ACT.23.18', 'So the centurion took him to the commander and said, “Paul the prisoner sent and asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.”'),
('ACT', 23, 19, 'ACT.23.19', 'The commander took the young man by the hand, drew him aside, and asked, “What do you need to tell me?”'),
('ACT', 23, 20, 'ACT.23.20', 'He answered, “The Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul to the Sanhedrin tomorrow on the pretext of acquiring more information about him.'),
('ACT', 23, 21, 'ACT.23.21', 'Do not let them persuade you, because more than forty men are waiting to ambush him. They have bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they have killed him; they are ready now, awaiting your consent.”'),
('ACT', 23, 22, 'ACT.23.22', 'So the commander dismissed the young man and instructed him, “Do not tell anyone that you have reported this to me.”'),
('ACT', 23, 23, 'ACT.23.23', 'Then he called two of his centurions and said, “Prepare two hundred soldiers, seventy horsemen, and two hundred spearmen to go to Caesarea in the third hour of the night.'),
('ACT', 23, 24, 'ACT.23.24', 'Provide mounts for Paul to take him safely to Governor Felix.”'),
('ACT', 23, 25, 'ACT.23.25', 'And he wrote the following letter:'),
('ACT', 23, 26, 'ACT.23.26', 'Claudius Lysias, To His Excellency, Governor Felix: Greetings.'),
('ACT', 23, 27, 'ACT.23.27', 'This man was seized by the Jews, and they were about to kill him when I came with my troops to rescue him. For I had learned that he is a Roman citizen,'),
('ACT', 23, 28, 'ACT.23.28', 'and since I wanted to understand their charges against him, I brought him down to their Sanhedrin.'),
('ACT', 23, 29, 'ACT.23.29', 'I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.'),
('ACT', 23, 30, 'ACT.23.30', 'When I was informed that there was a plot against the man, I sent him to you at once. I also instructed his accusers to present their case against him before you.'),
('ACT', 23, 31, 'ACT.23.31', 'So the soldiers followed their orders and brought Paul by night to Antipatris.'),
('ACT', 23, 32, 'ACT.23.32', 'The next day they returned to the barracks and let the horsemen go on with him.'),
('ACT', 23, 33, 'ACT.23.33', 'When the horsemen arrived in Caesarea, they delivered the letter to the governor and presented Paul to him.'),
('ACT', 23, 34, 'ACT.23.34', 'The governor read the letter and asked what province Paul was from. Learning that he was from Cilicia,'),
('ACT', 23, 35, 'ACT.23.35', 'he said, “I will hear your case when your accusers arrive.” Then he ordered that Paul be kept under guard in Herod’s Praetorium.'),
('ACT', 24, 1, 'ACT.24.1', 'Five days later the high priest Ananias came down with some elders and a lawyer named Tertullus, who presented to the governor their case against Paul.'),
('ACT', 24, 2, 'ACT.24.2', 'When Paul had been called in, Tertullus opened the prosecution: “Because of you, we have enjoyed a lasting peace, and your foresight has brought improvements to this nation.'),
('ACT', 24, 3, 'ACT.24.3', 'In every way and everywhere, most excellent Felix, we acknowledge this with all gratitude.'),
('ACT', 24, 4, 'ACT.24.4', 'But in order not to delay you any further, I beg your indulgence to hear us briefly.'),
('ACT', 24, 5, 'ACT.24.5', 'We have found this man to be a pestilence, stirring up dissension among the Jews all over the world. He is a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes,'),
('ACT', 24, 6, 'ACT.24.6', 'and he even tried to desecrate the temple; so we seized him.'),
('ACT', 24, 8, 'ACT.24.8', 'By examining him yourself, you will be able to learn the truth about all our charges against him.”'),
('ACT', 24, 9, 'ACT.24.9', 'The Jews concurred, asserting that these charges were true.'),
('ACT', 24, 10, 'ACT.24.10', 'When the governor motioned for Paul to speak, he began his response: “Knowing that you have been a judge over this nation for many years, I gladly make my defense.'),
('ACT', 24, 11, 'ACT.24.11', 'You can verify for yourself that no more than twelve days ago I went up to Jerusalem to worship.'),
('ACT', 24, 12, 'ACT.24.12', 'Yet my accusers did not find me debating with anyone in the temple or riling up a crowd in the synagogues or in the city.'),
('ACT', 24, 13, 'ACT.24.13', 'Nor can they prove to you any of their charges against me.'),
('ACT', 24, 14, 'ACT.24.14', 'I do confess to you, however, that I worship the God of our fathers according to the Way, which they call a sect. I believe everything that is laid down by the Law and written in the Prophets,'),
('ACT', 24, 15, 'ACT.24.15', 'and I have the same hope in God that they themselves cherish, that there will be a resurrection of both the righteous and the wicked.'),
('ACT', 24, 16, 'ACT.24.16', 'In this hope, I strive always to maintain a clear conscience before God and man.'),
('ACT', 24, 17, 'ACT.24.17', 'After several years, then, I returned to Jerusalem to bring alms to my people and to present offerings.'),
('ACT', 24, 18, 'ACT.24.18', 'At the time they found me in the temple, I was ceremonially clean and was not inciting a crowd or an uproar. But there are some Jews from the province of Asia'),
('ACT', 24, 19, 'ACT.24.19', 'who ought to appear before you and bring charges, if they have anything against me.'),
('ACT', 24, 20, 'ACT.24.20', 'Otherwise, let these men state for themselves any crime they found in me when I stood before the Sanhedrin,'),
('ACT', 24, 21, 'ACT.24.21', 'unless it was this one thing I called out as I stood in their presence: ‘It is concerning the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial before you today.’”'),
('ACT', 24, 22, 'ACT.24.22', 'Then Felix, who was well informed about the Way, adjourned the hearing and said, “When Lysias the commander comes, I will decide your case.”'),
('ACT', 24, 23, 'ACT.24.23', 'He ordered the centurion to keep Paul under guard, but to allow him some freedom and permit his friends to minister to his needs.'),
('ACT', 24, 24, 'ACT.24.24', 'After several days, Felix returned with his wife Drusilla, who was a Jewess. He sent for Paul and listened to him speak about faith in Christ Jesus.'),
('ACT', 24, 25, 'ACT.24.25', 'As Paul expounded on righteousness, self-control, and the coming judgment, Felix became frightened and said, “You may go for now. When I find the time, I will call for you.”'),
('ACT', 24, 26, 'ACT.24.26', 'At the same time, he was hoping that Paul would offer him a bribe. So he sent for Paul frequently and talked with him.'),
('ACT', 24, 27, 'ACT.24.27', 'After two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison.'),
('ACT', 25, 1, 'ACT.25.1', 'Three days after his arrival in the province, Festus went up from Caesarea to Jerusalem,'),
('ACT', 25, 2, 'ACT.25.2', 'where the chief priests and Jewish leaders presented their case against Paul. They urged Festus'),
('ACT', 25, 3, 'ACT.25.3', 'to grant them a concession against Paul by summoning him to Jerusalem, because they were preparing an ambush to kill him along the way.'),
('ACT', 25, 4, 'ACT.25.4', 'But Festus replied, “Paul is being held in Caesarea, and I myself am going there soon.'),
('ACT', 25, 5, 'ACT.25.5', 'So if this man has done anything wrong, let some of your leaders come down with me and accuse him there.”'),
('ACT', 25, 6, 'ACT.25.6', 'After spending no more than eight or ten days with them, Festus went down to Caesarea. The next day he sat on the judgment seat and ordered that Paul be brought in.'),
('ACT', 25, 7, 'ACT.25.7', 'When Paul arrived, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many serious charges that they could not prove.'),
('ACT', 25, 8, 'ACT.25.8', 'Then Paul made his defense: “I have committed no offense against the law of the Jews or against the temple or against Caesar.”'),
('ACT', 25, 9, 'ACT.25.9', 'But Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor, said to Paul, “Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem to stand trial before me on these charges?”'),
('ACT', 25, 10, 'ACT.25.10', 'Paul replied, “I am standing before the judgment seat of Caesar, where I ought to be tried. I have done nothing wrong to the Jews, as you yourself know very well.'),
('ACT', 25, 11, 'ACT.25.11', 'If, however, I am guilty of anything worthy of death, I do not refuse to die. But if there is no truth to their accusations against me, no one has the right to hand me over to them. I appeal to Caesar!”'),
('ACT', 25, 12, 'ACT.25.12', 'Then Festus conferred with his council and replied, “You have appealed to Caesar. To Caesar you will go!”'),
('ACT', 25, 13, 'ACT.25.13', 'After several days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice came down to Caesarea to pay their respects to Festus.'),
('ACT', 25, 14, 'ACT.25.14', 'Since they were staying several days, Festus laid out Paul’s case before the king: “There is a certain man whom Felix left in prison.'),
('ACT', 25, 15, 'ACT.25.15', 'While I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and elders of the Jews presented their case and requested a judgment against him.'),
('ACT', 25, 16, 'ACT.25.16', 'I told them that it is not the Roman custom to hand a man over before he has had an opportunity to face his accusers and defend himself against their charges.'),
('ACT', 25, 17, 'ACT.25.17', 'So when they came here with me, I did not delay. The next day I sat on the judgment seat and ordered that the man be brought in.'),
('ACT', 25, 18, 'ACT.25.18', 'But when his accusers rose to speak, they did not charge him with any of the crimes I had expected.'),
('ACT', 25, 19, 'ACT.25.19', 'They only had some contentions with him regarding their own religion and a certain Jesus who had died, but whom Paul affirmed to be alive.'),
('ACT', 25, 20, 'ACT.25.20', 'Since I was at a loss as to how to investigate these matters, I asked if he was willing to go to Jerusalem and be tried there on these charges.'),
('ACT', 25, 21, 'ACT.25.21', 'But when Paul appealed to be held over for the decision of the Emperor, I ordered that he be held until I could send him to Caesar.”'),
('ACT', 25, 22, 'ACT.25.22', 'Then Agrippa said to Festus, “I would like to hear this man myself.” “Tomorrow you will hear him,” Festus declared.'),
('ACT', 25, 23, 'ACT.25.23', 'The next day Agrippa and Bernice came with great pomp and entered the auditorium, along with the commanders and leading men of the city. And Festus ordered that Paul be brought in.'),
('ACT', 25, 24, 'ACT.25.24', 'Then Festus said, “King Agrippa and all who are present with us, you see this man. The whole Jewish community has petitioned me about him, both here and in Jerusalem, crying out that he ought not to live any longer.'),
('ACT', 25, 25, 'ACT.25.25', 'But I found he had done nothing worthy of death, and since he has now appealed to the Emperor, I decided to send him.'),
('ACT', 25, 26, 'ACT.25.26', 'I have nothing definite to write to our sovereign about him. Therefore I have brought him before all of you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, so that after this inquiry I may have something to write.'),
('ACT', 25, 27, 'ACT.25.27', 'For it seems unreasonable to me to send on a prisoner without specifying the charges against him.”'),
('ACT', 26, 1, 'ACT.26.1', 'Agrippa said to Paul, “You have permission to speak for yourself.” Then Paul stretched out his hand and began his defense:'),
('ACT', 26, 2, 'ACT.26.2', '“King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate to stand before you today to defend myself against all the accusations of the Jews,'),
('ACT', 26, 3, 'ACT.26.3', 'especially since you are acquainted with all the Jewish customs and controversies. I beg you, therefore, to listen to me patiently.'),
('ACT', 26, 4, 'ACT.26.4', 'Surely all the Jews know how I have lived from my earliest childhood among my own people, and also in Jerusalem.'),
('ACT', 26, 5, 'ACT.26.5', 'They have known me for a long time and can testify, if they are willing, that I lived as a Pharisee, adhering to the strictest sect of our religion.'),
('ACT', 26, 6, 'ACT.26.6', 'And now I stand on trial because of my hope in the promise that God made to our fathers,'),
('ACT', 26, 7, 'ACT.26.7', 'the promise our twelve tribes are hoping to see fulfilled as they earnestly serve God day and night. It is because of this hope, O king, that I am accused by the Jews.'),
('ACT', 26, 8, 'ACT.26.8', 'Why would any of you consider it incredible that God raises the dead?'),
('ACT', 26, 9, 'ACT.26.9', 'So then, I too was convinced that I ought to do all I could to oppose the name of Jesus of Nazareth.'),
('ACT', 26, 10, 'ACT.26.10', 'And that is what I did in Jerusalem. With authority from the chief priests I put many of the saints in prison, and when they were condemned to death, I cast my vote against them.'),
('ACT', 26, 11, 'ACT.26.11', 'I frequently had them punished in the synagogues, and I tried to make them blaspheme. In my raging fury against them, I even went to foreign cities to persecute them.'),
('ACT', 26, 12, 'ACT.26.12', 'In this pursuit I was on my way to Damascus with the authority and commission of the chief priests.'),
('ACT', 26, 13, 'ACT.26.13', 'About noon, O king, as I was on the road, I saw a light from heaven, brighter than the sun, shining around me and my companions.'),
('ACT', 26, 14, 'ACT.26.14', 'We all fell to the ground, and I heard a voice say to me in Hebrew, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads.’'),
('ACT', 26, 15, 'ACT.26.15', '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,’ the Lord replied.'),
('ACT', 26, 16, 'ACT.26.16', '‘But get up and stand on your feet. For I have appeared to you to appoint you as a servant and as a witness of what you have seen from Me and what I will show you.'),
('ACT', 26, 17, 'ACT.26.17', 'I will rescue you from your own people and from the Gentiles. I am sending you to them'),
('ACT', 26, 18, 'ACT.26.18', 'to open their eyes, so that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, that they may receive forgiveness of sins and an inheritance among those sanctified by faith in Me.’'),
('ACT', 26, 19, 'ACT.26.19', 'So then, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision.'),
('ACT', 26, 20, 'ACT.26.20', 'First to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, then to everyone in the region of Judea, and then to the Gentiles, I declared that they should repent and turn to God, performing deeds worthy of their repentance.'),
('ACT', 26, 21, 'ACT.26.21', 'For this reason the Jews seized me in the temple courts and tried to kill me.'),
('ACT', 26, 22, 'ACT.26.22', 'But I have had God’s help to this day, and I stand here to testify to small and great alike. I am saying nothing beyond what the prophets and Moses said would happen:'),
('ACT', 26, 23, 'ACT.26.23', 'that the Christ would suffer, and as the first to rise from the dead, would proclaim light to our people and to the Gentiles.”'),
('ACT', 26, 24, 'ACT.26.24', 'At this stage of Paul’s defense, Festus exclaimed in a loud voice, “You are insane, Paul! Your great learning is driving you to madness!”'),
('ACT', 26, 25, 'ACT.26.25', 'But Paul answered, “I am not insane, most excellent Festus; I am speaking words of truth and sobriety.'),
('ACT', 26, 26, 'ACT.26.26', 'For the king knows about these matters, and I can speak freely to him. I am confident that none of this has escaped his notice, because it was not done in a corner.'),
('ACT', 26, 27, 'ACT.26.27', 'King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you do.”'),
('ACT', 26, 28, 'ACT.26.28', 'Then Agrippa said to Paul, “Can you persuade me in such a short time to become a Christian?”'),
('ACT', 26, 29, 'ACT.26.29', '“Short time or long,” Paul replied, “I wish to God that not only you but all who hear me this day may become what I am, except for these chains.”'),
('ACT', 26, 30, 'ACT.26.30', 'Then the king and the governor rose, along with Bernice and those seated with them.'),
('ACT', 26, 31, 'ACT.26.31', 'On their way out, they said to one another, “This man has done nothing worthy of death or imprisonment.”'),
('ACT', 26, 32, 'ACT.26.32', 'And Agrippa said to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.”'),
('ACT', 27, 1, 'ACT.27.1', 'When it was decided that we would sail for Italy, Paul and some other prisoners were handed over to a centurion named Julius, who belonged to the Imperial Regiment.'),
('ACT', 27, 2, 'ACT.27.2', 'We boarded an Adramyttian ship about to sail for ports along the coast of Asia, and we put out to sea. Aristarchus, a Macedonian from Thessalonica, was with us.'),
('ACT', 27, 3, 'ACT.27.3', 'The next day we landed at Sidon, and Julius treated Paul with consideration, allowing him to visit his friends and receive their care.'),
('ACT', 27, 4, 'ACT.27.4', 'After putting out from there, we sailed to the lee of Cyprus because the winds were against us.'),
('ACT', 27, 5, 'ACT.27.5', 'And when we had sailed across the open sea off the coast of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra in Lycia.'),
('ACT', 27, 6, 'ACT.27.6', 'There the centurion found an Alexandrian ship sailing for Italy and put us on board.'),
('ACT', 27, 7, 'ACT.27.7', 'After sailing slowly for many days, we arrived off Cnidus. When the wind impeded us, we sailed to the lee of Crete, opposite Salmone.'),
('ACT', 27, 8, 'ACT.27.8', 'After we had moved along the coast with difficulty, we came to a place called Fair Havens, near the town of Lasea.'),
('ACT', 27, 9, 'ACT.27.9', 'By now much time had passed, and the voyage had already become dangerous because it was after the Fast. So Paul advised them,'),
('ACT', 27, 10, 'ACT.27.10', '“Men, I can see that our voyage will be filled with disaster and great loss, not only to ship and cargo, but to our own lives as well.”'),
('ACT', 27, 11, 'ACT.27.11', 'But contrary to Paul’s advice, the centurion was persuaded by the pilot and by the owner of the ship.'),
('ACT', 27, 12, 'ACT.27.12', 'Since the harbor was unsuitable to winter in, the majority decided to sail on, hoping that somehow they could reach Phoenix to winter there. Phoenix was a harbor in Crete facing both southwest and northwest.'),
('ACT', 27, 13, 'ACT.27.13', 'When a gentle south wind began to blow, they thought they had their opportunity. So they weighed anchor and sailed along, hugging the coast of Crete.'),
('ACT', 27, 14, 'ACT.27.14', 'But it was not long before a cyclone called the Northeaster swept down across the island.'),
('ACT', 27, 15, 'ACT.27.15', 'Unable to head into the wind, the ship was caught up. So we gave way and let ourselves be driven along.'),
('ACT', 27, 16, 'ACT.27.16', 'Passing to the lee of a small island called Cauda, we barely managed to secure the lifeboat.'),
('ACT', 27, 17, 'ACT.27.17', 'After hoisting it up, the crew used ropes to undergird the ship. And fearing that they would run aground on the sandbars of Syrtis, they lowered the sea anchor and were driven along.'),
('ACT', 27, 18, 'ACT.27.18', 'We were tossed so violently that the next day the men began to jettison the cargo.'),
('ACT', 27, 19, 'ACT.27.19', 'On the third day, they threw the ship’s tackle overboard with their own hands.'),
('ACT', 27, 20, 'ACT.27.20', 'When neither sun nor stars appeared for many days and the great storm continued to batter us, we abandoned all hope of being saved.'),
('ACT', 27, 21, 'ACT.27.21', 'After the men had gone a long time without food, Paul stood up among them and said, “Men, you should have followed my advice not to sail from Crete. Then you would have averted this disaster and loss.'),
('ACT', 27, 22, 'ACT.27.22', 'But now I urge you to keep up your courage, because you will not experience any loss of life, but only of the ship.'),
('ACT', 27, 23, 'ACT.27.23', 'For just last night an angel of the God to whom I belong and whom I serve stood beside me'),
('ACT', 27, 24, 'ACT.27.24', 'and said, ‘Do not be afraid, Paul; you must stand before Caesar. And look, God has granted you the lives of all who sail with you.’'),
('ACT', 27, 25, 'ACT.27.25', 'So take courage, men, for I believe God that it will happen just as He told me.'),
('ACT', 27, 26, 'ACT.27.26', 'However, we must run aground on some island.”'),
('ACT', 27, 27, 'ACT.27.27', 'On the fourteenth night we were still being driven across the Adriatic Sea. About midnight the sailors sensed they were approaching land.'),
('ACT', 27, 28, 'ACT.27.28', 'They took soundings and found that the water was twenty fathoms deep. Going a little farther, they took another set of soundings that read fifteen fathoms.'),
('ACT', 27, 29, 'ACT.27.29', 'Fearing that we would run aground on the rocks, they dropped four anchors from the stern and prayed for daybreak.'),
('ACT', 27, 30, 'ACT.27.30', 'Meanwhile, the sailors attempted to escape from the ship. Pretending to lower anchors from the bow, they let the lifeboat down into the sea.'),
('ACT', 27, 31, 'ACT.27.31', 'But Paul said to the centurion and the soldiers, “Unless these men remain with the ship, you cannot be saved.”'),
('ACT', 27, 32, 'ACT.27.32', 'So the soldiers cut the ropes to the lifeboat and set it adrift.'),
('ACT', 27, 33, 'ACT.27.33', 'Right up to daybreak, Paul kept urging them all to eat: “Today is your fourteenth day in constant suspense, without taking any food.'),
('ACT', 27, 34, 'ACT.27.34', 'So for your own preservation, I urge you to eat something, because not a single hair of your head will be lost.”'),
('ACT', 27, 35, 'ACT.27.35', 'After he had said this, Paul took bread and gave thanks to God in front of them all. Then he broke it and began to eat.'),
('ACT', 27, 36, 'ACT.27.36', 'They were all encouraged and took some food themselves.'),
('ACT', 27, 37, 'ACT.27.37', 'In all, there were 276 of us on board.'),
('ACT', 27, 38, 'ACT.27.38', 'After the men had eaten their fill, they lightened the ship by throwing the grain into the sea.'),
('ACT', 27, 39, 'ACT.27.39', 'When daylight came, they did not recognize the land, but they sighted a bay with a sandy beach, where they decided to run the ship aground if they could.'),
('ACT', 27, 40, 'ACT.27.40', 'Cutting away the anchors, they left them in the sea as they loosened the ropes that held the rudders. Then they hoisted the foresail to the wind and made for the beach.'),
('ACT', 27, 41, 'ACT.27.41', 'But the ship struck a sandbar and ran aground. The bow stuck fast and would not move, and the stern was being broken up by the pounding of the waves.'),
('ACT', 27, 42, 'ACT.27.42', 'The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners so none of them could swim to freedom.'),
('ACT', 27, 43, 'ACT.27.43', 'But the centurion, wanting to spare Paul’s life, thwarted their plan. He commanded those who could swim to jump overboard first and get to land.'),
('ACT', 27, 44, 'ACT.27.44', 'The rest were to follow on planks and various parts of the ship. In this way everyone was brought safely to land.'),
('ACT', 28, 1, 'ACT.28.1', 'Once we were safely ashore, we learned that the island was called Malta.'),
('ACT', 28, 2, 'ACT.28.2', 'The islanders showed us extraordinary kindness. They kindled a fire and welcomed all of us because it was raining and cold.'),
('ACT', 28, 3, 'ACT.28.3', 'Paul gathered a bundle of sticks, and as he laid them on the fire, a viper, driven out by the heat, fastened itself to his hand.'),
('ACT', 28, 4, 'ACT.28.4', 'When the islanders saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, “Surely this man is a murderer. Although he was saved from the sea, Justice has not allowed him to live.”'),
('ACT', 28, 5, 'ACT.28.5', 'But Paul shook the creature off into the fire and suffered no ill effects.'),
('ACT', 28, 6, 'ACT.28.6', 'The islanders were expecting him to swell up or suddenly drop dead. But after waiting a long time and seeing nothing unusual happen to him, they changed their minds and said he was a god.'),
('ACT', 28, 7, 'ACT.28.7', 'Nearby stood an estate belonging to Publius, the chief official of the island. He welcomed us and entertained us hospitably for three days.'),
('ACT', 28, 8, 'ACT.28.8', 'The father of Publius was sick in bed, suffering from fever and dysentery. Paul went in to see him, and after praying and placing his hands on him, he healed the man.'),
('ACT', 28, 9, 'ACT.28.9', 'After this had happened, the rest of the sick on the island came and were cured as well.'),
('ACT', 28, 10, 'ACT.28.10', 'The islanders honored us in many ways and supplied our needs when we were ready to sail.'),
('ACT', 28, 11, 'ACT.28.11', 'After three months we set sail in an Alexandrian ship that had wintered in the island. It had the Twin Brothers as a figurehead.'),
('ACT', 28, 12, 'ACT.28.12', 'Putting in at Syracuse, we stayed there three days.'),
('ACT', 28, 13, 'ACT.28.13', 'From there we weighed anchor and came to Rhegium. After one day, a south wind came up, and on the second day we arrived at Puteoli.'),
('ACT', 28, 14, 'ACT.28.14', 'There we found some brothers who invited us to spend the week with them. And so we came to Rome.'),
('ACT', 28, 15, 'ACT.28.15', 'The brothers there had heard about us and traveled as far as the Forum of Appius and the Three Taverns to meet us. When Paul saw them, he was encouraged and gave thanks to God.'),
('ACT', 28, 16, 'ACT.28.16', 'When we arrived in Rome, Paul was permitted to stay by himself, with a soldier to guard him.'),
('ACT', 28, 17, 'ACT.28.17', 'After three days, he called together the leaders of the Jews. When they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, although I have done nothing against our people or the customs of our fathers, I was taken prisoner in Jerusalem and handed over to the Romans.'),
('ACT', 28, 18, 'ACT.28.18', 'They examined me and wanted to release me, because there was no basis for a death sentence against me.'),
('ACT', 28, 19, 'ACT.28.19', 'But when the Jews objected, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, even though I have no charge to bring against my nation.'),
('ACT', 28, 20, 'ACT.28.20', 'So for this reason I have called to see you and speak with you. It is because of the hope of Israel that I am bound with this chain.”'),
('ACT', 28, 21, 'ACT.28.21', 'The leaders replied, “We have not received any letters about you from Judea, nor have any of the brothers from there reported or even mentioned anything bad about you.'),
('ACT', 28, 22, 'ACT.28.22', 'But we consider your views worth hearing, because we know that people everywhere are speaking against this sect.”'),
('ACT', 28, 23, 'ACT.28.23', 'So they set a day to meet with Paul, and many people came to the place he was staying. He expounded to them from morning to evening, testifying about the kingdom of God and persuading them about Jesus from the Law of Moses and the Prophets.'),
('ACT', 28, 24, 'ACT.28.24', 'Some of them were convinced by what he said, but others refused to believe.'),
('ACT', 28, 25, 'ACT.28.25', 'They disagreed among themselves and began to leave after Paul had made this final statement: “The Holy Spirit was right when He spoke to your fathers through Isaiah the prophet:'),
('ACT', 28, 26, 'ACT.28.26', '‘Go to this people and say, “You will be ever hearing but never understanding; you will be ever seeing but never perceiving.”'),
('ACT', 28, 27, 'ACT.28.27', 'For this people’s heart has grown callous; they hardly hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.’'),
('ACT', 28, 28, 'ACT.28.28', 'Be advised, therefore, that God’s salvation has been sent to the Gentiles, and they will listen!”'),
('ACT', 28, 30, 'ACT.28.30', 'Paul stayed there two full years in his own rented house, welcoming all who came to visit him.'),
('ACT', 28, 31, 'ACT.28.31', 'Boldly and freely he proclaimed the kingdom of God and taught about the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('ROM', 1, 1, 'ROM.1.1', 'Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus, called to be an apostle, and set apart for the gospel of God—'),
('ROM', 1, 2, 'ROM.1.2', 'the gospel He promised beforehand through His prophets in the Holy Scriptures,'),
('ROM', 1, 3, 'ROM.1.3', 'regarding His Son, who was a descendant of David according to the flesh,'),
('ROM', 1, 4, 'ROM.1.4', 'and who through the Spirit of holiness was declared with power to be the Son of God by His resurrection from the dead: Jesus Christ our Lord.'),
('ROM', 1, 5, 'ROM.1.5', 'Through Him and on behalf of His name, we received grace and apostleship to call all those among the Gentiles to the obedience that comes from faith.'),
('ROM', 1, 6, 'ROM.1.6', 'And you also are among those who are called to belong to Jesus Christ.'),
('ROM', 1, 7, 'ROM.1.7', 'To all in Rome who are loved by God and called to be saints: Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('ROM', 1, 8, 'ROM.1.8', 'First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for all of you, because your faith is being proclaimed all over the world.'),
('ROM', 1, 9, 'ROM.1.9', 'God, whom I serve with my spirit in preaching the gospel of His Son, is my witness how constantly I remember you'),
('ROM', 1, 10, 'ROM.1.10', 'in my prayers at all times, asking that now at last by God’s will I may succeed in coming to you.'),
('ROM', 1, 11, 'ROM.1.11', 'For I long to see you so that I may impart to you some spiritual gift to strengthen you,'),
('ROM', 1, 12, 'ROM.1.12', 'that is, that you and I may be mutually encouraged by each other’s faith.'),
('ROM', 1, 13, 'ROM.1.13', 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, how often I planned to come to you (but have been prevented from visiting until now), in order that I might have a harvest among you, just as I have had among the other Gentiles.'),
('ROM', 1, 14, 'ROM.1.14', 'I am obligated both to Greeks and non-Greeks, both to the wise and the foolish.'),
('ROM', 1, 15, 'ROM.1.15', 'That is why I am so eager to preach the gospel also to you who are in Rome.'),
('ROM', 1, 16, 'ROM.1.16', 'I am not ashamed of the gospel, because it is the power of God for salvation to everyone who believes, first to the Jew, then to the Greek.'),
('ROM', 1, 17, 'ROM.1.17', 'For the gospel reveals the righteousness of God that comes by faith from start to finish, just as it is written: “The righteous will live by faith.”'),
('ROM', 1, 18, 'ROM.1.18', 'The wrath of God is being revealed from heaven against all the godlessness and wickedness of men who suppress the truth by their wickedness.'),
('ROM', 1, 19, 'ROM.1.19', 'For what may be known about God is plain to them, because God has made it plain to them.'),
('ROM', 1, 20, 'ROM.1.20', 'For since the creation of the world God’s invisible qualities, His eternal power and divine nature, have been clearly seen, being understood from His workmanship, so that men are without excuse.'),
('ROM', 1, 21, 'ROM.1.21', 'For although they knew God, they neither glorified Him as God nor gave thanks to Him, but they became futile in their thinking and darkened in their foolish hearts.'),
('ROM', 1, 22, 'ROM.1.22', 'Although they claimed to be wise, they became fools,'),
('ROM', 1, 23, 'ROM.1.23', 'and exchanged the glory of the immortal God for images of mortal man and birds and animals and reptiles.'),
('ROM', 1, 24, 'ROM.1.24', 'Therefore God gave them over in the desires of their hearts to impurity for the dishonoring of their bodies with one another.'),
('ROM', 1, 25, 'ROM.1.25', 'They exchanged the truth of God for a lie, and worshiped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is forever worthy of praise! Amen.'),
('ROM', 1, 26, 'ROM.1.26', 'For this reason God gave them over to dishonorable passions. Even their women exchanged natural relations for unnatural ones.'),
('ROM', 1, 27, 'ROM.1.27', 'Likewise, the men abandoned natural relations with women and burned with lust for one another. Men committed indecent acts with other men and received in themselves the due penalty for their error.'),
('ROM', 1, 28, 'ROM.1.28', 'Furthermore, since they did not see fit to acknowledge God, He gave them up to a depraved mind, to do what ought not to be done.'),
('ROM', 1, 29, 'ROM.1.29', 'They have become filled with every kind of wickedness, evil, greed, and depravity. They are full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, and malice. They are gossips,'),
('ROM', 1, 30, 'ROM.1.30', 'slanderers, God-haters, insolent, arrogant, and boastful. They invent new forms of evil; they disobey their parents.'),
('ROM', 1, 31, 'ROM.1.31', 'They are senseless, faithless, heartless, merciless.'),
('ROM', 1, 32, 'ROM.1.32', 'Although they know God’s righteous decree that those who do such things are worthy of death, they not only continue to do these things, but also approve of those who practice them.'),
('ROM', 2, 1, 'ROM.2.1', 'You, therefore, have no excuse, you who pass judgment on another. For on whatever grounds you judge the other, you are condemning yourself, because you who pass judgment do the same things.'),
('ROM', 2, 2, 'ROM.2.2', 'And we know that God’s judgment against those who do such things is based on truth.'),
('ROM', 2, 3, 'ROM.2.3', 'So when you, O man, pass judgment on others, yet do the same things, do you think you will escape God’s judgment?'),
('ROM', 2, 4, 'ROM.2.4', 'Or do you disregard the riches of His kindness, tolerance, and patience, not realizing that God’s kindness leads you to repentance?'),
('ROM', 2, 5, 'ROM.2.5', 'But because of your hard and unrepentant heart, you are storing up wrath against yourself for the day of wrath, when God’s righteous judgment will be revealed.'),
('ROM', 2, 6, 'ROM.2.6', 'God “will repay each one according to his deeds.”'),
('ROM', 2, 7, 'ROM.2.7', 'To those who by perseverance in doing good seek glory, honor, and immortality, He will give eternal life.'),
('ROM', 2, 8, 'ROM.2.8', 'But for those who are self-seeking and who reject the truth and follow wickedness, there will be wrath and anger.'),
('ROM', 2, 9, 'ROM.2.9', 'There will be trouble and distress for every human being who does evil, first for the Jew, then for the Greek;'),
('ROM', 2, 10, 'ROM.2.10', 'but glory, honor, and peace for everyone who does good, first for the Jew, then for the Greek.'),
('ROM', 2, 11, 'ROM.2.11', 'For God does not show favoritism.'),
('ROM', 2, 12, 'ROM.2.12', 'All who sin apart from the law will also perish apart from the law, and all who sin under the law will be judged by the law.'),
('ROM', 2, 13, 'ROM.2.13', 'For it is not the hearers of the law who are righteous before God, but it is the doers of the law who will be declared righteous.'),
('ROM', 2, 14, 'ROM.2.14', 'Indeed, when Gentiles, who do not have the law, do by nature what the law requires, they are a law to themselves, even though they do not have the law.'),
('ROM', 2, 15, 'ROM.2.15', 'So they show that the work of the law is written on their hearts, their consciences also bearing witness, and their thoughts either accusing or defending them'),
('ROM', 2, 16, 'ROM.2.16', 'on the day when God will judge men’s secrets through Christ Jesus, as proclaimed by my gospel.'),
('ROM', 2, 17, 'ROM.2.17', 'Now you, if you call yourself a Jew; if you rely on the law and boast in God;'),
('ROM', 2, 18, 'ROM.2.18', 'if you know His will and approve of what is superior because you are instructed by the law;'),
('ROM', 2, 19, 'ROM.2.19', 'if you are convinced that you are a guide for the blind, a light for those in darkness,'),
('ROM', 2, 20, 'ROM.2.20', 'an instructor of the foolish, a teacher of infants, because you have in the law the embodiment of knowledge and truth—'),
('ROM', 2, 21, 'ROM.2.21', 'you, then, who teach others, do you not teach yourself? You who preach against stealing, do you steal?'),
('ROM', 2, 22, 'ROM.2.22', 'You who forbid adultery, do you commit adultery? You who abhor idols, do you rob temples?'),
('ROM', 2, 23, 'ROM.2.23', 'You who boast in the law, do you dishonor God by breaking the law?'),
('ROM', 2, 24, 'ROM.2.24', 'As it is written: “God’s name is blasphemed among the Gentiles because of you.”'),
('ROM', 2, 25, 'ROM.2.25', 'Circumcision has value if you observe the law, but if you break the law, your circumcision has become uncircumcision.'),
('ROM', 2, 26, 'ROM.2.26', 'If a man who is not circumcised keeps the requirements of the law, will not his uncircumcision be regarded as circumcision?'),
('ROM', 2, 27, 'ROM.2.27', 'The one who is physically uncircumcised yet keeps the law will condemn you who, even though you have the written code and circumcision, are a lawbreaker.'),
('ROM', 2, 28, 'ROM.2.28', 'A man is not a Jew because he is one outwardly, nor is circumcision only outward and physical.'),
('ROM', 2, 29, 'ROM.2.29', 'No, a man is a Jew because he is one inwardly, and circumcision is a matter of the heart, by the Spirit, not by the written code. Such a man’s praise does not come from men, but from God.'),
('ROM', 3, 1, 'ROM.3.1', 'What, then, is the advantage of being a Jew? Or what is the value of circumcision?'),
('ROM', 3, 2, 'ROM.3.2', 'Much in every way. First of all, they have been entrusted with the very words of God.'),
('ROM', 3, 3, 'ROM.3.3', 'What if some did not have faith? Will their lack of faith nullify God’s faithfulness?'),
('ROM', 3, 4, 'ROM.3.4', 'Certainly not! Let God be true and every man a liar. As it is written: “So that You may be proved right when You speak and victorious when You judge.”'),
('ROM', 3, 5, 'ROM.3.5', 'But if our unrighteousness highlights the righteousness of God, what shall we say? That God is unjust to inflict His wrath on us? I am speaking in human terms.'),
('ROM', 3, 6, 'ROM.3.6', 'Certainly not! In that case, how could God judge the world?'),
('ROM', 3, 7, 'ROM.3.7', 'However, if my falsehood accentuates God’s truthfulness, to the increase of His glory, why am I still condemned as a sinner?'),
('ROM', 3, 8, 'ROM.3.8', 'Why not say, as some slanderously claim that we say, “Let us do evil that good may result”? Their condemnation is deserved!'),
('ROM', 3, 9, 'ROM.3.9', 'What then? Are we any better? Not at all. For we have already made the charge that Jews and Greeks alike are all under sin.'),
('ROM', 3, 10, 'ROM.3.10', 'As it is written: “There is no one righteous, not even one.'),
('ROM', 3, 11, 'ROM.3.11', 'There is no one who understands, no one who seeks God.'),
('ROM', 3, 12, 'ROM.3.12', 'All have turned away, they have together become worthless; there is no one who does good, not even one.”'),
('ROM', 3, 13, 'ROM.3.13', '“Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.” “The venom of vipers is on their lips.”'),
('ROM', 3, 14, 'ROM.3.14', '“Their mouths are full of cursing and bitterness.”'),
('ROM', 3, 15, 'ROM.3.15', '“Their feet are swift to shed blood;'),
('ROM', 3, 16, 'ROM.3.16', 'ruin and misery lie in their wake,'),
('ROM', 3, 17, 'ROM.3.17', 'and the way of peace they have not known.”'),
('ROM', 3, 18, 'ROM.3.18', '“There is no fear of God before their eyes.”'),
('ROM', 3, 19, 'ROM.3.19', 'Now we know that whatever the law says, it says to those who are under the law, so that every mouth may be silenced and the whole world held accountable to God.'),
('ROM', 3, 20, 'ROM.3.20', 'Therefore no one will be justified in His sight by works of the law. For the law merely brings awareness of sin.'),
('ROM', 3, 21, 'ROM.3.21', 'But now, apart from the law, the righteousness of God has been revealed, as attested by the Law and the Prophets.'),
('ROM', 3, 22, 'ROM.3.22', 'And this righteousness from God comes through faith in Jesus Christ to all who believe. There is no distinction,'),
('ROM', 3, 23, 'ROM.3.23', 'for all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God,'),
('ROM', 3, 24, 'ROM.3.24', 'and are justified freely by His grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus.'),
('ROM', 3, 25, 'ROM.3.25', 'God presented Him as an atoning sacrifice in His blood through faith, in order to demonstrate His righteousness, because in His forbearance He had passed over the sins committed beforehand.'),
('ROM', 3, 26, 'ROM.3.26', 'He did this to demonstrate His righteousness at the present time, so as to be just and to justify the one who has faith in Jesus.'),
('ROM', 3, 27, 'ROM.3.27', 'Where, then, is boasting? It is excluded. On what principle? On that of works? No, but on that of faith.'),
('ROM', 3, 28, 'ROM.3.28', 'For we maintain that a man is justified by faith apart from works of the law.'),
('ROM', 3, 29, 'ROM.3.29', 'Is God the God of Jews only? Is He not the God of Gentiles too? Yes, of Gentiles too,'),
('ROM', 3, 30, 'ROM.3.30', 'since there is only one God, who will justify the circumcised by faith and the uncircumcised through that same faith.'),
('ROM', 3, 31, 'ROM.3.31', 'Do we, then, nullify the law by this faith? Certainly not! Instead, we uphold the law.'),
('ROM', 4, 1, 'ROM.4.1', 'What then shall we say that Abraham, our forefather according to the flesh, has discovered?'),
('ROM', 4, 2, 'ROM.4.2', 'If Abraham was indeed justified by works, he had something to boast about, but not before God.'),
('ROM', 4, 3, 'ROM.4.3', 'For what does the Scripture say? “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
('ROM', 4, 4, 'ROM.4.4', 'Now the wages of the worker are not credited as a gift, but as an obligation.'),
('ROM', 4, 5, 'ROM.4.5', 'However, to the one who does not work, but believes in Him who justifies the ungodly, his faith is credited as righteousness.'),
('ROM', 4, 6, 'ROM.4.6', 'And David speaks likewise of the blessedness of the man to whom God credits righteousness apart from works:'),
('ROM', 4, 7, 'ROM.4.7', '“Blessed are they whose lawless acts are forgiven, whose sins are covered.'),
('ROM', 4, 8, 'ROM.4.8', 'Blessed is the man whose sin the Lord will never count against him.”'),
('ROM', 4, 9, 'ROM.4.9', 'Is this blessing only on the circumcised, or also on the uncircumcised? We have been saying that Abraham’s faith was credited to him as righteousness.'),
('ROM', 4, 10, 'ROM.4.10', 'In what context was it credited? Was it after his circumcision, or before? It was not after, but before.'),
('ROM', 4, 11, 'ROM.4.11', 'And he received the sign of circumcision as a seal of the righteousness that he had by faith while he was still uncircumcised. So then, he is the father of all who believe but are not circumcised, in order that righteousness might be credited to them.'),
('ROM', 4, 12, 'ROM.4.12', 'And he is also the father of the circumcised who not only are circumcised, but who also walk in the footsteps of the faith that our father Abraham had before he was circumcised.'),
('ROM', 4, 13, 'ROM.4.13', 'For the promise to Abraham and his offspring that he would be heir of the world was not given through the law, but through the righteousness that comes by faith.'),
('ROM', 4, 14, 'ROM.4.14', 'For if those who live by the law are heirs, faith is useless and the promise is worthless,'),
('ROM', 4, 15, 'ROM.4.15', 'because the law brings wrath. And where there is no law, there is no transgression.'),
('ROM', 4, 16, 'ROM.4.16', 'Therefore, the promise comes by faith, so that it may rest on grace and may be guaranteed to all Abraham’s offspring—not only to those who are of the law, but also to those who are of the faith of Abraham. He is the father of us all.'),
('ROM', 4, 17, 'ROM.4.17', 'As it is written: “I have made you a father of many nations.” He is our father in the presence of God, in whom he believed, the God who gives life to the dead and calls into being what does not yet exist.'),
('ROM', 4, 18, 'ROM.4.18', 'Against all hope, Abraham in hope believed and so became the father of many nations, just as he had been told, “So shall your offspring be.”'),
('ROM', 4, 19, 'ROM.4.19', 'Without weakening in his faith, he acknowledged the decrepitness of his body (since he was about a hundred years old) and the lifelessness of Sarah’s womb.'),
('ROM', 4, 20, 'ROM.4.20', 'Yet he did not waver through disbelief in the promise of God, but was strengthened in his faith and gave glory to God,'),
('ROM', 4, 21, 'ROM.4.21', 'being fully persuaded that God was able to do what He had promised.'),
('ROM', 4, 22, 'ROM.4.22', 'This is why “it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
('ROM', 4, 23, 'ROM.4.23', 'Now the words “it was credited to him” were written not only for Abraham,'),
('ROM', 4, 24, 'ROM.4.24', 'but also for us, to whom righteousness will be credited—for us who believe in Him who raised Jesus our Lord from the dead.'),
('ROM', 4, 25, 'ROM.4.25', 'He was delivered over to death for our trespasses and was raised to life for our justification.'),
('ROM', 5, 1, 'ROM.5.1', 'Therefore, since we have been justified through faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ,'),
('ROM', 5, 2, 'ROM.5.2', 'through whom we have gained access by faith into this grace in which we stand. And we rejoice in the hope of the glory of God.'),
('ROM', 5, 3, 'ROM.5.3', 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in our sufferings, because we know that suffering produces perseverance;'),
('ROM', 5, 4, 'ROM.5.4', 'perseverance, character; and character, hope.'),
('ROM', 5, 5, 'ROM.5.5', 'And hope does not disappoint us, because God has poured out His love into our hearts through the Holy Spirit, whom He has given us.'),
('ROM', 5, 6, 'ROM.5.6', 'For at just the right time, while we were still powerless, Christ died for the ungodly.'),
('ROM', 5, 7, 'ROM.5.7', 'Very rarely will anyone die for a righteous man, though for a good man someone might possibly dare to die.'),
('ROM', 5, 8, 'ROM.5.8', 'But God proves His love for us in this: While we were still sinners, Christ died for us.'),
('ROM', 5, 9, 'ROM.5.9', 'Therefore, since we have now been justified by His blood, how much more shall we be saved from wrath through Him!'),
('ROM', 5, 10, 'ROM.5.10', 'For if, when we were enemies of God, we were reconciled to Him through the death of His Son, how much more, having been reconciled, shall we be saved through His life!'),
('ROM', 5, 11, 'ROM.5.11', 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received reconciliation.'),
('ROM', 5, 12, 'ROM.5.12', 'Therefore, just as sin entered the world through one man, and death through sin, so also death was passed on to all men, because all sinned.'),
('ROM', 5, 13, 'ROM.5.13', 'For sin was in the world before the law was given; but sin is not taken into account when there is no law.'),
('ROM', 5, 14, 'ROM.5.14', 'Nevertheless, death reigned from Adam until Moses, even over those who did not sin in the way that Adam transgressed. He is a pattern of the One to come.'),
('ROM', 5, 15, 'ROM.5.15', 'But the gift is not like the trespass. For if the many died by the trespass of the one man, how much more did God’s grace and the gift that came by the grace of the one man, Jesus Christ, abound to the many!'),
('ROM', 5, 16, 'ROM.5.16', 'Again, the gift is not like the result of the one man’s sin: The judgment that followed one sin brought condemnation, but the gift that followed many trespasses brought justification.'),
('ROM', 5, 17, 'ROM.5.17', 'For if, by the trespass of the one man, death reigned through that one man, how much more will those who receive the abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness reign in life through the one man, Jesus Christ!'),
('ROM', 5, 18, 'ROM.5.18', 'So then, just as one trespass brought condemnation for all men, so also one act of righteousness brought justification and life for all men.'),
('ROM', 5, 19, 'ROM.5.19', 'For just as through the disobedience of the one man the many were made sinners, so also through the obedience of the one man the many will be made righteous.'),
('ROM', 5, 20, 'ROM.5.20', 'The law came in so that the trespass would increase; but where sin increased, grace increased all the more,'),
('ROM', 5, 21, 'ROM.5.21', 'so that, just as sin reigned in death, so also grace might reign through righteousness to bring eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.'),
('ROM', 6, 1, 'ROM.6.1', 'What then shall we say? Shall we continue in sin so that grace may increase?'),
('ROM', 6, 2, 'ROM.6.2', 'Certainly not! How can we who died to sin live in it any longer?'),
('ROM', 6, 3, 'ROM.6.3', 'Or aren’t you aware that all of us who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into His death?'),
('ROM', 6, 4, 'ROM.6.4', 'We were therefore buried with Him through baptism into death, in order that, just as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, we too may walk in newness of life.'),
('ROM', 6, 5, 'ROM.6.5', 'For if we have been united with Him like this in His death, we will certainly also be united with Him in His resurrection.'),
('ROM', 6, 6, 'ROM.6.6', 'We know that our old self was crucified with Him so that the body of sin might be rendered powerless, that we should no longer be slaves to sin.'),
('ROM', 6, 7, 'ROM.6.7', 'For anyone who has died has been freed from sin.'),
('ROM', 6, 8, 'ROM.6.8', 'Now if we died with Christ, we believe that we will also live with Him.'),
('ROM', 6, 9, 'ROM.6.9', 'For we know that since Christ was raised from the dead, He cannot die again; death no longer has dominion over Him.'),
('ROM', 6, 10, 'ROM.6.10', 'The death He died, He died to sin once for all; but the life He lives, He lives to God.'),
('ROM', 6, 11, 'ROM.6.11', 'So you too must count yourselves dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus.'),
('ROM', 6, 12, 'ROM.6.12', 'Therefore do not let sin reign in your mortal body so that you obey its desires.'),
('ROM', 6, 13, 'ROM.6.13', 'Do not present the parts of your body to sin as instruments of wickedness, but present yourselves to God as those who have been brought from death to life; and present the parts of your body to Him as instruments of righteousness.'),
('ROM', 6, 14, 'ROM.6.14', 'For sin shall not be your master, because you are not under law, but under grace.'),
('ROM', 6, 15, 'ROM.6.15', 'What then? Shall we sin because we are not under law, but under grace? Certainly not!'),
('ROM', 6, 16, 'ROM.6.16', 'Do you not know that when you offer yourselves as obedient slaves, you are slaves to the one you obey, whether you are slaves to sin leading to death, or to obedience leading to righteousness?'),
('ROM', 6, 17, 'ROM.6.17', 'But thanks be to God that, though you once were slaves to sin, you wholeheartedly obeyed the form of teaching to which you were committed.'),
('ROM', 6, 18, 'ROM.6.18', 'You have been set free from sin and have become slaves to righteousness.'),
('ROM', 6, 19, 'ROM.6.19', 'I am speaking in human terms because of the weakness of your flesh. Just as you used to offer the parts of your body in slavery to impurity and to escalating wickedness, so now offer them in slavery to righteousness leading to holiness.'),
('ROM', 6, 20, 'ROM.6.20', 'For when you were slaves to sin, you were free of obligation to righteousness.'),
('ROM', 6, 21, 'ROM.6.21', 'What fruit did you reap at that time from the things of which you are now ashamed? The outcome of those things is death.'),
('ROM', 6, 22, 'ROM.6.22', 'But now that you have been set free from sin and have become slaves to God, the fruit you reap leads to holiness, and the outcome is eternal life.'),
('ROM', 6, 23, 'ROM.6.23', 'For the wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('ROM', 7, 1, 'ROM.7.1', 'Do you not know, brothers (for I am speaking to those who know the law), that the law has authority over a man only as long as he lives?'),
('ROM', 7, 2, 'ROM.7.2', 'For instance, a married woman is bound by law to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is released from the law of marriage.'),
('ROM', 7, 3, 'ROM.7.3', 'So then, if she is joined to another man while her husband is still alive, she is called an adulteress; but if her husband dies, she is free from that law and is not an adulteress if she marries another man.'),
('ROM', 7, 4, 'ROM.7.4', 'Therefore, my brothers, you also died to the law through the body of Christ, that you might belong to another, to Him who was raised from the dead, in order that we might bear fruit to God.'),
('ROM', 7, 5, 'ROM.7.5', 'For when we lived according to the flesh, the sinful passions aroused by the law were at work in our bodies, bearing fruit for death.'),
('ROM', 7, 6, 'ROM.7.6', 'But now, having died to what bound us, we have been released from the law, so that we serve in the new way of the Spirit, and not in the old way of the written code.'),
('ROM', 7, 7, 'ROM.7.7', 'What then shall we say? Is the law sin? Certainly not! Indeed, I would not have been mindful of sin if not for the law. For I would not have been aware of coveting if the law had not said, “Do not covet.”'),
('ROM', 7, 8, 'ROM.7.8', 'But sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, produced in me every kind of covetous desire. For apart from the law, sin is dead.'),
('ROM', 7, 9, 'ROM.7.9', 'Once I was alive apart from the law; but when the commandment came, sin sprang to life and I died.'),
('ROM', 7, 10, 'ROM.7.10', 'So I discovered that the very commandment that was meant to bring life actually brought death.'),
('ROM', 7, 11, 'ROM.7.11', 'For sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, deceived me and through the commandment put me to death.'),
('ROM', 7, 12, 'ROM.7.12', 'So then, the law is holy, and the commandment is holy, righteous, and good.'),
('ROM', 7, 13, 'ROM.7.13', 'Did that which is good, then, become death to me? Certainly not! But in order that sin might be exposed as sin, it produced death in me through what was good, so that through the commandment sin might become utterly sinful.'),
('ROM', 7, 14, 'ROM.7.14', 'We know that the law is spiritual; but I am unspiritual, sold as a slave to sin.'),
('ROM', 7, 15, 'ROM.7.15', 'I do not understand what I do. For what I want to do, I do not do. But what I hate, I do.'),
('ROM', 7, 16, 'ROM.7.16', 'And if I do what I do not want to do, I admit that the law is good.'),
('ROM', 7, 17, 'ROM.7.17', 'In that case, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.'),
('ROM', 7, 18, 'ROM.7.18', 'I know that nothing good lives in me, that is, in my flesh; for I have the desire to do what is good, but I cannot carry it out.'),
('ROM', 7, 19, 'ROM.7.19', 'For I do not do the good I want to do. Instead, I keep on doing the evil I do not want to do.'),
('ROM', 7, 20, 'ROM.7.20', 'And if I do what I do not want, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.'),
('ROM', 7, 21, 'ROM.7.21', 'So this is the principle I have discovered: When I want to do good, evil is right there with me.'),
('ROM', 7, 22, 'ROM.7.22', 'For in my inner being I delight in God’s law.'),
('ROM', 7, 23, 'ROM.7.23', 'But I see another law at work in my body, warring against the law of my mind and holding me captive to the law of sin that dwells within me.'),
('ROM', 7, 24, 'ROM.7.24', 'What a wretched man I am! Who will rescue me from this body of death?'),
('ROM', 7, 25, 'ROM.7.25', 'Thanks be to God, through Jesus Christ our Lord! So then, with my mind I serve the law of God, but with my flesh I serve the law of sin.'),
('ROM', 8, 1, 'ROM.8.1', 'Therefore, there is now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus.'),
('ROM', 8, 2, 'ROM.8.2', 'For in Christ Jesus the law of the Spirit of life set you free from the law of sin and death.'),
('ROM', 8, 3, 'ROM.8.3', 'For what the law was powerless to do in that it was weakened by the flesh, God did by sending His own Son in the likeness of sinful man, as an offering for sin. He thus condemned sin in the flesh,'),
('ROM', 8, 4, 'ROM.8.4', 'so that the righteous standard of the law might be fulfilled in us, who do not walk according to the flesh but according to the Spirit.'),
('ROM', 8, 5, 'ROM.8.5', 'Those who live according to the flesh set their minds on the things of the flesh; but those who live according to the Spirit set their minds on the things of the Spirit.'),
('ROM', 8, 6, 'ROM.8.6', 'The mind of the flesh is death, but the mind of the Spirit is life and peace,'),
('ROM', 8, 7, 'ROM.8.7', 'because the mind of the flesh is hostile to God: It does not submit to God’s law, nor can it do so.'),
('ROM', 8, 8, 'ROM.8.8', 'Those controlled by the flesh cannot please God.'),
('ROM', 8, 9, 'ROM.8.9', 'You, however, are controlled not by the flesh, but by the Spirit, if the Spirit of God lives in you. And if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ, he does not belong to Christ.'),
('ROM', 8, 10, 'ROM.8.10', 'But if Christ is in you, your body is dead because of sin, yet your spirit is alive because of righteousness.'),
('ROM', 8, 11, 'ROM.8.11', 'And if the Spirit of Him who raised Jesus from the dead is living in you, He who raised Christ Jesus from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through His Spirit, who lives in you.'),
('ROM', 8, 12, 'ROM.8.12', 'Therefore, brothers, we have an obligation, but it is not to the flesh, to live according to it.'),
('ROM', 8, 13, 'ROM.8.13', 'For if you live according to the flesh, you will die; but if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body, you will live.'),
('ROM', 8, 14, 'ROM.8.14', 'For all who are led by the Spirit of God are sons of God.'),
('ROM', 8, 15, 'ROM.8.15', 'For you did not receive a spirit of slavery that returns you to fear, but you received the Spirit of adoption to sonship, by whom we cry, “Abba! Father!”'),
('ROM', 8, 16, 'ROM.8.16', 'The Spirit Himself testifies with our spirit that we are God’s children.'),
('ROM', 8, 17, 'ROM.8.17', 'And if we are children, then we are heirs: heirs of God and co-heirs with Christ—if indeed we suffer with Him, so that we may also be glorified with Him.'),
('ROM', 8, 18, 'ROM.8.18', 'I consider that our present sufferings are not comparable to the glory that will be revealed in us.'),
('ROM', 8, 19, 'ROM.8.19', 'The creation waits in eager expectation for the revelation of the sons of God.'),
('ROM', 8, 20, 'ROM.8.20', 'For the creation was subjected to futility, not by its own will, but because of the One who subjected it, in hope'),
('ROM', 8, 21, 'ROM.8.21', 'that the creation itself will be set free from its bondage to decay and brought into the glorious freedom of the children of God.'),
('ROM', 8, 22, 'ROM.8.22', 'We know that the whole creation has been groaning together in the pains of childbirth until the present time.'),
('ROM', 8, 23, 'ROM.8.23', 'Not only that, but we ourselves, who have the firstfruits of the Spirit, groan inwardly as we wait eagerly for our adoption as sons, the redemption of our bodies.'),
('ROM', 8, 24, 'ROM.8.24', 'For in this hope we were saved; but hope that is seen is no hope at all. Who hopes for what he can already see?'),
('ROM', 8, 25, 'ROM.8.25', 'But if we hope for what we do not yet see, we wait for it patiently.'),
('ROM', 8, 26, 'ROM.8.26', 'In the same way, the Spirit helps us in our weakness. For we do not know how we ought to pray, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us with groans too deep for words.'),
('ROM', 8, 27, 'ROM.8.27', 'And He who searches our hearts knows the mind of the Spirit, because the Spirit intercedes for the saints according to the will of God.'),
('ROM', 8, 28, 'ROM.8.28', 'And we know that God works all things together for the good of those who love Him, who are called according to His purpose.'),
('ROM', 8, 29, 'ROM.8.29', 'For those God foreknew, He also predestined to be conformed to the image of His Son, so that He would be the firstborn among many brothers.'),
('ROM', 8, 30, 'ROM.8.30', 'And those He predestined, He also called; those He called, He also justified; those He justified, He also glorified.'),
('ROM', 8, 31, 'ROM.8.31', 'What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?'),
('ROM', 8, 32, 'ROM.8.32', 'He who did not spare His own Son but gave Him up for us all, how will He not also, along with Him, freely give us all things?'),
('ROM', 8, 33, 'ROM.8.33', 'Who will bring any charge against God’s elect? It is God who justifies.'),
('ROM', 8, 34, 'ROM.8.34', 'Who is there to condemn us? For Christ Jesus, who died, and more than that was raised to life, is at the right hand of God—and He is interceding for us.'),
('ROM', 8, 35, 'ROM.8.35', 'Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? Shall trouble or distress or persecution or famine or nakedness or danger or sword?'),
('ROM', 8, 36, 'ROM.8.36', 'As it is written: “For Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”'),
('ROM', 8, 37, 'ROM.8.37', 'No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through Him who loved us.'),
('ROM', 8, 38, 'ROM.8.38', 'For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor principalities, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,'),
('ROM', 8, 39, 'ROM.8.39', 'neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('ROM', 9, 1, 'ROM.9.1', 'I speak the truth in Christ; I am not lying, as confirmed by my conscience in the Holy Spirit.'),
('ROM', 9, 2, 'ROM.9.2', 'I have deep sorrow and unceasing anguish in my heart.'),
('ROM', 9, 3, 'ROM.9.3', 'For I could wish that I myself were cursed and cut off from Christ for the sake of my brothers, my own flesh and blood,'),
('ROM', 9, 4, 'ROM.9.4', 'the people of Israel. Theirs is the adoption as sons; theirs the divine glory and the covenants; theirs the giving of the law, the temple worship, and the promises.'),
('ROM', 9, 5, 'ROM.9.5', 'Theirs are the patriarchs, and from them proceeds the human descent of Christ, who is God over all, forever worthy of praise! Amen.'),
('ROM', 9, 6, 'ROM.9.6', 'It is not as though God’s word has failed. For not all who are descended from Israel are Israel.'),
('ROM', 9, 7, 'ROM.9.7', 'Nor because they are Abraham’s descendants are they all his children. On the contrary, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”'),
('ROM', 9, 8, 'ROM.9.8', 'So it is not the children of the flesh who are God’s children, but it is the children of the promise who are regarded as offspring.'),
('ROM', 9, 9, 'ROM.9.9', 'For this is what the promise stated: “At the appointed time I will return, and Sarah will have a son.”'),
('ROM', 9, 10, 'ROM.9.10', 'Not only that, but Rebecca’s children were conceived by one man, our father Isaac.'),
('ROM', 9, 11, 'ROM.9.11', 'Yet before the twins were born or had done anything good or bad, in order that God’s plan of election might stand,'),
('ROM', 9, 12, 'ROM.9.12', 'not by works but by Him who calls, she was told, “The older will serve the younger.”'),
('ROM', 9, 13, 'ROM.9.13', 'So it is written: “Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.”'),
('ROM', 9, 14, 'ROM.9.14', 'What then shall we say? Is God unjust? Certainly not!'),
('ROM', 9, 15, 'ROM.9.15', 'For He says to Moses: “I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.”'),
('ROM', 9, 16, 'ROM.9.16', 'So then, it does not depend on man’s desire or effort, but on God’s mercy.'),
('ROM', 9, 17, 'ROM.9.17', 'For the Scripture says to Pharaoh: “I raised you up for this very purpose, that I might display My power in you, and that My name might be proclaimed in all the earth.”'),
('ROM', 9, 18, 'ROM.9.18', 'Therefore God has mercy on whom He wants to have mercy, and He hardens whom He wants to harden.'),
('ROM', 9, 19, 'ROM.9.19', 'One of you will say to me, “Then why does God still find fault? For who can resist His will?”'),
('ROM', 9, 20, 'ROM.9.20', 'But who are you, O man, to talk back to God? Shall what is formed say to Him who formed it, “Why did You make me like this?”'),
('ROM', 9, 21, 'ROM.9.21', 'Does not the potter have the right to make from the same lump of clay one vessel for special occasions and another for common use?'),
('ROM', 9, 22, 'ROM.9.22', 'What if God, intending to show His wrath and make His power known, bore with great patience the vessels of His wrath, prepared for destruction?'),
('ROM', 9, 23, 'ROM.9.23', 'What if He did this to make the riches of His glory known to the vessels of His mercy, whom He prepared in advance for glory—'),
('ROM', 9, 24, 'ROM.9.24', 'including us, whom He has called not only from the Jews, but also from the Gentiles?'),
('ROM', 9, 25, 'ROM.9.25', 'As He says in Hosea: “I will call them ‘My People’ who are not My people, and I will call her ‘My Beloved’ who is not My beloved,”'),
('ROM', 9, 26, 'ROM.9.26', 'and, “It will happen that in the very place where it was said to them, ‘You are not My people,’ they will be called ‘sons of the living God.’”'),
('ROM', 9, 27, 'ROM.9.27', 'Isaiah cries out concerning Israel: “Though the number of the Israelites is like the sand of the sea, only the remnant will be saved.'),
('ROM', 9, 28, 'ROM.9.28', 'For the Lord will carry out His sentence on the earth thoroughly and decisively.”'),
('ROM', 9, 29, 'ROM.9.29', 'It is just as Isaiah foretold: “Unless the Lord of Hosts had left us descendants, we would have become like Sodom, we would have resembled Gomorrah.”'),
('ROM', 9, 30, 'ROM.9.30', 'What then will we say? That the Gentiles, who did not pursue righteousness, have obtained it, a righteousness that is by faith;'),
('ROM', 9, 31, 'ROM.9.31', 'but Israel, who pursued a law of righteousness, has not attained it.'),
('ROM', 9, 32, 'ROM.9.32', 'Why not? Because their pursuit was not by faith, but as if it were by works. They stumbled over the stumbling stone,'),
('ROM', 9, 33, 'ROM.9.33', 'as it is written: “See, I lay in Zion a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
('ROM', 10, 1, 'ROM.10.1', 'Brothers, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for the Israelites is for their salvation.'),
('ROM', 10, 2, 'ROM.10.2', 'For I testify about them that they are zealous for God, but not on the basis of knowledge.'),
('ROM', 10, 3, 'ROM.10.3', 'Because they were ignorant of God’s righteousness and sought to establish their own, they did not submit to God’s righteousness.'),
('ROM', 10, 4, 'ROM.10.4', 'For Christ is the end of the law, to bring righteousness to everyone who believes.'),
('ROM', 10, 5, 'ROM.10.5', 'For concerning the righteousness that is by the law, Moses writes: “The man who does these things will live by them.”'),
('ROM', 10, 6, 'ROM.10.6', 'But the righteousness that is by faith says: “Do not say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ (that is, to bring Christ down)'),
('ROM', 10, 7, 'ROM.10.7', 'or, ‘Who will descend into the Abyss?’ (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead).”'),
('ROM', 10, 8, 'ROM.10.8', 'But what does it say? “The word is near you; it is in your mouth and in your heart,” that is, the word of faith we are proclaiming:'),
('ROM', 10, 9, 'ROM.10.9', 'that if you confess with your mouth, “Jesus is Lord,” and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead, you will be saved.'),
('ROM', 10, 10, 'ROM.10.10', 'For with your heart you believe and are justified, and with your mouth you confess and are saved.'),
('ROM', 10, 11, 'ROM.10.11', 'It is just as the Scripture says: “Anyone who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
('ROM', 10, 12, 'ROM.10.12', 'For there is no difference between Jew and Greek: The same Lord is Lord of all, and gives richly to all who call on Him,'),
('ROM', 10, 13, 'ROM.10.13', 'for, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.”'),
('ROM', 10, 14, 'ROM.10.14', 'How then can they call on the One in whom they have not believed? And how can they believe in the One of whom they have not heard? And how can they hear without someone to preach?'),
('ROM', 10, 15, 'ROM.10.15', 'And how can they preach unless they are sent? As it is written: “How beautiful are the feet of those who bring good news!”'),
('ROM', 10, 16, 'ROM.10.16', 'But not all of them welcomed the good news. For Isaiah says, “Lord, who has believed our message?”'),
('ROM', 10, 17, 'ROM.10.17', 'Consequently, faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ.'),
('ROM', 10, 18, 'ROM.10.18', 'But I ask, did they not hear? Indeed they did: “Their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world.”'),
('ROM', 10, 19, 'ROM.10.19', 'I ask instead, did Israel not understand? First, Moses says: “I will make you jealous by those who are not a nation; I will make you angry by a nation without understanding.”'),
('ROM', 10, 20, 'ROM.10.20', 'And Isaiah boldly says: “I was found by those who did not seek Me; I revealed Myself to those who did not ask for Me.”'),
('ROM', 10, 21, 'ROM.10.21', 'But as for Israel he says: “All day long I have held out My hands to a disobedient and obstinate people.”'),
('ROM', 11, 1, 'ROM.11.1', 'I ask then, did God reject His people? Certainly not! I am an Israelite myself, a descendant of Abraham, from the tribe of Benjamin.'),
('ROM', 11, 2, 'ROM.11.2', 'God did not reject His people, whom He foreknew. Do you not know what the Scripture says about Elijah, how he appealed to God against Israel:'),
('ROM', 11, 3, 'ROM.11.3', '“Lord, they have killed Your prophets and torn down Your altars. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well”?'),
('ROM', 11, 4, 'ROM.11.4', 'And what was the divine reply to him? “I have reserved for Myself seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal.”'),
('ROM', 11, 5, 'ROM.11.5', 'In the same way, at the present time there is a remnant chosen by grace.'),
('ROM', 11, 6, 'ROM.11.6', 'And if it is by grace, then it is no longer by works. Otherwise, grace would no longer be grace.'),
('ROM', 11, 7, 'ROM.11.7', 'What then? What Israel was seeking, it failed to obtain, but the elect did. The others were hardened,'),
('ROM', 11, 8, 'ROM.11.8', 'as it is written: “God gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that could not see, and ears that could not hear, to this very day.”'),
('ROM', 11, 9, 'ROM.11.9', 'And David says: “May their table become a snare and a trap, a stumbling block and a retribution to them.'),
('ROM', 11, 10, 'ROM.11.10', 'May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.”'),
('ROM', 11, 11, 'ROM.11.11', 'I ask then, did they stumble so as to fall beyond recovery? Certainly not! However, because of their trespass, salvation has come to the Gentiles to make Israel jealous.'),
('ROM', 11, 12, 'ROM.11.12', 'But if their trespass means riches for the world, and their failure means riches for the Gentiles, how much greater riches will their fullness bring!'),
('ROM', 11, 13, 'ROM.11.13', 'I am speaking to you Gentiles. Inasmuch as I am the apostle to the Gentiles, I magnify my ministry'),
('ROM', 11, 14, 'ROM.11.14', 'in the hope that I may provoke my own people to jealousy and save some of them.'),
('ROM', 11, 15, 'ROM.11.15', 'For if their rejection is the reconciliation of the world, what will their acceptance be but life from the dead?'),
('ROM', 11, 16, 'ROM.11.16', 'If the first part of the dough is holy, so is the whole batch; if the root is holy, so are the branches.'),
('ROM', 11, 17, 'ROM.11.17', 'Now if some branches have been broken off, and you, a wild olive shoot, have been grafted in among the others to share in the nourishment of the olive root,'),
('ROM', 11, 18, 'ROM.11.18', 'do not boast over those branches. If you do, remember this: You do not support the root, but the root supports you.'),
('ROM', 11, 19, 'ROM.11.19', 'You will say then, “Branches were broken off so that I could be grafted in.”'),
('ROM', 11, 20, 'ROM.11.20', 'That is correct: They were broken off because of unbelief, but you stand by faith. Do not be arrogant, but be afraid.'),
('ROM', 11, 21, 'ROM.11.21', 'For if God did not spare the natural branches, He will certainly not spare you either.'),
('ROM', 11, 22, 'ROM.11.22', 'Take notice, therefore, of the kindness and severity of God: severity to those who fell, but kindness to you, if you continue in His kindness. Otherwise you also will be cut off.'),
('ROM', 11, 23, 'ROM.11.23', 'And if they do not persist in unbelief, they will be grafted in, for God is able to graft them in again.'),
('ROM', 11, 24, 'ROM.11.24', 'For if you were cut from a wild olive tree, and contrary to nature were grafted into one that is cultivated, how much more readily will these, the natural branches, be grafted into their own olive tree!'),
('ROM', 11, 25, 'ROM.11.25', 'I do not want you to be ignorant of this mystery, brothers, so that you will not be conceited: A hardening in part has come to Israel, until the full number of the Gentiles has come in.'),
('ROM', 11, 26, 'ROM.11.26', 'And so all Israel will be saved, as it is written: “The Deliverer will come from Zion; He will remove godlessness from Jacob.'),
('ROM', 11, 27, 'ROM.11.27', 'And this is My covenant with them when I take away their sins.”'),
('ROM', 11, 28, 'ROM.11.28', 'Regarding the gospel, they are enemies on your account; but regarding election, they are loved on account of the patriarchs.'),
('ROM', 11, 29, 'ROM.11.29', 'For God’s gifts and His call are irrevocable.'),
('ROM', 11, 30, 'ROM.11.30', 'Just as you who formerly disobeyed God have now received mercy through their disobedience,'),
('ROM', 11, 31, 'ROM.11.31', 'so they too have now disobeyed, in order that they too may now receive mercy through the mercy shown to you.'),
('ROM', 11, 32, 'ROM.11.32', 'For God has consigned everyone to disobedience so that He may have mercy on everyone.'),
('ROM', 11, 33, 'ROM.11.33', 'O, the depth of the riches of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How unsearchable are His judgments, and untraceable His ways!'),
('ROM', 11, 34, 'ROM.11.34', '“Who has known the mind of the Lord? Or who has been His counselor?”'),
('ROM', 11, 35, 'ROM.11.35', '“Who has first given to God, that God should repay him?”'),
('ROM', 11, 36, 'ROM.11.36', 'For from Him and through Him and to Him are all things. To Him be the glory forever! Amen.'),
('ROM', 12, 1, 'ROM.12.1', 'Therefore I urge you, brothers, on account of God’s mercy, to offer your bodies as living sacrifices, holy and pleasing to God, which is your spiritual service of worship.'),
('ROM', 12, 2, 'ROM.12.2', 'Do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind. Then you will be able to test and approve what is the good, pleasing, and perfect will of God.'),
('ROM', 12, 3, 'ROM.12.3', 'For by the grace given me I say to every one of you: Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but think of yourself with sober judgment, according to the measure of faith God has given you.'),
('ROM', 12, 4, 'ROM.12.4', 'Just as each of us has one body with many members, and not all members have the same function,'),
('ROM', 12, 5, 'ROM.12.5', 'so in Christ we who are many are one body, and each member belongs to one another.'),
('ROM', 12, 6, 'ROM.12.6', 'We have different gifts according to the grace given us. If one’s gift is prophecy, let him use it in proportion to his faith;'),
('ROM', 12, 7, 'ROM.12.7', 'if it is serving, let him serve; if it is teaching, let him teach;'),
('ROM', 12, 8, 'ROM.12.8', 'if it is encouraging, let him encourage; if it is giving, let him give generously; if it is leading, let him lead with diligence; if it is showing mercy, let him do it cheerfully.'),
('ROM', 12, 9, 'ROM.12.9', 'Love must be sincere. Detest what is evil; cling to what is good.'),
('ROM', 12, 10, 'ROM.12.10', 'Be devoted to one another in brotherly love. Outdo yourselves in honoring one another.'),
('ROM', 12, 11, 'ROM.12.11', 'Do not let your zeal subside; keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord.'),
('ROM', 12, 12, 'ROM.12.12', 'Be joyful in hope, patient in affliction, persistent in prayer.'),
('ROM', 12, 13, 'ROM.12.13', 'Share with the saints who are in need. Practice hospitality.'),
('ROM', 12, 14, 'ROM.12.14', 'Bless those who persecute you. Bless and do not curse.'),
('ROM', 12, 15, 'ROM.12.15', 'Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.'),
('ROM', 12, 16, 'ROM.12.16', 'Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but associate with the lowly. Do not be conceited.'),
('ROM', 12, 17, 'ROM.12.17', 'Do not repay anyone evil for evil. Carefully consider what is right in the eyes of everybody.'),
('ROM', 12, 18, 'ROM.12.18', 'If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone.'),
('ROM', 12, 19, 'ROM.12.19', 'Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”'),
('ROM', 12, 20, 'ROM.12.20', 'On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”'),
('ROM', 12, 21, 'ROM.12.21', 'Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good.'),
('ROM', 13, 1, 'ROM.13.1', 'Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God.'),
('ROM', 13, 2, 'ROM.13.2', 'Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves.'),
('ROM', 13, 3, 'ROM.13.3', 'For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad. Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority? Then do what is right, and you will have his approval.'),
('ROM', 13, 4, 'ROM.13.4', 'For he is God’s servant for your good. But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain. He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer.'),
('ROM', 13, 5, 'ROM.13.5', 'Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience.'),
('ROM', 13, 6, 'ROM.13.6', 'This is also why you pay taxes. For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work.'),
('ROM', 13, 7, 'ROM.13.7', 'Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due.'),
('ROM', 13, 8, 'ROM.13.8', 'Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law.'),
('ROM', 13, 9, 'ROM.13.9', 'The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”'),
('ROM', 13, 10, 'ROM.13.10', 'Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law.'),
('ROM', 13, 11, 'ROM.13.11', 'And do this, understanding the occasion. The hour has come for you to wake up from your slumber, for our salvation is nearer now than when we first believed.'),
('ROM', 13, 12, 'ROM.13.12', 'The night is nearly over; the day has drawn near. So let us lay aside the deeds of darkness and put on the armor of light.'),
('ROM', 13, 13, 'ROM.13.13', 'Let us behave decently, as in the daytime, not in carousing and drunkenness, not in sexual immorality and debauchery, not in dissension and jealousy.'),
('ROM', 13, 14, 'ROM.13.14', 'Instead, clothe yourselves with the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the desires of the flesh.'),
('ROM', 14, 1, 'ROM.14.1', 'Accept him whose faith is weak, without passing judgment on his opinions.'),
('ROM', 14, 2, 'ROM.14.2', 'For one person has faith to eat all things, while another, who is weak, eats only vegetables.'),
('ROM', 14, 3, 'ROM.14.3', 'The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him.'),
('ROM', 14, 4, 'ROM.14.4', 'Who are you to judge someone else’s servant? To his own master he stands or falls. And he will stand, for the Lord is able to make him stand.'),
('ROM', 14, 5, 'ROM.14.5', 'One person regards a certain day above the others, while someone else considers every day alike. Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind.'),
('ROM', 14, 6, 'ROM.14.6', 'He who observes a special day does so to the Lord; he who eats does so to the Lord, for he gives thanks to God; and he who abstains does so to the Lord and gives thanks to God.'),
('ROM', 14, 7, 'ROM.14.7', 'For none of us lives to himself alone, and none of us dies to himself alone.'),
('ROM', 14, 8, 'ROM.14.8', 'If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord.'),
('ROM', 14, 9, 'ROM.14.9', 'For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living.'),
('ROM', 14, 10, 'ROM.14.10', 'Why, then, do you judge your brother? Or why do you belittle your brother? For we will all stand before God’s judgment seat.'),
('ROM', 14, 11, 'ROM.14.11', 'It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”'),
('ROM', 14, 12, 'ROM.14.12', 'So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God.'),
('ROM', 14, 13, 'ROM.14.13', 'Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way.'),
('ROM', 14, 14, 'ROM.14.14', 'I am convinced and fully persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean in itself. But if anyone regards something as unclean, then for him it is unclean.'),
('ROM', 14, 15, 'ROM.14.15', 'If your brother is distressed by what you eat, you are no longer acting in love. Do not by your eating destroy your brother, for whom Christ died.'),
('ROM', 14, 16, 'ROM.14.16', 'Do not allow what you consider good, then, to be spoken of as evil.'),
('ROM', 14, 17, 'ROM.14.17', 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking, but of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.'),
('ROM', 14, 18, 'ROM.14.18', 'For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men.'),
('ROM', 14, 19, 'ROM.14.19', 'So then, let us pursue what leads to peace and to mutual edification.'),
('ROM', 14, 20, 'ROM.14.20', 'Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food. All food is clean, but it is wrong for a man to let his eating be a stumbling block.'),
('ROM', 14, 21, 'ROM.14.21', 'It is better not to eat meat or drink wine or to do anything to cause your brother to stumble.'),
('ROM', 14, 22, 'ROM.14.22', 'Keep your belief about such matters between yourself and God. Blessed is the one who does not condemn himself by what he approves.'),
('ROM', 14, 23, 'ROM.14.23', 'But the one who has doubts is condemned if he eats, because his eating is not from faith; and everything that is not from faith is sin.'),
('ROM', 15, 1, 'ROM.15.1', 'We who are strong ought to bear with the shortcomings of the weak and not to please ourselves.'),
('ROM', 15, 2, 'ROM.15.2', 'Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up.'),
('ROM', 15, 3, 'ROM.15.3', 'For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”'),
('ROM', 15, 4, 'ROM.15.4', 'For everything that was written in the past was written for our instruction, so that through endurance and the encouragement of the Scriptures, we might have hope.'),
('ROM', 15, 5, 'ROM.15.5', 'Now may the God who gives endurance and encouragement grant you harmony with one another in Christ Jesus,'),
('ROM', 15, 6, 'ROM.15.6', 'so that with one mind and one voice you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('ROM', 15, 7, 'ROM.15.7', 'Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God.'),
('ROM', 15, 8, 'ROM.15.8', 'For I tell you that Christ has become a servant of the circumcised on behalf of God’s truth, to confirm the promises made to the patriarchs,'),
('ROM', 15, 9, 'ROM.15.9', 'so that the Gentiles may glorify God for His mercy. As it is written: “Therefore I will praise You among the Gentiles; I will sing hymns to Your name.”'),
('ROM', 15, 10, 'ROM.15.10', 'Again, it says: “Rejoice, O Gentiles, with His people.”'),
('ROM', 15, 11, 'ROM.15.11', 'And again: “Praise the Lord, all you Gentiles, and extol Him, all you peoples.”'),
('ROM', 15, 12, 'ROM.15.12', 'And once more, Isaiah says: “The Root of Jesse will appear, One who will arise to rule over the Gentiles; in Him the Gentiles will put their hope.”'),
('ROM', 15, 13, 'ROM.15.13', 'Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you believe in Him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.'),
('ROM', 15, 14, 'ROM.15.14', 'I myself am convinced, my brothers, that you yourselves are full of goodness, brimming with knowledge, and able to instruct one another.'),
('ROM', 15, 15, 'ROM.15.15', 'However, I have written you a bold reminder on some points, because of the grace God has given me'),
('ROM', 15, 16, 'ROM.15.16', 'to be a minister of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles in the priestly service of the gospel of God, so that the Gentiles might become an offering acceptable to God, sanctified by the Holy Spirit.'),
('ROM', 15, 17, 'ROM.15.17', 'Therefore I exult in Christ Jesus in my service to God.'),
('ROM', 15, 18, 'ROM.15.18', 'I will not presume to speak of anything except what Christ has accomplished through me in leading the Gentiles to obedience by word and deed,'),
('ROM', 15, 19, 'ROM.15.19', 'by the power of signs and wonders, and by the power of the Spirit of God. So from Jerusalem all the way around to Illyricum, I have fully proclaimed the gospel of Christ.'),
('ROM', 15, 20, 'ROM.15.20', 'In this way I have aspired to preach the gospel where Christ was not known, so that I would not be building on someone else’s foundation.'),
('ROM', 15, 21, 'ROM.15.21', 'Rather, as it is written: “Those who were not told about Him will see, and those who have not heard will understand.”'),
('ROM', 15, 22, 'ROM.15.22', 'That is why I have often been hindered from coming to you.'),
('ROM', 15, 23, 'ROM.15.23', 'But now that there are no further opportunities for me in these regions, and since I have longed for many years to visit you,'),
('ROM', 15, 24, 'ROM.15.24', 'I hope to see you on my way to Spain. And after I have enjoyed your company for a while, you can equip me for my journey.'),
('ROM', 15, 25, 'ROM.15.25', 'Now, however, I am on my way to Jerusalem to serve the saints there.'),
('ROM', 15, 26, 'ROM.15.26', 'For Macedonia and Achaia were pleased to make a contribution for the poor among the saints in Jerusalem.'),
('ROM', 15, 27, 'ROM.15.27', 'They were pleased to do it, and indeed they owe it to them. For if the Gentiles have shared in their spiritual blessings, they are obligated to minister to them with material blessings.'),
('ROM', 15, 28, 'ROM.15.28', 'So after I have completed this service and have safely delivered this bounty to them, I will set off to Spain by way of you.'),
('ROM', 15, 29, 'ROM.15.29', 'I know that when I come to you, I will come in the fullness of the blessing of Christ.'),
('ROM', 15, 30, 'ROM.15.30', 'Now I urge you, brothers, by our Lord Jesus Christ and by the love of the Spirit, to join me in my struggle by praying to God for me.'),
('ROM', 15, 31, 'ROM.15.31', 'Pray that I may be delivered from the unbelievers in Judea, and that my service in Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints there,'),
('ROM', 15, 32, 'ROM.15.32', 'so that by God’s will I may come to you with joy and together with you be refreshed.'),
('ROM', 15, 33, 'ROM.15.33', 'The God of peace be with all of you. Amen.'),
('ROM', 16, 1, 'ROM.16.1', 'I commend to you our sister Phoebe, a servant of the church in Cenchrea.'),
('ROM', 16, 2, 'ROM.16.2', 'Welcome her in the Lord in a manner worthy of the saints, and assist her with anything she may need from you. For she has been a great help to many people, including me.'),
('ROM', 16, 3, 'ROM.16.3', 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus,'),
('ROM', 16, 4, 'ROM.16.4', 'who have risked their lives for me. Not only I but all the churches of the Gentiles are grateful to them.'),
('ROM', 16, 5, 'ROM.16.5', 'Greet also the church that meets at their house. Greet my beloved Epenetus, who was the first convert to Christ in the province of Asia.'),
('ROM', 16, 6, 'ROM.16.6', 'Greet Mary, who has worked very hard for you.'),
('ROM', 16, 7, 'ROM.16.7', 'Greet Andronicus and Junia, my fellow countrymen and fellow prisoners. They are outstanding among the apostles, and they were in Christ before I was.'),
('ROM', 16, 8, 'ROM.16.8', 'Greet Ampliatus, my beloved in the Lord.'),
('ROM', 16, 9, 'ROM.16.9', 'Greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ, and my beloved Stachys.'),
('ROM', 16, 10, 'ROM.16.10', 'Greet Apelles, who is approved in Christ. Greet those who belong to the household of Aristobulus.'),
('ROM', 16, 11, 'ROM.16.11', 'Greet Herodion, my fellow countryman. Greet those from the household of Narcissus who are in the Lord.'),
('ROM', 16, 12, 'ROM.16.12', 'Greet Tryphena and Tryphosa, women who have worked hard in the Lord. Greet my beloved Persis, who has worked very hard in the Lord.'),
('ROM', 16, 13, 'ROM.16.13', 'Greet Rufus, chosen in the Lord, and his mother, who has been a mother to me as well.'),
('ROM', 16, 14, 'ROM.16.14', 'Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the brothers with them.'),
('ROM', 16, 15, 'ROM.16.15', 'Greet Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas and all the saints with them.'),
('ROM', 16, 16, 'ROM.16.16', 'Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ send you greetings.'),
('ROM', 16, 17, 'ROM.16.17', 'Now I urge you, brothers, to watch out for those who create divisions and obstacles that are contrary to the teaching you have learned. Turn away from them.'),
('ROM', 16, 18, 'ROM.16.18', 'For such people are not serving our Lord Christ, but their own appetites. By smooth talk and flattery they deceive the hearts of the naive.'),
('ROM', 16, 19, 'ROM.16.19', 'Everyone has heard about your obedience, so I rejoice over you. But I want you to be wise about what is good and innocent about what is evil.'),
('ROM', 16, 20, 'ROM.16.20', 'The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.'),
('ROM', 16, 21, 'ROM.16.21', 'Timothy, my fellow worker, sends you greetings, as do Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my fellow countrymen.'),
('ROM', 16, 22, 'ROM.16.22', 'I, Tertius, who wrote down this letter, greet you in the Lord.'),
('ROM', 16, 23, 'ROM.16.23', 'Gaius, who has hosted me and all the church, sends you greetings. Erastus, the city treasurer, sends you greetings, as does our brother Quartus.'),
('ROM', 16, 25, 'ROM.16.25', 'Now to Him who is able to strengthen you by my gospel and by the proclamation of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery concealed for ages past'),
('ROM', 16, 26, 'ROM.16.26', 'but now revealed and made known through the writings of the prophets by the command of the eternal God, in order to lead all nations to the obedience that comes from faith—'),
('ROM', 16, 27, 'ROM.16.27', 'to the only wise God be glory forever through Jesus Christ! Amen.'),
('1CO', 1, 1, '1CO.1.1', 'Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,'),
('1CO', 1, 2, '1CO.1.2', 'To the church of God in Corinth, to those sanctified in Christ Jesus and called to be holy, together with all those everywhere who call on the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, their Lord and ours:'),
('1CO', 1, 3, '1CO.1.3', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1CO', 1, 4, '1CO.1.4', 'I always thank my God for you because of the grace He has given you in Christ Jesus.'),
('1CO', 1, 5, '1CO.1.5', 'For in Him you have been enriched in every way, in all speech and all knowledge,'),
('1CO', 1, 6, '1CO.1.6', 'because our testimony about Christ was confirmed in you.'),
('1CO', 1, 7, '1CO.1.7', 'Therefore you do not lack any spiritual gift as you eagerly await the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1CO', 1, 8, '1CO.1.8', 'He will sustain you to the end, so that you will be blameless on the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1CO', 1, 9, '1CO.1.9', 'God, who has called you into fellowship with His Son Jesus Christ our Lord, is faithful.'),
('1CO', 1, 10, '1CO.1.10', 'I appeal to you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions among you and that you may be united in mind and conviction.'),
('1CO', 1, 11, '1CO.1.11', 'My brothers, some from Chloe’s household have informed me that there are quarrels among you.'),
('1CO', 1, 12, '1CO.1.12', 'What I mean is this: Individuals among you are saying, “I follow Paul,” “I follow Apollos,” “I follow Cephas,” or “I follow Christ.”'),
('1CO', 1, 13, '1CO.1.13', 'Is Christ divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Were you baptized into the name of Paul?'),
('1CO', 1, 14, '1CO.1.14', 'I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,'),
('1CO', 1, 15, '1CO.1.15', 'so no one can say that you were baptized into my name.'),
('1CO', 1, 16, '1CO.1.16', 'Yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanas; beyond that I do not remember if I baptized anyone else.'),
('1CO', 1, 17, '1CO.1.17', 'For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel, not with words of wisdom, lest the cross of Christ be emptied of its power.'),
('1CO', 1, 18, '1CO.1.18', 'For the message of the cross is foolishness to those who are perishing, but to us who are being saved it is the power of God.'),
('1CO', 1, 19, '1CO.1.19', 'For it is written: “I will destroy the wisdom of the wise; the intelligence of the intelligent I will frustrate.”'),
('1CO', 1, 20, '1CO.1.20', 'Where is the wise man? Where is the scribe? Where is the philosopher of this age? Has not God made foolish the wisdom of the world?'),
('1CO', 1, 21, '1CO.1.21', 'For since in the wisdom of God the world through its wisdom did not know Him, God was pleased through the foolishness of what was preached to save those who believe.'),
('1CO', 1, 22, '1CO.1.22', 'Jews demand signs and Greeks search for wisdom,'),
('1CO', 1, 23, '1CO.1.23', 'but we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling block to Jews and foolishness to Gentiles,'),
('1CO', 1, 24, '1CO.1.24', 'but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power of God and the wisdom of God.'),
('1CO', 1, 25, '1CO.1.25', 'For the foolishness of God is wiser than man’s wisdom, and the weakness of God is stronger than man’s strength.'),
('1CO', 1, 26, '1CO.1.26', 'Brothers, consider the time of your calling: Not many of you were wise by human standards; not many were powerful; not many were of noble birth.'),
('1CO', 1, 27, '1CO.1.27', 'But God chose the foolish things of the world to shame the wise; God chose the weak things of the world to shame the strong.'),
('1CO', 1, 28, '1CO.1.28', 'He chose the lowly and despised things of the world, and the things that are not, to nullify the things that are,'),
('1CO', 1, 29, '1CO.1.29', 'so that no one may boast in His presence.'),
('1CO', 1, 30, '1CO.1.30', 'It is because of Him that you are in Christ Jesus, who has become for us wisdom from God: our righteousness, holiness, and redemption.'),
('1CO', 1, 31, '1CO.1.31', 'Therefore, as it is written: “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”'),
('1CO', 2, 1, '1CO.2.1', 'When I came to you, brothers, I did not come with eloquence or wisdom as I proclaimed to you the testimony about God.'),
('1CO', 2, 2, '1CO.2.2', 'For I resolved to know nothing while I was with you except Jesus Christ and Him crucified.'),
('1CO', 2, 3, '1CO.2.3', 'I came to you in weakness and fear, and with much trembling.'),
('1CO', 2, 4, '1CO.2.4', 'My message and my preaching were not with persuasive words of wisdom, but with a demonstration of the Spirit’s power,'),
('1CO', 2, 5, '1CO.2.5', 'so that your faith would not rest on men’s wisdom, but on God’s power.'),
('1CO', 2, 6, '1CO.2.6', 'Among the mature, however, we speak a message of wisdom—but not the wisdom of this age or of the rulers of this age, who are coming to nothing.'),
('1CO', 2, 7, '1CO.2.7', 'No, we speak of the mysterious and hidden wisdom of God, which He destined for our glory before time began.'),
('1CO', 2, 8, '1CO.2.8', 'None of the rulers of this age understood it. For if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.'),
('1CO', 2, 9, '1CO.2.9', 'Rather, as it is written: “No eye has seen, no ear has heard, no heart has imagined, what God has prepared for those who love Him.”'),
('1CO', 2, 10, '1CO.2.10', 'But God has revealed it to us by the Spirit. The Spirit searches all things, even the deep things of God.'),
('1CO', 2, 11, '1CO.2.11', 'For who among men knows the thoughts of man except his own spirit within him? So too, no one knows the thoughts of God except the Spirit of God.'),
('1CO', 2, 12, '1CO.2.12', 'We have not received the spirit of the world, but the Spirit who is from God, that we may understand what God has freely given us.'),
('1CO', 2, 13, '1CO.2.13', 'And this is what we speak, not in words taught us by human wisdom, but in words taught by the Spirit, expressing spiritual truths in spiritual words.'),
('1CO', 2, 14, '1CO.2.14', 'The natural man does not accept the things that come from the Spirit of God. For they are foolishness to him, and he cannot understand them, because they are spiritually discerned.'),
('1CO', 2, 15, '1CO.2.15', 'The spiritual man judges all things, but he himself is not subject to anyone’s judgment.'),
('1CO', 2, 16, '1CO.2.16', '“For who has known the mind of the Lord, so as to instruct Him?” But we have the mind of Christ.'),
('1CO', 3, 1, '1CO.3.1', 'Brothers, I could not address you as spiritual, but as worldly—as infants in Christ.'),
('1CO', 3, 2, '1CO.3.2', 'I gave you milk, not solid food, for you were not yet ready for solid food. In fact, you are still not ready,'),
('1CO', 3, 3, '1CO.3.3', 'for you are still worldly. For since there is jealousy and dissension among you, are you not worldly? Are you not walking in the way of man?'),
('1CO', 3, 4, '1CO.3.4', 'For when one of you says, “I follow Paul,” and another, “I follow Apollos,” are you not mere men?'),
('1CO', 3, 5, '1CO.3.5', 'What then is Apollos? And what is Paul? They are servants through whom you believed, as the Lord has assigned to each his role.'),
('1CO', 3, 6, '1CO.3.6', 'I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow.'),
('1CO', 3, 7, '1CO.3.7', 'So neither he who plants nor he who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow.'),
('1CO', 3, 8, '1CO.3.8', 'He who plants and he who waters are one in purpose, and each will be rewarded according to his own labor.'),
('1CO', 3, 9, '1CO.3.9', 'For we are God’s fellow workers; you are God’s field, God’s building.'),
('1CO', 3, 10, '1CO.3.10', 'By the grace God has given me, I laid a foundation as an expert builder, and someone else is building on it. But each one must be careful how he builds.'),
('1CO', 3, 11, '1CO.3.11', 'For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid, which is Jesus Christ.'),
('1CO', 3, 12, '1CO.3.12', 'If anyone builds on this foundation using gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or straw,'),
('1CO', 3, 13, '1CO.3.13', 'his workmanship will be evident, because the Day will bring it to light. It will be revealed with fire, and the fire will prove the quality of each man’s work.'),
('1CO', 3, 14, '1CO.3.14', 'If what he has built survives, he will receive a reward.'),
('1CO', 3, 15, '1CO.3.15', 'If it is burned up, he will suffer loss. He himself will be saved, but only as if through the flames.'),
('1CO', 3, 16, '1CO.3.16', 'Do you not know that you yourselves are God’s temple, and that God’s Spirit dwells in you?'),
('1CO', 3, 17, '1CO.3.17', 'If anyone destroys God’s temple, God will destroy him; for God’s temple is holy, and you are that temple.'),
('1CO', 3, 18, '1CO.3.18', 'Let no one deceive himself. If any of you thinks he is wise in this age, he should become a fool, so that he may become wise.'),
('1CO', 3, 19, '1CO.3.19', 'For the wisdom of this world is foolishness in God’s sight. As it is written: “He catches the wise in their craftiness.”'),
('1CO', 3, 20, '1CO.3.20', 'And again, “The Lord knows that the thoughts of the wise are futile.”'),
('1CO', 3, 21, '1CO.3.21', 'Therefore, stop boasting in men. All things are yours,'),
('1CO', 3, 22, '1CO.3.22', 'whether Paul or Apollos or Cephas or the world or life or death or the present or the future. All of them belong to you,'),
('1CO', 3, 23, '1CO.3.23', 'and you belong to Christ, and Christ belongs to God.'),
('1CO', 4, 1, '1CO.4.1', 'So then, men ought to regard us as servants of Christ and stewards of the mysteries of God.'),
('1CO', 4, 2, '1CO.4.2', 'Now it is required of stewards that they be found faithful.'),
('1CO', 4, 3, '1CO.4.3', 'I care very little, however, if I am judged by you or by any human court. In fact, I do not even judge myself.'),
('1CO', 4, 4, '1CO.4.4', 'My conscience is clear, but that does not vindicate me. It is the Lord who judges me.'),
('1CO', 4, 5, '1CO.4.5', 'Therefore judge nothing before the appointed time; wait until the Lord comes. He will bring to light what is hidden in darkness and will expose the motives of men’s hearts. At that time each will receive his praise from God.'),
('1CO', 4, 6, '1CO.4.6', 'Brothers, I have applied these things to myself and Apollos for your benefit, so that you may learn from us not to go beyond what is written. Then you will not take pride in one man over another.'),
('1CO', 4, 7, '1CO.4.7', 'For who makes you so superior? What do you have that you did not receive? And if you did receive it, why do you boast as though you did not?'),
('1CO', 4, 8, '1CO.4.8', 'Already you have all you want. Already you have become rich. Without us, you have become kings. How I wish you really were kings, so that we might be kings with you!'),
('1CO', 4, 9, '1CO.4.9', 'For it seems to me that God has displayed us apostles at the end of the procession, like prisoners appointed for death. We have become a spectacle to the whole world, to angels as well as to men.'),
('1CO', 4, 10, '1CO.4.10', 'We are fools for Christ, but you are wise in Christ. We are weak, but you are strong. You are honored, but we are dishonored.'),
('1CO', 4, 11, '1CO.4.11', 'To this very hour we are hungry and thirsty, we are poorly clothed, we are brutally treated, we are homeless.'),
('1CO', 4, 12, '1CO.4.12', 'We work hard with our own hands. When we are vilified, we bless; when we are persecuted, we endure it;'),
('1CO', 4, 13, '1CO.4.13', 'when we are slandered, we answer gently. Up to this moment we have become the scum of the earth, the refuse of the world.'),
('1CO', 4, 14, '1CO.4.14', 'I am not writing this to shame you, but to warn you as my beloved children.'),
('1CO', 4, 15, '1CO.4.15', 'Even if you have ten thousand guardians in Christ, you do not have many fathers; for in Christ Jesus I became your father through the gospel.'),
('1CO', 4, 16, '1CO.4.16', 'Therefore I urge you to imitate me.'),
('1CO', 4, 17, '1CO.4.17', 'That is why I have sent you Timothy, my beloved and faithful child in the Lord. He will remind you of my way of life in Christ Jesus, which is exactly what I teach everywhere in every church.'),
('1CO', 4, 18, '1CO.4.18', 'Some of you have become arrogant, as if I were not coming to you.'),
('1CO', 4, 19, '1CO.4.19', 'But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing, and then I will find out not only what these arrogant people are saying, but what power they have.'),
('1CO', 4, 20, '1CO.4.20', 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of talk but of power.'),
('1CO', 4, 21, '1CO.4.21', 'Which do you prefer? Shall I come to you with a rod, or in love and with a gentle spirit?'),
('1CO', 5, 1, '1CO.5.1', 'It is actually reported that there is sexual immorality among you, and of a kind that is intolerable even among pagans: A man has his father’s wife.'),
('1CO', 5, 2, '1CO.5.2', 'And you are proud! Shouldn’t you rather have been stricken with grief and have removed from your fellowship the man who did this?'),
('1CO', 5, 3, '1CO.5.3', 'Although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I have already pronounced judgment on the one who did this, just as if I were present.'),
('1CO', 5, 4, '1CO.5.4', 'When you are assembled in the name of our Lord Jesus and I am with you in spirit, along with the power of the Lord Jesus,'),
('1CO', 5, 5, '1CO.5.5', 'hand this man over to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, so that his spirit may be saved on the Day of the Lord.'),
('1CO', 5, 6, '1CO.5.6', 'Your boasting is not good. Do you not know that a little leaven works through the whole batch of dough?'),
('1CO', 5, 7, '1CO.5.7', 'Get rid of the old leaven, that you may be a new unleavened batch, as you really are. For Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed.'),
('1CO', 5, 8, '1CO.5.8', 'Therefore let us keep the feast, not with the old bread, leavened with malice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and of truth.'),
('1CO', 5, 9, '1CO.5.9', 'I wrote you in my letter not to associate with sexually immoral people.'),
('1CO', 5, 10, '1CO.5.10', 'I was not including the sexually immoral of this world, or the greedy and swindlers, or idolaters. In that case you would have to leave this world.'),
('1CO', 5, 11, '1CO.5.11', 'But now I am writing you not to associate with anyone who claims to be a brother but is sexually immoral or greedy, an idolater or a verbal abuser, a drunkard or a swindler. With such a man do not even eat.'),
('1CO', 5, 12, '1CO.5.12', 'What business of mine is it to judge those outside the church? Are you not to judge those inside?'),
('1CO', 5, 13, '1CO.5.13', 'God will judge those outside. “Expel the wicked man from among you.”'),
('1CO', 6, 1, '1CO.6.1', 'If any of you has a grievance against another, how dare he go to law before the unrighteous instead of before the saints!'),
('1CO', 6, 2, '1CO.6.2', 'Do you not know that the saints will judge the world? And if you are to judge the world, are you not competent to judge trivial cases?'),
('1CO', 6, 3, '1CO.6.3', 'Do you not know that we will judge angels? How much more the things of this life!'),
('1CO', 6, 4, '1CO.6.4', 'So if you need to settle everyday matters, do you appoint as judges those of no standing in the church?'),
('1CO', 6, 5, '1CO.6.5', 'I say this to your shame. Is there really no one among you wise enough to arbitrate between his brothers?'),
('1CO', 6, 6, '1CO.6.6', 'Instead, one brother goes to law against another, and this in front of unbelievers!'),
('1CO', 6, 7, '1CO.6.7', 'The very fact that you have lawsuits among you means that you are thoroughly defeated already. Why not rather be wronged? Why not rather be cheated?'),
('1CO', 6, 8, '1CO.6.8', 'Instead, you yourselves cheat and do wrong, even against your own brothers!'),
('1CO', 6, 9, '1CO.6.9', 'Do you not know that the wicked will not inherit the kingdom of God? Do not be deceived: Neither the sexually immoral, nor idolaters, nor adulterers, nor men who submit to or perform homosexual acts,'),
('1CO', 6, 10, '1CO.6.10', 'nor thieves, nor the greedy, nor drunkards, nor verbal abusers, nor swindlers, will inherit the kingdom of God.'),
('1CO', 6, 11, '1CO.6.11', 'And that is what some of you were. But you were washed, you were sanctified, you were justified, in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ and by the Spirit of our God.'),
('1CO', 6, 12, '1CO.6.12', '“Everything is permissible for me,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible for me,” but I will not be mastered by anything.'),
('1CO', 6, 13, '1CO.6.13', '“Food for the stomach and the stomach for food,” but God will destroy them both. The body is not intended for sexual immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body.'),
('1CO', 6, 14, '1CO.6.14', 'By His power God raised the Lord from the dead, and He will raise us also.'),
('1CO', 6, 15, '1CO.6.15', 'Do you not know that your bodies are members of Christ? Shall I then take the members of Christ and unite them with a prostitute? Never!'),
('1CO', 6, 16, '1CO.6.16', 'Or don’t you know that he who unites himself with a prostitute is one with her in body? For it is said, “The two will become one flesh.”'),
('1CO', 6, 17, '1CO.6.17', 'But he who unites himself with the Lord is one with Him in spirit.'),
('1CO', 6, 18, '1CO.6.18', 'Flee from sexual immorality. Every other sin a man can commit is outside his body, but he who sins sexually sins against his own body.'),
('1CO', 6, 19, '1CO.6.19', 'Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received from God? You are not your own;'),
('1CO', 6, 20, '1CO.6.20', 'you were bought at a price. Therefore glorify God with your body.'),
('1CO', 7, 1, '1CO.7.1', 'Now for the matters you wrote about: It is good to abstain from sexual relations.'),
('1CO', 7, 2, '1CO.7.2', 'But because there is so much sexual immorality, each man should have his own wife, and each woman her own husband.'),
('1CO', 7, 3, '1CO.7.3', 'The husband should fulfill his marital duty to his wife, and likewise the wife to her husband.'),
('1CO', 7, 4, '1CO.7.4', 'The wife does not have authority over her own body, but the husband. Likewise the husband does not have authority over his own body, but the wife.'),
('1CO', 7, 5, '1CO.7.5', 'Do not deprive each other, except by mutual consent and for a time, so you may devote yourselves to prayer. Then come together again, so that Satan will not tempt you through your lack of self-control.'),
('1CO', 7, 6, '1CO.7.6', 'I say this as a concession, not as a command.'),
('1CO', 7, 7, '1CO.7.7', 'I wish that all men were as I am. But each man has his own gift from God; one has this gift, another has that.'),
('1CO', 7, 8, '1CO.7.8', 'Now to the unmarried and widows I say this: It is good for them to remain unmarried, as I am.'),
('1CO', 7, 9, '1CO.7.9', 'But if they cannot control themselves, let them marry. For it is better to marry than to burn with passion.'),
('1CO', 7, 10, '1CO.7.10', 'To the married I give this command (not I, but the Lord): A wife must not separate from her husband.'),
('1CO', 7, 11, '1CO.7.11', 'But if she does, she must remain unmarried or else be reconciled to her husband. And a husband must not divorce his wife.'),
('1CO', 7, 12, '1CO.7.12', 'To the rest I say this (I, not the Lord): If a brother has an unbelieving wife and she is willing to live with him, he must not divorce her.'),
('1CO', 7, 13, '1CO.7.13', 'And if a woman has an unbelieving husband and he is willing to live with her, she must not divorce him.'),
('1CO', 7, 14, '1CO.7.14', 'For the unbelieving husband is sanctified through his believing wife, and the unbelieving wife is sanctified through her believing husband. Otherwise your children would be unclean, but now they are holy.'),
('1CO', 7, 15, '1CO.7.15', 'But if the unbeliever leaves, let him go. The believing brother or sister is not bound in such cases. God has called you to live in peace.'),
('1CO', 7, 16, '1CO.7.16', 'How do you know, wife, whether you will save your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?'),
('1CO', 7, 17, '1CO.7.17', 'Regardless, each one should lead the life that the Lord has assigned to him and to which God has called him. This is what I prescribe in all the churches.'),
('1CO', 7, 18, '1CO.7.18', 'Was a man already circumcised when he was called? He should not become uncircumcised. Was a man still uncircumcised when called? He should not be circumcised.'),
('1CO', 7, 19, '1CO.7.19', 'Circumcision is nothing and uncircumcision is nothing. Keeping God’s commandments is what counts.'),
('1CO', 7, 20, '1CO.7.20', 'Each one should remain in the situation he was in when he was called.'),
('1CO', 7, 21, '1CO.7.21', 'Were you a slave when you were called? Do not let it concern you—but if you can gain your freedom, take the opportunity.'),
('1CO', 7, 22, '1CO.7.22', 'For he who was a slave when he was called by the Lord is the Lord’s freedman. Conversely, he who was a free man when he was called is Christ’s slave.'),
('1CO', 7, 23, '1CO.7.23', 'You were bought at a price; do not become slaves of men.'),
('1CO', 7, 24, '1CO.7.24', 'Brothers, each one should remain in the situation he was in when God called him.'),
('1CO', 7, 25, '1CO.7.25', 'Now about virgins, I have no command from the Lord, but I give a judgment as one who by the Lord’s mercy is trustworthy.'),
('1CO', 7, 26, '1CO.7.26', 'Because of the present crisis, I think it is good for a man to remain as he is.'),
('1CO', 7, 27, '1CO.7.27', 'Are you committed to a wife? Do not seek to be released. Are you free of commitment? Do not look for a wife.'),
('1CO', 7, 28, '1CO.7.28', 'But if you do marry, you have not sinned. And if a virgin marries, she has not sinned. But those who marry will face troubles in this life, and I want to spare you this.'),
('1CO', 7, 29, '1CO.7.29', 'What I am saying, brothers, is that the time is short. From now on those who have wives should live as if they had none;'),
('1CO', 7, 30, '1CO.7.30', 'those who weep, as if they did not; those who are joyful, as if they were not; those who make a purchase, as if they had nothing;'),
('1CO', 7, 31, '1CO.7.31', 'and those who use the things of this world, as if not dependent on them. For this world in its present form is passing away.'),
('1CO', 7, 32, '1CO.7.32', 'I want you to be free from concern. The unmarried man is concerned about the work of the Lord, how he can please the Lord.'),
('1CO', 7, 33, '1CO.7.33', 'But the married man is concerned about the affairs of this world, how he can please his wife,'),
('1CO', 7, 34, '1CO.7.34', 'and his interests are divided. The unmarried woman or virgin is concerned about the work of the Lord, how she can be holy in both body and spirit. But the married woman is concerned about the affairs of this world, how she can please her husband.'),
('1CO', 7, 35, '1CO.7.35', 'I am saying this for your own good, not to restrict you, but in order to promote proper decorum and undivided devotion to the Lord.'),
('1CO', 7, 36, '1CO.7.36', 'However, if someone thinks he is acting inappropriately toward his betrothed, and if she is beyond her youth and they ought to marry, let him do as he wishes; he is not sinning; they should get married.'),
('1CO', 7, 37, '1CO.7.37', 'But the man who is firmly established in his heart and under no constraint, with control over his will and resolve in his heart not to marry the virgin, he will do well.'),
('1CO', 7, 38, '1CO.7.38', 'So then, he who marries the virgin does well, but he who does not marry her does even better.'),
('1CO', 7, 39, '1CO.7.39', 'A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is free to marry anyone she wishes, as long as he belongs to the Lord.'),
('1CO', 7, 40, '1CO.7.40', 'In my judgment, however, she is happier if she remains as she is. And I think that I too have the Spirit of God.'),
('1CO', 8, 1, '1CO.8.1', 'Now about food sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up.'),
('1CO', 8, 2, '1CO.8.2', 'The one who thinks he knows something does not yet know as he ought to know.'),
('1CO', 8, 3, '1CO.8.3', 'But the one who loves God is known by God.'),
('1CO', 8, 4, '1CO.8.4', 'So about eating food sacrificed to idols: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one.'),
('1CO', 8, 5, '1CO.8.5', 'For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth (as there are many so-called gods and lords),'),
('1CO', 8, 6, '1CO.8.6', 'yet for us there is but one God, the Father, from whom all things came and for whom we exist. And there is but one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things came and through whom we exist.'),
('1CO', 8, 7, '1CO.8.7', 'But not everyone has this knowledge. Some people are still so accustomed to idols that they eat such food as if it were sacrificed to an idol. And since their conscience is weak, it is defiled.'),
('1CO', 8, 8, '1CO.8.8', 'But food does not bring us closer to God: We are no worse if we do not eat, and no better if we do.'),
('1CO', 8, 9, '1CO.8.9', 'Be careful, however, that your freedom does not become a stumbling block to the weak.'),
('1CO', 8, 10, '1CO.8.10', 'For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged to eat food sacrificed to idols?'),
('1CO', 8, 11, '1CO.8.11', 'So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed by your knowledge.'),
('1CO', 8, 12, '1CO.8.12', 'By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ.'),
('1CO', 8, 13, '1CO.8.13', 'Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble.'),
('1CO', 9, 1, '1CO.9.1', 'Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Have I not seen Jesus our Lord? Are you yourselves not my workmanship in the Lord?'),
('1CO', 9, 2, '1CO.9.2', 'Even if I am not an apostle to others, surely I am to you. For you are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord.'),
('1CO', 9, 3, '1CO.9.3', 'This is my defense to those who scrutinize me:'),
('1CO', 9, 4, '1CO.9.4', 'Have we no right to food and to drink?'),
('1CO', 9, 5, '1CO.9.5', 'Have we no right to take along a believing wife, as do the other apostles and the Lord’s brothers and Cephas?'),
('1CO', 9, 6, '1CO.9.6', 'Or are Barnabas and I the only apostles who must work for a living?'),
('1CO', 9, 7, '1CO.9.7', 'Who serves as a soldier at his own expense? Who plants a vineyard and does not eat of its fruit? Who tends a flock and does not drink of its milk?'),
('1CO', 9, 8, '1CO.9.8', 'Do I say this from a human perspective? Doesn’t the Law say the same thing?'),
('1CO', 9, 9, '1CO.9.9', 'For it is written in the Law of Moses: “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.” Is it about oxen that God is concerned?'),
('1CO', 9, 10, '1CO.9.10', 'Isn’t He actually speaking on our behalf? Indeed, this was written for us, because when the plowman plows and the thresher threshes, they should also expect to share in the harvest.'),
('1CO', 9, 11, '1CO.9.11', 'If we have sown spiritual seed among you, is it too much for us to reap a material harvest from you?'),
('1CO', 9, 12, '1CO.9.12', 'If others have this right to your support, shouldn’t we have it all the more? But we did not exercise this right. Instead, we put up with anything rather than hinder the gospel of Christ.'),
('1CO', 9, 13, '1CO.9.13', 'Do you not know that those who work in the temple eat of its food, and those who serve at the altar partake of its offerings?'),
('1CO', 9, 14, '1CO.9.14', 'In the same way, the Lord has prescribed that those who preach the gospel should receive their living from the gospel.'),
('1CO', 9, 15, '1CO.9.15', 'But I have not used any of these rights. And I am not writing this to suggest that something be done for me. Indeed, I would rather die than let anyone nullify my boast.'),
('1CO', 9, 16, '1CO.9.16', 'Yet when I preach the gospel, I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated to preach. Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!'),
('1CO', 9, 17, '1CO.9.17', 'If my preaching is voluntary, I have a reward. But if it is not voluntary, I am still entrusted with a responsibility.'),
('1CO', 9, 18, '1CO.9.18', 'What then is my reward? That in preaching the gospel I may offer it free of charge, and so not use up my rights in preaching it.'),
('1CO', 9, 19, '1CO.9.19', 'Though I am free of obligation to anyone, I make myself a slave to everyone, to win as many as possible.'),
('1CO', 9, 20, '1CO.9.20', 'To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win the Jews. To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law.'),
('1CO', 9, 21, '1CO.9.21', 'To those without the law I became like one without the law (though I am not outside the law of God but am under the law of Christ), to win those without the law.'),
('1CO', 9, 22, '1CO.9.22', 'To the weak I became weak, to win the weak. I have become all things to all people so that by all possible means I might save some.'),
('1CO', 9, 23, '1CO.9.23', 'I do all this for the sake of the gospel, so that I may share in its blessings.'),
('1CO', 9, 24, '1CO.9.24', 'Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize? Run in such a way as to take the prize.'),
('1CO', 9, 25, '1CO.9.25', 'Everyone who competes in the games trains with strict discipline. They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable.'),
('1CO', 9, 26, '1CO.9.26', 'Therefore I do not run aimlessly; I do not fight like I am beating the air.'),
('1CO', 9, 27, '1CO.9.27', 'No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified.'),
('1CO', 10, 1, '1CO.10.1', 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, that our forefathers were all under the cloud, and that they all passed through the sea.'),
('1CO', 10, 2, '1CO.10.2', 'They were all baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea.'),
('1CO', 10, 3, '1CO.10.3', 'They all ate the same spiritual food'),
('1CO', 10, 4, '1CO.10.4', 'and drank the same spiritual drink; for they drank from the spiritual rock that accompanied them, and that rock was Christ.'),
('1CO', 10, 5, '1CO.10.5', 'Nevertheless, God was not pleased with most of them, for they were struck down in the wilderness.'),
('1CO', 10, 6, '1CO.10.6', 'These things took place as examples to keep us from craving evil things as they did.'),
('1CO', 10, 7, '1CO.10.7', 'Do not be idolaters, as some of them were. As it is written: “The people sat down to eat and drink and got up to indulge in revelry.”'),
('1CO', 10, 8, '1CO.10.8', 'We should not commit sexual immorality, as some of them did, and in one day twenty-three thousand of them died.'),
('1CO', 10, 9, '1CO.10.9', 'We should not test Christ, as some of them did, and were killed by snakes.'),
('1CO', 10, 10, '1CO.10.10', 'And do not complain, as some of them did, and were killed by the destroying angel.'),
('1CO', 10, 11, '1CO.10.11', 'Now these things happened to them as examples and were written down as warnings for us, on whom the fulfillment of the ages has come.'),
('1CO', 10, 12, '1CO.10.12', 'So the one who thinks he is standing firm should be careful not to fall.'),
('1CO', 10, 13, '1CO.10.13', 'No temptation has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape, so that you can stand up under it.'),
('1CO', 10, 14, '1CO.10.14', 'Therefore, my beloved, flee from idolatry.'),
('1CO', 10, 15, '1CO.10.15', 'I speak to reasonable people; judge for yourselves what I say.'),
('1CO', 10, 16, '1CO.10.16', 'Is not the cup of blessing that we bless a participation in the blood of Christ? And is not the bread that we break a participation in the body of Christ?'),
('1CO', 10, 17, '1CO.10.17', 'Because there is one loaf, we who are many are one body; for we all partake of the one loaf.'),
('1CO', 10, 18, '1CO.10.18', 'Consider the people of Israel: Are not those who eat the sacrifices fellow partakers in the altar?'),
('1CO', 10, 19, '1CO.10.19', 'Am I suggesting, then, that food sacrificed to an idol is anything, or that an idol is anything?'),
('1CO', 10, 20, '1CO.10.20', 'No, but the sacrifices of pagans are offered to demons, not to God. And I do not want you to be participants with demons.'),
('1CO', 10, 21, '1CO.10.21', 'You cannot drink the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons too; you cannot partake in the table of the Lord and the table of demons too.'),
('1CO', 10, 22, '1CO.10.22', 'Are we trying to provoke the Lord to jealousy? Are we stronger than He?'),
('1CO', 10, 23, '1CO.10.23', '“Everything is permissible,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible,” but not everything is edifying.'),
('1CO', 10, 24, '1CO.10.24', 'No one should seek his own good, but the good of others.'),
('1CO', 10, 25, '1CO.10.25', 'Eat anything sold in the meat market without raising questions of conscience,'),
('1CO', 10, 26, '1CO.10.26', 'for, “The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness thereof.”'),
('1CO', 10, 27, '1CO.10.27', 'If an unbeliever invites you to a meal and you want to go, eat anything set before you without raising questions of conscience.'),
('1CO', 10, 28, '1CO.10.28', 'But if someone tells you, “This food was offered to idols,” then do not eat it, for the sake of the one who told you and for the sake of conscience—'),
('1CO', 10, 29, '1CO.10.29', 'the other one’s conscience, I mean, not your own. For why should my freedom be determined by someone else’s conscience?'),
('1CO', 10, 30, '1CO.10.30', 'If I partake in the meal with thankfulness, why am I denounced because of that for which I give thanks?'),
('1CO', 10, 31, '1CO.10.31', 'So whether you eat or drink or whatever you do, do it all to the glory of God.'),
('1CO', 10, 32, '1CO.10.32', 'Do not become a stumbling block, whether to Jews or Greeks or the church of God—'),
('1CO', 10, 33, '1CO.10.33', 'as I also try to please everyone in all I do. For I am not seeking my own good, but the good of many, that they may be saved.'),
('1CO', 11, 1, '1CO.11.1', 'You are to imitate me, just as I imitate Christ.'),
('1CO', 11, 2, '1CO.11.2', 'Now I commend you for remembering me in everything and for maintaining the traditions, just as I passed them on to you.'),
('1CO', 11, 3, '1CO.11.3', 'But I want you to understand that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God.'),
('1CO', 11, 4, '1CO.11.4', 'Every man who prays or prophesies with his head covered dishonors his head.'),
('1CO', 11, 5, '1CO.11.5', 'And every woman who prays or prophesies with her head uncovered dishonors her head, for it is just as if her head were shaved.'),
('1CO', 11, 6, '1CO.11.6', 'If a woman does not cover her head, she should have her hair cut off. And if it is shameful for a woman to have her hair cut or shaved off, she should cover her head.'),
('1CO', 11, 7, '1CO.11.7', 'A man ought not to cover his head, since he is the image and glory of God; but the woman is the glory of man.'),
('1CO', 11, 8, '1CO.11.8', 'For man did not come from woman, but woman from man.'),
('1CO', 11, 9, '1CO.11.9', 'Neither was man created for woman, but woman for man.'),
('1CO', 11, 10, '1CO.11.10', 'For this reason a woman ought to have a sign of authority on her head, because of the angels.'),
('1CO', 11, 11, '1CO.11.11', 'In the Lord, however, woman is not independent of man, nor is man independent of woman.'),
('1CO', 11, 12, '1CO.11.12', 'For just as woman came from man, so also man is born of woman. But everything comes from God.'),
('1CO', 11, 13, '1CO.11.13', 'Judge for yourselves: Is it proper for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered?'),
('1CO', 11, 14, '1CO.11.14', 'Doesn’t nature itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a disgrace to him,'),
('1CO', 11, 15, '1CO.11.15', 'but that if a woman has long hair, it is her glory? For long hair is given to her as a covering.'),
('1CO', 11, 16, '1CO.11.16', 'If anyone is inclined to dispute this, we have no other practice, nor do the churches of God.'),
('1CO', 11, 17, '1CO.11.17', 'In the following instructions I have no praise to offer, because your gatherings do more harm than good.'),
('1CO', 11, 18, '1CO.11.18', 'First of all, I hear that when you come together as a church, there are divisions among you, and in part I believe it.'),
('1CO', 11, 19, '1CO.11.19', 'And indeed, there must be differences among you to show which of you are approved.'),
('1CO', 11, 20, '1CO.11.20', 'Now then, when you come together, it is not the Lord’s Supper you eat.'),
('1CO', 11, 21, '1CO.11.21', 'For as you eat, each of you goes ahead without sharing his meal. While one remains hungry, another gets drunk.'),
('1CO', 11, 22, '1CO.11.22', 'Don’t you have your own homes in which to eat and drink? Or do you despise the church of God and humiliate those who have nothing? What can I say to you? Shall I praise you for this? No, I will not!'),
('1CO', 11, 23, '1CO.11.23', 'For I received from the Lord what I also passed on to you: The Lord Jesus, on the night He was betrayed, took bread,'),
('1CO', 11, 24, '1CO.11.24', 'and when He had given thanks, He broke it and said, “This is My body, which is for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”'),
('1CO', 11, 25, '1CO.11.25', 'In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood; do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of Me.”'),
('1CO', 11, 26, '1CO.11.26', 'For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim the Lord’s death until He comes.'),
('1CO', 11, 27, '1CO.11.27', 'Therefore, whoever eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner will be guilty of sinning against the body and blood of the Lord.'),
('1CO', 11, 28, '1CO.11.28', 'Each one must examine himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup.'),
('1CO', 11, 29, '1CO.11.29', 'For anyone who eats and drinks without recognizing the body eats and drinks judgment on himself.'),
('1CO', 11, 30, '1CO.11.30', 'That is why many among you are weak and sick, and a number of you have fallen asleep.'),
('1CO', 11, 31, '1CO.11.31', 'Now if we judged ourselves properly, we would not come under judgment.'),
('1CO', 11, 32, '1CO.11.32', 'But when we are judged by the Lord, we are being disciplined so that we will not be condemned with the world.'),
('1CO', 11, 33, '1CO.11.33', 'So, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for one another.'),
('1CO', 11, 34, '1CO.11.34', 'If anyone is hungry, he should eat at home, so that when you come together it will not result in judgment. And when I come, I will give instructions about the remaining matters.'),
('1CO', 12, 1, '1CO.12.1', 'Now about spiritual gifts, brothers, I do not want you to be uninformed.'),
('1CO', 12, 2, '1CO.12.2', 'You know that when you were pagans, you were influenced and led astray to mute idols.'),
('1CO', 12, 3, '1CO.12.3', 'Therefore I inform you that no one who is speaking by the Spirit of God says, “Jesus be cursed,” and no one can say, “Jesus is Lord,” except by the Holy Spirit.'),
('1CO', 12, 4, '1CO.12.4', 'There are different gifts, but the same Spirit.'),
('1CO', 12, 5, '1CO.12.5', 'There are different ministries, but the same Lord.'),
('1CO', 12, 6, '1CO.12.6', 'There are different ways of working, but the same God works all things in all people.'),
('1CO', 12, 7, '1CO.12.7', 'Now to each one the manifestation of the Spirit is given for the common good.'),
('1CO', 12, 8, '1CO.12.8', 'To one there is given through the Spirit the message of wisdom, to another the message of knowledge by the same Spirit,'),
('1CO', 12, 9, '1CO.12.9', 'to another faith by the same Spirit, to another gifts of healing by that one Spirit,'),
('1CO', 12, 10, '1CO.12.10', 'to another the working of miracles, to another prophecy, to another distinguishing between spirits, to another speaking in various tongues, and to still another the interpretation of tongues.'),
('1CO', 12, 11, '1CO.12.11', 'All these are the work of one and the same Spirit, who apportions them to each one as He determines.'),
('1CO', 12, 12, '1CO.12.12', 'The body is a unit, though it is composed of many parts. And although its parts are many, they all form one body. So it is with Christ.'),
('1CO', 12, 13, '1CO.12.13', 'For in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, slave or free, and we were all given one Spirit to drink.'),
('1CO', 12, 14, '1CO.12.14', 'For the body does not consist of one part, but of many.'),
('1CO', 12, 15, '1CO.12.15', 'If the foot should say, “Because I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.'),
('1CO', 12, 16, '1CO.12.16', 'And if the ear should say, “Because I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.'),
('1CO', 12, 17, '1CO.12.17', 'If the whole body were an eye, where would the sense of hearing be? If the whole body were an ear, where would the sense of smell be?'),
('1CO', 12, 18, '1CO.12.18', 'But in fact, God has arranged the members of the body, every one of them, according to His design.'),
('1CO', 12, 19, '1CO.12.19', 'If they were all one part, where would the body be?'),
('1CO', 12, 20, '1CO.12.20', 'As it is, there are many parts, but one body.'),
('1CO', 12, 21, '1CO.12.21', 'The eye cannot say to the hand, “I do not need you.” Nor can the head say to the feet, “I do not need you.”'),
('1CO', 12, 22, '1CO.12.22', 'On the contrary, the parts of the body that seem to be weaker are indispensable,'),
('1CO', 12, 23, '1CO.12.23', 'and the parts we consider less honorable, we treat with greater honor. And our unpresentable parts are treated with special modesty,'),
('1CO', 12, 24, '1CO.12.24', 'whereas our presentable parts have no such need. But God has composed the body and has given greater honor to the parts that lacked it,'),
('1CO', 12, 25, '1CO.12.25', 'so that there should be no division in the body, but that its members should have mutual concern for one another.'),
('1CO', 12, 26, '1CO.12.26', 'If one part suffers, every part suffers with it; if one part is honored, every part rejoices with it.'),
('1CO', 12, 27, '1CO.12.27', 'Now you are the body of Christ, and each of you is a member of it.'),
('1CO', 12, 28, '1CO.12.28', 'And in the church God has appointed first of all apostles, second prophets, third teachers, then workers of miracles, and those with gifts of healing, helping, administration, and various tongues.'),
('1CO', 12, 29, '1CO.12.29', 'Are all apostles? Are all prophets? Are all teachers? Do all work miracles?'),
('1CO', 12, 30, '1CO.12.30', 'Do all have gifts of healing? Do all speak in tongues? Do all interpret?'),
('1CO', 12, 31, '1CO.12.31', 'But eagerly desire the greater gifts. And now I will show you the most excellent way.'),
('1CO', 13, 1, '1CO.13.1', 'If I speak in the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love, I am only a ringing gong or a clanging cymbal.'),
('1CO', 13, 2, '1CO.13.2', 'If I have the gift of prophecy and can fathom all mysteries and all knowledge, and if I have absolute faith so as to move mountains, but have not love, I am nothing.'),
('1CO', 13, 3, '1CO.13.3', 'If I give all I possess to the poor and exult in the surrender of my body, but have not love, I gain nothing.'),
('1CO', 13, 4, '1CO.13.4', 'Love is patient, love is kind. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud.'),
('1CO', 13, 5, '1CO.13.5', 'It is not rude, it is not self-seeking, it is not easily angered, it keeps no account of wrongs.'),
('1CO', 13, 6, '1CO.13.6', 'Love takes no pleasure in evil, but rejoices in the truth.'),
('1CO', 13, 7, '1CO.13.7', 'It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things.'),
('1CO', 13, 8, '1CO.13.8', 'Love never fails. But where there are prophecies, they will cease; where there are tongues, they will be restrained; where there is knowledge, it will be dismissed.'),
('1CO', 13, 9, '1CO.13.9', 'For we know in part and we prophesy in part,'),
('1CO', 13, 10, '1CO.13.10', 'but when the perfect comes, the partial passes away.'),
('1CO', 13, 11, '1CO.13.11', 'When I was a child, I talked like a child, I thought like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I became a man, I set aside childish ways.'),
('1CO', 13, 12, '1CO.13.12', 'Now we see but a dim reflection as in a mirror; then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part; then I shall know fully, even as I am fully known.'),
('1CO', 13, 13, '1CO.13.13', 'And now these three remain: faith, hope, and love; but the greatest of these is love.'),
('1CO', 14, 1, '1CO.14.1', 'Earnestly pursue love and eagerly desire spiritual gifts, especially the gift of prophecy.'),
('1CO', 14, 2, '1CO.14.2', 'For he who speaks in a tongue does not speak to men, but to God. Indeed, no one understands him; he utters mysteries in the Spirit.'),
('1CO', 14, 3, '1CO.14.3', 'But he who prophesies speaks to men for their edification, encouragement, and comfort.'),
('1CO', 14, 4, '1CO.14.4', 'The one who speaks in a tongue edifies himself, but the one who prophesies edifies the church.'),
('1CO', 14, 5, '1CO.14.5', 'I wish that all of you could speak in tongues, but I would rather have you prophesy. He who prophesies is greater than one who speaks in tongues, unless he interprets so that the church may be edified.'),
('1CO', 14, 6, '1CO.14.6', 'Now, brothers, if I come to you speaking in tongues, how will I benefit you, unless I bring you some revelation or knowledge or prophecy or teaching?'),
('1CO', 14, 7, '1CO.14.7', 'Even in the case of lifeless instruments, such as the flute or harp, how will anyone recognize the tune they are playing unless the notes are distinct?'),
('1CO', 14, 8, '1CO.14.8', 'Again, if the trumpet sounds a muffled call, who will prepare for battle?'),
('1CO', 14, 9, '1CO.14.9', 'So it is with you. Unless you speak intelligible words with your tongue, how will anyone know what you are saying? You will just be speaking into the air.'),
('1CO', 14, 10, '1CO.14.10', 'Assuredly, there are many different languages in the world, yet none of them is without meaning.'),
('1CO', 14, 11, '1CO.14.11', 'If, then, I do not know the meaning of someone’s language, I am a foreigner to the speaker, and he is a foreigner to me.'),
('1CO', 14, 12, '1CO.14.12', 'It is the same with you. Since you are eager to have spiritual gifts, strive to excel in gifts that build up the church.'),
('1CO', 14, 13, '1CO.14.13', 'Therefore, the one who speaks in a tongue should pray that he may interpret.'),
('1CO', 14, 14, '1CO.14.14', 'For if I pray in a tongue, my spirit prays, but my mind is unfruitful.'),
('1CO', 14, 15, '1CO.14.15', 'What then shall I do? I will pray with my spirit, but I will also pray with my mind. I will sing with my spirit, but I will also sing with my mind.'),
('1CO', 14, 16, '1CO.14.16', 'Otherwise, if you speak a blessing in spirit, how can someone who is uninstructed say “Amen” to your thanksgiving, since he does not know what you are saying?'),
('1CO', 14, 17, '1CO.14.17', 'You may be giving thanks well enough, but the other one is not edified.'),
('1CO', 14, 18, '1CO.14.18', 'I thank God that I speak in tongues more than all of you.'),
('1CO', 14, 19, '1CO.14.19', 'But in the church, I would rather speak five coherent words to instruct others than ten thousand words in a tongue.'),
('1CO', 14, 20, '1CO.14.20', 'Brothers, stop thinking like children. In regard to evil be infants, but in your thinking be mature.'),
('1CO', 14, 21, '1CO.14.21', 'It is written in the Law: “By strange tongues and foreign lips I will speak to this people, but even then they will not listen to Me, says the Lord.”'),
('1CO', 14, 22, '1CO.14.22', 'Tongues, then, are a sign, not for believers, but for unbelievers. Prophecy, however, is for believers, not for unbelievers.'),
('1CO', 14, 23, '1CO.14.23', 'So if the whole church comes together and everyone speaks in tongues, and some who are uninstructed or some unbelievers come in, will they not say that you are out of your minds?'),
('1CO', 14, 24, '1CO.14.24', 'But if an unbeliever or uninstructed person comes in while everyone is prophesying, he will be convicted and called to account by all,'),
('1CO', 14, 25, '1CO.14.25', 'and the secrets of his heart will be made known. So he will fall facedown and worship God, proclaiming, “God is truly among you!”'),
('1CO', 14, 26, '1CO.14.26', 'What then shall we say, brothers? When you come together, everyone has a psalm or a teaching, a revelation, a tongue, or an interpretation. All of these must be done to build up the church.'),
('1CO', 14, 27, '1CO.14.27', 'If anyone speaks in a tongue, two, or at most three, should speak in turn, and someone must interpret.'),
('1CO', 14, 28, '1CO.14.28', 'But if there is no interpreter, he should remain silent in the church and speak only to himself and God.'),
('1CO', 14, 29, '1CO.14.29', 'Two or three prophets should speak, and the others should weigh carefully what is said.'),
('1CO', 14, 30, '1CO.14.30', 'And if a revelation comes to someone who is seated, the first speaker should stop.'),
('1CO', 14, 31, '1CO.14.31', 'For you can all prophesy in turn so that everyone may be instructed and encouraged.'),
('1CO', 14, 32, '1CO.14.32', 'The spirits of prophets are subject to prophets.'),
('1CO', 14, 33, '1CO.14.33', 'For God is not a God of disorder, but of peace—as in all the churches of the saints.'),
('1CO', 14, 34, '1CO.14.34', 'Women are to be silent in the churches. They are not permitted to speak, but must be in submission, as the law says.'),
('1CO', 14, 35, '1CO.14.35', 'If they wish to inquire about something, they are to ask their own husbands at home; for it is dishonorable for a woman to speak in the church.'),
('1CO', 14, 36, '1CO.14.36', 'Did the word of God originate with you? Or are you the only ones it has reached?'),
('1CO', 14, 37, '1CO.14.37', 'If anyone considers himself a prophet or spiritual person, let him acknowledge that what I am writing you is the Lord’s command.'),
('1CO', 14, 38, '1CO.14.38', 'But if anyone ignores this, he himself will be ignored.'),
('1CO', 14, 39, '1CO.14.39', 'So, my brothers, be eager to prophesy, and do not forbid speaking in tongues.'),
('1CO', 14, 40, '1CO.14.40', 'But everything must be done in a proper and orderly manner.'),
('1CO', 15, 1, '1CO.15.1', 'Now, brothers, I want to remind you of the gospel I preached to you, which you received, and in which you stand firm.'),
('1CO', 15, 2, '1CO.15.2', 'By this gospel you are saved, if you hold firmly to the word I preached to you. Otherwise, you have believed in vain.'),
('1CO', 15, 3, '1CO.15.3', 'For what I received I passed on to you as of first importance: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,'),
('1CO', 15, 4, '1CO.15.4', 'that He was buried, that He was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,'),
('1CO', 15, 5, '1CO.15.5', 'and that He appeared to Cephas and then to the Twelve.'),
('1CO', 15, 6, '1CO.15.6', 'After that, He appeared to more than five hundred brothers at once, most of whom are still living, though some have fallen asleep.'),
('1CO', 15, 7, '1CO.15.7', 'Then He appeared to James, then to all the apostles.'),
('1CO', 15, 8, '1CO.15.8', 'And last of all He appeared to me also, as to one of untimely birth.'),
('1CO', 15, 9, '1CO.15.9', 'For I am the least of the apostles and am unworthy to be called an apostle, because I persecuted the church of God.'),
('1CO', 15, 10, '1CO.15.10', 'But by the grace of God I am what I am, and His grace to me was not in vain. No, I worked harder than all of them—yet not I, but the grace of God that was with me.'),
('1CO', 15, 11, '1CO.15.11', 'Whether, then, it was I or they, this is what we preach, and this is what you believed.'),
('1CO', 15, 12, '1CO.15.12', 'But if it is preached that Christ has been raised from the dead, how can some of you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?'),
('1CO', 15, 13, '1CO.15.13', 'If there is no resurrection of the dead, then not even Christ has been raised.'),
('1CO', 15, 14, '1CO.15.14', 'And if Christ has not been raised, our preaching is worthless, and so is your faith.'),
('1CO', 15, 15, '1CO.15.15', 'In that case, we are also exposed as false witnesses about God. For we have testified about God that He raised Christ from the dead, but He did not raise Him if in fact the dead are not raised.'),
('1CO', 15, 16, '1CO.15.16', 'For if the dead are not raised, then not even Christ has been raised.'),
('1CO', 15, 17, '1CO.15.17', 'And if Christ has not been raised, your faith is futile; you are still in your sins.'),
('1CO', 15, 18, '1CO.15.18', 'Then those also who have fallen asleep in Christ have perished.'),
('1CO', 15, 19, '1CO.15.19', 'If our hope in Christ is for this life alone, we are to be pitied more than all men.'),
('1CO', 15, 20, '1CO.15.20', 'But Christ has indeed been raised from the dead, the firstfruits of those who have fallen asleep.'),
('1CO', 15, 21, '1CO.15.21', 'For since death came through a man, the resurrection of the dead comes also through a man.'),
('1CO', 15, 22, '1CO.15.22', 'For as in Adam all die, so in Christ all will be made alive.'),
('1CO', 15, 23, '1CO.15.23', 'But each in his own turn: Christ the firstfruits; then at His coming, those who belong to Him.'),
('1CO', 15, 24, '1CO.15.24', 'Then the end will come, when He hands over the kingdom to God the Father after He has destroyed all dominion, authority, and power.'),
('1CO', 15, 25, '1CO.15.25', 'For He must reign until He has put all His enemies under His feet.'),
('1CO', 15, 26, '1CO.15.26', 'The last enemy to be destroyed is death.'),
('1CO', 15, 27, '1CO.15.27', 'For “God has put everything under His feet.” Now when it says that everything has been put under Him, this clearly does not include the One who put everything under Him.'),
('1CO', 15, 28, '1CO.15.28', 'And when all things have been subjected to Him, then the Son Himself will be made subject to Him who put all things under Him, so that God may be all in all.'),
('1CO', 15, 29, '1CO.15.29', 'If these things are not so, what will those do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead are not raised at all, why are people baptized for them?'),
('1CO', 15, 30, '1CO.15.30', 'And why do we endanger ourselves every hour?'),
('1CO', 15, 31, '1CO.15.31', 'I face death every day, brothers, as surely as I boast about you in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('1CO', 15, 32, '1CO.15.32', 'If I fought wild beasts in Ephesus for human motives, what did I gain? If the dead are not raised, “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die.”'),
('1CO', 15, 33, '1CO.15.33', 'Do not be deceived: “Bad company corrupts good character.”'),
('1CO', 15, 34, '1CO.15.34', 'Sober up as you ought, and stop sinning; for some of you are ignorant of God. I say this to your shame.'),
('1CO', 15, 35, '1CO.15.35', 'But someone will ask, “How are the dead raised? With what kind of body will they come?”'),
('1CO', 15, 36, '1CO.15.36', 'You fool! What you sow does not come to life unless it dies.'),
('1CO', 15, 37, '1CO.15.37', 'And what you sow is not the body that will be, but just a seed, perhaps of wheat or something else.'),
('1CO', 15, 38, '1CO.15.38', 'But God gives it a body as He has designed, and to each kind of seed He gives its own body.'),
('1CO', 15, 39, '1CO.15.39', 'Not all flesh is the same: Men have one kind of flesh, animals have another, birds another, and fish another.'),
('1CO', 15, 40, '1CO.15.40', 'There are also heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. But the splendor of the heavenly bodies is of one degree, and the splendor of the earthly bodies is of another.'),
('1CO', 15, 41, '1CO.15.41', 'The sun has one degree of splendor, the moon another, and the stars another; and star differs from star in splendor.'),
('1CO', 15, 42, '1CO.15.42', 'So will it be with the resurrection of the dead: What is sown is perishable; it is raised imperishable.'),
('1CO', 15, 43, '1CO.15.43', 'It is sown in dishonor; it is raised in glory. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power.'),
('1CO', 15, 44, '1CO.15.44', 'It is sown a natural body; it is raised a spiritual body. If there is a natural body, there is also a spiritual body.'),
('1CO', 15, 45, '1CO.15.45', 'So it is written: “The first man Adam became a living being”; the last Adam a life-giving spirit.'),
('1CO', 15, 46, '1CO.15.46', 'The spiritual, however, was not first, but the natural, and then the spiritual.'),
('1CO', 15, 47, '1CO.15.47', 'The first man was of the dust of the earth, the second man from heaven.'),
('1CO', 15, 48, '1CO.15.48', 'As was the earthly man, so also are those who are of the earth; and as is the heavenly man, so also are those who are of heaven.'),
('1CO', 15, 49, '1CO.15.49', 'And just as we have borne the likeness of the earthly man, so also shall we bear the likeness of the heavenly man.'),
('1CO', 15, 50, '1CO.15.50', 'Now I declare to you, brothers, that flesh and blood cannot inherit the kingdom of God, nor does the perishable inherit the imperishable.'),
('1CO', 15, 51, '1CO.15.51', 'Listen, I tell you a mystery: We will not all sleep, but we will all be changed—'),
('1CO', 15, 52, '1CO.15.52', 'in an instant, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound, the dead will be raised imperishable, and we will be changed.'),
('1CO', 15, 53, '1CO.15.53', 'For the perishable must be clothed with the imperishable, and the mortal with immortality.'),
('1CO', 15, 54, '1CO.15.54', 'When the perishable has been clothed with the imperishable and the mortal with immortality, then the saying that is written will come to pass: “Death has been swallowed up in victory.”'),
('1CO', 15, 55, '1CO.15.55', '“Where, O Death, is your victory? Where, O Death, is your sting?”'),
('1CO', 15, 56, '1CO.15.56', 'The sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law.'),
('1CO', 15, 57, '1CO.15.57', 'But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ!'),
('1CO', 15, 58, '1CO.15.58', 'Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast and immovable. Always excel in the work of the Lord, because you know that your labor in the Lord is not in vain.'),
('1CO', 16, 1, '1CO.16.1', 'Now about the collection for the saints, you are to do as I directed the churches of Galatia:'),
('1CO', 16, 2, '1CO.16.2', 'On the first day of every week, each of you should set aside a portion of his income, saving it up, so that when I come no collections will be needed.'),
('1CO', 16, 3, '1CO.16.3', 'Then, on my arrival, I will send letters with those you recommend to carry your gift to Jerusalem.'),
('1CO', 16, 4, '1CO.16.4', 'And if it is advisable for me to go also, they can travel with me.'),
('1CO', 16, 5, '1CO.16.5', 'After I go through Macedonia, however, I will come to you; for I will be going through Macedonia.'),
('1CO', 16, 6, '1CO.16.6', 'Perhaps I will stay with you awhile, or even spend the winter, so that you can help me on my journey, wherever I go.'),
('1CO', 16, 7, '1CO.16.7', 'For I do not want to see you now only in passing; I hope to spend some time with you, if the Lord permits.'),
('1CO', 16, 8, '1CO.16.8', 'But I will stay in Ephesus until Pentecost,'),
('1CO', 16, 9, '1CO.16.9', 'because a great door for effective work has opened to me, even though many oppose me.'),
('1CO', 16, 10, '1CO.16.10', 'If Timothy comes, see to it that he has nothing to fear while he is with you, for he is doing the work of the Lord, just as I am.'),
('1CO', 16, 11, '1CO.16.11', 'No one, then, should treat him with contempt. Send him on his way in peace so that he can return to me, for I am expecting him along with the brothers.'),
('1CO', 16, 12, '1CO.16.12', 'Now about our brother Apollos: I strongly urged him to go to you with the brothers. He was not at all inclined to go now, but he will go when he has the opportunity.'),
('1CO', 16, 13, '1CO.16.13', 'Be on the alert. Stand firm in the faith. Be men of courage. Be strong.'),
('1CO', 16, 14, '1CO.16.14', 'Do everything in love.'),
('1CO', 16, 15, '1CO.16.15', 'You know that Stephanas and his household were the first converts in Achaia, and they have devoted themselves to the service of the saints. Now I urge you, brothers,'),
('1CO', 16, 16, '1CO.16.16', 'to submit to such as these, and to every fellow worker and laborer.'),
('1CO', 16, 17, '1CO.16.17', 'I am glad that Stephanas, Fortunatus, and Achaicus have arrived, because they have supplied what was lacking from you.'),
('1CO', 16, 18, '1CO.16.18', 'For they refreshed my spirit and yours as well. Show your appreciation, therefore, to such men.'),
('1CO', 16, 19, '1CO.16.19', 'The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.'),
('1CO', 16, 20, '1CO.16.20', 'All the brothers here send you greetings. Greet one another with a holy kiss.'),
('1CO', 16, 21, '1CO.16.21', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul.'),
('1CO', 16, 22, '1CO.16.22', 'If anyone does not love the Lord, let him be under a curse. Come, O Lord!'),
('1CO', 16, 23, '1CO.16.23', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with you.'),
('1CO', 16, 24, '1CO.16.24', 'My love be with all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen.'),
('2CO', 1, 1, '2CO.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God in Corinth, together with all the saints throughout Achaia:'),
('2CO', 1, 2, '2CO.1.2', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('2CO', 1, 3, '2CO.1.3', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of compassion and the God of all comfort,'),
('2CO', 1, 4, '2CO.1.4', 'who comforts us in all our troubles, so that we can comfort those in any trouble with the comfort we ourselves have received from God.'),
('2CO', 1, 5, '2CO.1.5', 'For just as the sufferings of Christ overflow to us, so also through Christ our comfort overflows.'),
('2CO', 1, 6, '2CO.1.6', 'If we are afflicted, it is for your comfort and salvation; if we are comforted, it is for your comfort, which accomplishes in you patient endurance of the same sufferings we experience.'),
('2CO', 1, 7, '2CO.1.7', 'And our hope for you is sure, because we know that just as you share in our sufferings, so also you will share in our comfort.'),
('2CO', 1, 8, '2CO.1.8', 'We do not want you to be unaware, brothers, of the hardships we encountered in the province of Asia. We were under a burden far beyond our ability to endure, so that we despaired even of life.'),
('2CO', 1, 9, '2CO.1.9', 'Indeed, we felt we were under the sentence of death, in order that we would not trust in ourselves, but in God, who raises the dead.'),
('2CO', 1, 10, '2CO.1.10', 'He has delivered us from such a deadly peril, and He will deliver us. In Him we have placed our hope that He will yet again deliver us,'),
('2CO', 1, 11, '2CO.1.11', 'as you help us by your prayers. Then many will give thanks on our behalf for the favor shown us in answer to their prayers.'),
('2CO', 1, 12, '2CO.1.12', 'For this is our boast: Our conscience testifies that we have conducted ourselves in the world, and especially in relation to you, in the holiness and sincerity that are from God—not in worldly wisdom, but in the grace of God.'),
('2CO', 1, 13, '2CO.1.13', 'For we do not write you anything that is beyond your ability to read and understand. And I hope that you will understand us completely,'),
('2CO', 1, 14, '2CO.1.14', 'as you have already understood us in part, that you may boast of us just as we will boast of you in the day of our Lord Jesus.'),
('2CO', 1, 15, '2CO.1.15', 'Confident of this, I planned to visit you first, so that you might receive a double blessing.'),
('2CO', 1, 16, '2CO.1.16', 'I wanted to visit you on my way to Macedonia, and to return to you from Macedonia, and then to have you help me on my way to Judea.'),
('2CO', 1, 17, '2CO.1.17', 'When I planned this, did I do it carelessly? Or do I make my plans by human standards, so as to say “Yes, yes” and also “No, no”?'),
('2CO', 1, 18, '2CO.1.18', 'But as surely as God is faithful, our message to you is not “Yes” and “No.”'),
('2CO', 1, 19, '2CO.1.19', 'For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was proclaimed among you by me and Silvanus and Timothy, was not “Yes” and “No,” but in Him it has always been “Yes.”'),
('2CO', 1, 20, '2CO.1.20', 'For all the promises of God are “Yes” in Christ. And so through Him, our “Amen” is spoken to the glory of God.'),
('2CO', 1, 21, '2CO.1.21', 'Now it is God who establishes both us and you in Christ. He anointed us,'),
('2CO', 1, 22, '2CO.1.22', 'placed His seal on us, and put His Spirit in our hearts as a pledge of what is to come.'),
('2CO', 1, 23, '2CO.1.23', 'I call God as my witness that it was in order to spare you that I did not return to Corinth.'),
('2CO', 1, 24, '2CO.1.24', 'Not that we lord it over your faith, but we are fellow workers with you for your joy, because it is by faith that you stand firm.'),
('2CO', 2, 1, '2CO.2.1', 'So I made up my mind not to make another painful visit to you.'),
('2CO', 2, 2, '2CO.2.2', 'For if I grieve you, who is left to cheer me but those whom I have grieved?'),
('2CO', 2, 3, '2CO.2.3', 'I wrote as I did so that on my arrival I would not be grieved by those who ought to make me rejoice. I had confidence in all of you, that you would share my joy.'),
('2CO', 2, 4, '2CO.2.4', 'For through many tears I wrote you out of great distress and anguish of heart, not to grieve you but to let you know how much I love you.'),
('2CO', 2, 5, '2CO.2.5', 'Now if anyone has caused grief, he has not grieved me but all of you—to some degree, not to overstate it.'),
('2CO', 2, 6, '2CO.2.6', 'The punishment imposed on him by the majority is sufficient for him.'),
('2CO', 2, 7, '2CO.2.7', 'So instead, you ought to forgive and comfort him, so that he will not be overwhelmed by excessive sorrow.'),
('2CO', 2, 8, '2CO.2.8', 'Therefore I urge you to reaffirm your love for him.'),
('2CO', 2, 9, '2CO.2.9', 'My purpose in writing you was to see if you would stand the test and be obedient in everything.'),
('2CO', 2, 10, '2CO.2.10', 'If you forgive anyone, I also forgive him. And if I have forgiven anything, I have forgiven it in the presence of Christ for your sake,'),
('2CO', 2, 11, '2CO.2.11', 'in order that Satan should not outwit us. For we are not unaware of his schemes.'),
('2CO', 2, 12, '2CO.2.12', 'Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,'),
('2CO', 2, 13, '2CO.2.13', 'I had no peace in my spirit, because I did not find my brother Titus there. So I said goodbye to them and went on to Macedonia.'),
('2CO', 2, 14, '2CO.2.14', 'But thanks be to God, who always leads us triumphantly as captives in Christ and through us spreads everywhere the fragrance of the knowledge of Him.'),
('2CO', 2, 15, '2CO.2.15', 'For we are to God the sweet aroma of Christ among those who are being saved and those who are perishing.'),
('2CO', 2, 16, '2CO.2.16', 'To the one we are an odor that brings death, to the other a fragrance that brings life. And who is qualified for such a task?'),
('2CO', 2, 17, '2CO.2.17', 'For we are not like so many others, who peddle the word of God for profit. On the contrary, in Christ we speak before God with sincerity, as men sent from God.'),
('2CO', 3, 1, '2CO.3.1', 'Are we beginning to commend ourselves again? Or do we need, like some people, letters of recommendation to you or from you?'),
('2CO', 3, 2, '2CO.3.2', 'You yourselves are our letter, inscribed on our hearts, known and read by everyone.'),
('2CO', 3, 3, '2CO.3.3', 'It is clear that you are a letter from Christ, the result of our ministry, written not with ink but with the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone but on tablets of human hearts.'),
('2CO', 3, 4, '2CO.3.4', 'Such confidence before God is ours through Christ.'),
('2CO', 3, 5, '2CO.3.5', 'Not that we are competent in ourselves to claim that anything comes from us, but our competence comes from God.'),
('2CO', 3, 6, '2CO.3.6', 'And He has qualified us as ministers of a new covenant, not of the letter but of the Spirit; for the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.'),
('2CO', 3, 7, '2CO.3.7', 'Now if the ministry of death, which was engraved in letters on stone, came with such glory that the Israelites could not gaze at the face of Moses because of its fleeting glory,'),
('2CO', 3, 8, '2CO.3.8', 'will not the ministry of the Spirit be even more glorious?'),
('2CO', 3, 9, '2CO.3.9', 'For if the ministry of condemnation was glorious, how much more glorious is the ministry of righteousness!'),
('2CO', 3, 10, '2CO.3.10', 'Indeed, what was once glorious has no glory now in comparison to the glory that surpasses it.'),
('2CO', 3, 11, '2CO.3.11', 'For if what was fading away came with glory, how much greater is the glory of that which endures!'),
('2CO', 3, 12, '2CO.3.12', 'Therefore, since we have such a hope, we are very bold.'),
('2CO', 3, 13, '2CO.3.13', 'We are not like Moses, who would put a veil over his face to keep the Israelites from gazing at the end of what was fading away.'),
('2CO', 3, 14, '2CO.3.14', 'But their minds were closed. For to this day the same veil remains at the reading of the old covenant. It has not been lifted, because only in Christ can it be removed.'),
('2CO', 3, 15, '2CO.3.15', 'And even to this day when Moses is read, a veil covers their hearts.'),
('2CO', 3, 16, '2CO.3.16', 'But whenever anyone turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away.'),
('2CO', 3, 17, '2CO.3.17', 'Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom.'),
('2CO', 3, 18, '2CO.3.18', 'And we, who with unveiled faces all reflect the glory of the Lord, are being transformed into His image with intensifying glory, which comes from the Lord, who is the Spirit.'),
('2CO', 4, 1, '2CO.4.1', 'Therefore, since God in His mercy has given us this ministry, we do not lose heart.'),
('2CO', 4, 2, '2CO.4.2', 'Instead, we have renounced secret and shameful ways. We do not practice deceit, nor do we distort the word of God. On the contrary, by open proclamation of the truth, we commend ourselves to every man’s conscience in the sight of God.'),
('2CO', 4, 3, '2CO.4.3', 'And even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those who are perishing.'),
('2CO', 4, 4, '2CO.4.4', 'The god of this age has blinded the minds of unbelievers, so they cannot see the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God.'),
('2CO', 4, 5, '2CO.4.5', 'For we do not proclaim ourselves, but Jesus Christ as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus’ sake.'),
('2CO', 4, 6, '2CO.4.6', 'For God, who said, “Let light shine out of darkness,” made His light shine in our hearts to give us the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.'),
('2CO', 4, 7, '2CO.4.7', 'Now we have this treasure in jars of clay to show that this surpassingly great power is from God and not from us.'),
('2CO', 4, 8, '2CO.4.8', 'We are hard pressed on all sides, but not crushed; perplexed, but not in despair;'),
('2CO', 4, 9, '2CO.4.9', 'persecuted, but not forsaken; struck down, but not destroyed.'),
('2CO', 4, 10, '2CO.4.10', 'We always carry around in our body the death of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our body.'),
('2CO', 4, 11, '2CO.4.11', 'For we who are alive are always consigned to death for Jesus’ sake, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our mortal body.'),
('2CO', 4, 12, '2CO.4.12', 'So then, death is at work in us, but life is at work in you.'),
('2CO', 4, 13, '2CO.4.13', 'And in keeping with what is written, “I believed, therefore I have spoken,” we who have the same spirit of faith also believe and therefore speak,'),
('2CO', 4, 14, '2CO.4.14', 'knowing that the One who raised the Lord Jesus will also raise us with Jesus and present us with you in His presence.'),
('2CO', 4, 15, '2CO.4.15', 'All this is for your benefit, so that the grace that is extending to more and more people may cause thanksgiving to overflow, to the glory of God.'),
('2CO', 4, 16, '2CO.4.16', 'Therefore we do not lose heart. Though our outer self is wasting away, yet our inner self is being renewed day by day.'),
('2CO', 4, 17, '2CO.4.17', 'For our light and momentary affliction is producing for us an eternal weight of glory that is far beyond comparison.'),
('2CO', 4, 18, '2CO.4.18', 'So we fix our eyes not on what is seen, but on what is unseen. For what is seen is temporary, but what is unseen is eternal.'),
('2CO', 5, 1, '2CO.5.1', 'For we know that if the earthly tent we live in is dismantled, we have a building from God, an eternal house in heaven, not built by human hands.'),
('2CO', 5, 2, '2CO.5.2', 'For in this tent we groan, longing to be clothed with our heavenly dwelling,'),
('2CO', 5, 3, '2CO.5.3', 'because when we are clothed, we will not be found naked.'),
('2CO', 5, 4, '2CO.5.4', 'For while we are in this tent, we groan under our burdens, because we do not wish to be unclothed but clothed, so that our mortality may be swallowed up by life.'),
('2CO', 5, 5, '2CO.5.5', 'And it is God who has prepared us for this very purpose and has given us the Spirit as a pledge of what is to come.'),
('2CO', 5, 6, '2CO.5.6', 'Therefore we are always confident, although we know that while we are at home in the body, we are away from the Lord.'),
('2CO', 5, 7, '2CO.5.7', 'For we walk by faith, not by sight.'),
('2CO', 5, 8, '2CO.5.8', 'We are confident, then, and would prefer to be away from the body and at home with the Lord.'),
('2CO', 5, 9, '2CO.5.9', 'So we aspire to please Him, whether we are at home in this body or away from it.'),
('2CO', 5, 10, '2CO.5.10', 'For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ, that each one may receive his due for the things done in the body, whether good or bad.'),
('2CO', 5, 11, '2CO.5.11', 'Therefore, since we know what it means to fear the Lord, we try to persuade men. What we are is clear to God, and I hope it is clear to your conscience as well.'),
('2CO', 5, 12, '2CO.5.12', 'We are not commending ourselves to you again. Instead, we are giving you an occasion to be proud of us, so that you can answer those who take pride in appearances rather than in the heart.'),
('2CO', 5, 13, '2CO.5.13', 'If we are out of our mind, it is for God; if we are of sound mind, it is for you.'),
('2CO', 5, 14, '2CO.5.14', 'For Christ’s love compels us, because we are convinced that One died for all, therefore all died.'),
('2CO', 5, 15, '2CO.5.15', 'And He died for all, that those who live should no longer live for themselves, but for Him who died for them and was raised again.'),
('2CO', 5, 16, '2CO.5.16', 'So from now on we regard no one according to the flesh. Although we once regarded Christ in this way, we do so no longer.'),
('2CO', 5, 17, '2CO.5.17', 'Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old has passed away. Behold, the new has come!'),
('2CO', 5, 18, '2CO.5.18', 'All this is from God, who reconciled us to Himself through Christ and gave us the ministry of reconciliation:'),
('2CO', 5, 19, '2CO.5.19', 'that God was reconciling the world to Himself in Christ, not counting men’s trespasses against them. And He has committed to us the message of reconciliation.'),
('2CO', 5, 20, '2CO.5.20', 'Therefore we are ambassadors for Christ, as though God were making His appeal through us. We implore you on behalf of Christ: Be reconciled to God.'),
('2CO', 5, 21, '2CO.5.21', 'God made Him who knew no sin to be sin on our behalf, so that in Him we might become the righteousness of God.'),
('2CO', 6, 1, '2CO.6.1', 'As God’s fellow workers, then, we urge you not to receive God’s grace in vain.'),
('2CO', 6, 2, '2CO.6.2', 'For He says: “In the time of favor I heard you, and in the day of salvation I helped you.” Behold, now is the time of favor; now is the day of salvation!'),
('2CO', 6, 3, '2CO.6.3', 'We put no obstacle in anyone’s way, so that no one can discredit our ministry.'),
('2CO', 6, 4, '2CO.6.4', 'Rather, as servants of God we commend ourselves in every way: in great endurance; in troubles, hardships, and calamities;'),
('2CO', 6, 5, '2CO.6.5', 'in beatings, imprisonments, and riots; in labor, sleepless nights, and hunger;'),
('2CO', 6, 6, '2CO.6.6', 'in purity, knowledge, patience, and kindness; in the Holy Spirit and in sincere love;'),
('2CO', 6, 7, '2CO.6.7', 'in truthful speech and in the power of God; with the weapons of righteousness in the right hand and in the left;'),
('2CO', 6, 8, '2CO.6.8', 'through glory and dishonor, slander and praise; viewed as imposters, yet genuine;'),
('2CO', 6, 9, '2CO.6.9', 'unknown, yet well-known; dying, and yet we live on; punished, yet not killed;'),
('2CO', 6, 10, '2CO.6.10', 'sorrowful, yet always rejoicing; poor, yet making many rich; having nothing, and yet possessing everything.'),
('2CO', 6, 11, '2CO.6.11', 'We have spoken freely to you, Corinthians. Our hearts are open wide.'),
('2CO', 6, 12, '2CO.6.12', 'It is not our affection, but yours, that is restrained.'),
('2CO', 6, 13, '2CO.6.13', 'As a fair exchange—I speak as to my children—open wide your hearts also.'),
('2CO', 6, 14, '2CO.6.14', 'Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers. For what partnership can righteousness have with wickedness? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?'),
('2CO', 6, 15, '2CO.6.15', 'What harmony is there between Christ and Belial? Or what does a believer have in common with an unbeliever?'),
('2CO', 6, 16, '2CO.6.16', 'What agreement can exist between the temple of God and idols? For we are the temple of the living God. As God has said: “I will dwell with them and walk among them, and I will be their God, and they will be My people.”'),
('2CO', 6, 17, '2CO.6.17', '“Therefore come out from among them and be separate, says the Lord. Touch no unclean thing, and I will receive you.”'),
('2CO', 6, 18, '2CO.6.18', 'And: “I will be a Father to you, and you will be My sons and daughters, says the Lord Almighty.”'),
('2CO', 7, 1, '2CO.7.1', 'Therefore, beloved, since we have these promises, let us cleanse ourselves from everything that defiles body and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God.'),
('2CO', 7, 2, '2CO.7.2', 'Make room for us in your hearts. We have wronged no one, we have corrupted no one, we have exploited no one.'),
('2CO', 7, 3, '2CO.7.3', 'I do not say this to condemn you. I have said before that you so occupy our hearts that we live and die together with you.'),
('2CO', 7, 4, '2CO.7.4', 'Great is my confidence in you; great is my pride in you; I am filled with encouragement; in all our troubles my joy overflows.'),
('2CO', 7, 5, '2CO.7.5', 'For when we arrived in Macedonia, our bodies had no rest, but we were pressed from every direction—conflicts on the outside, fears within.'),
('2CO', 7, 6, '2CO.7.6', 'But God, who comforts the downcast, comforted us by the arrival of Titus,'),
('2CO', 7, 7, '2CO.7.7', 'and not only by his arrival, but also by the comfort he had received from you. He told us about your longing, your mourning, and your zeal for me, so that I rejoiced all the more.'),
('2CO', 7, 8, '2CO.7.8', 'Even if I caused you sorrow by my letter, I do not regret it. Although I did regret it—for I see that my letter caused you sorrow, but only for a short time—'),
('2CO', 7, 9, '2CO.7.9', 'yet now I rejoice, not because you were made sorrowful, but because your sorrow led you to repentance. For you felt the sorrow that God had intended, and so were not harmed in any way by us.'),
('2CO', 7, 10, '2CO.7.10', 'Godly sorrow brings repentance that leads to salvation without regret, but worldly sorrow brings death.'),
('2CO', 7, 11, '2CO.7.11', 'Consider what this godly sorrow has produced in you: what earnestness, what eagerness to clear yourselves, what indignation, what alarm, what longing, what zeal, what vindication! In every way you have proved yourselves to be innocent in this matter.'),
('2CO', 7, 12, '2CO.7.12', 'So even though I wrote to you, it was not on account of the one who did wrong or the one who was harmed, but rather that your earnestness on our behalf would be made clear to you in the sight of God.'),
('2CO', 7, 13, '2CO.7.13', 'On account of this, we are encouraged. In addition to our own encouragement, we were even more delighted by the joy of Titus. For his spirit has been refreshed by all of you.'),
('2CO', 7, 14, '2CO.7.14', 'Indeed, I was not embarrassed by anything I had boasted to him about you. But just as everything we said to you was true, so our boasting to Titus has proved to be true as well.'),
('2CO', 7, 15, '2CO.7.15', 'And his affection for you is even greater when he remembers that you were all obedient as you welcomed him with fear and trembling.'),
('2CO', 7, 16, '2CO.7.16', 'I rejoice that I can have complete confidence in you.'),
('2CO', 8, 1, '2CO.8.1', 'Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia.'),
('2CO', 8, 2, '2CO.8.2', 'In the terrible ordeal they suffered, their abundant joy and deep poverty overflowed into rich generosity.'),
('2CO', 8, 3, '2CO.8.3', 'For I testify that they gave according to their ability and even beyond it. Of their own accord,'),
('2CO', 8, 4, '2CO.8.4', 'they earnestly pleaded with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints.'),
('2CO', 8, 5, '2CO.8.5', 'And not only did they do as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and then to us, through the will of God.'),
('2CO', 8, 6, '2CO.8.6', 'So we urged Titus to help complete your act of grace, just as he had started it.'),
('2CO', 8, 7, '2CO.8.7', 'But just as you excel in everything—in faith, in speech, in knowledge, in complete earnestness, and in the love we inspired in you—see that you also excel in this grace of giving.'),
('2CO', 8, 8, '2CO.8.8', 'I am not giving a command, but I am testing the sincerity of your love through the earnestness of others.'),
('2CO', 8, 9, '2CO.8.9', 'For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sake He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich.'),
('2CO', 8, 10, '2CO.8.10', 'And this is my opinion about what is helpful for you in this matter: Last year you were the first not only to give, but even to have such a desire.'),
('2CO', 8, 11, '2CO.8.11', 'Now finish the work, so that you may complete it with the same eager desire, according to your means.'),
('2CO', 8, 12, '2CO.8.12', 'For if the eagerness is there, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what he does not have.'),
('2CO', 8, 13, '2CO.8.13', 'It is not our intention that others may be relieved while you are burdened, but that there may be equality.'),
('2CO', 8, 14, '2CO.8.14', 'At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. This way there will be equality.'),
('2CO', 8, 15, '2CO.8.15', 'As it is written: “He who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall.”'),
('2CO', 8, 16, '2CO.8.16', 'But thanks be to God, who put into the heart of Titus the same devotion I have for you.'),
('2CO', 8, 17, '2CO.8.17', 'For not only did he welcome our appeal, but he is eagerly coming to you of his own volition.'),
('2CO', 8, 18, '2CO.8.18', 'Along with Titus we are sending the brother who is praised by all the churches for his work in the gospel.'),
('2CO', 8, 19, '2CO.8.19', 'More than that, this brother was chosen by the churches to accompany us with the gracious offering we administer to honor the Lord Himself and to show our eagerness to help.'),
('2CO', 8, 20, '2CO.8.20', 'We want to avoid any criticism of the way we administer this generous gift.'),
('2CO', 8, 21, '2CO.8.21', 'For we are taking great care to do what is right, not only in the eyes of the Lord, but also in the eyes of men.'),
('2CO', 8, 22, '2CO.8.22', 'And we are sending along with them our brother who has proven his earnestness to us many times and in many ways, and now even more so by his great confidence in you.'),
('2CO', 8, 23, '2CO.8.23', 'As for Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker among you. As for our brothers, they are messengers of the churches, the glory of Christ.'),
('2CO', 8, 24, '2CO.8.24', 'In full view of the churches, then, show these men the proof of your love and the reason for our boasting about you.'),
('2CO', 9, 1, '2CO.9.1', 'Now about the service to the saints, there is no need for me to write to you.'),
('2CO', 9, 2, '2CO.9.2', 'For I know your eagerness to help, and I have been boasting to the Macedonians that since last year you in Achaia were prepared to give. And your zeal has stirred most of them to do likewise.'),
('2CO', 9, 3, '2CO.9.3', 'But I am sending the brothers in order that our boasting about you in this matter should not prove empty, but that you will be prepared, just as I said.'),
('2CO', 9, 4, '2CO.9.4', 'Otherwise, if any Macedonians come with me and find you unprepared, we—to say nothing of you—would be ashamed of having been so confident.'),
('2CO', 9, 5, '2CO.9.5', 'So I thought it necessary to urge the brothers to visit you beforehand and make arrangements for the generous gift you had promised. This way, your gift will be prepared generously and not begrudgingly.'),
('2CO', 9, 6, '2CO.9.6', 'Remember this: Whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and whoever sows generously will also reap generously.'),
('2CO', 9, 7, '2CO.9.7', 'Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver.'),
('2CO', 9, 8, '2CO.9.8', 'And God is able to make all grace abound to you, so that in all things, at all times, having all that you need, you will abound in every good work.'),
('2CO', 9, 9, '2CO.9.9', 'As it is written: “He has scattered abroad His gifts to the poor; His righteousness endures forever.”'),
('2CO', 9, 10, '2CO.9.10', 'Now He who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your store of seed and will increase the harvest of your righteousness.'),
('2CO', 9, 11, '2CO.9.11', 'You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, and through us your generosity will produce thanksgiving to God.'),
('2CO', 9, 12, '2CO.9.12', 'For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God.'),
('2CO', 9, 13, '2CO.9.13', 'Because of the proof this ministry provides, the saints will glorify God for your obedient confession of the gospel of Christ, and for the generosity of your contribution to them and to all the others.'),
('2CO', 9, 14, '2CO.9.14', 'And their prayers for you will express their affection for you, because of the surpassing grace God has given you.'),
('2CO', 9, 15, '2CO.9.15', 'Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift!'),
('2CO', 10, 1, '2CO.10.1', 'Now by the mildness and gentleness of Christ, I appeal to you—I, Paul, who am humble when face to face with you, but bold when away.'),
('2CO', 10, 2, '2CO.10.2', 'I beg you that when I come I may not need to be as bold as I expect toward those who presume that we live according to the flesh.'),
('2CO', 10, 3, '2CO.10.3', 'For though we live in the flesh, we do not wage war according to the flesh.'),
('2CO', 10, 4, '2CO.10.4', 'The weapons of our warfare are not the weapons of the flesh. Instead, they have divine power to demolish strongholds.'),
('2CO', 10, 5, '2CO.10.5', 'We demolish arguments and every presumption set up against the knowledge of God; and we take captive every thought to make it obedient to Christ.'),
('2CO', 10, 6, '2CO.10.6', 'And we will be ready to punish every act of disobedience, as soon as your obedience is complete.'),
('2CO', 10, 7, '2CO.10.7', 'You are looking at outward appearances. If anyone is confident that he belongs to Christ, he should remind himself that we belong to Christ just as much as he does.'),
('2CO', 10, 8, '2CO.10.8', 'For even if I boast somewhat excessively about the authority the Lord gave us for building you up rather than tearing you down, I will not be ashamed.'),
('2CO', 10, 9, '2CO.10.9', 'I do not want to seem to be trying to frighten you by my letters.'),
('2CO', 10, 10, '2CO.10.10', 'For some say, “His letters are weighty and forceful, but his physical presence is unimpressive, and his speaking is of no account.”'),
('2CO', 10, 11, '2CO.10.11', 'Such people should consider that what we are in our letters when absent, we will be in our actions when present.'),
('2CO', 10, 12, '2CO.10.12', 'We do not dare to classify or compare ourselves with some who commend themselves. When they measure themselves by themselves and compare themselves with themselves, they show their ignorance.'),
('2CO', 10, 13, '2CO.10.13', 'We, however, will not boast beyond our limits, but only within the field of influence that God has assigned to us—a field that reaches even to you.'),
('2CO', 10, 14, '2CO.10.14', 'We are not overstepping our bounds, as if we had not come to you. Indeed, we were the first to reach you with the gospel of Christ.'),
('2CO', 10, 15, '2CO.10.15', 'Neither do we boast beyond our limits in the labors of others. But we hope that as your faith increases, our area of influence among you will greatly increase as well,'),
('2CO', 10, 16, '2CO.10.16', 'so that we can preach the gospel in the regions beyond you. Then we will not be boasting in the work already done in another man’s territory.'),
('2CO', 10, 17, '2CO.10.17', 'Rather, “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”'),
('2CO', 10, 18, '2CO.10.18', 'For it is not the one who commends himself who is approved, but the one whom the Lord commends.'),
('2CO', 11, 1, '2CO.11.1', 'I hope you will put up with a little of my foolishness, but you are already doing that.'),
('2CO', 11, 2, '2CO.11.2', 'I am jealous for you with a godly jealousy. For I promised you to one husband, to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.'),
('2CO', 11, 3, '2CO.11.3', 'I am afraid, however, that just as Eve was deceived by the serpent’s cunning, your minds may be led astray from your simple and pure devotion to Christ.'),
('2CO', 11, 4, '2CO.11.4', 'For if someone comes and proclaims a Jesus other than the One we proclaimed, or if you receive a different spirit than the One you received, or a different gospel than the one you accepted, you put up with it very easily.'),
('2CO', 11, 5, '2CO.11.5', 'I consider myself in no way inferior to those “super-apostles.”'),
('2CO', 11, 6, '2CO.11.6', 'Although I am not a polished speaker, I am certainly not lacking in knowledge. We have made this clear to you in every way possible.'),
('2CO', 11, 7, '2CO.11.7', 'Was it a sin for me to humble myself in order to exalt you, because I preached the gospel of God to you free of charge?'),
('2CO', 11, 8, '2CO.11.8', 'I robbed other churches by accepting their support in order to serve you.'),
('2CO', 11, 9, '2CO.11.9', 'And when I was with you and in need, I was not a burden to anyone; for the brothers who came from Macedonia supplied my needs. I have refrained from being a burden to you in any way, and I will continue to do so.'),
('2CO', 11, 10, '2CO.11.10', 'As surely as the truth of Christ is in me, this boasting of mine will not be silenced in the regions of Achaia.'),
('2CO', 11, 11, '2CO.11.11', 'Why? Because I do not love you? God knows I do!'),
('2CO', 11, 12, '2CO.11.12', 'But I will keep on doing what I am doing, in order to undercut those who want an opportunity to be regarded as our equals in the things of which they boast.'),
('2CO', 11, 13, '2CO.11.13', 'For such men are false apostles, deceitful workers, masquerading as apostles of Christ.'),
('2CO', 11, 14, '2CO.11.14', 'And no wonder, for Satan himself masquerades as an angel of light.'),
('2CO', 11, 15, '2CO.11.15', 'It is not surprising, then, if his servants masquerade as servants of righteousness. Their end will correspond to their actions.'),
('2CO', 11, 16, '2CO.11.16', 'I repeat: Let no one take me for a fool. But if you do, then receive me as a fool, so that I too may boast a little.'),
('2CO', 11, 17, '2CO.11.17', 'In this confident boasting of mine, I am not speaking as the Lord would, but as a fool.'),
('2CO', 11, 18, '2CO.11.18', 'Since many are boasting according to the flesh, I too will boast.'),
('2CO', 11, 19, '2CO.11.19', 'For you gladly put up with fools, since you are so wise.'),
('2CO', 11, 20, '2CO.11.20', 'In fact, you even put up with anyone who enslaves you or exploits you or takes advantage of you or exalts himself or strikes you in the face.'),
('2CO', 11, 21, '2CO.11.21', 'To my shame I concede that we were too weak for that! Speaking as a fool, however, I can match what anyone else dares to boast about.'),
('2CO', 11, 22, '2CO.11.22', 'Are they Hebrews? So am I. Are they Israelites? So am I. Are they descendants of Abraham? So am I.'),
('2CO', 11, 23, '2CO.11.23', 'Are they servants of Christ? (I am speaking as if I were out of my mind.) I am so much more: in harder labor, in more imprisonments, in worse beatings, in frequent danger of death.'),
('2CO', 11, 24, '2CO.11.24', 'Five times I received from the Jews the forty lashes minus one.'),
('2CO', 11, 25, '2CO.11.25', 'Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. I spent a night and a day in the open sea.'),
('2CO', 11, 26, '2CO.11.26', 'In my frequent journeys, I have been in danger from rivers and from bandits, in danger from my countrymen and from the Gentiles, in danger in the city and in the country, in danger on the sea and among false brothers,'),
('2CO', 11, 27, '2CO.11.27', 'in labor and toil and often without sleep, in hunger and thirst and often without food, in cold and exposure.'),
('2CO', 11, 28, '2CO.11.28', 'Apart from these external trials, I face daily the pressure of my concern for all the churches.'),
('2CO', 11, 29, '2CO.11.29', 'Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who is led into sin, and I do not burn with grief?'),
('2CO', 11, 30, '2CO.11.30', 'If I must boast, I will boast of the things that show my weakness.'),
('2CO', 11, 31, '2CO.11.31', 'The God and Father of the Lord Jesus, who is forever worthy of praise, knows that I am not lying.'),
('2CO', 11, 32, '2CO.11.32', 'In Damascus, the governor under King Aretas secured the city of the Damascenes in order to arrest me.'),
('2CO', 11, 33, '2CO.11.33', 'But I was lowered in a basket through a window in the wall and escaped his grasp.'),
('2CO', 12, 1, '2CO.12.1', 'I must go on boasting. Although there is nothing to gain, I will go on to visions and revelations from the Lord.'),
('2CO', 12, 2, '2CO.12.2', 'I know a man in Christ who fourteen years ago was caught up to the third heaven. Whether it was in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows.'),
('2CO', 12, 3, '2CO.12.3', 'And I know that this man—whether in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows—'),
('2CO', 12, 4, '2CO.12.4', 'was caught up to Paradise. The things he heard were inexpressible, things that man is not permitted to tell.'),
('2CO', 12, 5, '2CO.12.5', 'I will boast about such a man, but I will not boast about myself, except in my weaknesses.'),
('2CO', 12, 6, '2CO.12.6', 'Even if I wanted to boast, I would not be a fool, because I would be speaking the truth. But I refrain, so no one will credit me with more than he sees in me or hears from me,'),
('2CO', 12, 7, '2CO.12.7', 'or because of these surpassingly great revelations. So to keep me from becoming conceited, I was given a thorn in my flesh, a messenger of Satan, to torment me.'),
('2CO', 12, 8, '2CO.12.8', 'Three times I pleaded with the Lord to take it away from me.'),
('2CO', 12, 9, '2CO.12.9', 'But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.'),
('2CO', 12, 10, '2CO.12.10', 'That is why, for the sake of Christ, I delight in weaknesses, in insults, in hardships, in persecutions, in difficulties. For when I am weak, then I am strong.'),
('2CO', 12, 11, '2CO.12.11', 'I have become a fool, but you drove me to it. In fact, you should have commended me, since I am in no way inferior to those “super-apostles,” even though I am nothing.'),
('2CO', 12, 12, '2CO.12.12', 'The marks of a true apostle—signs, wonders, and miracles—were performed among you with great perseverance.'),
('2CO', 12, 13, '2CO.12.13', 'In what way were you inferior to the other churches, except that I was not a burden to you? Forgive me this wrong!'),
('2CO', 12, 14, '2CO.12.14', 'See, I am ready to come to you a third time, and I will not be a burden, because I am not seeking your possessions, but you. For children should not have to save up for their parents, but parents for their children.'),
('2CO', 12, 15, '2CO.12.15', 'And for the sake of your souls, I will most gladly spend my money and myself. If I love you more, will you love me less?'),
('2CO', 12, 16, '2CO.12.16', 'Be that as it may, I was not a burden to you; but crafty as I am, I caught you by trickery.'),
('2CO', 12, 17, '2CO.12.17', 'Did I exploit you by anyone I sent you?'),
('2CO', 12, 18, '2CO.12.18', 'I urged Titus to visit you, and I sent our brother with him. Did Titus exploit you in any way? Did we not walk in the same Spirit and follow in the same footsteps?'),
('2CO', 12, 19, '2CO.12.19', 'Have you been thinking all along that we were making a defense to you? We speak before God in Christ, and all of this, beloved, is to build you up.'),
('2CO', 12, 20, '2CO.12.20', 'For I am afraid that when I come, I may not find you as I wish, and you may not find me as you wish. I fear that there may be quarreling, jealousy, rage, rivalry, slander, gossip, arrogance, and disorder.'),
('2CO', 12, 21, '2CO.12.21', 'I am afraid that when I come again, my God will humble me before you, and I will be grieved over many who have sinned earlier and have not repented of their acts of impurity, sexual immorality, and debauchery.'),
('2CO', 13, 1, '2CO.13.1', 'This is the third time I am coming to you. “Every matter must be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.”'),
('2CO', 13, 2, '2CO.13.2', 'I already warned you the second time I was with you. So now in my absence I warn those who sinned earlier and everyone else: If I return, I will not spare anyone,'),
('2CO', 13, 3, '2CO.13.3', 'since you are demanding proof that Christ is speaking through me. He is not weak in dealing with you but is powerful among you.'),
('2CO', 13, 4, '2CO.13.4', 'For He was indeed crucified in weakness, yet He lives by God’s power. For we are also weak in Him, yet by God’s power we will live with Him concerning you.'),
('2CO', 13, 5, '2CO.13.5', 'Examine yourselves to see whether you are in the faith; test yourselves. Do you not realize that Jesus Christ is in you—unless you fail the test?'),
('2CO', 13, 6, '2CO.13.6', 'And I hope you will realize that we have not failed the test.'),
('2CO', 13, 7, '2CO.13.7', 'Now we pray to God that you will not do anything wrong—not that we will appear to have stood the test, but that you will do what is right, even if we appear to have failed.'),
('2CO', 13, 8, '2CO.13.8', 'For we cannot do anything against the truth, but only for the truth.'),
('2CO', 13, 9, '2CO.13.9', 'In fact, we rejoice when we are weak but you are strong, and our prayer is for your perfection.'),
('2CO', 13, 10, '2CO.13.10', 'This is why I write these things while absent, so that when I am present I will not need to be severe in my use of the authority that the Lord gave me for building you up, not for tearing you down.'),
('2CO', 13, 11, '2CO.13.11', 'Finally, brothers, rejoice! Aim for perfect harmony, encourage one another, be of one mind, live in peace. And the God of love and peace will be with you.'),
('2CO', 13, 12, '2CO.13.12', 'Greet one another with a holy kiss.'),
('2CO', 13, 13, '2CO.13.13', 'All the saints send you greetings.'),
('2CO', 13, 14, '2CO.13.14', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with all of you.'),
('GAL', 1, 1, 'GAL.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle—sent not from men nor by man, but by Jesus Christ and God the Father, who raised Him from the dead—'),
('GAL', 1, 2, 'GAL.1.2', 'and all the brothers with me, To the churches of Galatia:'),
('GAL', 1, 3, 'GAL.1.3', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ,'),
('GAL', 1, 4, 'GAL.1.4', 'who gave Himself for our sins to rescue us from the present evil age, according to the will of our God and Father,'),
('GAL', 1, 5, 'GAL.1.5', 'to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
('GAL', 1, 6, 'GAL.1.6', 'I am amazed how quickly you are deserting the One who called you by the grace of Christ and are turning to a different gospel—'),
('GAL', 1, 7, 'GAL.1.7', 'which is not even a gospel. Evidently some people are troubling you and trying to distort the gospel of Christ.'),
('GAL', 1, 8, 'GAL.1.8', 'But even if we or an angel from heaven should preach a gospel contrary to the one we preached to you, let him be under a curse!'),
('GAL', 1, 9, 'GAL.1.9', 'As we have said before, so now I say again: If anyone is preaching to you a gospel contrary to the one you received, let him be under a curse!'),
('GAL', 1, 10, 'GAL.1.10', 'Am I now seeking the approval of men, or of God? Or am I striving to please men? If I were still trying to please men, I would not be a servant of Christ.'),
('GAL', 1, 11, 'GAL.1.11', 'For I want you to know, brothers, that the gospel I preached was not devised by man.'),
('GAL', 1, 12, 'GAL.1.12', 'I did not receive it from any man, nor was I taught it; rather, I received it by revelation from Jesus Christ.'),
('GAL', 1, 13, 'GAL.1.13', 'For you have heard of my former way of life in Judaism, how severely I persecuted the church of God and tried to destroy it.'),
('GAL', 1, 14, 'GAL.1.14', 'I was advancing in Judaism beyond many of my contemporaries and was extremely zealous for the traditions of my fathers.'),
('GAL', 1, 15, 'GAL.1.15', 'But when God, who set me apart from my mother’s womb and called me by His grace, was pleased'),
('GAL', 1, 16, 'GAL.1.16', 'to reveal His Son in me so that I might preach Him among the Gentiles, I did not rush to consult with flesh and blood,'),
('GAL', 1, 17, 'GAL.1.17', 'nor did I go up to Jerusalem to the apostles who came before me, but I went into Arabia and later returned to Damascus.'),
('GAL', 1, 18, 'GAL.1.18', 'Only after three years did I go up to Jerusalem to confer with Cephas, and I stayed with him fifteen days.'),
('GAL', 1, 19, 'GAL.1.19', 'But I saw none of the other apostles except James, the Lord’s brother.'),
('GAL', 1, 20, 'GAL.1.20', 'I assure you before God that what I am writing to you is no lie.'),
('GAL', 1, 21, 'GAL.1.21', 'Later I went to the regions of Syria and Cilicia.'),
('GAL', 1, 22, 'GAL.1.22', 'I was personally unknown, however, to the churches of Judea that are in Christ.'),
('GAL', 1, 23, 'GAL.1.23', 'They only heard the account: “The man who formerly persecuted us is now preaching the faith he once tried to destroy.”'),
('GAL', 1, 24, 'GAL.1.24', 'And they glorified God because of me.'),
('GAL', 2, 1, 'GAL.2.1', 'Fourteen years later I went up again to Jerusalem, accompanied by Barnabas. I took Titus along also.'),
('GAL', 2, 2, 'GAL.2.2', 'I went in response to a revelation and set before them the gospel that I preach among the Gentiles. But I spoke privately to those recognized as leaders, for fear that I was running or had already run in vain.'),
('GAL', 2, 3, 'GAL.2.3', 'Yet not even Titus, who was with me, was compelled to be circumcised, even though he was a Greek.'),
('GAL', 2, 4, 'GAL.2.4', 'This issue arose because some false brothers had come in under false pretenses to spy on our freedom in Christ Jesus, in order to enslave us.'),
('GAL', 2, 5, 'GAL.2.5', 'We did not give in to them for a moment, so that the truth of the gospel would remain with you.'),
('GAL', 2, 6, 'GAL.2.6', 'But as for the highly esteemed—whatever they were makes no difference to me; God does not show favoritism—those leaders added nothing to me.'),
('GAL', 2, 7, 'GAL.2.7', 'On the contrary, they saw that I had been entrusted to preach the gospel to the uncircumcised, just as Peter had been to the circumcised.'),
('GAL', 2, 8, 'GAL.2.8', 'For the One who was at work in Peter’s apostleship to the circumcised was also at work in my apostleship to the Gentiles.'),
('GAL', 2, 9, 'GAL.2.9', 'And recognizing the grace that I had been given, James, Cephas, and John—those reputed to be pillars—gave me and Barnabas the right hand of fellowship, so that we should go to the Gentiles, and they to the circumcised.'),
('GAL', 2, 10, 'GAL.2.10', 'They only asked us to remember the poor, the very thing I was eager to do.'),
('GAL', 2, 11, 'GAL.2.11', 'When Cephas came to Antioch, however, I opposed him to his face, because he stood condemned.'),
('GAL', 2, 12, 'GAL.2.12', 'For before certain men came from James, he used to eat with the Gentiles. But when they arrived, he began to draw back and separate himself, for fear of those in the circumcision group.'),
('GAL', 2, 13, 'GAL.2.13', 'The other Jews joined him in his hypocrisy, so that by their hypocrisy even Barnabas was led astray.'),
('GAL', 2, 14, 'GAL.2.14', 'When I saw that they were not walking in line with the truth of the gospel, I said to Cephas in front of them all, “If you, who are a Jew, live like a Gentile and not like a Jew, how can you compel the Gentiles to live like Jews?”'),
('GAL', 2, 15, 'GAL.2.15', 'We who are Jews by birth and not Gentile “sinners”'),
('GAL', 2, 16, 'GAL.2.16', 'know that a man is not justified by works of the law, but by faith in Jesus Christ. So we, too, have believed in Christ Jesus, that we may be justified by faith in Christ and not by works of the law, because by works of the law no one will be justified.'),
('GAL', 2, 17, 'GAL.2.17', 'But if, while we seek to be justified in Christ, we ourselves are found to be sinners, does that make Christ a minister of sin? Certainly not!'),
('GAL', 2, 18, 'GAL.2.18', 'If I rebuild what I have already torn down, I prove myself to be a lawbreaker.'),
('GAL', 2, 19, 'GAL.2.19', 'For through the law I died to the law so that I might live to God.'),
('GAL', 2, 20, 'GAL.2.20', 'I have been crucified with Christ, and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me. The life I live in the body, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself up for me.'),
('GAL', 2, 21, 'GAL.2.21', 'I do not set aside the grace of God. For if righteousness comes through the law, then Christ died for nothing.'),
('GAL', 3, 1, 'GAL.3.1', 'O foolish Galatians! Who has bewitched you? Before your very eyes Jesus Christ was clearly portrayed as crucified.'),
('GAL', 3, 2, 'GAL.3.2', 'I would like to learn just one thing from you: Did you receive the Spirit by works of the law, or by hearing with faith?'),
('GAL', 3, 3, 'GAL.3.3', 'Are you so foolish? After starting in the Spirit, are you now finishing in the flesh?'),
('GAL', 3, 4, 'GAL.3.4', 'Have you suffered so much for nothing, if it really was for nothing?'),
('GAL', 3, 5, 'GAL.3.5', 'Does God lavish His Spirit on you and work miracles among you because you practice the law, or because you hear and believe?'),
('GAL', 3, 6, 'GAL.3.6', 'So also, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
('GAL', 3, 7, 'GAL.3.7', 'Understand, then, that those who have faith are sons of Abraham.'),
('GAL', 3, 8, 'GAL.3.8', 'The Scripture foresaw that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, and foretold the gospel to Abraham: “All nations will be blessed through you.”'),
('GAL', 3, 9, 'GAL.3.9', 'So those who have faith are blessed along with Abraham, the man of faith.'),
('GAL', 3, 10, 'GAL.3.10', 'All who rely on works of the law are under a curse. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who does not continue to do everything written in the Book of the Law.”'),
('GAL', 3, 11, 'GAL.3.11', 'Now it is clear that no one is justified before God by the law, because, “The righteous will live by faith.”'),
('GAL', 3, 12, 'GAL.3.12', 'The law, however, is not based on faith; on the contrary, “The man who does these things will live by them.”'),
('GAL', 3, 13, 'GAL.3.13', 'Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who is hung on a tree.”'),
('GAL', 3, 14, 'GAL.3.14', 'He redeemed us in order that the blessing promised to Abraham would come to the Gentiles in Christ Jesus, so that by faith we might receive the promise of the Spirit.'),
('GAL', 3, 15, 'GAL.3.15', 'Brothers, let me put this in human terms. Even a human covenant, once it is ratified, cannot be canceled or amended.'),
('GAL', 3, 16, 'GAL.3.16', 'The promises were spoken to Abraham and to his seed. The Scripture does not say, “and to seeds,” meaning many, but “and to your seed,” meaning One, who is Christ.'),
('GAL', 3, 17, 'GAL.3.17', 'What I mean is this: The law that came 430 years later does not revoke the covenant previously established by God, so as to nullify the promise.'),
('GAL', 3, 18, 'GAL.3.18', 'For if the inheritance depends on the law, then it no longer depends on a promise; but God freely granted it to Abraham through a promise.'),
('GAL', 3, 19, 'GAL.3.19', 'Why then was the law given? It was added because of transgressions, until the arrival of the seed to whom the promise referred. It was administered through angels by a mediator.'),
('GAL', 3, 20, 'GAL.3.20', 'A mediator is unnecessary, however, for only one party; but God is one.'),
('GAL', 3, 21, 'GAL.3.21', 'Is the law, then, opposed to the promises of God? Certainly not! For if a law had been given that could impart life, then righteousness would certainly have come from the law.')
) as x(osis, chapter, verse, ref, body)
join public.books b on b.osis_code = x.osis
join public.bible_versions v on v.id = b.version_id and v.code = 'BSB'
join public.chapters c on c.book_id = b.id and c.number = x.chapter
on conflict (chapter_id, number) do update set osis_ref = excluded.osis_ref, text = excluded.text;
